AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00087,US_OMB_2025_00087,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Homeland Security,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN,AI for Autonomous Situational Awareness,Department of Homeland Security; CBP; United States,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,RETIRED,종료,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DHS-P2,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00088,US_OMB_2025_00088,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Homeland Security,Cybersecurity,UNKNOWN,Malware Reverse Engineering,Department of Homeland Security; CISA; Cybersecurity; United States,A report is generated from malware samples submitted to the analysis pipeline that is then used by human analysts to facilitate the malware triage process. Additional recommendations are displayed via plugins to reverse engineering tools.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"This use case delivers improved internal government tools for reverse engineering of malware and speeding the development of cyber threat intelligence that can be shared across the government and with CISA partners. Threat actors can leverage the same malware for long periods of time, so having the ability to improve analysis and generation of shareable cyber threat intelligence forces threat actors to spend more resources generating new malware. Machine learning and other analytical tools are leveraged to guide malware analysts and automate elements of the manual reverse engineering process. Automation of tasks such as triage and indicator extraction allow threat hunting analysts to meet high demand and focus more on adversary response.","This AI capability uses deep learning to assist CISA analysts with understanding the content of malware samples, automating tasks such as triage and indicator extraction.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DHS-107,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00089,US_OMB_2025_00089,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Homeland Security,Admin Functions,UNKNOWN,Draft Tailored Summaries of Media Materials for Different Publication Channels,Department of Homeland Security; CISA; Admin Functions; United States,An interface is provided for pre-publication documents to be uploaded. The system will then automatically generate appropriate messaging using approved templates and tag the documents for review prior to publication.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,The Large Language Models (LLMs) will summarize information from historical publications and pre-production documents intended for external publication.,This AI capability accelerates the process of drafting summarized content for CISA’s published products.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DHS-2335,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00090,US_OMB_2025_00090,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Homeland Security,Cybersecurity,"CyberSentry has developed numerous machine learning-based detections to identify trends, patterns, and anomalies in network data that ultimately result in both automated and manual triage by analysts.",Critical Infrastructure Network Anomaly Detection,Department of Homeland Security; CISA; Cybersecurity; United States,"An interface is provided for analysts to query cybersecurity data, and dashboards are provided with potential cybersecurity alerts, including anomalies detected through predictive models and rule-based heuristics.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"This use case delivers improved internal government tools for hunting and detection of malicious threat actors on critical infrastructure networks. It automates manual data fusion and correlation processes and highlights potential anomalies, allowing CISA analysts to focus more time on hunting adversaries.","CyberSentry currently ingests hundreds of terabytes of data from Critical Infrastructure Partners every single day. At petabyte-scale over all collected network data, CyberSentry required a way to filter through the noise to be able to detect Advanced Persistent Threat (APT) and Nation State malicious activity happening within our Partners' networks. CyberSentry has developed numerous machine learning-based detections to identify trends, patterns, and anomalies in network data that ultimately result in both automated and manual triage by analysts.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DHS-106,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00091,US_OMB_2025_00091,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Homeland Security,Admin Functions,"Currently, retrieving and synthesizing content from hundreds of government documents is a slow, manual process.",CISAChat,Department of Homeland Security; CISA; Admin Functions; United States,LLM generated response to the questions posed on uploaded content.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Currently, multiple CISA program offices are using contractor staff to review pre-production content and other internal materials to develop summaries, key themes, and improve clarity. Leveraging a Generative AI solution improves internal agency Customer Experience (CX) and saves staff time.","Currently, retrieving and synthesizing content from hundreds of government documents is a slow, manual process. CISA users need the capability to answer questions, generate summaries, and produce textual responses efficiently using a broad range of information sources—from CISA publications to DHS mandates. AI can streamline and accelerate this workflow by automating information extraction and response generation.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DHS-2306,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00092,US_OMB_2025_00092,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Homeland Security,Admin Functions,UNKNOWN,Automated Detection of Personally Identifiable Information (PII) in Cybersecurity Data,Department of Homeland Security; CISA; Admin Functions; United States,The system sends flagged data rows with potential PII to humans for review.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Automated PII Detection and Review Process uses analytics to identify and manage potential PII in submissions. If PII is flagged, the submission is sent to CISA analysts, who are guided by AI to review and confirm or reject the detection, redacting information if necessary. Privacy experts monitor the system and provide feedback. The system learns from this feedback, ensuring compliance with privacy regulations and improving efficiency by reducing false positives. Regular audits ensure the process remains trustworthy and effective.","To enhance privacy, this AI tool uses Natural Language Processing (NLP) to automatically flag potential PII for review and removal by CISA analysts.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DHS-4,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
