AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00213,US_OMB_2025_00213,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Homeland Security,IT,UNKNOWN,Risk Management Framework (RMF) Automation,Department of Homeland Security; USCG; IT; United States,The primary output is document generation specific to cybersecurity needs. It also can provide knowledge to user for translating and monitors/flags system breaches.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"RMF Automation will cut ATO processing time by more than half by handling repetitive tasks so compliance teams can focus on strategy and still make final decisions. It will speed up documentation and assessments, provide near real-time risk insights, and help collect and manage security evidence to demonstrate compliance.","Provides feature to help users understand complex security and privacy controls into plain language, monitoring of system/security, and generates documents such as FedRamp packages",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DHS-2740,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00214,US_OMB_2025_00214,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Homeland Security,Other,UNKNOWN,FLIR 280 HD,Department of Homeland Security; USCG; Other; United States,The operator views a image of the maritime domain. The AI draws boxes around suspected persons in the water to direct the operator to further investigate those anomalous detections.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Enhanced ability to detect persons in the water to more rapidly deploy life-saving resources.,Rapid detection of distressed persons in the water.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DHS-2745,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00215,US_OMB_2025_00215,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Homeland Security,Admin Functions,"A lack of a comprehensive data-driven tool for informing marine inspection policy has left policymakers to make decisions based on qualitative and anecdotal information, resulting in less-than-optimal allocation of limited marine inspection resources.",Adaptive Risk Model for Inspected Small Passenger Vessels,Department of Homeland Security; USCG; Admin Functions; United States,Numerical score that compares vessels predicted safety risk relative to each other.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"The Small Passenger Vessels Safety Task Force uses machine learning and expert input to build a flexible analysis tool that identifies the main causes of marine casualties and calculates a risk score for each vessel in the largest segment of the U.S.-inspected fleet. By using a logistic regression–based model with basic machine learning, this effort improves how inspectors are allocated, sharpens the focus on higher-risk vessels, and strengthens oversight to improve passenger safety.","A lack of a comprehensive data-driven tool for informing marine inspection policy has left policymakers to make decisions based on qualitative and anecdotal information, resulting in less-than-optimal allocation of limited marine inspection resources.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DHS-178,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00216,US_OMB_2025_00216,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Homeland Security,Service Delivery,UNKNOWN,USCIS Document Translation Service,Department of Homeland Security; USCIS; Service Delivery; United States,The service delivers an image-to-image translation that is displayed side by side with the original document to aid officer in reviewing the evidence and preparing for the interview.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Integrate AI and GenAI models trained on relevant subject matter (e.g., immigration law, visa/immigration applications, family/adoption certificates, and other sourced processing materials) to provide fast, accurate translation of written or other digital documents in various languages. Real-time Interpretation: Utilizing AI and GenAI-powered speech-to-speech, speech-to-text translation tools for efficient communication, consultations, and other interactions within DHS. Across all DHS components the need to support language translation and transcription is crucial for operations and adjudications.",Reduce the man hours needed for translating evidence documents by leveraging AI document translation technology,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DHS-2305,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00217,US_OMB_2025_00217,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Homeland Security,Service Delivery,UNKNOWN,USCIS Speech Translation Service,Department of Homeland Security; USCIS; Service Delivery; United States,Provides speech to speech and speech to text translation in multiple languages through government-issued iPads.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Reduce the manpower needed to verbally communicate with applicants and ensure that they are directed in an accurate and efficient manner.,"Provide efficient communication, consultations, and other live applicant interactions in USCIS offices.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DHS-2514,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00218,US_OMB_2025_00218,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Homeland Security,Benefits Processing,UNKNOWN,Extended Automated Name Harvesting (eANH),Department of Homeland Security; USCIS; Benefits Processing; United States,Extracted names and DOBs,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Since users no longer need to read through the entire set of case evidence, which is often hundreds of pages, this should decrease case processing time while retaining the same or better performance.","OIT is developing a solution that systematically extracts text from evidence documents, identifies aliases and DOBs from the extracted text.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DHS-2627,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00219,US_OMB_2025_00219,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Homeland Security,Admin Functions,UNKNOWN,Sentiment Analysis -FOD Field Offices Complaints and Reviews,Department of Homeland Security; USCIS; Admin Functions; United States,A graph which categorizes the data into different sentiments using databricks dashboard to see how the customer service can be improved. Does not give any recommendation or decision.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,This system indicates the positive or negative feelings people express in their feedback to the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services (USCIS). Survey results categorized to specify the sentiments as positive negative or neutral tone in an excel dashboard.,"The AI solution helps USCIS Field Offices efficiently analyze and categorize large volumes of complaints by using machine learning to identify sentiment trends (positive, negative, or neutral) in public feedback.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DHS-2386,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00220,US_OMB_2025_00220,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Homeland Security,Admin Functions,"USCIS staff currently lack access to AI tools that can accelerate routine knowledge work while maintaining the security, compliance, and privacy requirements specific to USCIS operations. Existing commercial AI solutions cannot access USCIS-specific documents and data, cannot be customized to immigration-specific workflows, and pose data security risks.",Private Artificial Intelligence (AI) Tech Hub (PAiTH),Department of Homeland Security; USCIS; Admin Functions; United States,"PAiTH will generate text-based outputs customized to the user's organizational persona: Legal Persona: Legal research summaries, statute and regulation citations (INA, CFR), case law analysis, draft legal memoranda outlines, document summaries with legal issue identification; Contracts Persona: Market research summaries, FAR/HSAR regulatory guidance, acquisition planning support, vendor comparison analyses, contract language suggestions; Language Translation Persona: Text-to-text translations between English and other languages for immigration documents and communications; Developer Persona: Code generation in various programming languages, code documentation, unit test creation, debugging suggestions, technical documentation drafts; Security Persona: Security compliance checklists, control mapping guidance, risk assessment frameworks, security documentation templates; CFO Persona: Financial research summaries, regulatory compliance guidance, budget justification drafts, data call response templates, training material summaries. All outputs will be text-based responses generated by the AI model, presented in a chat interface, and restricted to authorized USCIS personnel. Outputs will include appropriate disclaimers (e.g., ""This is AI-generated research support, not legal advice"" for legal persona) and accompanying policy will require human review before being used in any official decision-making, formal communications, and/or reporting.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"The purpose of PAiTH is to provide USCIS employees with an internal, secure AI assistant that delivers role-specific support for knowledge work tasks. The system will offer six persona-based assistants aligned to core USCIS job functions, each trained and prompted to provide relevant, accurate responses for that role's responsibilities. Intended benefits of PAiTH include: Increased Efficiency: Staff can quickly obtain research, draft language, translations, and technical guidance without manual searching through documents or external research; Role-Specific Accuracy: Persona-based responses tailored to each user's organizational function (legal, contracting, development, etc.) provide more relevant and useful outputs than generic AI; Data Security and Compliance: Internal deployment protects PII and sensitive USCIS data while maintaining compliance with federal security and privacy requirements; Controlled Access to USCIS Knowledge: AI can leverage USCIS-specific documents, policies, and data sources that are inaccessible to commercial AI tools, keeping sensitive information within USCIS boundaries; Standardization: Consistent AI-assisted workflows across the agency reduce variability in research and drafting quality; and Cost Savings: Reduces time spent on routine knowledge tasks, allowing staff to focus on complex decision-making and judgment-based work.","USCIS staff currently lack access to AI tools that can accelerate routine knowledge work while maintaining the security, compliance, and privacy requirements specific to USCIS operations. Existing commercial AI solutions cannot access USCIS-specific documents and data, cannot be customized to immigration-specific workflows, and pose data security risks. Staff spend significant time on tasks that AI could assist with—such as legal research, document drafting, language translation, code generation, and regulatory compliance checks—but have no approved internal AI capability. Additionally, different organizational roles have vastly different AI assistance needs (e.g., attorneys need legal citations; developers need code; contracting officers need FAR guidance, budget officers need access to sensitive internal fiscal data), requiring a solution that adapts to the user's function rather than providing generic responses. PAiTH will also promote USCIS innovation by enabling testing of a variety of large language models and AI platforms, while informing approaches on prompt generation, cost containment and workforce literacy.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DHS-2599,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00221,US_OMB_2025_00221,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Homeland Security,Law Enforcement,UNKNOWN,Text Analytics Data Science Sentence Similarity Model,Department of Homeland Security; USCIS; Law Enforcement; United States,"Text Analytics does not make predictions, recommendations, or decisions. It is merely a research tool that identifies potential patterns, while remaining agnostic as to whether those patterns identify potential fraud, national security, and/or public safety concerns. Instead, trained staff evaluate the patterns to determine whether they identify potential concerns and then validate and/or invalidate those potential concerns through the course of their investigations or adjudications.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Text Analytics augments the tedious and time-consuming manual process to identify potential fraud, national security, and/or public safety concerns and enables the identification of such concerns across jurisdictional boundaries. It increases the integrity of immigration programs, strengthens officers’ confidence in their work, and contributes to the reduction in customer wait times.","The Text Analytics capability employs machine learning and data graphing techniques to identify patterns that may indicate potential fraud, national security, and/or public safety concerns by scanning the digitized narrative sections of the associated applications and looking for common language patterns.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DHS-130,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00222,US_OMB_2025_00222,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""enterprise_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Homeland Security,Admin Functions,UNKNOWN,Automated Realtime Global Organization Specialist (ARGOS) for Company Registration Submissions to E-Verify,Department of Homeland Security; USCIS; Admin Functions; United States,Responses back to a user dashboard accessible internally only by VAC Management and Program Analyst (MPA) personnel. Keywords relating to the MPA's work interest are extracted if present and risk scores are assigned to the open-source collected information. The data is presented to the MPA on the GUI (graphical user interface) dashboard.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"ARGOS sentiment analysis produces a risk score and keyword extraction identifies the keyword category of interest to the VAC MPAs (management and program analyst) for the aggregated open-source information to help quickly identify any pertinent information to aid the MPAs in their open-source investigation of company applications. This saves potentially thousands of MPA man hours in open-source investigation and creates a single source-of-truth for each MPAs investigation of a company application. This, in turn, allows for quicker application processing and, if risk of company fraud exists, much faster referral processing time quickening the next-step referral to FDNS for further investigations.",The goal of the use case is to leverage sentiment analysis in ARGOS to streamline the process and accelerate work for the individual who is researching a company that has submitted its information for registration to E-Verify.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DHS-181,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00223,US_OMB_2025_00223,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Homeland Security,Admin Functions,"ML plays a key role in the continuous improvement of these models, ultimately reducing the need for manual case reviews.",Verification Match Model,Department of Homeland Security; USCIS; Admin Functions; United States,A recommendation and score that indicates person-and-record match probability used by verification systems (E-verify and SAVE) to improve accuracy in initial system response,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Leveraging AI in the USCIS verification matching process of known records across systems is beneficial because it streamlines existing USCIS review by 1) improving associated system accuracy, 2) reducing human-error by automating person-and-record match scoring, and 3) matching at a higher volume than traditional tools or manual processes can capably achieve.","By consolidating these into a single, unified Verification Match Model within a separate microservice, the use case aims to improve the accuracy of responses and reduce the need for manual review. ML plays a key role in the continuous improvement of these models, ultimately reducing the need for manual case reviews.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DHS-2384,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00224,US_OMB_2025_00224,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Homeland Security,Law Enforcement,UNKNOWN,I-765 - USCIS Facial Recognition through IDENT (1:1 Face Recognition/Validation),Department of Homeland Security; USCIS; Law Enforcement; United States,Match or no match response from IDENT.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,This will allow the user to complete the biometric verification requirement without having to attend an appointment at am Applicant Support Center. This reduces the burden on the beneficiary as well as reducing demands on USCIS Applicant Service Center resources.,"Using the Automated Biometric Identification System (IDENT) makes this process nearly instant and greatly enhances processing efficiency without compromising the effectiveness of current identity verification methods. Additionally, new rules created by the FBI’s Compact Council require biometric verification to perform fingerprint resubmissions for different filing reasons than the original fingerprint capture. Facial verification brings USCIS into compliance with this rule change. Furthermore, performing facial verification increases the integrity of information and identities by identifying conflicts early on, preventing issues from becoming pervasive across immigration systems.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DHS-413,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00225,US_OMB_2025_00225,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Homeland Security,Law Enforcement,UNKNOWN,Person-Centric Identity Services Deduplication Model,Department of Homeland Security; USCIS; Law Enforcement; United States,"Numerical likelihood score which is used to determine if the record belongs to the individual. Likelihood scores are subjected to a high threshold (.98, maximum 1) to assess whether the record belongs to the individual.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Using Machine Learning allows us to improve entity resolution as compared to rule based system. PCIS offers the ability to see a person's immigration history organized in one place. Specific benefits do or will include: an organized summary view of the identity with the individual's latest photo from PCIS; full immigration history including receipts associated with the applicant, regardless of case management system; mailing, physical, and safe history of the individual organized in reverse chronological order, allowing users to easily find the most recent address; and all identifiers associated with the applicant, including A-Numbers, FINs, SSNs, SSNs, ELIS account numbers, passport numbers, etc.","Critical to the success of PCIS is the entity resolution and de-deduplication of individual records from various systems of records to create a complete picture of a person. Using machine learning (ML), the model can identify which case management records belong to the same unique individual with a high degree of confidence. This allows PCIS to compile a full immigration history for an individual without the need for time-consuming research across multiple disparate systems. The de-duplication model plays a critical role in the entity resolution and surfacing of a person and all their associated records. The ML models are more resilient to fuzzy matches and handle varying data fill rates more reliably.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DHS-55,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00226,US_OMB_2025_00226,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Homeland Security,Law Enforcement,UNKNOWN,Biometrics Enrollment Tool (BET) Fingerprint Quality Check,Department of Homeland Security; USCIS; Law Enforcement; United States,"Numerical Fingerprint Quality score, which is compared against fingerprint quality thresholds (per finger and per set of fingerprints) to align with FBI specifications",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"BET assists in determining if the fingerprint taken is good enough quality to pass the FBI fingerprint check process. It provides immediate feedback when a set of prints is likely to be rejected by the FBI by incorporating machine learning models into the BET application. The FBI will not disclose their quality grading criteria for fingerprints, leaving BET with the responsibility of determining quality to prevent unnecessary secondary encounters with applicants.","This effort aims to maximize the number of successful FBI submissions while minimizing the number of fingerprint recaptures necessary. The output is a Numerical Fingerprint Quality score, which is compared against fingerprint quality thresholds (per finger and per set of fingerprints) to align with FBI specifications.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DHS-14,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00227,US_OMB_2025_00227,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Homeland Security,Service Delivery,Adjudicators spend significant amount of time manually harvesting aliases and dates of birth (DOBs) from identity history summary (IdHS) report attached to the ELIS case as part of the Manual Name Harvesting Task during case processing.,Automated Name and Date of Birth (DOB) Harvesting Service,Department of Homeland Security; USCIS; Service Delivery; United States,Suggested Names and DOBs from IdHS record.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,To reduce the amount of adjudicative time spent manually harvesting aliases and dates of birth (DOBs) from identity history summary (IdHS) report attached to the ELIS case as part of the Manual Name Harvesting Task during case processing.,Adjudicators spend significant amount of time manually harvesting aliases and dates of birth (DOBs) from identity history summary (IdHS) report attached to the ELIS case as part of the Manual Name Harvesting Task during case processing.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DHS-180,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00228,US_OMB_2025_00228,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Homeland Security,Service Delivery,UNKNOWN,ELIS Card Photo Validation Service,Department of Homeland Security; USCIS; Service Delivery; United States,Response back to user based on the pre-defined quality checks if the uploaded photo meets USCIS requirements. Users still have the option to ignore the warnings and upload the photo.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Ensuring beneficiary uploaded photos meet USCIS requirements. This helps ensure photos are correct before making ID cards, saving adjudicator time and avoiding delays.",The card photo validation solution was developed to validate each submitted photo against a set of business-defined requirements in near-real-time in order to eliminate rejections/RFEs for the user uploaded photos.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DHS-189,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00229,US_OMB_2025_00229,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Homeland Security,Cybersecurity,UNKNOWN,AI Security and Monitoring,Department of Homeland Security; USCIS; Cybersecurity; United States,"The AI System outputs risk alerts, compliance reports, and audit logs. It predicts threats, recommends policy adjustment, and semi-autonomously enforces guardrails. It secures data and AI usage via blocking, masking, and context-aware decisions.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"The gateway will secure enterprise AI use by discovering shadow AI, enforcing guardrails, and preventing data spills. Its benefits include improved compliance, reduced risk, real time protection, and enhanced visibility. Organizations are empowered to securely and efficiently adopt AI.","Organizations adopting AI face a number of risks from data leaks, shadow AI, and unsecured outputs.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DHS-2543,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00230,US_OMB_2025_00230,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Homeland Security,Cybersecurity,UNKNOWN,User Entity and Behavior Analytics (UEBA) for Security Operations (SecOps) Anomaly Identification,Department of Homeland Security; USCIS; Cybersecurity; United States,Output of the Machine Learning is an alert with all artifacts for the SOC to investigate. The alert is used as a recommendation to prioritize specific investigations in the SOC ticket queue.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"UEBA's purpose is to review USCIS system logs to determine when an entity is performing actions that are anomalous. An entity can be classified as a workstation, server or an internal USCIS system account. The UEBA ingests logs from systems to perform analytics based off of models that are manually created and maintained. UEBA uses the models to apply a risk score to the entity which the risk score is then used to create a case (or ticket) for Security Operations analyst review. The AI reviews the action of the analyst to adjust the risk scoring for future events. Output would assist in prioritizing cyber events for further manual investigation.","User Entity and Behavior Analytics (UEBA) assists USCIS Security Operations (SecOps) in identifying behavioral anomalies that most likely indicate malicious intent or heightened risk associated with user identities and endpoint hosts accessing the USCIS network. The analytics provide risk scoring, which helps USCIS SecOps to prioritize highest risk incidents first.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DHS-372,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00231,US_OMB_2025_00231,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Homeland Security,Law Enforcement,UNKNOWN,Person-Centric Identity Services Information Compilation Check,Department of Homeland Security; USCIS; Law Enforcement; United States,"Numerical likelihood score which is used to determine the validity of the A# presented. Likelihood scores are subjected to a high threshold (.98, maximum 1) to assess whether the A# presented belongs to the individual.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"The aim of this use case is to leverage machine learning to test the accuracy of PCIS to identify and manage associations between individuals and their assigned A-numbers, which is a unique 7, 8, or 9 digit number assigned to a noncitizen by DHS. The A-Number plays a critical role in surfacing of a person and all their associated records from across PCIS.",The output of the use case is the numerical confidence score which is used to determine the validity of the A-number presented in search results. The confidence score identifies which records from within PCIS best match search criteria for an A-number.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DHS-56,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00232,US_OMB_2025_00232,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Homeland Security,Service Delivery,UNKNOWN,ELIS Evidence Classifier Service,Department of Homeland Security; USCIS; Service Delivery; United States,"Tagged evidence. The system inputs an image (scanned document from Lockbox) and outputs either a specific label, such as ""Border Crossing Card - Front,"" or no label if that document is not recognized as one of the classes.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"To enable end users to navigate directly to the page(s) containing evidence documents of interest instead of sifting through large PDF documents. Evidence tagging intends to accelerate case processing by identifying specific types of documents (e.g., I-589, passport photo spread, marriage certificate) and applying a metadata tag to that document object in ELIS. This way, when a user opens a case with potentially hundreds of pages of evidence documents, rather than scrolling through them one at a time to find a specific document of interest, they have clickable ""bookmarks"" in the UI generated from these tags that will jump directly to the corresponding page.",The adjudicators and contractors spends too much time sifting through digital evidence documents for relevant information.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DHS-16,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00233,US_OMB_2025_00233,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Homeland Security,Admin Functions,UNKNOWN,Intelligent Document Processing (IDP) for I-539 Form Digitization,Department of Homeland Security; USCIS; Admin Functions; United States,"Input - one digital file comprised of all pages of a 539 benefit application. Output - multiple digital files comprised of the individual documents submitted as part of the 539 benefit application. These will include the 539 form, any other USCIS forms, and image files of other supporting documents such as Passports, Driver's license, Marriage Certificate, Bank Statement, etc. All pages of the original digital file are accounted for and stored. Any pages not identified by the tool are referred to a human for document type resolution.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"IDP for the I-539 makes use of an AI-enhanced tool to identify, categorize, and create separate images for each document type submitted as part of the 539 benefit application. Prior to implementation of this use case, all pages of a 539 application were scanned and stored as a single document in the content management system. The benefit is reduced case processing time for adjudicators by identifying and classifying supporting documents for ease of use. An additional benefit is to bring digital images into compliance with NARA standards.","Before the use case, all pages of a I-539 application were scanned and stored as a single document in the content management system, delaying adjudication and not meeting National Archives and Records Administration (NARA) standards. The tool uses a learning model to identify, classify, and separate individual documents into their component parts for storage.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DHS-2385,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00234,US_OMB_2025_00234,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Homeland Security,Benefits Processing,UNKNOWN,PDF Intake (PDFI) for myUSCIS,Department of Homeland Security; USCIS; Benefits Processing; United States,"The output of this AI system is structured information about the validation rules applied to the input form as well as the extracted contents of filled fields on the form, presented in a JSON format readable by both humans and machines that is consistent with existing ELIS databases.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Develop a service that can extract relevant fields from a scanned PDF submitted through MyUSCIS and build a JSON as an output to the ELIS microservice. The new service will utilize AWS Bedrock provided foundation model. It is an engineering solution that minimizes development time to add new forms or form revisions with high accuracy.,Scanned PDFs submitted through MyUSCIS must be validated against form-specific business rules related to both the overall document and the contents of specific fields. Constructed a service that can process a scanned input document and return all information pertinent to these validation rules in a consistent structure (JSON) to a user-facing ELIS microservice. The GenAI powered library utilizes Amazon Bedrock – Anthropic Claude 3.7 Sonnet V1 Foundation Model to extract data from PDF forms. The service provides ability to submit forms online through MyUSCIS UI to Lockbox instead of via mail.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,S3_DOCUMENT_INTELLIGENCE,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DHS-2598,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00235,US_OMB_2025_00235,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Homeland Security,Admin Functions,UNKNOWN,AI Interview Simulator for Officer Training,Department of Homeland Security; USCIS; Admin Functions; United States,"The AI Interview Simulator generates human-like conversation in a text format, specially trained and tuned for RAIO Officer training.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,The AI Interview Simulator mimics live interviews to provide an analysis of the type of responses elicited in a mock interview. This training platform accelerates the competency of the interviews by providing a format for the trainees to practice soliciting testimony from applicants through a chat-based user interface.,"By simulating realistic applicant responses to officer questions, the AI Interview Simulator enables the RAIO trainees to refine their interview techniques without requiring any additional resources from experienced officer trainers or peers.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DHS-366,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
