AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00441,US_OMB_2025_00441,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Commerce,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN,Grants Program Administration - Inquiry management Chatbot Pilot,Department of Commerce; NTIA; United States,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,UNKNOWN,단계 미확인,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOC-201,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00442,US_OMB_2025_00442,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Commerce,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN,Grants Program Administration - BEAD Monitoring Plan Agent Pilot,Department of Commerce; NTIA; United States,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"The AI system—referred to as the BEAD Monitoring Agent—is designed to enhance the ability of Federal Program Officers (FPOs) to support Eligible Entities (EEs) in monitoring their subrecipients after a Final Proposal (FP) is approved. The motivation for deploying this AI is grounded in NTIA’s need to rapidly and effectively understand the contents of each EE’s FP to support post-award monitoring. Benefits: 1. Faster, More Thorough Review: The AI agent quickly reviews EE subgrantee monitoring plans by comparing them against a “gold standard,” helping FPOs identify best practices, inconsistencies, and gaps 2. Enhanced Risk Mitigation: By providing recommendations on oversight and potential mitigation actions, the AI helps identify areas where closer monitoring or NTIA support may be needed 3. Standardization and Transparency: The AI outputs enable more standardized and data-driven oversight across diverse plans, informing risk assessments and follow-up activities",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,UNKNOWN,단계 미확인,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOC-202,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00443,US_OMB_2025_00443,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Commerce,UNKNOWN,"Reduced Burden on Entities: Utilizes information already submitted to NTIA, combined with federally available data, to minimize the effort required by entities in preparing the initial draft of a tiered EA.",Grants Program Administration - Tiered Environmental Assessment AI Pilot,Department of Commerce; NTIA; United States,"The NTIA Tiered EA AI Pilot leverages AI to streamline the initial drafting of the “Affected Environment” section in NTIA Tiered Environmental Assessment templates by integrating project-specific data and geospatial resources. The pilot aims to evaluate AI’s effectiveness in drafting content within the tiered EA; if successful, NTIA may expand the use case to provide eligible entities with pre-populated tiered EAs based on submitted information, rather than blank templates, to accelerate permitting.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"The NTIA Tiered EA AI Pilot leverages AI to streamline the initial drafting of the “Affected Environment” section in NTIA Tiered Environmental Assessment templates by integrating project-specific data and geospatial resources. The pilot aims to evaluate AI’s effectiveness in drafting content within the tiered EA; if successful, NTIA may expand the use case to provide eligible entities with pre-populated tiered EAs based on submitted information, rather than blank templates, to accelerate permitting. Benefits: 1. Efficiency: Automates a typically time-consuming, manual process, reducing turnaround time for drafting EAs. 2. Consistency and Standardization: By pre-populating sections with structured data and draft text, the AI helps ensure consistency across assessments and adherence to templates. 3. Reduced Burden on Entities: Utilizes information already submitted to NTIA, combined with federally available data, to minimize the effort required by entities in preparing the initial draft of a tiered EA.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,UNKNOWN,단계 미확인,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOC-203,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00444,US_OMB_2025_00444,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Commerce,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN,"NTIA Grants Portal (NGP) - AI Summarization, Analytics, and Automations",Department of Commerce; NTIA; United States,"Our team is exploring using AI to support our grant program administration, specifically supporting some AI-enable knowledge management for our internal team and supporting reviews of post award technical/progress/performance/financial reports to identify trends, identify inconsistencies, increase efficiencies in processing and monitoring tasks, etc.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Our team is exploring using AI to support our grant program administration, specifically supporting some AI-enable knowledge management for our internal team and supporting reviews of post award technical/progress/performance/financial reports to identify trends, identify inconsistencies, increase efficiencies in processing and monitoring tasks, etc. The latter may be more a mix of predictive and generative AI.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,UNKNOWN,단계 미확인,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOC-204,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00445,US_OMB_2025_00445,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Commerce,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN,Using AI to assess the AI-readiness of Commerce data,Department of Commerce; OS; United States,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,The system measures the ability of large language models to accurately respond to questions that require an understanding of federal statistical open data resources. It will help the Department identify data quality gaps and improve the quality of departmental data by making it AI-ready.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,UNKNOWN,단계 미확인,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOC-205,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00446,US_OMB_2025_00446,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Commerce,UNKNOWN,"This tool enhances accessibility, reduces administrative burden, and improves service delivery to state, local, and tribal government partners.",BAS Assist,Department of Commerce; OS; United States,"BAS Assist is being developed and deployed in alignment with the Department’s enterprise AI risk management protocols, including those articulated under Section 3(a) of M-25-21 for inventory reporting, post-deployment monitoring, and incident response.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"BAS Assist, a generative AI chatbot that supports users of the enterprise BAS applications. BAS Assist provides real-time guidance in natural, conversational language, enabling users to more effectively complete application tasks, resolve common issues, and access technical assistance without requiring direct staff intervention. This tool enhances accessibility, reduces administrative burden, and improves service delivery to state, local, and tribal government partners. BAS Assist is being developed and deployed in alignment with the Department’s enterprise AI risk management protocols, including those articulated under Section 3(a) of M-25-21 for inventory reporting, post-deployment monitoring, and incident response.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,UNKNOWN,단계 미확인,,S2_AGENT_CONVERSATIONAL_AI,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOC-206,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00447,US_OMB_2025_00447,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Commerce,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN,DOC Chat,Department of Commerce; OS; United States,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,UNKNOWN,단계 미확인,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOC-207,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00448,US_OMB_2025_00448,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Commerce,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN,USAi.gov,Department of Commerce; OS; United States,"USAI.gov enables bureaus to rapidly pilot and scale AI use cases—ranging from document drafting and data summarization to policy analysis—within a controlled environment that incorporates enterprise risk management, security safeguards, and privacy protections. This effort embodies a DOC enterprise approach to technology modernization, ensuring that bureaus leverage shared resources to realize efficiencies, reduce duplication, and accelerate innovation.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"The Department is deploying USAI.gov, a government-wide generative AI capability provided by the General Services Administration (GSA), designed to provide employees with secure, role-appropriate access to advanced large-language-model tools. USAI.gov enables bureaus to rapidly pilot and scale AI use cases—ranging from document drafting and data summarization to policy analysis—within a controlled environment that incorporates enterprise risk management, security safeguards, and privacy protections. This effort embodies a DOC enterprise approach to technology modernization, ensuring that bureaus leverage shared resources to realize efficiencies, reduce duplication, and accelerate innovation. Governance for USAI.gov is planned for coordination through the Office of the Chief Information Officer (OCIO), in close consultation with bureau CIOs, bureau AI Leads, and functional area experts across cybersecurity, data governance, privacy, civil rights, and acquisitions.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,UNKNOWN,단계 미확인,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOC-208,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
