AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00554,US_OMB_2025_00554,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Energy,Science,UNKNOWN,In-pixel AI for future tracking detectors,Department of Energy; FNAL - Fermi National Accelerator (SC43 OIM); Science; United States,"A recommendation of whether to save data based on AI classifier. Or, a fast inference of track parameters to be used for fast selection",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,AI algorithms are implemented in on-detector electronics in order to reduce data size and enable processing at high rates.,This project explores novel AI-on-chip technology for intelligent detectors embedded with sensing technology,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOE-66,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
