AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00557,US_OMB_2025_00557,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Energy,Science,UNKNOWN,Uncertainty Quantification and Instrument Automation to enable next generation cosmological discoveries,Department of Energy; FNAL - Fermi National Accelerator (SC43 OIM); Science; United States,ai algorithms,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,create new methods for uncertainty quantification in AI,"This project will develop AI-based tools to enable critical sectors for near-future cosmic applications. Uncertainty quantification is essential for performing discovery science now, and simulation-based inference offers a new approach. The automated",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOE-69,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00558,US_OMB_2025_00558,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Energy,Science,UNKNOWN,READS: Real-time Edge AI for Distributed Systems,Department of Energy; FNAL - Fermi National Accelerator (SC43 OIM); Science; United States,The ML outputs of the system are inferences as to the origin of beam loss in the Main Injector acclerator enclosure and also suggested regulation ramps to best improve the Spill Duty Factor in the Delivery Ring for Mu2e,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"READS has two sub-projects. The first project created the means to stream live Main Injector and Recycler accelerator beam loss monitor data. This data is then fed to an AI model deployed on an FPGA so that it can infer, in realtime, the origin of beam loss, either Main Injector or Recycler, for each beam loss monitor in the tunnel enclosure. The second project aimed to improve upon traditional resonant beam extraction regulation techiniques using AI for use in the Fermilab Delivery Ring and Mu2e.",This project will develop and deploy low-latency controls and prediction algorithms at the Fermilab accelerator complex,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOE-70,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00559,US_OMB_2025_00559,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Energy,Science,UNKNOWN,Simulation-based inference for cosmology,Department of Energy; FNAL - Fermi National Accelerator (SC43 OIM); Science; United States,prediction of numerical values of cosmology,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,DOE ECA award. apply SBI to strong lensing and cmb to infer cosmological parameters,"This project will develop and use simulation-based inference to estimate cosmological parameters related to cosmic acceleration in the early and late universe — via the cosmic microwave background and strong gravitational lensing, respectively. This",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOE-71,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00560,US_OMB_2025_00560,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Energy,Science,UNKNOWN,Denoising Diffusion to Accelerate Detector Simulation,Department of Energy; FNAL - Fermi National Accelerator (SC43 OIM); Science; United States,The AI system outputs simulated detector hits (energy deposits) in one or more subdetectors of the particle physics experiment.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"This effort is exploring generative AI to replace costly detector simulation. This would enable faster, more accurate simulation, accelerating and enhancing scientific results and allowing easier use of GPU coprocessors at HPC centers.",This program aims to develop generative models for quickly simulating showers of particles in calorimeters for LHC experiments,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOE-716,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
