AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00812,US_OMB_2025_00812,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,Service Delivery,"This will help users quickly identify and apply resources relevant to their workflows, reduce manual search time, and improve access to credible scientific evidence for decision-making.",Assessment Inventory and Monitoring (AIM) Chatbot,Department of the Interior; BLM; Service Delivery; United States,"Text-based recommendations based on internal guidance documents, monitoring methodologies, and example uses case pertaining to monitoring. The outputs direct the users that the AI responses are strictly for information gathering purposes.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Data collected under the AIM program are made available for both internal BLM use in decision making and public consumption.,"The AIM program provides access to data from 73,000+ monitoring locations and offers tools, guidance, and workflows to support BLM staff in structured, repeatable data collection and application. While resources enhance decision-making, their volume makes discovery and use challenging, often requiring AIM team support. To streamline access, we propose a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) chatbot that uses AI to summarize documents and tools via metadata and embedded PDFs, enabling natural language queries. This will help users quickly identify and apply resources relevant to their workflows, reduce manual search time, and improve access to credible scientific evidence for decision-making. The chatbot will also free AIM staff to focus on advanced analysis by handling basic inquiries, increasing efficiency and capacity for both users and the Bureau.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,S2_AGENT_CONVERSATIONAL_AI|S3_DOCUMENT_INTELLIGENCE,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0053,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00813,US_OMB_2025_00813,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,Admin Functions,UNKNOWN,NEPA Document Generation,Department of the Interior; BLM; Admin Functions; United States,content for NEPA documents.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Faster processing and writing of NEPA documents, which can often be time intensive.","Utilize generative AI to generate content for NEPA documentation. Will gather information from ePlanning, and with the link from other systems will be able to draw the project information from that system into ePlanning and then into a CE. We have the templates mapped with about 35% of the information coming from either ePlanning or ePlanning/MLRS.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,S7_GENERATIVE_CONTENT_CREATION,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0051,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00814,US_OMB_2025_00814,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,Admin Functions,UNKNOWN,GraphRAG Comment Analysis and Management Solution,Department of the Interior; BLM; Admin Functions; United States,"Analysis, binning, categorization, and responses.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Speed of comment response. Handle the responses and consolidate responses.,"Comment analysis - identifying and binning comments from the public. Will intake comments from a variety of sources and AI then breaks them down by issue area. Anticipate training that model with NEPA projects, rulemaking, and public comments on a draft document.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0050,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00815,US_OMB_2025_00815,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,IT,UNKNOWN,User guides/training provided in chat form,Department of the Interior; BLM; IT; United States,Recommendation for the business user on how to accomplish their tasks in an efficient and accurate way.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"We have 10 applications, each with user guides that range from minimal to over 200 pages. This will create efficiency by helping the staff finding relevant information when needed. This should reduce the amount of training material and user guides created","We have multiple systems with multiple user guides that are 200 plus pages. Additionally, we have a significant amount of training material. Our customer survey responses always identify that they are not usable because they are so dense and they are often needed in the field, i.e., they are too cumbersome to download and read on tablets and phones. I would like them to be available to the AI as source material so that our users can ask specific questions. I want to do this without having to rewrite and format the PDF documents. The applications are only for internal users, and the documentation is not considered sensitive. If this use case works, I have other documentation I would like to also consider in the future.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0049,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
