AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00827,US_OMB_2025_00827,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,Energy and Environment,"Currently, BSEE manually reviews each report to determine if a platform requires further audits, a process that is both time and labor intensive.",Level 1 Survey Report Corrosion Level Classification,Department of the Interior; BSEE; Energy and Environment; United States,The outputs will include a comparison between the original corrosion level assigned to each image in the Level 1 Survey and the corresponding level determined by the machine learning algorithm.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Support a more efficient and accurate review of Level 1 Survey photo corrosion levels,"Offshore operators conduct Level 1 surveys annually to report on platform structural integrity, as mandated by 30 CFR 250.901(a)(7), and submit these surveys to BSEE. Each survey includes a corrosion assessment of the platform with accompanying photos. Each area is assigned a coating grade and are key indicators of a platforms overall structural health. Currently, BSEE manually reviews each report to determine if a platform requires further audits, a process that is both time and labor intensive.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0257,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00828,US_OMB_2025_00828,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,Energy and Environment,UNKNOWN,Well Activity Report Classification,Department of the Interior; BSEE; Energy and Environment; United States,Decision on what type of significant event a well activity report should report.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Enable quicker detection of significant well events to help BSEE personnel mitigate risks and address issues more efficiently.,Researching the use of Masked Language Models and Convolutional deep neural networks to identify classification systems for significant well event using data from Well Activity Reports.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0256,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00829,US_OMB_2025_00829,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,Energy and Environment,UNKNOWN,Autonomous Drone Inspections,Department of the Interior; BSEE; Energy and Environment; United States,"Multiple outputs for inspections, including decisions on corrosion levels, if a platform is boardable, does it have methane leaks.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Increase the inspection capabilities and efficiency of inspections through the use of small autonomous uncrewed aerial systems (sUAS).,"The Bureau of Safety and Environmental Enforcement within the Department Of Interior, is requesting a trade study of the feasibility of autonomously inspecting off-shore facilities that are non-boardable due to various hazards. These inspections are currently performed by inspectors at a stand off distance from the non-boardable facility on board boats, helicopters, or from land. The distance between the personnel and the facility reduces the quality of inspections that are possible for non-boardable facilities.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0255,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00830,US_OMB_2025_00830,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,Admin Functions,"For Department of Justice litigation or other records research and discovery, this doubles the page count, making manual review unnecessarily time-consuming and resource-intensive. Automating blank page detection with Non-Generative AI (e.g., Azure Computer Vision and Document Intelligence Read) helps streamline this process and reduce burden.",Non-Generative AI use for Trust Information Analysis and Reporting Tool [2024 INV#WO0000000110516],Department of the Interior; BTFA; Admin Functions; United States,The output provides the final documents with the blank pages removed.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Staff no longer need to inspect and remove every blank page. Fewer pages to review means lower costs for records storage and contract/labor expenses. Enables BTFA to respond more quickly to DOJ litigation requests by streamlining document preparation.,"When records are scanned, both front and back pages are captured, even though back pages are generally blank. For Department of Justice litigation or other records research and discovery, this doubles the page count, making manual review unnecessarily time-consuming and resource-intensive. Automating blank page detection with Non-Generative AI (e.g., Azure Computer Vision and Document Intelligence Read) helps streamline this process and reduce burden.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0002,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00831,US_OMB_2025_00831,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,IT,UNKNOWN,"Integration of AI, specifically CoPilot for GitHub, for BTFA Software Development Life Cycle Process for DME and O&M applications.",Department of the Interior; BTFA; IT; United States,changes in source code after review by application/dba staff along with appropriate testing before going to production.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Due to reduce staffing, BTFA needs to integrate AI for its DME and O&M of applications and servers (database/application/web/etc) which has sophisticated code base. AI has show promise in reducing staff hours for all phases of SDLC.","Reductions in BTFA Application and Database Staff has lead to increase workload for remaining staff for DME and O&M activities of applications and servers. This code is considered sophisticated in nature, code resides in Azure App Workspace (Web/Function/Logic Apps) and standalone applications and servers.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0001,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00832,US_OMB_2025_00832,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,Science,UNKNOWN,Development of a computer vision model to monitor for early detection of habitat loss across the landscape. [2024 INV#DOI-65],Department of the Interior; FWS; Science; United States,"AI-powered computer vision enables early detection of habitat loss, allowing faster, more accurate responses to threats. This supports better conservation decisions and helps protect and recover threatened and endangered species.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"AI-powered computer vision enables early detection of habitat loss, allowing faster, more accurate responses to threats. This supports better conservation decisions and helps protect and recover threatened and endangered species.","The U.S. Fish and Wildlife Service is planning to partner with the Chesapeake Conservancy, an NGO, to develop a computer vision model to monitor for early detection of habitat loss across the landscape, a significant threat to biodiversity, including threatened and endangered species. By using a computer vision model one can rapidly identify and flag areas where habitat loss may be occurring due to natural or human-caused disturbances. Early detection can facilitate rapid responses, when appropriate, or allow practitioners to accurately calculate habitat loss over time. More accurate estimates of habitat loss allow for better management decisions and potentially shorter recovery times for threatened and endangered species.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0254,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00833,US_OMB_2025_00833,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,Science,"The ECOSphere species workflow relies on extracting relevant ecological and biological insights from a vast and continuously growing repository of unstructured documents, currently numbering in the millions. Manual review and summarization of these documents is infeasible due to scale, time constraints, and resource limitations.",Summarization of documents and output to ECOSphere species workflow [2024 INV#DOI-63],Department of the Interior; FWS; Science; United States,"Structured Summaries of Documents Concise, machine-readable summaries of scientific, regulatory, and technical documents. Key metadata extraction (e.g., species name, habitat, threats, geographic location, publication date). Relevance Scoring AI-generated confidence scores indicating the relevance of each document to specific species or ecological topics. Taxonomic and Thematic Tagging Automatic tagging of documents with species names, ecological terms, and conservation themes to support search and filtering. Workflow-Ready Data Packages Summarized content formatted for direct ingestion into ECOSphere workflows (e.g., JSON, XML, or database-ready formats). Audit Trail and Traceability Links to original documents and AI-generated summaries for transparency and validation. Integration Logs and Metrics Reports on the number of documents processed, summary accuracy, and integration success rates.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Implementing AI-powered document summarization for the ECOSphere species workflow will significantly enhance operational efficiency by automating the extraction of key insights from millions of unstructured documents. This will reduce manual workload, acc","The ECOSphere species workflow relies on extracting relevant ecological and biological insights from a vast and continuously growing repository of unstructured documents, currently numbering in the millions. Manual review and summarization of these documents is infeasible due to scale, time constraints, and resource limitations. There is a critical need for an AI-driven solution that can automatically ingest, analyze, and summarize large volumes of scientific and technical documents, and seamlessly output structured summaries into the ECOSphere workflow. This will enhance data accessibility, accelerate species-related research, and support timely decision-making in environmental and conservation efforts.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK|F04_UNSTRUCTURED_INFORMATION_COMPLEXITY,S3_DOCUMENT_INTELLIGENCE,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0184,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00834,US_OMB_2025_00834,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,Admin Functions,UNKNOWN,DocketScope,Department of the Interior; FWS; Admin Functions; United States,Produce extractive summaries of comments. Detect general sentiment and requests for comment period extensions or public meeting requests. AI tools are supplemental and intended to aid in efficiently identifying key information within comments. Results are verified by analysts during comment review.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Use AI capabilities and detections to assist with timely and accurate comment analysis.,Facilitate review of public comments.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0040,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00835,US_OMB_2025_00835,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,Energy and Environment,UNKNOWN,AI for Offshore Energy: Innovative Technology Streamlines Marine Wildlife Surveys [2024 INV#DOI-66],Department of the Interior; FWS; Energy and Environment; United States,Abundance and distribution data on migratory birds,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Counts of migratory birds with a high degree of accuracy, long-term cost efficiency, safety is improved for pilots due to remote sensing technology","Offshore energy development requires environmental assessments; using AI technology to conduct offshore migratory bird counts can efficiently provide such data, however, substantial automation is required",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0033,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00836,US_OMB_2025_00836,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,Service Delivery,UNKNOWN,AI-Powered Wildlife Monitoring on National Wildlife Refuges,Department of the Interior; FWS; Service Delivery; United States,"Counts of migratory birds. For waterfowl, data can inform harvest management and provide spatially explicit abundance estimates. For whooping crane, goal is to monitor population trends.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Cost efficiency and improved data quality.,"For whooping crane, traditional survey approach is to estimate population size by conducting 6 repeated surveys due to limits of human observer surveys. Surveys of waterfowl are experimental and looking to improve the accuracy of surveys and to obtain improved measures of population sizes.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0029,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00837,US_OMB_2025_00837,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,Service Delivery,Current survey approach has excessive variability that cannot be biologically explained.,Implementation of Artificial Intelligence to Estimate Population Size of a Migratory Bird from Aerial Thermal Imagery [2024 INV#DOI-67],Department of the Interior; FWS; Service Delivery; United States,A population estimate and distribution data for this hunted migratory bird.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Improved safety for pilots and crew because of remote sensing methods, potential for cost efficiency if approach is fully implemented, and improves data quality to inform harvest management.",Current survey approach has excessive variability that cannot be biologically explained. New approach is warranted to inform harvest management,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0028,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00838,US_OMB_2025_00838,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,Science,UNKNOWN,Atlas.ti (Qualitative Data Analysis Software),Department of the Interior; FWS; Science; United States,"There are currently no or limited AI outputs as those features are not currently supported. However, future outputs could include automated assessment of themes, sentiment analysis, and summarization of responses.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,The software increases the efficiency of qualitative data analyses and could automate labor-intensive tasks. A qualified social scientist is involved in the final analysis and insights to ensure accuracy and compliance with regulatory standards.,"Existing software, such as Excel, was insufficient for the increasing quantity of qualitative data collected, necessitating the need for specialized software geared towards qualitative data analyses.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0027,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00840,US_OMB_2025_00840,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,Science,UNKNOWN,AI data harvesting project – ECOSphere [2024 INV#DOI-62],Department of the Interior; FWS; Science; United States,"The pilot will deliver an AI-powered system that automatically extracts and transforms species-related data from uploaded files into ETK’s required format. It will also produce trained models, a functioning QA feedback loop, and a final report evaluating performance and scalability.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"The data ingestion process will be automated, enabling the system to extract, classify, and transform data from various file types without human intervention. Species data will become available more quickly, allowing for faster decision-making.","How can we automate the extraction, classification, and transformation of heterogeneous species-related files (e.g., PDFs, Word docs, Excel sheets, images) uploaded by biologists into structured formats compatible with the ETK system, while ensuring accuracy, scalability, and minimal manual intervention?",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0014,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00841,US_OMB_2025_00841,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,Service Delivery,"Users face significant difficulties when interacting with the system due to a lack of personalized experiences, delayed and imprecise query responses, poor application form guidance, and an overall unintuitive user interface—resulting in reduced efficiency, increased errors, and lower user satisfaction.",ePermits: Chatbot Implementation and Permit Application Wizard Tools,Department of the Interior; FWS; Service Delivery; United States,"Natural Language Responses, Intent Recognition & Routing, Dynamic Form Assistance, Knowledge Base Integration, Contextual Follow-ups, Escalation to Human Agent, Multimodal Outputs. We do not use agentic AI systems in our permit processing workflows. All AI-assisted recommendations are subject to human review and approval. A qualified human reviewer will always be involved in the final decision-making process to ensure accuracy, accountability, and compliance with regulatory standards.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Enhance functionality, improve user experience, assist in acceleration of ePermits processing and align with modern technological and security standards to support mission of conserving, protecting, and enhancing fish, wildlife, plants, and their habitats","Users face significant difficulties when interacting with the system due to a lack of personalized experiences, delayed and imprecise query responses, poor application form guidance, and an overall unintuitive user interface—resulting in reduced efficiency, increased errors, and lower user satisfaction.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,F08_ERROR_COMPLIANCE_RISK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0012,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain 