AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00986,US_OMB_2025_00986,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,Science,UNKNOWN,[Un]supervised clustering of [non-]earthquake signals commonly recorded on regional seismic networks,Department of the Interior; USGS; Science; United States,"Events will be automatically classified as seismogenic (e.g., eathquakes or explosions) surficial mass motions (e.g., falls or slides) using statistical metrics extracted from real-time seismic waveform data.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"By automatically discriminating the different sources that generate observed seismic signals, we can more accurately catalog the events and respond to them in more timely, appropriate ways.","Surficial mass movements (SMMs), such as landslides and rockfalls, have seismic signatures distinct from other routinely-recorded seismic sources like earthquakes and explosions. This project aims to develop a classification scheme to differentiate between seismic signals generated by different sources, especially for those generated by vertical processes (""fall"") versus those generated by horizontal processes (""slides"").",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0121,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00987,US_OMB_2025_00987,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,Science,UNKNOWN,Inference of PFAS precursor compositions,Department of the Interior; USGS; Science; United States,Tabular data of predicted PFAS precursor compositions.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Improved understanding of PFAS compositions, sources, and transport mechanisms will improve mitigation strategies. These improvements have the potential to reduce mitigation costs while improving overall outcomes.","This approach will allow for better identification of PFAS source zones and materials, and will enable better estimation of transport processes",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0110,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00988,US_OMB_2025_00988,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,Science,UNKNOWN,Using Graph Neural Networks for development of nonergodic earthquake ground-motion models,Department of the Interior; USGS; Science; United States,"Generates predictions of ground motion that account for local site and path effects, improving accuracy of seismic hazard models.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"This work may help improves seismic ground motion predictions, guiding safer construction and disaster planning while reducing long-term costs.","May ultimately enable better hazard assessment, reduces potential disaster costs, and improves the accuracy of public hazard maps and building guidelines.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0118,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00989,US_OMB_2025_00989,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,Science,UNKNOWN,Modeling Rupture Directivity Effects on Ground Motion Using Neural Networks,Department of the Interior; USGS; Science; United States,The outputs here are adjustments to the median and standard deviation of ground-motion model predictions. The AI system predicts the amplified ground motion effects due to rupture directivity and are used to refine seismic hazard assessments in a computationally lightweight manner.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,computationally efficient method to improve seismic hazard modeling by incorporating rupture directivity effects,"We use Artificial Neural Networks (ANNs) to more accurately modeling ground motion amplification effects caused by rupture directivity during earthquakes. These effects are complex and challenging to capture using traditional methods, which can impact the accuracy of seismic hazard assessments.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0120,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
