AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00991,US_OMB_2025_00991,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,Science,UNKNOWN,LLM-Assisted Volcanic Alert Monitoring,Department of the Interior; USGS; Science; United States,Data collection,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Currently, this process can involve manual checks, which are time-consuming. This project aims to create a rapid, efficient, and resilient method for gathering this critical data, increasing the quality of our situational awareness and value",The primary goal of this project is to automate the monitoring of volcanic alert levels from the public websites of our partner observatories.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0109,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00992,US_OMB_2025_00992,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,Science,UNKNOWN,USGS Flow Photo Explorer [2024 INV#WO0000000109196],Department of the Interior; USGS; Science; United States,Predicted relative flow hydrograph.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"cost savings, increased safety for employees and the public","The Flow Photo Explorer (FPE) is an integrated database, machine learning, and data visualization platform for monitoring streamflow and other hydrologic conditions using timelapse images. The goal of this project is to develop new approaches for collecting hydrologic data in streams, lakes, and other waterbodies, especially in places where traditional monitoring methods and technologies are not feasible or cost-prohibitive. FPE uses an artificial intelligence/machine learning (AI/ML) deep learning model to estimate relative streamflow using timelapse imagery. The model is trained using pairs of images for which a person (a.k.a. an annotator) has selected which of the two images in each pair appears to have more flow. From this, the model learns how to sort the images from lowest to highest apparent flow. The rankings of the sorted images then serve as indicators of the relative amount of streamflow.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0117,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00993,US_OMB_2025_00993,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,Science,Mapping prairie dog colonies in national is labor intensive and costly.,Synthesizing mapping and monitoring data to understand fluctuations in prairie dog colony size and densities in Theodore Roosevelt National Park [2024 INV#WO0000000109308],Department of the Interior; USGS; Science; United States,Prediction and map of the location of prairie dog colonies.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Cost and time savings,Mapping prairie dog colonies in national is labor intensive and costly. One of the aims of this project is to develop open-source methods for mapping prairie dog colonies using satellite data.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0116,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00994,US_OMB_2025_00994,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,Science,UNKNOWN,Coastal Change Likelihood: Synthesizing change factors using supervised learning,Department of the Interior; USGS; Science; United States,"The system produces maps of future coastal change, along with an indicator of the primary hazard(s) that produce the estimated change.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"The Coastal Change Likelihood project is a computer-aided synthesis of the factors that determine future coastal landscape change that can be used by decision makers to support adaptation, mitigation, and prioritization of coastal zone resources and infra",A supervised machine-learning framework (support vector machine algorithm) is used to predict future decadal-scale coastal change and its primary driver by combining over 20 published coastal geospatial datasets that describe the coastal landscape and the hazards that affect it.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0115,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_00995,US_OMB_2025_00995,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,Science,UNKNOWN,Improving Prediction Capabilities for Barrier Island Landscape Change,Department of the Interior; USGS; Science; United States,Data products include landcover maps and change maps; Publications describe model validation for coastal natural hazards and landscape evolution; Continued development of AI/ML methods and workflows to inform landscape change assessments.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"More accurate and longer-term information leads to more efficient and effective resource management, protecting property and national interests.","This research uses several AI/ML tools to observe and analyze coastal landscape change at critical habitats along barrier islands. The work employs traditional ML methods (random forest model), and more cutting-edge methods, like foundation models (e.g. Segment Anything). AI tools that leverage human-in-the-loop methods (e.g. Doodler) enable efficient and reliable landcover map creation from aerial and satellite imagery and enhanced historical imagery that provides important long-term perspectives of landcover change. This work aids land management decision-making and risk assessments and provides data for model validation.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0114,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
