AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01024,US_OMB_2025_01024,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,Science,UNKNOWN,PFAS Groundwater Model,Department of the Interior; USGS; Science; United States,prediction,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Predictions of PFAS in groundwater across the US. The intention is that the results can serve to inform states where sampling is needed and to reduce costs associated with sampling areas that aren't likely to have PFAS.,We are building a model (likely random forest or boosted regression tree) to predict PFAS concentrations in groundwater supplies in the US.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0078,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01025,US_OMB_2025_01025,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,Science,UNKNOWN,ATLAS,Department of the Interior; USGS; Science; United States,A catalog of metadata about published datasets that supports user queries through agentic AI.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"The AI will accelerate the mineral resource assessment process and provide a model for other types of resource assessments. By improving efficiency, accuracy, and transparency of assessment workflows, AI tools can help USGS deliver results more rapidly","Literature review and data compilation is the most time-consuming phase of the mineral resource assessment workflow (https://www.usgs.gov/media/images/usgs-mineral-resource-assessment-workflow). Identifying and extracting datasets referenced in historical documents, journal articles and published databases is currently done using traditional methods of browsing the web, downloading manuscripts and datasets, and extracting relevant data. The AI system will automatically extract metadata about datasets from manuscripts and make it available to users in a catalog. By supporting user queries of the extracted metadata, the system will enable assessment scientists to identify data sources much more quickly. The tool is intended to support other AI tools down the line that facilitate data extraction and synthesis. The system will also be useful for tracking lineage and usage of published datasets, helping to assure data quality and assess impact.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0077,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01026,US_OMB_2025_01026,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,Energy and Environment,UNKNOWN,Flor-AI: Developing a Remotely Sensed Image Classification Method for Inventory and Monitoring of Flora in Digital UAS Imagery,Department of the Interior; USGS; Energy and Environment; United States,"AI outputs will include the location, counts, and coverage area of wild lupine populations in the target areas. Imagery will also be processed into orthomosaics and published.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Benefits of using UAS and AI for this work include more efficient surveys of large landscapes, reduced costs associated with staffing for on-the-ground surveys, and faster generation of maps for planning management actions.","This project supports the management of oak-pine barrens on the Necedah National Wildlife Refuge, Wisconsin. Necedah NWR staff conduct habitat management actions (prescribed burning, mowing, seeding, and herbicide application) to increase wild lupine (Lupinus perennis) abundance for the endangered Karner blue butterfly (Lycaeides melissa samuelis). This project will use uncrewed aerial systems (UAS) to collect imagery and apply artificial intelligence to efficiently process imagery and detect lupine. Model performance and the overall project workflow will inform future efforts and may be applied to additional vegetation monitoring programs.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0079,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01027,US_OMB_2025_01027,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,Energy and Environment,UNKNOWN,Automating the Detection and Classification of Wildlife in Aerial Imagery [2024 INV#WO0000000109409],Department of the Interior; USGS; Energy and Environment; United States,"AI outputs will include the location and counts of birds and other wildlife in offshore areas. Imagery, annotations, and code will also be published.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"This work will support BOEM's activities to manage resources within the OCS Planning Areas, informing decisions about lease area selection and mitigation strategies. Using AI will reduce the time, cost, and risk associated with aerial surveys","The tools and workflows developed by this project will be used by the Bureau of Ocean Energy Management (BOEM) to assess wildlife populations as part of planning and monitoring for offshore energy development. BOEM requires information on the environmental sensitivity of marine species and marine productivity to make informed decisions regarding offshore oil and gas energy infrastructure placement and mitigation measures. This is mandated by the Outer Continental Shelf Lands Act (OCSLA Section 18(2)(G)), which requires the Secretary of the Interior to consider these factors when determining the size, timing, and location of future lease sales for the National Oil and Gas Leasing Program.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0075,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01028,US_OMB_2025_01028,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,Science,UNKNOWN,Automated identification of ducks from hunter-submitted photos using deep learning models,Department of the Interior; USGS; Science; United States,composition of waterfowl harvest,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,cost savings and improved efficiency in an operational monitoring program,species identification of photographs of hunter-shot ducks for use in waterfowl harvest management,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0074,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01029,US_OMB_2025_01029,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,Science,UNKNOWN,Automated photographic identification of Eastern box turtles,Department of the Interior; USGS; Science; United States,output is pairwise match or confidence scores and clusters of putative photo matches,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"efficiencies in field data collection, allows data from community/citizen science to be used in monitoring activities, allows for the application of more sophisticated capture-recapture models",Matching photographs from a database of photos to determine capture history of individuals which can then be used in capture-recapture models to estimate population size and demographic parameters.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0073,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01030,US_OMB_2025_01030,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,Emergency Mgmt,UNKNOWN,Machine learning in remote sensing-based wildfire and natural resource risk assessments,Department of the Interior; USGS; Emergency Mgmt; United States,"Maps of risk, prediction of which factors contribute to risk, highlight areas for potential mitigation actions.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Predictions inform land management planning and decision-making to mitigate risk and save American taxpayers millions of dollars in damage from the additive effect of these stressors.,"Predict the risks of wildfire, drought, and invasive species spread on assets of value to the American public",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0072,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01031,US_OMB_2025_01031,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,Science,UNKNOWN,Pathogen identification in salmon,Department of the Interior; USGS; Science; United States,prediction,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,ability to aid in the conservation of sensitive salmon species,"Ichthyophonus, the most ecological and economically important pathogen of wild marine fish, is hypothesized to be a major driver of premature mortality in Yukon River Chinook salmon. Currently, evaluation of Ichthyophonus infection in salmon requires lethal sampling, which is often prohibited in rapidly declining populations. We are using a transcriptomic approach in conjunction with random forest modelling to identify a panel of biomarkers capable of identifying Ichthyophonus in salmon using a non-lethal muscle tissue sample.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0071,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01032,US_OMB_2025_01032,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,Other,UNKNOWN,Telemetry Analysis Learning Algorithm (TALA),Department of the Interior; USGS; Other; United States,Alerts to limit violations and prediction of subsystem failures observed in satellite telemetry.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Increased efficiencies in trending and analysis of satellite health and safety telemetry.,Applies machine learning to analyze operational data from agency-managed systems to support maintenance and reliability objectives.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0070,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01033,US_OMB_2025_01033,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,Science,UNKNOWN,LANDFIRE,Department of the Interior; USGS; Science; United States,"LANDFIRE produces a variety of geospatial products to support the fire community, including Existing Vegetation Cover, Existing Vegetation Type, Existing Vegetation Height, Environmental Site Potential, Biophysical Settings, and more.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"LANDFIRE produces a variety of geospatial products to support the fire community, including Existing Vegetation Cover, Existing Vegetation Type, Existing Vegetation Height, Environmental Site Potential, Biophysical Settings, and more","USGS EROS has provided the expertise and staff to conduct LANDFIRE mapping for over 20 years. LANDFIRE products provide the nationally consistent, high-quality vegetation and fuels data needed to support wildfire management, land-use planning, ecosystem restoration, and habitat management. By producing and updating these datasets, EROS ensures that federal, state, tribal, and local partners all work from the same trusted information, improving coordination and decision-making. The national scope and scientific rigor of EROS mapping make LANDFIRE an indispensable foundation for assessing risk, allocating resources, and sustaining resilient landscapes across the United States.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0069,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01034,US_OMB_2025_01034,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,Science,UNKNOWN,Invasive Grass Mapping,Department of the Interior; USGS; Science; United States,"Weekly maps depicting invasive exotic annual grass extent and coverage for the western United States, with weekly products from early April to early July.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"DNNs have greatly improved our ability to accurately map invasive annual exotic grasses. We now produce weekly estimates of invasive grasses for the western US from early April until July, providing fire and land managers with critical data.","USGS mapping of invasive exotic annual grasses is critical because these species, such as cheatgrass, alter ecosystems by increasing the frequency and intensity of wildfires and outcompeting native vegetation. Accurate, large-scale maps help land managers anticipate fire risk, prioritize restoration efforts, and guide grazing or herbicide treatments. Beyond fire management, these maps support wildlife habitat conservation, water resource protection, and long-term monitoring of ecosystem change, providing essential information for both local decision-making and national land management strategies.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0068,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01035,US_OMB_2025_01035,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,Science,UNKNOWN,Evapotranspiration mapping and monitoring,Department of the Interior; USGS; Science; United States,"ET maps for the Western US, used as input to the OpenET project. Also on-demand generation of global ET.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"An improved ET product means a more informed farmer, allowing them to efficiently manage water resources and the crops that depend on them. The use of AI improves our ability to characterize surface temperature boundary conditions","Mapping evapotranspiration (ET) with remote sensing is essential because it provides a consistent, large-scale view of how water is being used across landscapes. In agriculture, ET maps help farmers and water managers track crop water use, improve irrigation efficiency, and manage limited water resources more sustainably. Beyond farming, ET mapping supports drought monitoring, groundwater management, ecosystem health assessments, and fire fuel moisture assessments by showing how water and energy cycles vary over space and time. Without remote sensing, this kind of detailed, spatially explicit information would be impossible to obtain at regional or global scales. AI was used by USGS EROS to improve our ability to map ET, using multi-layer perceptrons and DNNs.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0067,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01036,US_OMB_2025_01036,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,Science,UNKNOWN,National Land Cover Database (NLCD) [2024 INV#WO0000000107887],Department of the Interior; USGS; Science; United States,Maps of land cover change over time for the United States.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Our revamping of the NLCD methodology with a series of 3 linked deep learning models has allowed us to improve the product, reduce latency of delivery, and to produce that product more cheaply.","Characterization of the physical land cover is critical for managing the lands, waters, and resources of the United States. The National Land Cover Database (NLCD) is easily one of the most widely used datasets produced within the Department of Interior, with applications including natural resource management, hydrology, biodiversity and habitat, energy and minerals, natural disasters, agricultural sustainability, and more. The criticality of these data demand 1) frequent updates, and 2) a characterization of how our landscapes are changing across time and space. Our linkage of three deep learning models, including a generative transformer-based AI model, has been vital for not only improving our characterization of the landscape with NLCD, but for enabling us to produce land cover products faster and more efficiently. The application of AI to this problem has saved the government valuable resources.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0066,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01037,US_OMB_2025_01037,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,Science,UNKNOWN,DARPAs CriticalMAAS [2024 INV#WO0000000108419; WO0000000096527],Department of the Interior; USGS; Science; United States,Predictive maps,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Assessment of the domestic availability of critical minerals. Insight into the U.S. critical mineral supply landscape. Evaluation of national critical mineral supply chains. Analysis of domestic sources and supply of critical minerals.,"Identify patterns in the data, isolate those that correlate with known mineral deposits, and integrate these with other geospatial layers to generate a predictive map for guiding future mineral exploration.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0065,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01038,US_OMB_2025_01038,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,Science,UNKNOWN,"Willamette Regional IWAAs, gradient boosted ML stream temperature modeling.",Department of the Interior; USGS; Science; United States,The AI system outputs daily modeled stream temperatures.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"The expected benefits and outcomes are improved stream temperature predictions, which is a cornerstone of the integrated water availability assessment for the region, and methods that are transferable across the basin.",Improve model predictions of stream temperature across the basin over traditional methods.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0064,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01039,US_OMB_2025_01039,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Interior,Science,UNKNOWN,"Mapping wood and wood hazards in the Willamette Basin, Oregon",Department of the Interior; USGS; Science; United States,The system output is mapping the location and extent of large wood pre and post wildfires,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"This work will help inform infrastructure hazards such as at dams and bridges, as well as to river users, such as rafters, inter-tubers, and fishermen.","Large wood in rivers pose hazards to people and infrastructure, particularly post wildfire. This work uses neural network models to map large wood in rivers from aerial imagery to understand how wood is distributed throughout river systems pre and post wildfire.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOI-0063,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
