AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01064,US_OMB_2025_01064,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,IT,UNKNOWN,Digital.ai,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / ATF; IT; United States,ATF has not evaluated the AI features in detail since other non-AI products are currently being used to serve the purposes for which digital.ai uses AI.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,ATF is not using any of the available AI features.,"Digital.ai is used as ATF's enterprise tool for managing agile software development projects. It is used to capture user stories (requirements) and manage the processes of prioritization, implementation, testing, and close-out of the user stories. None of the AI features available within digital.ai are currently in use, but the use case is being reported because they are available within the product. AI features involve analysis of project status, supporting automated test generation, and automating software releases. ATF uses other non-AI products for these purposes.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0012,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01065,US_OMB_2025_01065,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""enterprise_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Procurement and Finance Mgmt,UNKNOWN,Dun & Bradstreet Business Establishments Data,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / ATF; Procurement and Finance Mgmt; United States,"The AI features generate risk indicators, show relationships, help focus examination resources.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"The expected benefit is more targeted attention on atypical organizations, improving efficiency and reducing randomness.","The purpose of the AI use case in Dun & Bradstreet Business Establishments Data is to analyze business information, detect irregularities, and assess potential risks more efficiently. AI-driven data integration, anomaly detection, and trend analysis automate what would otherwise be intensive manual evaluations.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,S4_PREDICTION_DETECTION,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0014,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01066,US_OMB_2025_01066,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Law Enforcement,UNKNOWN,Axon Evidence.com,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / ATF; Law Enforcement; United States,"Evidence.com AI capabilities will output bounding boxes around heads that are identified in videos, for input to redaction processes. These AI functions are not being operationally used.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Evidence.com provides AI-based features that identify the presence of heads in videos and can perform automated redaction. This would increase the efficiency of redacting video evidence for release. However, ATF is not operationally using them.","ATF's use of Axon body-worn cameras and the associated evidence.com service are integral to ensuring ATF's compliance with DOJ policy documented in DOJ OIG, Inspector General Manual, Volume III, Chapter 236, Body Worn Camera Program. Body cam videos are transferred to the Axon Evidence.com service, which includes AI-based features for performing recognition of heads in videos for the purpose of redaction. ATF has performed limited testing of these capabilities, but is not operationally using them.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0015,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01067,US_OMB_2025_01067,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Admin Functions,UNKNOWN,Federal Docket Management System,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / ATF; Admin Functions; United States,It is the place where agencies receive comments that are electronically submitted in response to a rulemaking. It allows agencies to make those comments public facing.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"This product permits agencies to review the electronic comments received in response to rulemaking. The features in FDMS allow agencies to bulk post up to 1,000 comments allowing the public to see their comments faster.","This system allows agencies to receive comments that are submitted electronically in response to rulemaking initiatives. The system has features that categorize comments based on text analytics, allows agencies to make those comments public facing or redact them, and allows agencies to download the comments.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0016,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01068,US_OMB_2025_01068,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Law Enforcement,UNKNOWN,FINDER,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / ATF; Law Enforcement; United States,"The AI features map trends, highlight recurrent factors, and propose focus points, reducing manual data reviews.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,The expected benefit is more strategic attention to areas that may reduce negative outcomes or enhance preparedness.,"The purpose of the AI use case in FINDER is to sift through violent crime and firearms trafficking data more efficiently. By employing machine learning to highlight significant patterns, suspects, or trends, it automates tasks that would normally require manual, resource-intensive reviews. This leads to quicker identification of essential insights, improves operational effectiveness, and ensures that effort is directed at the most pertinent leads, enhancing both speed and precision in investigative processes.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0017,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01069,US_OMB_2025_01069,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Law Enforcement,"By automating map-based data correlation, pattern discovery, and geospatial analysis, the system reduces manual data plotting and interpretation.",First Two,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / ATF; Law Enforcement; United States,"The AI features visualize activity geographically, spotlight frequent places, and suggest beneficial attention areas.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"The expected benefit is more efficient focus on frequently visited places/people, enhancing resource allocation where location matters.","The purpose of the AI use case in First Two is to link individuals to specific locations and visualize spatial relationships that might be important. By automating map-based data correlation, pattern discovery, and geospatial analysis, the system reduces manual data plotting and interpretation. This results in quicker recognition of significant activity areas, improved allocation of resources to critical locations, and overall enhancement of operational responsiveness and strategic planning.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0018,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01070,US_OMB_2025_01070,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Law Enforcement,"This advanced approach reduces manual searching, enhances accuracy in linking data points, and strategically directs focus toward high-value leads, improving overall investigative efficiency and decision-making.",LexisNexis Accurint,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / ATF; Law Enforcement; United States,"The AI features compile overviews, note aliases, highlight patterns, giving clear reference points for exploration.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"The expected benefit is accelerated ID of important figures/relationships, skipping disjointed dataset searches.","The purpose of the AI use case in LexisNexis Accurint is to merge and analyze an array of public and proprietary records to build a clearer picture of individuals and entities. By automating data integration, filtering, and pattern recognition, it expedites the identification of relevant subjects and connections. This advanced approach reduces manual searching, enhances accuracy in linking data points, and strategically directs focus toward high-value leads, improving overall investigative efficiency and decision-making.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0019,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01071,US_OMB_2025_01071,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN,LexisNexis Babel Street,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / ATF; United States,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,RETIRED,종료,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0020,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01072,US_OMB_2025_01072,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Law Enforcement,"By employing AI-driven classification, entity resolution, and data linking, it reduces the manual workload needed to extract meaningful insights.",Mark43 Public Safety Records,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / ATF; Law Enforcement; United States,"The AI features categorize documents, flag repeated factors, and highlight patterns hidden without assistance.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"The expected benefit is better informed decisionmaking, allowing focus on data likely to yield meaningful insights.","The purpose of the AI use case in Mark43 Public Safety Records is to organize, categorize, and correlate extensive law enforcement data from various sources. By employing AI-driven classification, entity resolution, and data linking, it reduces the manual workload needed to extract meaningful insights. This empowers users to identify key relationships and patterns more rapidly, increases data accuracy, and supports more strategic use of investigative resources, ultimately improving both timeliness and quality of public safety operations.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0021,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01073,US_OMB_2025_01073,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""enterprise_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Procurement and Finance Mgmt,"By applying AI-driven pattern recognition, risk assessment, and anomaly detection, it streamlines what would be a tedious manual review process.",National Insurance Crime Bureau ISO ClaimSearch,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / ATF; Procurement and Finance Mgmt; United States,"The AI features produce lists of flagged claims, show patterns, and suggest where deeper validation might help.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"The expected benefit is more effective resource use, targeting claims that differ from typical patterns rather than all equally.","The purpose of the AI use case in National Insurance Crime Bureau ISO ClaimSearch is to analyze insurance claim data and highlight suspicious patterns or anomalies more efficiently. By applying AI-driven pattern recognition, risk assessment, and anomaly detection, it streamlines what would be a tedious manual review process. This leads to faster fraud identification, more accurate targeting of problematic claims, and better resource utilization, ultimately strengthening investigative outcomes.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,S4_PREDICTION_DETECTION,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0022,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01074,US_OMB_2025_01074,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Law Enforcement,UNKNOWN,Operational Planning Analytics Risk Management Solution (OPARMS),Department of Justice; Department of Justice / ATF; Law Enforcement; United States,1. Risk rating of proposed operations 2. Recommendations for resource allocation based on risk ratings,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Improve operational planning, data collection, and risk mitigation. Reduce time to fill out op plans. Increase accuracy of data entered into ops plans by populating info from other ATF systems. Reduce approval times by routing and tracking op plans through OPARMS. Increase collection of operations planning and after action reports. Collect and store data to begin developing the analytics for calculating and identifying risk in operations allowing team members to better mitigate those risks.","The Operational Planning Analytics Risk Management Solution (OPARMS) creates op plans within ATF's case management system, eliminating the previous system for generating op plans. ATF anticipates that OPARMS will also provide dashboard overviews of the op plans and risk data for all op plans.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0024,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01075,US_OMB_2025_01075,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Law Enforcement,UNKNOWN,Palantir (via access to external state LE system),Department of Justice; Department of Justice / ATF; Law Enforcement; United States,Unknown. ATF only uses the system to perform standard search functions of information which state agency chooses to share with law enforcement partners.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"ATF use of the state LE partner Palantir system is limited to searching for information which the state agency chooses to share with law enforcement partners. ATF has no involvement with, any knowledge of, or any expected benefits from use of AI by the state agency which runs the system.","This use case is being reported because Palantir has AI-based capabilities. However, ATF only accesses Palantir through task force partnerships with the a state law enforcement (LE) partner. The state LE agency uses Palantir as their case management system, and ATF's use is limited to searching for information which the state LE agency chooses to share with law enforcement partners. ATF has no involvement with or any knowledge of use of AI features by the state agency which runs the system.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0025,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01076,US_OMB_2025_01076,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Law Enforcement,UNKNOWN,ShotSpotter (via access to external state/local systems),Department of Justice; Department of Justice / ATF; Law Enforcement; United States,Outputs sensor reports of gunshots and activity of investigative interest.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Rapid detection of gunshots, which can help to decrease the time to respond to a violent crime.",Rapidly locate gunshots and activity of potential investigative interest to alert relevant law enforcement agencies.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0028,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01077,US_OMB_2025_01077,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Procurement and Finance Mgmt,"By integrating AI-driven anomaly detection, trend analysis, and risk scoring, it simplifies manual review and directs attention to truly irregular transfers.",Southwest Border Transaction Record Analysis Center (SWBTRAC),Department of Justice; Department of Justice / ATF; Procurement and Finance Mgmt; United States,"The AI features provide alerts, highlight unusual transfers, and explain why certain activities warrant closer observation.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"The expected benefit is faster recognition of outlier scenarios, focusing on meaningful transactions rather than all equally.","The purpose of the AI use case in Southwest Border Transaction Record Analysis Center (SWBTRAC) is to monitor cross-border financial transactions and identify unusual activities more efficiently. By integrating AI-driven anomaly detection, trend analysis, and risk scoring, it simplifies manual review and directs attention to truly irregular transfers. This approach ensures that investigative focus is applied judiciously, improves accuracy, and enhances strategic use of resources in addressing cross-border financial concerns.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,S4_PREDICTION_DETECTION,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0029,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01078,US_OMB_2025_01078,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Law Enforcement,"This significantly reduces manual workload, sharpens the accuracy of identifying individuals of interest, and ensures that investigative energies are invested where they can yield the most valuable insights.",Spokeo,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / ATF; Law Enforcement; United States,"The AI features assemble contact info, historical records, and related data into a cohesive presentation.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"The expected benefit is quicker access to comprehensive background details, easily identifying individuals of interest.","The purpose of the AI use case in Spokeo is to aggregate and enrich publicly accessible personal data to create comprehensive profiles. AI-based entity resolution, data linkage, and pattern recognition automate the task of piecing together scattered details. This significantly reduces manual workload, sharpens the accuracy of identifying individuals of interest, and ensures that investigative energies are invested where they can yield the most valuable insights.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0030,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01079,US_OMB_2025_01079,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Law Enforcement,UNKNOWN,Thomson Reuters CLEAR,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / ATF; Law Enforcement; United States,"The AI features organize profiles, indicate links, and suggest deeper review areas, streamlining fragmented processes.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"The expected benefit is reduced manual effort, enabling quicker discovery of relevant profiles/relationships.","The purpose of the AI use case in Thomson Reuters Clear is to consolidate and analyze diverse records, creating coherent profiles of individuals and entities. By applying AI-driven data integration, entity resolution, and intelligent filtering, it automates traditionally manual tasks. This leads to faster identification of subjects of interest, improved accuracy in linking related data points, and a more strategic use of time and resources. Ultimately, AI integration enhances investigative effectiveness, reduces errors, and supports more targeted research.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0031,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01080,US_OMB_2025_01080,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Law Enforcement,"By implementing AI for entity resolution, risk scoring, and pattern detection, it replaces manual data handling with automated insights.",TransUnion TLOxp Online Investigative Services,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / ATF; Law Enforcement; United States,"The AI features highlight key personal details, indicate anomalies, and present data in a structured format for deeper inquiry.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"The expected benefit is better time/effort use, focusing on subjects/data points that seem more meaningful.","The purpose of the AI use case in TransUnion TLOxp Online Investigative Services is to gather and analyze diverse personal, financial, and asset-related data more effectively. By implementing AI for entity resolution, risk scoring, and pattern detection, it replaces manual data handling with automated insights. This accelerates the discovery of meaningful leads, reduces errors, and ensures attention is concentrated on cases truly warranting further review, improving both accuracy and resource allocation.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,S5_OPTIMIZATION_DECISION_SUPPORT,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0032,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01081,US_OMB_2025_01081,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Admin Functions,UNKNOWN,Veritone Redact,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / ATF; Admin Functions; United States,The AI system in Veritone Redact outputs recommendations and automated actions to support the redaction of sensitive information within audio and video files. It intelligently identifies personally identifiable information and other confidential content that may need to be redacted under legal exemptions. All suggested redactions are reviewed and approved by human staff to ensure compliance with legal standards.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"The expected benefits of the AI use case in Veritone Redact involve enhancing the efficiency and accuracy of redacting sensitive information within audio and video files. By automating the identification and redaction of personally identifiable information and other confidential content, the AI reduces the time and effort required from staff to process multimedia materials. This leads to faster turnaround times for releasing information, thereby reducing customer wait times for FOIA requests. The AI-driven redaction process also helps ensure compliance with privacy laws and regulations, minimizing the risk of inadvertently disclosing sensitive information. These efficiencies result in cost savings through reduced labor hours and improved resource allocation. Overall, the AI in Veritone Redact is expected to improve operational efficiency, enhance compliance, and support timely access to information for the public.",The purpose of the AI use case in Veritone Redact is to support ATF in processing Freedom of Information Act (FOIA) requests by automating the redaction of sensitive information within audio and video files.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0033,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
