AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01085,US_OMB_2025_01085,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Law Enforcement,"The AI capabilities reduce time-consuming manual reviews, improve accuracy in spotting significant trends, and help allocate investigative resources more effectively for timely and well-informed actions.",Thomson Reuters Vigilant Vehicle Manager,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / ATF; Law Enforcement; United States,"The AI features produce overviews of vehicle activity, highlight recurring patterns, and point to areas for further review.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,License plate reader systems are used by law enforcement to assist with identification of vehicles associated with criminal investigations. ATF has no role in training or managing AI capabilities which are incidental to providing the service.,"The purpose of the AI use case in Thomson Reuters Vigilant Vehicle Manager is to intelligently organize, correlate, and analyze large volumes of license plate and vehicle sightings data. By automating the identification of recurring patterns and providing data-driven insights, it streamlines the workflow for identifying vehicles that may warrant attention. The AI capabilities reduce time-consuming manual reviews, improve accuracy in spotting significant trends, and help allocate investigative resources more effectively for timely and well-informed actions.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0038,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
