AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01094,US_OMB_2025_01094,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Law Enforcement,UNKNOWN,Bloomberg (AI Assisted Legal Research),Department of Justice; Department of Justice / ATR; Law Enforcement; United States,Summarization of caselaw,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Increases the speed at which attorneys can review and evaluate case law to determine if it is applicable to their current investigations.,Provides AI-assisted research to help streamline legal research and document review.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0322,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01095,US_OMB_2025_01095,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Admin Functions,UNKNOWN,ATR Generative Artificial Intelligence Test,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / ATR; Admin Functions; United States,"Open-source research, summarizing publicly available documents.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"This initiative will enable ATR to embrace AI technology responsibly consistent with Presidential Action and various departmental guidance, allowing ATR personnel to optimize and modernize their work processes.",Facilitate access to AI tools by ATR personnel.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0331,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01096,US_OMB_2025_01096,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Law Enforcement,UNKNOWN,ATR Expert/Consulting with Bates White,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / ATR; Law Enforcement; United States,The output data may be provided to experts and support staffs working for the State Attorneys General who are cooperating with ATR on investigations and litigations. The output data will be returned to ATR for use by internal ATR economists.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Assist in preliminary data processing, including document summarization, name standardization, and text extraction. This includes “cleaning” the data for additional processing, performing the equivalent of a “find and replace” function to standardize names. The Bates White system may use AI to summarize the general content of documents.",The AI tool will ingest all the data sets and work to standardize them so that the Bates White expert and team can use the data to run economic models.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0332,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01097,US_OMB_2025_01097,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,IT,UNKNOWN,Salesforce,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / CIV; IT; United States,"Enabling Infrastructure: creates foundational capability for AI applications rather than direct AI outputs; enables other use cases to generate their respective predictions, recommendations, and automated actions.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"(1) Creates a replicable model for DOJ-wide adoption by establishing standardized cloud architecture and data integration frameworks that can be scaled across components. Demonstrates how breaking down legacy data silos enables coordinated, AI-driven insights and business intelligence capabilities that support department-wide resource allocation and investigative priorities. (2) Leverages JMD's established AWS Landing Zone to accelerate cloud adoption and builds upon existing data governance frameworks and system modernization efforts across DOJ components. The migration integrates with current cloud-based systems through the AWS Landing Zone infrastructure, enabling AI-powered business intelligence capabilities without duplicating technology investments. (3) Completing the migration to AI-native cloud infrastructure and deploying an AI-driven business intelligence dashboard that enables Division leadership to explore patterns and trends across the litigation portfolio.","This initiative modernizes our current on-premise and matter management databases and storage systems by migrating to cloud-based platforms specifically architected for AI integration and enhanced system interoperability. Our existing applications and data are currently hosted on-premise systems that create fundamental barriers to AI implementation, limiting data accessibility, constraining scalability, and preventing the real-time data integration that modern AI tools require.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0045,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01098,US_OMB_2025_01098,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,IT,UNKNOWN,Enabling eDiscovery Platform AI,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / CIV; IT; United States,"Prioritizations, Classifications, Recommendations: document priority rankings, privilege classifications, review recommendations.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"(1) Increases data availability and accessibility for integration with AI platforms through hosting on a scalable platform, in alignment with DOJ Data Strategy Goal #1 ""Enterprise Data Management."" Creates replicable enterprise capabilities that other DOJ components can adopt. (2) Allows migration to our existing environments more quickly. Discovery process will be streamlined with increased prioritization of review and lessens the time for manual privilege reviews. (3) AI enabled workflows available to Division litigating teams for privilege review, case strategy and prioritized document review.","Migrate CORA data to Relativity One or Everlaw, cloud based solutions to enable Relativity's and Everlaw's AI tools for review prioritization, privilege review and other advanced eDiscovery utilities. Utilize internal or third party-tools for AI-assisted collection and data processing, including image and voice recognition and analysis of complex data formats. Integrate E-Discovery tools into case management processes. This initiative transforms litigation support capabilities by leveraging AI to accelerate document review processes, reduce discovery costs, and improve case preparation efficiency and effectiveness.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0301,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01099,US_OMB_2025_01099,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Admin Functions,UNKNOWN,Claims Program Predictive Fraud Analytics,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / CIV; Admin Functions; United States,"Predictions, Classifications, Scores: fraud probability scores, claim authenticity classifications, risk alerts.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"(1) Strengthens the Civil Division's capabilities in administering victim compensation programs by identifying potentially fraudulent medical claims, duplicate submissions, and identity fraud. (2) Builds upon existing Civil Division case management systems and medical claim review processes. Leverages ongoing fraud detection initiatives across DOJ components, integrates with established medical record verification systems, and utilizes existing partnerships with healthcare providers and medical review contractors. (3) Improvement in fraudulent claim detection rates, prevention of fraudulent payouts annually, reduction in false positive flags affecting legitimate claimants, faster claim processing times for verified submissions, and improved coordination metrics with investigative agencies on fraud referrals.","Deploy advanced AI analytics to detect fraudulent claims and suspicious patterns in compensation claims programs, including the September 11th Victims Compensation Fund, Radiation Exposure Compensation Act, Camp LeJeune Justice Act, and other federal victim assistance programs. This initiative protects program integrity, ensures resources reach legitimate claimants, and maintains public trust in federal compensation systems. Aligns with Administration priorities on combating fraud, protecting taxpayer funds, and ensuring justice for claimants.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0314,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01100,US_OMB_2025_01100,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Admin Functions,"DOJ attorneys spend significant time manually researching case law and regulatory precedents across jurisdictions, often missing obscure authorities or evolving standards.",AI-powered Legal Research,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / CIV; Admin Functions; United States,"Recommendations, Classifications, Scores: research recommendations, precedent relevance scores, conflict alerts.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"(1) Enhances DOJ's litigation effectiveness by ensuring comprehensive legal research, reducing research time per case, and improving argument quality through better precedent identification. Strengthens government's ability to defend federal programs and policies with more thorough legal foundations. (2) Builds on existing Westlaw/Lexis subscriptions, DOJ brief bank, and PACER databases. Integrates with current legal research workflows and citation management systems. (3) Reduction in research hours per brief; increase in relevant precedents cited; improved appellate success rates; measurable improvement in legal argument comprehensiveness.","DOJ attorneys spend significant time manually researching case law and regulatory precedents across jurisdictions, often missing obscure authorities or evolving standards. This initiative deploys an AI-powered legal research platform that synthesizes case law, flags conflicts or shifts in standards, and provides confidence scores for relevance, automatically updating as new decisions are published. Aligns with E.O. 14179’s innovation directive and M-25-21’s efficiency requirements.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0333,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01101,US_OMB_2025_01101,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Law Enforcement,Federal litigators face increasing challenges with AI-manipulated evidence and documents from opposing parties.,AI-generated Content Detector,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / CIV; Law Enforcement; United States,"Classifications, Predictions: AI-generation probability scores, document authenticity flags, content manipulation alerts, disclosure requirement notifications.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"(1) Enhanced litigation integrity by identifying potentially manipulated evidence, protecting court proceedings from AI-generated misinformation and ensuring compliance with local court rules. (2) Builds on existing document review platforms and federal privilege protection protocols. (3) Improved evidence verification accuracy; reduced risk of submitting hallucinated data; enhanced compliance with AI disclosure requirements; increased attorney confidence in document authenticity.",Federal litigators face increasing challenges with AI-manipulated evidence and documents from opposing parties. An AI tool could be used to flag potentially AI-generated content.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,S7_GENERATIVE_CONTENT_CREATION,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0334,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01102,US_OMB_2025_01102,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Law Enforcement,"Office of Immigration Litigation (OIL) faces significant backlogs, with repetitive or frivolous claims slowing progress and foreign-language evidence creating bottlenecks.",AI-Enabled Workflow Automation,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / CIV; Law Enforcement; United States,"Classifications, Automated Translations, Recommendations: case priority classifications, language translations, processing recommendations.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"(1) Reduces immigration case backlogs, ensures consistent treatment of claims, and improves responsiveness to federal courts. (2) Builds on OIL case management systems, United States Citizenship and Immigration Services data feeds, and DOJ translation contract costs.(3) Reduced backlog size; fewer attorney hours per case; translation accuracy benchmarks met. Increase in fraudulent/frivolous and repetitive claims.","Office of Immigration Litigation (OIL) faces significant backlogs, with repetitive or frivolous claims slowing progress and foreign-language evidence creating bottlenecks. This initiative uses Natural Language Processing for triage and automate translation to accelerate case processing. It aligns with M-25-21’s innovation and governance principles by improving efficiency while preserving human oversight.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0335,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01103,US_OMB_2025_01103,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Law Enforcement,UNKNOWN,AI-enabled Legal Argument Harmonization,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / CIV; Law Enforcement; United States,"Recommendations, Validations: argument alignment suggestions, citation verification, position harmonization recommendations.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,(1) Enhances DOJ credibility before the court; avoids conflicting arguments. (2) Uses DOJ appellate brief bank and legal research/citation tools. (3) Reduction in conflicting arguments; % of briefs citation-validated; improved appellate outcomes.,"Conflicting arguments across DOJ branches can weaken credibility in appellate courts. This initiative deploys AI to mine arguments across briefs, harmonize DOJ positions, and validate citations. It advances M-25-21’s governance requirement for consistent positions and E.O. 14179’s push for efficiency.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0336,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01104,US_OMB_2025_01104,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Law Enforcement,"Federal agencies and recipients of federal funding must certify compliance with various civil rights statutes, but DOJ lacks efficient methods to verify the accuracy of these certifications. Manual review of compliance documentation is resource-intensive and often occurs only after complaints are filed, allowing violations to persist and potentially expand.",AI-enabled Compliance Verification,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / CIV; Law Enforcement; United States,"Classifications, Predictions, Recommendations: compliance risk assessments, violation predictions, investigation recommendations.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"(1) Strengthens DOJ's ability to enforce civil rights laws through the False Claims Act by identifying clear-cut compliance violations earlier in the process. Protects taxpayer funds from flowing to entities that falsely certify compliance while ensuring federal programs achieve their intended civil rights objectives (2) Leverages FCA compliance databases, Civil Rights Division patterns, and initial whistleblower submission channels. (3) Focus on objective, verifiable metrics such as statistical disparities in outcomes, missing required documentation, or contradictions between certifications and published policies. Number of suspicious certifications flagged; investigations initiated; successful FCA settlements or recoveries.","Federal agencies and recipients of federal funding must certify compliance with various civil rights statutes, but DOJ lacks efficient methods to verify the accuracy of these certifications. Manual review of compliance documentation is resource-intensive and often occurs only after complaints are filed, allowing violations to persist and potentially expand. False certifications can result in continued federal funding to non-compliant entities, undermining civil rights enforcement and wasting taxpayer resources. Aligns with E.O. 14179's innovation requirements and M-25-21's public trust and governance pillars.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0337,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01105,US_OMB_2025_01105,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Law Enforcement,UNKNOWN,AI-Enabled Briefing Assistant,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / CIV; Law Enforcement; United States,"Content Generation, Recommendations: draft legal briefs, argument suggestions, citation recommendations, consistency checks.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"(1) This initiative strengthens the federal government’s ability to protect statutory authority and defend policy actions across all agencies. (2) Reduction in attorney hours per brief; mitigation of hallucinated citations; measurable improvement in argument consistency across cases. (3) Builds on DOJ’s existing “brief bank,” eDiscovery platforms, and PACER data archives.","Federal Programs Branch (FPB) attorneys face overwhelming records and pressure to maintain consistent arguments across circuits. FPB faces immense workloads defending statutes and federal programs, often requiring rapid analysis of massive records and consistent legal arguments across circuits. This initiative will deploy a retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) tool trained on DOJ filings and administrative records to accelerate drafting and ensure consistency. It directly aligns with E.O. 14179 (removing barriers to AI adoption) and OMB M-25-21 (innovation, governance, and public trust).",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,S1_KNOWLEDGE_RETRIEVAL_RAG,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0338,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01106,US_OMB_2025_01106,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Law Enforcement,"Fraud diverts billions in taxpayer funds but manual review of records is too slow to catch early misconduct. Fraud cases involve sifting through vast amounts of structured and unstructured data, often too large for manual review to detect early fraud signals.",AI-driven Fraud Detection,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / CIV; Law Enforcement; United States,"Predictions, Classifications, Alerts: fraud risk scores, anomaly alerts, pattern classifications.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"(1) Bolsters DOJ’s mission to prevent waste, fraud, and abuse in taxpayer-funded health programs, strengthening enforcement under the FCA. (2) Builds on existing Medicare/Medicaid data feeds, OIG case frameworks, previous FCA healthcare enforcement analytics, and ongoing interagency fraud task force initiatives.(3) Increase in early identification of false claims; recovery dollars secured; reduced investigation timelines.","Fraud diverts billions in taxpayer funds but manual review of records is too slow to catch early misconduct. Fraud cases involve sifting through vast amounts of structured and unstructured data, often too large for manual review to detect early fraud signals. This initiative will apply AI-enabled anomaly detection to efficiently synthesize insights from vast data collections and uncover fraudulent patterns. It aligns with M-25-21’s public trust priority by safeguarding taxpayer funds and E.O. 14179’s innovation directive.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK|F04_UNSTRUCTURED_INFORMATION_COMPLEXITY,S4_PREDICTION_DETECTION,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0339,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01107,US_OMB_2025_01107,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Law Enforcement,"An AI tool could pull both structured data from settlement databases, together with unstructured settlement memoranda, and analyze settlement risk, valuation, and qualitative factors.",AI-assisted Settlement Data and Risk Analysis,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / CIV; Law Enforcement; United States,"Analytics, Predictions, Recommendations: settlement risk assessments, valuation analyses, pattern identification, natural language query responses from structured and unstructured data.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"(1) Improved settlement decision-making through comprehensive risk and valuation analysis, leading to more favorable outcomes for the government and taxpayers. (2) Builds on existing Salesforce migration initiatives and settlement databases while adding natural language query capabilities. (3) Reduced attorney time per settlement analysis; improved consistency in settlement valuations; better risk assessment accuracy; enhanced ability to identify settlement patterns and trends.","Settlements require knowledge of both valuation and risk for frequent types of litigation. An AI tool could pull both structured data from settlement databases, together with unstructured settlement memoranda, and analyze settlement risk, valuation, and qualitative factors. Users can use natural language to query one or both sources of data.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,F04_UNSTRUCTURED_INFORMATION_COMPLEXITY,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0340,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01108,US_OMB_2025_01108,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,IT,UNKNOWN,AI-assisted Legacy Code Modernization,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / CIV; IT; United States,"Code Generation, Recommendations, Predictions: modernized code output, optimization recommendations, vulnerability predictions.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"(1) Modernized applications improve resilience, reduce security risk, and lower long-term IT O&M costs, directly supporting DOJ’s modernization and cybersecurity priorities. (2) Builds on DOJ CIO modernization roadmaps, Federal IT dashboards, and prior migration initiatives to cloud platforms. (3) Reduction in legacy system maintenance costs, outages and performance loss; # of applications successfully migrated; cybersecurity vulnerabilities reduced.","This initiative uses AI-assisted code translation and refactoring tools to automatically convert legacy code into modern, secure languages (e.g., Java, Python) while flagging logic gaps and optimizing for cloud environments. Aligns with E.O. 14179’s innovation directive and M-25-21’s governance requirements.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0341,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01109,US_OMB_2025_01109,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,IT,UNKNOWN,AI Powered Data Governance,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / CIV; IT; United States,"Classifications, Recommendations, Automated Actions: content categorization, retention recommendations, duplicate identification.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"(1) Reduces costs, improves compliance with records management/FOIA, and data governance. Boosts transparency by making DOJ data discoverable and reusable. (2) DOJ records systems, NARA retention schedules, existing FOIA/eDiscovery platforms. (3) Measurable data storage savings; % of files tagged with metadata; improved FOIA response times.","This initiative deploys AI-driven data governance and metadata management to auto-tag, catalog, and enforce retention, while identifying duplicate/low-value files. Aligns with M-25-21 governance & E.O. 14179 innovation.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0343,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01110,US_OMB_2025_01110,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Admin Functions,UNKNOWN,AI Personal Assistant,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / CIV; Admin Functions; United States,"Recommendations, Alerts: deadline notifications, task prioritization suggestions, productivity optimization recommendations, calendar conflict alerts, project milestone tracking.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"(1) Improved attorney productivity and case management efficiency, enabling better service delivery to client agencies and more effective litigation outcomes. (2) Builds on existing calendar systems, email platforms, and case-tracking databases while maintaining attorney-client privilege protections. (3) Reduced missed deadlines; improved task prioritization; enhanced productivity metrics; better work-life balance for attorneys; increased case management efficiency.","Complex litigation requires intensive time and project management. AI assistants can analyze calendars, emails, case-tracking sheets, and schedules. It can flag deadlines, note high-priority tasks, and suggest productivity techniques for managing complex projects. Attorneys could create additional notifications or project management integrations to improve efficiency.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0344,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01111,US_OMB_2025_01111,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Admin Functions,UNKNOWN,AI Meeting Assistant,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / CIV; Admin Functions; United States,"Transcriptions, Summaries, Extractions: meeting transcripts, summary reports, action item lists, outcome tags.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"(1) Increases productivity by ensuring institutional knowledge is captured, searchable, and integrated into case management systems, reducing duplication and oversight risks. (2) Integrates with Microsoft Teams, Outlook, OneNote, and other knowledge management systems. (3) Increase proficiency in % of meetings transcribed and summarized; attorney time saved; # of action items captured and completed.","This initiative deploys AI-enabled meeting assistants that provide real-time transcription, generate concise summaries, identify action items, and tag outcomes to case files. Aligns with E.O. 14179’s innovation goals and M-25-21’s efficiency and transparency pillars.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0345,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01112,US_OMB_2025_01112,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Law Enforcement,UNKNOWN,Mass Claim Tool,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / CIV; Law Enforcement; United States,"Content Generation, Classifications, Automation: template letters, claim category assignments, automated data entry, standardized filing generation, quality control flags.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"(1) Ensures statutory compliance for mass claims processing, protecting the government's legal defenses while providing timely relief to eligible claimants. (2) Builds on existing RECA program infrastructure and mass claims databases while incorporating specialized medical data handling and privilege protections. (3) Achievement of statutory processing deadlines; reduced attorney hours per claim; improved consistency in claim categorization; automated template generation; enhanced quality control processes; increased claimant satisfaction through faster processing.","Components with mass claims, such as RECA must respond to tens of thousands of similar claims within statutorily defined timelines, or the U.S. forfeits its defenses. Tools to quickly process mass claims, including template letter generation, claim categorization, and automated data entry of standardized filings could meet urgent needs.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0346,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01113,US_OMB_2025_01113,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Law Enforcement,UNKNOWN,AI Evidence and Claim Consolidation,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / CIV; Law Enforcement; United States,"Summaries, Classifications, Predictions: document summaries, duplicate detection, inconsistency flagging, settlement predictions.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"1) Improves the government’s litigation posture in high-value torts, reduces exposure to excessive payouts, and ensures equitable and efficient claims processing.(2) Builds on DOJ medical record review systems and HHS/VA data integration, along with Relativity/CORA settlement, damages, and entitlement databases. (3) Faster evidence review; detection and elimination of duplicate claims; creating more effective and consistent settlements; increased dismissal or settlement of weak claims; attorney time saved.","This initiative applies AI to synthesize records, summarize expert reports and depositions, and identify duplicate claims. It also uses AI to identify inconsistencies between records and plaintiff claims, identify red flag legal issues, and create templates to respond to frequent or high-volume litigation. It also allows for analysis of settlement and damages databases to identify outlier trends. It supports M-25-21’s public trust pillar and E.O. 14179’s innovation agenda.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0347,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01114,US_OMB_2025_01114,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,IT,UNKNOWN,ChatBot,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / COPS; IT; United States,Response,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,The Intelligent Bot tool is implemented using Question and Answer (QnA) Maker and the Language Understanding (LUIS) services which is developed using the Microsoft Azure Software As A Service (SAAS) infrastructure in the Cloud on the COPS website. This will allow COPS to easily implement a brand new knowledge base of questions and answers feature on the site which will respond via a chat box based on a question entered by the customer.,"The Chatbot responds to the questions, allowing staff to focus on other priorities.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,S2_AGENT_CONVERSATIONAL_AI,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0046,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01115,US_OMB_2025_01115,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,IT,UNKNOWN,BMC Helix ITSM,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / CRM; IT; United States,"Prediction, recommendation",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Increase IT service desk productivity, prevent issues before they occur, and decrease user downtime.","BMC Helix's ITSM AI capabilities include Proactive Problem Management and Incident Correlation, which will allow CRM's IT Service Desk to more efficiently identify issues, resolve incidents, automate case routing, and perform root cause analysis.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0047,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01116,US_OMB_2025_01116,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Law Enforcement,UNKNOWN,Thomson Reuters CLEAR - License Plate Recognition,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / CRM; Law Enforcement; United States,"Object recognition, OCR, prediction",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Streamline investigations, reducing the need to search multiple platforms, while saving costs and allowing investigators to more quickly identify relevant information.","CLEAR LPR enables investigators to identify location history for license plates, connect addresses and individuals of interest to a vehicle's location and obtain images of a vehicle. CRM uses CLEAR LPR to aid in investigations.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0048,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
