AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01159,US_OMB_2025_01159,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,IT,UNKNOWN,Parse and Capture Data Submitted by Laboratories to the NFLIS Program,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / DEA; IT; United States,Extraction of information into a matrix of rows and columns which links identified substances to individual drug exhibits.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Cost savings, reduced customer wait times, and improved accuracy of reporting.",Collecting and entering information from registrants in the National Forensic Laboratory Information System (NFLIS) program takes considerable time and effort and is prone to human error,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0355,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01160,US_OMB_2025_01160,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Admin Functions,UNKNOWN,Managing Document Digital Signatures,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / DEA; Admin Functions; United States,"DEA/DOJ digital cloud base signatures can be integrated with an existing AI platform/application. AI outputs: AI assisted review, automated tagging, custom extractions, agreement summaries and chatbot for user help.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Saves time and effort by integrating identity verification while reducing the amount of storage required for documents.,"It is currently time-consuming, and challenging, to collect digital signatures from DOJ personnel into one source document. Utilizing AI would intend to manage the document workflow by using a single upgraded storage location with advanced security features.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0356,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01161,US_OMB_2025_01161,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Admin Functions,UNKNOWN,Creating and Maintaining IT Security Packages for Authorizations,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / DEA; Admin Functions; United States,"Generated implementation statements for security packages, reporting, trending, dashboarding",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Reduces costs while enabling use to maintain compliance and consistency,"Cybersecurity personnel want to automate the identification of security controls that can have implementation statements, create and maintain security packages for authorizations, keep up with compliance requirements, and more quickly onboard new systems and applications.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0357,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01162,US_OMB_2025_01162,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Law Enforcement,UNKNOWN,Community Outreach Chatbot that Helps the Public Consume Prevention Resources,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / DEA; Law Enforcement; United States,"1. Delivery of DEA publications (digital, hard copies for individuals, and bulk copies for organizations / events); 2. Connect users with best content fit; 3. Allow users to request DEA participation in community events; 4. Increase user skills and understanding to prevent substance use through the generation of answers derived from DEA content; 5. Connect users with DEA partners that provide content outside of CPO scope.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Increased usage of drug use prevention resources by citizens. Extends the reach of CPO into communities who have a high risk of drug abuse.,"Many citizens may not have the time to explore the copious library of DEA Community Outreach and Prevention Support (CPO) resources. By training AI on these resources, citizens can ask plain language questions and get succinct answers.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0358,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01163,US_OMB_2025_01163,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Law Enforcement,"TOMSS (Technical Operations Management Support System will provide call-deflection to ease the customer interaction burden on call center representatives, registration program specialists, and Diversion Investigators. The AI will provide consistent, accurate responses to repetitive queries and replace manual workloads.",Chatbot to Answer Diversion Registrants' Queries About Registration and Compliance Issues,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / DEA; Law Enforcement; United States,"• Policy-grounded responses to registrant inquiries (text output). • Deflection metrics and analytics (call volume reduction, FAQ trends). • Context-based prompts or redirects to DEA.gov resources. • Guardrail logic to return “no response” for non-registrant or ungrounded prompts.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,30–40% reduction in repetitive calls and emails. • 15–25% reduction in agent workload. • 100% of chatbot responses sourced from verified DEA policy. • 24/7 access to authoritative self-service guidance for registrants.,"TOMSS (Technical Operations Management Support System will provide call-deflection to ease the customer interaction burden on call center representatives, registration program specialists, and Diversion Investigators. The AI will provide consistent, accurate responses to repetitive queries and replace manual workloads.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0359,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01164,US_OMB_2025_01164,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Law Enforcement,"The Targeting & Special Projects Unit (DOIT) has identified a critical need to capture, convert, and process both structured and unstructured text from scanned case documents to support advanced analysis and trend forecasting.",Capture and Convert Structured Data from Scanned Case Documents to Support Advanced Analysis and Trend Forecasting,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / DEA; Law Enforcement; United States,The anticipated output for this AI use case will include text for documentation and CSV for excel spreadsheet analytical work.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Save valuable investigative time that can be used to focus on the results of the analysis. Conducting more comprehensive analysis on the data will improve trend forecasting, strengthen investigative strategies, and support a more predictive, data-driven approach.","The Targeting & Special Projects Unit (DOIT) has identified a critical need to capture, convert, and process both structured and unstructured text from scanned case documents to support advanced analysis and trend forecasting. This initiative will leverage an optical character recognition (OCR) solution capable of extracting both typed and handwritten content from diverse sources, including medical notes, invoices, and statements. Captured text will be transformed into a standardized, machine-readable format (e.g., CSV) and integrated into a relational database. From there, advanced analytical techniques will be applied to reveal hidden structures, patterns, and relationships within the data. By unlocking this information, we aim to enhance our ability to anticipate trends, strengthen investigative strategies, and move toward a more predictive, data-driven approach",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,F04_UNSTRUCTURED_INFORMATION_COMPLEXITY,S4_PREDICTION_DETECTION,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0360,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01165,US_OMB_2025_01165,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Law Enforcement,"This current workflow relies on manual data entry into spreadsheets, leading to errors, inconsistencies, and excessive investigative time.",Auditing Diversion Registrant Inventories of Controlled Substances,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / DEA; Law Enforcement; United States,Outputs may be data reports to support Diversion Control Division's mission and better serve the registrant community.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Reduces the amount of investigator time per audit by automating the extraction of key fields (e.g., item, quantity, cost, dates) from invoices and auto-populating computation charts. Standardized extraction and reconciliation eliminates human entry errors and decreases audit reconciliation error rates. Real-time flagging of discrepancies (e.g., inventory errors, excess sales, mismatched destruction records, possible fraudulent records) hastens the detection of potential diversion. Frees investigators to focus on high-value investigative activities and field operations, saving thousands in costs. Provides an auditable trail of extraction and reconciliation for internal and external audits. Maintains full audit-ready compliance for all registrants and a tangible audit trail for legal proceedings.","Diversion Investigators regularly conduct accountability audits of Registrants' management of controlled substances in order to detect diversion. Registrants sometimes submit hundreds of pages of invoices, receipts, and logs, which must be reconciled against inventory and movement records to ensure that the audits balance. Diversion Investigators review these and mark them for review if there is non-compliance with regulations, such as missing information or missed signatures. This current workflow relies on manual data entry into spreadsheets, leading to errors, inconsistencies, and excessive investigative time.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK|F08_ERROR_COMPLIANCE_RISK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0361,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01166,US_OMB_2025_01166,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Law Enforcement,DEA investigators currently rely on manual manipulation of data in spreadsheets to conduct Prescription Monitoring Program (PMP) analysis.,Analyzing Prescription Monitoring Program Data,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / DEA; Law Enforcement; United States,Quantitative data reports and analyses,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Increases operational efficiency by automating data preparation, risk identification, and initial narrative generation. Average time spent to produce a PMP decreased from ten to two hours (minus 80%). By employing consistent, data-driven risk analysis, increases the proportion of high-value investigations that result in successful enforcement or administrative outcomes. Reallocates Diversion Investigator effort to higher-value tasks (e.g., field operations, strategic planning), producing a labor cost benefit in the thousands per Diversion Investigator based on average pay and number of PMPs analyzed. Faster identification of prescribing anomalies supports earlier public health interventions and reduces community exposure to diverted pharmaceuticals. A single, centrally managed AI service can be provisioned to all DEA field offices, ensuring uniform analytic standards.","DEA investigators currently rely on manual manipulation of data in spreadsheets to conduct Prescription Monitoring Program (PMP) analysis. This requires 8-10 hours of labor (data extraction, cleaning, cross referencing, narrative synthesis), and, since investigators analyze data in different ways, results vary. There is little consistency across the agency or even between investigators in terms of what data is examined and there is no easy way to identify patterns such as MMEs, combinations, and early fills.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0362,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
