AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01365,US_OMB_2025_01365,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,Law Enforcement,UNKNOWN,Thomson Reuters CLEAR,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / USNCB; Law Enforcement; United States,Data,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Timely access to key data in the pursuit of persons of interest,Access to large data sets used for locating persons of interest.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0239,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01366,US_OMB_2025_01366,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Justice,IT,UNKNOWN,USTP AI Assistant,Department of Justice; Department of Justice / USTP; IT; United States,Given the outputs range due to the specific AI Assistants objective USTP will provide a couple of examples that are in Pre-Deployment Technical Feasibility testing now: 1). HR Assistant - Trained on USTP's SharePoint Intranet pages to answer common questions about various human resources support issues. 2). Briefing Assistant - Review public documents that were previous submitted USTP briefs on specific bankruptcy cases to easily search and find these cases.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Intended benefits of using Microsoft AI services would be to enable USTP staff to find information quickly on relevant questions they may have. The use cases tested in Pre-Deployment phase would help reduce Help Desk calls and increase productivity of users enabling them to find technical information quickly. Potential to help generate new content based on pilot testing.,"Intended purpose is to enable USTP's IT team to understand the process to develop, test, tune and use Microsoft various AI services--Azure Open AI, Azure Open AI Foundry, Microsoft Copilot Studio. A secondary purpose is understanding the full costs and time to develop and implement a use case from start to finish. A tertiary purpose is to ensure the Generative AI service is providing useful responses and value given the cost and time to setup and deploy.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOJ-0240,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01367,US_OMB_2025_01367,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Labor,Other - Applied Mathematical Sciences,UNKNOWN,OEWS Occupation Autocoder,Department of Labor; BLS; Other - Applied Mathematical Sciences; United States,6-digit Standard Occupational Classification (SOC) codes,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Improving data accuracy and saving time for SOC coders,The input is state-submitted response files that include occupation title and sometimes job description of the surveyed units. The autocoder reads the job title and assigns up to two 6-digit Standard Occupational Classification (SOC) codes along with their probabilities as recommendations for human coders. Codes above a certain threshold are appended to the submitted response file and sent back to states to assist them with their SOC code assignment.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOL-19,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01368,US_OMB_2025_01368,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Labor,Other - Applied Mathematical Sciences,UNKNOWN,Scanner Data Product Classification,Department of Labor; BLS; Other - Applied Mathematical Sciences; United States,Entry Level Item Codes,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Efficiency of item classification efforts,"BLS receives bulk data from some corporations related to the cost of goods they sell and services they provide. Consumer Price Index (CPI) staff have hand-coded a segment of the items in these data into Entry Level Item (ELI) codes. To accept and make use of these bulk data transfers at scale, BLS has begun to use machine learning to label data with ELI codes. The machine learning model takes as input word frequency counts from item descriptions. Logistic regression is then used to estimate the probability of each item being classified in each ELI category based on the word frequency categorizations. The highest probability category is selected for inclusion in the data. Any selected classifications that do not meet a certain probability threshold are flagged for human review. Benefits: real-time turnaround, productivity improvements, cost savings.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOL-20,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01369,US_OMB_2025_01369,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Labor,Other - Applied Mathematical Sciences,UNKNOWN,Expenditure Classification Autocoder,Department of Labor; BLS; Other - Applied Mathematical Sciences; United States,BLS-internal item codes (expenditure classification categories),UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Efficiency of expenditure classification efforts,Assigns expense classification categories to reported expenses from Consumer Expenditure Diary Survey respondents.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOL-21,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01370,US_OMB_2025_01370,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Labor,Other - Applied Mathematical Sciences,UNKNOWN,Computer-Assisted Coding: SOII Autocoder,Department of Labor; BLS; Other - Applied Mathematical Sciences; United States,SOC and OIICS codes,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Efficiency and data quality improvements,"The Survey of Occupational Injuries and Illnesses (SOII) collects hundreds of thousands of narratives describing cases of work-related injury and illness annually. Using narratives and other relevant information, SOII Autocoder automatically assigns classifications for SOII elements, which include worker occupation, nature of the injury, part of body affected, event that resulted in the injury, source and secondary source (if it exists) that caused the injury. This process used to be performed entirely by human staff.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOL-28,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01371,US_OMB_2025_01371,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Labor,Other - Applied Mathematical Sciences,UNKNOWN,CFOI Record Matching,Department of Labor; BLS; Other - Applied Mathematical Sciences; United States,Similarity score between records,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Efficiency and data quality improvements,"The Census of Fatal Occupational Injuries (CFOI) collects and publishes a complete count of work-related fatal injuries and descriptive data on their circumstances. The CFOI Record Matching programs matches records from various sources, including Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) Information System (OIS) files, news articles, and Quarterly Census of Employment and Wages (QCEW), to identify missing or inconsistent data in CFOI.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOL-29,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01372,US_OMB_2025_01372,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Labor,Other - Applied Mathematical Sciences,UNKNOWN,CPS OTC Prediction,Department of Labor; BLS; Other - Applied Mathematical Sciences; United States,"worker's time off was paid, or whether they get paid hourly or not",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Efficiency and data quality improvements,"The BLS productivity office publishes measures of hours worked by major sector and industry. As part of the calculation for this measure, BLS uses Current Employment Statistics (CES) data on hours paid is used to estimate hours for payroll workers. Additional adjustments are made to this measure, such as removing paid time off (PTO), adding off-the-clock (OTC) hours, and adding in hours worked by self-employed and unpaid family workers. BLS uses the Current Population Survey (CPS) dataset to identify the amount of hours that are worked off-the-clock (OTC) by workers. There are some workers in the CPS dataset that do not report whether their time off was paid, or whether they get paid hourly or not. This data needs to be imputed to calculate the ratio of total hours worked to paid hours worked. A random forest model is used to predict the responses for workers that did not report this information by training it on characteristics (such as industry, occupation, education level, age, etc.) of respondents that have reported that information.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOL-35,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01373,US_OMB_2025_01373,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Labor,Other - Applied Mathematical Sciences,UNKNOWN,Sample Refinement: Frame API,Department of Labor; BLS; Other - Applied Mathematical Sciences; United States,Similarity score between records,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Efficiency and data quality improvements,"BLS establishment-based surveys, such as the Survey of Occupational Injuries and Illnesses (SOII), the National Compensation Survey (NCS), and the Occupational Requirements Survey (ORS), use the Longitudinal Database (LDB) as the frame for their survey samples. For each of these programs, there is a significant time-lag between when the sample is drawn for a program and when data collection begins. A critical and time-consuming part of data collection is sample refinement: checking the latest Quarterly Census of Employment and Wages (QCEW) and LDB data to adjust for any changes to the sampled establishment during that time-lag. The QCEW/LDB Frame API allows fast retrieval of the latest QCEW/LDB data for a nationwide sample so that users can perform sample refinement more efficiently. The SOII program uses the Frame API to perform over 20 sample refinement comparison checks, which outputs a report for the data collectors. The Frame API uses TF-IDF vectors and cosine similarity to compare company names, mailing addresses, and unit descriptions between the survey sample and the latest QCEW/LDB data to determine what components may have changed. The Frame API also has the flexibility for the users to match records using other combinations of variables.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOL-36,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01374,US_OMB_2025_01374,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Labor,Other - Applied Mathematical Sciences,UNKNOWN,CE Interview Item Code Estimation,Department of Labor; BLS; Other - Applied Mathematical Sciences; United States,Expense Classification Category,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Improves data quality by identifying potentially incorrect misclassifications from data collection for human review,Recommends expense classification categories for Consumer Expenditure Interview Survey expense responses.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOL-37,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01375,US_OMB_2025_01375,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Labor,Other - Applied Mathematical Sciences,UNKNOWN,CE Interview Imputations,Department of Labor; BLS; Other - Applied Mathematical Sciences; United States,These output numbers are rounded up to the nearest whole value or rounded to 0 if negative. The output is only used to complete the Consumer Price Index.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Uses more sophisticated statistical techniques to estimate missing values,Imputes missing expenditure values in the Consumer Expenditure Interview Survey when respondents answer “don’t know” or refuse to provide an expense amount.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOL-38,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
