AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01390,US_OMB_2025_01390,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Labor,Admin Functions,UNKNOWN,ETA Grants Monitoring Tool through Doc Explorer,Department of Labor; ETA; Admin Functions; United States,Summaries and Question answer,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Saves time during site visit. Enhances monitoring efficiency and ensures accurate, timely use of Grants","Automates review of grant documents to detect anomalies, delays, and compliance issues. Improves consistency and accuracy in monitoring across programs.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOL-47,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01391,US_OMB_2025_01391,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Labor,Other,"By enabling inspectors to access inspection checklists, capture photos and videos, and input data through voice commands, the headset reduces reliance on manual data entry and handheld devices in mining environments.",AI Headset,Department of Labor; MSHA; Other; United States,"Outputs: For MSHA inspectors using the Inspection Application System (IAS), the AI system outputs of the AI headset are designed to streamline field operations, enhance safety, and improve data accuracy. These outputs are delivered through a combination of visual, audio, and data-driven interfaces that support real-time decision-making and documentation. The primary output is a high-resolution micro-display that appears in the inspector’s line of sight, showing inspection forms and data entry screens, mine data, safety protocols, or previous violation histories pulled from IAS or the Mine Data Retrieval System (MDRS)",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Improve Inspection Onsite Documentation Time: The intended purpose of the AI headset is to provide a hands-free, voice-activated wearable solution that enhances the productivity, safety, and effectiveness of frontline government workers, such as MSHA inspectors. The expected benefits include significant cost savings through reduced inspection times and fewer repeat site visits, as well as improved documentation accuracy through real-time photo, video, and voice note capture. The device also enables live communication with remote experts, accelerating decision-making and reducing downtime.","Inspection: An AI headset offers a hands-free, voice-controlled solution that enhances the efficiency, safety, and accuracy of MSHA inspectors using the Inspection Application System (IAS). By enabling inspectors to access inspection checklists, capture photos and videos, and input data through voice commands, the headset reduces reliance on manual data entry and handheld devices in mining environments. It also supports real-time communication with field office supervisors and data collection, streamlining the inspection process and improving documentation. When integrated with IAS or compatible platforms, an AI headset can significantly modernize field inspections, ensuring better compliance and faster reporting.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,DOL-44,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
