AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01549,US_OMB_2025_01549,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Environmental Protection Agency,Law Enforcement,UNKNOWN,AI-Enhanced Facility Finder,Environmental Protection Agency; OECA; Law Enforcement; United States,"The model outputs the geolocation of facilities at increased likelihood of needing an industrial stormwater permit but lacking one. It also outputs a risk score, from “No risk” to “High Risk” for permitted facilities, which is used as one of many inputs by human reviewers.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"AI-Enhanced Facility Finder saves time for EPA employees by identifying facilities most likely to lack necessary industrial stormwater permits, which are then reviewed by humans. Testing at the state level has shown these identifications increase the number of facilities that are permitted and monitored, resulting in cleaner water for Americans.","Many facilities are required to register for industrial stormwater permits but do not do so. To find unpermitted facilities, EPA personnel use approaches that are time-consuming, inefficient, and infeasible to scale to the millions of facilities in the U.S.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,75,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
