AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01570,US_OMB_2025_01570,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Federal Communications Commission,IT,"Currently, this process is performed manually by staff, which is time-consuming and prone to inconsistency.",Automated Complaint Categorization for Enforcement Bureau,Federal Communications Commission; Enforcement Bureau (EB); IT; United States,"The AI system produces categorized complaint data in Excel format. These files are stored in a shared drive and are later visualized using Microstrategy dashboards. Users do not interact directly with the model; instead, they access the model’s outputs through reports and visualizations. The model is updated approximately every six months to ensure continued accuracy and relevance.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"The AI system improves operational efficiency by reducing the manual workload for staff, allowing them to focus on higher-priority enforcement activities. It enhances consistency in complaint categorization, which supports more accurate reporting and analysis. Faster processing of complaints enables quicker responses to public concerns, and the structured data output supports better decision-making and policy development aligned with the agency’s mission.","The AI model is designed to automate the categorization of consumer complaints received by the Enforcement Bureau. Currently, this process is performed manually by staff, which is time-consuming and prone to inconsistency. The model uses natural language processing (NLP) to classify complaint text based on predefined categories, streamlining the workflow and improving accuracy.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,FCC-0005,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01571,US_OMB_2025_01571,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Federal Communications Commission,IT,"Enables staff to efficiently manage and organize SharePoint content by automating repetitive tasks such as document tagging, summarization, and permission updates, reducing manual effort and improving consistency across teams.",SharePoint Copilot for Workflow Automation,Federal Communications Commission; Office of Engineering and Technology (OET); IT; United States,"(1) Automatically tags and summarizes documents stored in SharePoint libraries; (2) Updates permissions and metadata based on user input or predefined rules; and (3) Generates structured content insights to support collaboration, compliance, and workflow optimization.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Improves internal collaboration and operational efficiency across FCC bureaus and offices by streamlining content workflows. This allows staff to focus on higher-value work, supports faster service delivery, and enhances responsiveness to public needs through better-organized and accessible information.","Enables staff to efficiently manage and organize SharePoint content by automating repetitive tasks such as document tagging, summarization, and permission updates, reducing manual effort and improving consistency across teams.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,FCC-0004,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01572,US_OMB_2025_01572,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Federal Communications Commission,IT,Accelerates legacy code analysis and documentation that would otherwise require extensive manual review.,AI-Enhanced ULS Reverse Engineering,Federal Communications Commission; Wireless Telecommunications Bureau (WTB); IT; United States,"(1) Extracts and documents business logic, data flows, and application architecture from legacy code; (2) Generates visual models such as business process diagrams, integration maps, and data flow diagrams; and (3) Produces structured documentation including source code analysis, performance metrics, and modernization-ready technical artifacts.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Accelerates the analysis and documentation of legacy code in the Universal Licensing System (ULS), reducing manual workload and enabling timely reverse engineering. This supports long-term modernization of the ULS application, helping the agency maintain a scalable, reliable licensing system and improving service delivery to the general public.",Accelerates legacy code analysis and documentation that would otherwise require extensive manual review.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,FCC-0001,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01573,US_OMB_2025_01573,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Federal Communications Commission,IT,"Manually reviewing and analyzing large volumes of public comments, which is time-consuming, inconsistent, and resource-intensive for legal teams by automating the identification of key legal themes, sentiment, and duplicate content to support faster, more consistent, and scalable legal analysis.",Comment Legal Analysis & Review Assistant,Federal Communications Commission; Wireless Telecommunications Bureau (WTB); IT; United States,"(1) Summarizes public comments to identify sentiment, key themes, and stakeholder positions across submissions; (2) Links relevant legal context—such as statutes and FCC rulings to help staff assess alignment with existing frameworks; and (3) Generates formatted outputs (e.g., internal memos, dashboards, summaries) for use by legal, policy, and communications staff.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Improves the agency’s ability to review public comments quickly and consistently, supporting more efficient, informed, and legally grounded rulemaking.","Manually reviewing and analyzing large volumes of public comments, which is time-consuming, inconsistent, and resource-intensive for legal teams by automating the identification of key legal themes, sentiment, and duplicate content to support faster, more consistent, and scalable legal analysis.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK|F06_HIGH_VOLUME_SCALABILITY_BOTTLENECK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,FCC-0003,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01574,US_OMB_2025_01574,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Federal Communications Commission,IT,"The AI system is designed to solve the challenge of extracting and organizing critical information embedded in attachments submitted across FCC licensing systems. Currently, staff must manually search through multiple systems and thousands of documents to locate ownership details and other key data, which is inefficient and time-consuming.",Automated Attachment Intelligence for FCC Licensing Systems,Federal Communications Commission; Wireless Telecommunications Bureau (WTB); IT; United States,"The AI system outputs structured data extracted from document attachments, including named entities such as company names, individuals, and locations. These entities are categorized, normalized, and stored in a searchable database. The system also supports keyword monitoring, watchlist alerts, and reporting capabilities. Outputs are accessible to authorized FCC staff through integrated tools like Power BI and Power Apps, and are designed to support internal research and analysis workflows.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"The AI solution will enhance the FCC’s ability to research telecommunications entities, particularly in support of national security efforts such as identifying foreign ownership and monitoring compliance with the Covered List. It will reduce the time and effort required to compile case materials, improve the accuracy of investigations, and enable faster decision-making. These improvements support the FCC’s mission to protect the communications infrastructure and ensure regulatory compliance, ultimately benefiting the public by strengthening oversight and enforcement capabilities.","The AI system is designed to solve the challenge of extracting and organizing critical information embedded in attachments submitted across FCC licensing systems. Currently, staff must manually search through multiple systems and thousands of documents to locate ownership details and other key data, which is inefficient and time-consuming. The proposed solution automates this process using AI-powered OCR and entity recognition, enabling faster and more accurate access to relevant information.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,FCC-0006,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01575,US_OMB_2025_01575,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Federal Communications Commission,IT,"Solves the challenge of efficiently analyzing large volumes of public comments by automating sentiment analysis, deduplication, and summarization.",ECFS Comment Analytics Deduplication Services (CADS),Federal Communications Commission; Wireline Competition Bureau (WCB); IT; United States,"(1) Classifies public comments and filings by sentiment (pro, neutral, against); (2) Identifies and removes duplicate and near-duplicate submissions using clustering algorithms; and (3) Generates AI-powered summaries of filings and attachments to support efficient review and decision-making",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Accelerated and more accurate analysis of public comments, enabling the FCC to better understand public sentiment on net neutrality, reduce manual review burdens, and make more informed, transparent, and timely regulatory decisions that reflect public input.","Solves the challenge of efficiently analyzing large volumes of public comments by automating sentiment analysis, deduplication, and summarization.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,RETIRED,종료,F06_HIGH_VOLUME_SCALABILITY_BOTTLENECK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,FCC-0002,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
