AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01611,US_OMB_2025_01611,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""enterprise_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation,Other,"Currently, claims specialists spend countless hours manually reviewing trust agreements to extract grantor/settlor and beneficiary information.",Trust Document Entity Extraction,Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation; Division of Resolutions and Receiverships; Other; United States,"The extracted data, which will include key data elements, such as grantor/settler and beneficiaries from Trust Agreements, along with the original Trust Agreement will be presented to users through an application user interface.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,This will reduce the time and cost to transpose information from Trust Agreements.,"Currently, claims specialists spend countless hours manually reviewing trust agreements to extract grantor/settlor and beneficiary information. Implementing OCR and Llama to automate key data extraction from these agreements will significantly make the process faster, more efficient, and more accurate while eliminating the potential for manual errors.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,FDIC – 52,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01612,US_OMB_2025_01612,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""enterprise_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation,Other,UNKNOWN,Trust Document Entity Extraction - LLM,Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation; Division of Resolutions and Receiverships; Other; United States,"By using the LLM, the extracted data will include key data elements, such as grantor/settler and beneficiaries from Trust Agreements along with the original Trust Agreement, which will be presented to users through an application user interface. This will automate the extraction of key information from trust agreements to match and verify customer form inputs.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"The current trust document review process is labor intensive and may require further reviews by legal experts, hence, prolonging the processing time. Using a LLM to automate the extraction of data will reduce manual effort and improve the quality of data extracted from trust documents.","The current trust document review process is labor intensive and may require further reviews by legal experts, hence, prolonging the processing time. By leveraging the use of a Large Language Model to automate the extraction of key information from trust agreements to match and verify customer form input, this will lead to a faster, accurate and efficient workflow for claims specialists.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,S3_DOCUMENT_INTELLIGENCE,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,FDIC – 53,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01613,US_OMB_2025_01613,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""enterprise_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation,Other,"The current process for managing restitution order data lacks efficiency, making it difficult to effectively identify, track, classify, and resolve these orders.",Restitution Order AI Assistance,Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation; Division of Resolutions and Receiverships; Other; United States,Restitution order data in structured format.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"This is a strategic solution to enhance the identification, tracking, classification, and resolution of restitution order workload, ultimately supporting the FDIC’s mission to maximize recoveries from failed financial institutions The outputs will include restitution order dataset, case resolution report, consolidated recovery statement, loss estimation and asset tracking metrics.","The current process for managing restitution order data lacks efficiency, making it difficult to effectively identify, track, classify, and resolve these orders. This hinders the FDIC's ability to maximize recoveries from failed financial institutions. Implementing a strategic solution to enhance the identification, tracking, classification, and resolution of restitution order data will improve efficiency and ultimately support the FDIC's mission to maximize recoveries from failed financial institutions.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,FDIC-62,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01614,US_OMB_2025_01614,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""enterprise_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation,Other,UNKNOWN,Provisional Holds Model,Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation; Division of Resolutions and Receiverships; Other; United States,This solution will enable FDIC to proactively manage financial risk by estimating potential overpayments under different levels of provisional holds in the absence of current account-level data and provide strategic insights needed to optimize our financial holds.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"The model supports the provisional holds process by estimating potential overpayment. Appropriate provisional holds allow depositors access to their funds in a timely manner, while controlling risks to the DIF from overpaying uninsured depositors during a bank failure.","This solution will enable the FDIC to proactively manage financial risk by providing the ability to estimate potential overpayments, even without real-time account-level data. The strategic insights gained will allow for the optimization of financial holds, minimizing both overpayment risk and operational inefficiencies.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,FDIC-63,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
