AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01703,US_OMB_2025_01703,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,General Services Administration,IT,"The AI is intended to solve the problem of inefficient information retrieval within the ASSIST system, where users currently spend up to 5 minutes per search due to a basic keyword-matching search solution.",ASSIST Global Search and Inference,General Services Administration; IT; United States,"The goal is to reduce search time by 90% by implementing a context-aware, AI-powered search and structured data aggregation experience, allowing users to find accurate information using natural language in 30 seconds or less per query.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"The AI is intended to solve the problem of inefficient information retrieval within the ASSIST system, where users currently spend up to 5 minutes per search due to a basic keyword-matching search solution. The goal is to reduce search time by 90% by implementing a context-aware, AI-powered search and structured data aggregation experience, allowing users to find accurate information using natural language in 30 seconds or less per query.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,UNKNOWN,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01704,US_OMB_2025_01704,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,General Services Administration,Procurement and Finance Mgmt,"The AI is intended to solve the problem of significant manual effort and time spent on data entry within the end-to-end acquisition workflow, where data is received in various file formats.",ASSIST Auto Copy and Summarize,General Services Administration; Procurement and Finance Mgmt; United States,"Currently, data entry per contract typically takes between 45 minutes and one hour, and the proposed solution aims to automate this process to reduce per-contract data entry time by 80%.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"The AI is intended to solve the problem of significant manual effort and time spent on data entry within the end-to-end acquisition workflow, where data is received in various file formats. Currently, data entry per contract typically takes between 45 minutes and one hour, and the proposed solution aims to automate this process to reduce per-contract data entry time by 80%.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,UNKNOWN,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01705,US_OMB_2025_01705,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,General Services Administration,Admin Functions,"The AI is intended to solve the problem of manual document review and categorization by Contracting Officers (COs) within the ASSIST Electronic Contract File (ECF) system. Currently, COs spend significant time reviewing and categorizing 20-50 documents per acquisition, leading to approximately 100-150 monthly help desk calls from new COs seeking guidance due to the manual effort and potential for errors.",ASSIST ECF Autoclassification and Summary,General Services Administration; Admin Functions; United States,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"The AI is intended to solve the problem of manual document review and categorization by Contracting Officers (COs) within the ASSIST Electronic Contract File (ECF) system. Currently, COs spend significant time reviewing and categorizing 20-50 documents per acquisition, leading to approximately 100-150 monthly help desk calls from new COs seeking guidance due to the manual effort and potential for errors.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK|F08_ERROR_COMPLIANCE_RISK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,UNKNOWN,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
