AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01779,US_OMB_2025_01779,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Health and Human Services,IT,UNKNOWN,AI DevOps - Improving Development and CI/CD Operations,Department of Health and Human Services; HHS/AHRQ/CFACT; IT; United States,"Integrating AI into DevOps pipeline can boost efficiency, enhance code quality, and accelerate development cycle. AI code review uses artificial intelligence algorithms to analyze source code for potential issues. Initial integration of AI code review can assist in detecting bugs, security vulnerabilities, performance bottlenecks, and deviations from coding standards.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Integrating AI into DevOps pipeline can boost efficiency, enhance code quality, and accelerate development cycle. AI code review uses artificial intelligence algorithms to analyze source code for potential issues. Initial integration of AI code review can assist in detecting bugs, security vulnerabilities, performance bottlenecks, and deviations from coding standards.","Introducing AI to DevOps can identify and reduce errors, shorten release cycles, and empower development teams with data-driven insights, resulting in faster continuous integration and shorter development lifecycles.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,UNKNOWN,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01780,US_OMB_2025_01780,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Health and Human Services,IT,UNKNOWN,AHRQ Search,Department of Health and Human Services; HHS/AHRQ/CQuIPS; IT; United States,"This AI use case aims to optimize search results by adjusting their ranking, ensuring that the most pertinent information is displayed at the top. It also enhances search effectiveness by adding synonyms to queries behind the scenes. It further improves user experience by auto-completing queries as they are being typed, and showing related searches that might offer additional valuable insights. The system also proposes content tags automatically, leveraging machine learning to assess existing content tagging patterns. Additionally, it suggests spelling corrections and reformats search queries based on data from Google Analytics.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"This AI use case aims to optimize search results by adjusting their ranking, ensuring that the most pertinent information is displayed at the top. It also enhances search effectiveness by adding synonyms to queries behind the scenes. It further improves user experience by auto-completing queries as they are being typed, and showing related searches that might offer additional valuable insights. The system also proposes content tags automatically, leveraging machine learning to assess existing content tagging patterns. Additionally, it suggests spelling corrections and reformats search queries based on data from Google Analytics.","Organization wide search that includes Relevancy Tailoring, Auto-generation Synonyms, Automated Suggestions, Suggested Related Content, Auto Tagging, and ""Did you mean?"" to allow visitors to find specific content. This AI use case enhances our agency's efficiency and user experience by optimizing search results, auto-completing queries, suggesting relevant searches and content tags, as well as proposing spelling corrections.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,UNKNOWN,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
