AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01975,US_OMB_2025_01975,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Health and Human Services,Service Delivery,UNKNOWN,AI to Improve Public Access to the Administrative Appeals Process,Department of Health and Human Services; HHS/DAB/OS; Service Delivery; United States,Reliable data on appellant filing activity and meta data the agency will use to analyze workloads and allocate resources.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,DAB adjudicatory divisions rely heavily on electronically filed (E-filed) appeals. Most appellants access E-filing through the DAB's website. A chatbot on the website will reduce filing errors and improve customer experience by directing appellants to the correct DAB adjudicatory division responsible for deciding their appeal.,More effectively leverage online resources to better assist the public and reduce the number of misfiled appeals submitted to the Departmental Appeals Board (DAB) via electronic filing.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,UNKNOWN,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01976,US_OMB_2025_01976,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Health and Human Services,Other,UNKNOWN,AI Use Policy Tool,Department of Health and Human Services; HHS/DAB/OS; Other; United States,Analysis of large volumes of data that can be used to address common errors and supports the development of targeted training and job aid.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"The DAB is responsible for issuing fair, impartial, legally correct and defensible determinations which serve as the final decision of the DHHS Secretary. The AI quality review large language model (LLM) tool will use an LLM to create algorithms that run behind our case tracking system to randomly select certain DAB decisions to identify potential quality review issues. The LLM will scan DAB decisions to ensure compliance with quality review standards (e.g., protect PHI, PII and FTI). Benefits include more effective quality review and faster identification of data trends that may require additional analysis.",Ensure public confidence in the integrity of DAB decisions by maximizing quality review standards and reducing errors.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,UNKNOWN,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01977,US_OMB_2025_01977,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Health and Human Services,Other,UNKNOWN,Resources to Assist the Advisory Board In Identifying AI Tools for Use In An Adjudication Environment,Department of Health and Human Services; HHS/DAB/OS; Other; United States,Enhanced workload data that can be used to allocate resources to the DAB's various adjudicatory divisions.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Use AI to analyze data received from appellants and interested parties to identify trends, increase efficiency in case processing and improve adjudication outcomes.","Agency adjudication activities require the analysis of large quantities of data to conduct docket analysis, identify efficiencies in case processing, and conduct 508 compliance required to make decisions available to the public.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,UNKNOWN,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01978,US_OMB_2025_01978,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Health and Human Services,Health and Medical,UNKNOWN,LLM-Assisted VAERS Analyses,Department of Health and Human Services; HHS/FDA/CBER; Health and Medical; United States,To provide reviewers adhoc VAERS queries.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Build capacity for and assess the application of a LLM to VAERS (Vaccine Adverse Events Reporting System) to provide reviewers adhoc VAERS queries and efficiently generate customized query outputs. Efficiently generate customized query outputs of VAERS queries for reviewers.,"Extraction of relevant information, tabulation of data, find patterns across adverse events reports, and generate hypotheses for further investigations.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,UNKNOWN,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01979,US_OMB_2025_01979,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Health and Human Services,IT,UNKNOWN,Process Large Amount of Submitted Docket Comments,Department of Health and Human Services; HHS/FDA/CBER; IT; United States,To provide reviewers adhoc VAERS queries.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"To enhance the automatic process of dockets, we have created an AI/ML tool in CBER/HIVE that automatically download dockets and process them to accelerate the review of docket comments, significantly improving the efficiency and accuracy of our regulatory processes. Efficiently generate customized query outputs of VAERS queries for reviewers.","Deduplication of public comments, and generating draft sentiment analysis and grouping of comments",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,UNKNOWN,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01980,US_OMB_2025_01980,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Health and Human Services,Health and Medical,"Specifically, it aims to address issues of inefficiency, delays in identifying deficiencies and information overload.",HIVE AI Pilot,Department of Health and Human Services; HHS/FDA/CBER; Health and Medical; United States,The system's output include: 1. review discipline recommendations - automated suggestions for the most appropriate review disciplines for each incoming submission. 2. highlighted key data - generates reports highlighting critical information to facilitate quicker understanding by RPMs and reviewers. 3. Summaries - reports summarizing large documents to potentially accelerate review.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Overall, is designed to improve efficiency and effectiveness of the regulatory review process, allowing for quicker and well-informed decision making","The AI is intended to assist in solving several problems related to the review process for INDs. Specifically, it aims to address issues of inefficiency, delays in identifying deficiencies and information overload. By providing recommendations for review disciplines, it helps reviewers to quickly identify potential review disciplines that are required. By identifying grossly deficient submissions early on, it reduces the workload and highlighting key data helps reviewers to focus on higher-level tasks that require their expertise.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,UNKNOWN,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01981,US_OMB_2025_01981,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Health and Human Services,Health and Medical,UNKNOWN,AI and Vaccine Labeling,Department of Health and Human Services; HHS/FDA/CBER; Health and Medical; United States,"The AI system's output is a list of similarities and differences between vaccine label sections, as well as highlighted changes or updates to vaccine labels. Additionally, it may identify duplicate or similar vaccines and provide recommendations for label revisions or updates. The system generates summarized information about vaccine ingredients, approval timelines, and other relevant details. These outputs would be presented in a user-friendly format, such as tables, charts, or highlighted text, to facilitate easy review and analysis by the user.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Enhance the vaccine label review process, making it more efficient and effective.","The app is designed to streamline vaccine label review processes, offering several key features to simplify and improve efficiency. It includes MedDRA integration for term searches, comprehensive search across all vaccine documents, and vaccine-specific information retrieval. Additionally, the app provides lookup functionality for approval timelines and active ingredients, as well as tools for detecting duplicates and comparing section content using AI-enhanced technology.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,UNKNOWN,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01982,US_OMB_2025_01982,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Health and Human Services,Health and Medical,Manual classification of facility supply chain roles from FDA industry submissions (356h forms) is time-consuming and inefficient,Renamed: 356H Machine Learning (ML) Facility Supply Chain Role Classification Previously: 356H ML Facility Supply Chain Role Classification,Department of Health and Human Services; HHS/FDA/CDER; Health and Medical; United States,Extracts a facility's supply chain role from industry submissions and displays identified roles on a data-stewards screen for human verification and final determination.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Improve the efficiency of evaluating 356H forms to assess a facility's supply chain role, thereby decreasing the time required for the processing of submissions and enabling faster oversight of drug manufacturing facilities.",Manual classification of facility supply chain roles from FDA industry submissions (356h forms) is time-consuming and inefficient,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,UNKNOWN,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01983,US_OMB_2025_01983,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Health and Human Services,Health and Medical,"Manual and subjective assessment process for Field Alert Reports (FARs) can lead to inconsistency in prioritizing and assessing reports, potentially leading to ineffective resource allocation where the same level of formality is being applied for all issues, regardless of risk.",Renamed: Risk-based FAR Review & Decision Support Previously: Field Alert Reports (FAR) Prioritization Model,Department of Health and Human Services; HHS/FDA/CDER; Health and Medical; United States,"AI-based machine learning classification of FAR risk into low, medium, and high; provides insights on problem clusters, rare-events, and source variables.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Assist Field Alert Report (FAR) reviewers by providing objective intelligence and insights that help prioritize the highest risk reports, potentially reducing response time to high-risk issues while maintaining human oversight of all decisions and leading to Agency resources being used more efficiently.","Manual and subjective assessment process for Field Alert Reports (FARs) can lead to inconsistency in prioritizing and assessing reports, potentially leading to ineffective resource allocation where the same level of formality is being applied for all issues, regardless of risk.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,S5_OPTIMIZATION_DECISION_SUPPORT,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,UNKNOWN,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01984,US_OMB_2025_01984,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Health and Human Services,Health and Medical,UNKNOWN,Analytics-Driven Supplement Evaluation (ASE),Department of Health and Human Services; HHS/FDA/CDER; Health and Medical; United States,"Using a Convolutional Neural Network (NN) model, in combination with a rules-based approach, produces an output that helps staff triage CBE submission review",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"This AI use case supports the triage and staff assignment process for the review of post-market Change Being Effected (CBE) supplement submissions, improving review efficiency and consistency while ensuring appropriate regulatory oversight.","Exponential increase in post-approval chemistry, manufacturing, and controls (CMC) change submissions, with 80% being Changes Being Effected (CBE-30/0) notifications that may be suitable for systematic analytics-driven evaluation.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,UNKNOWN,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
