AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01986,US_OMB_2025_01986,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Health and Human Services,Health and Medical,UNKNOWN,MedWatch Dashboard,Department of Health and Human Services; HHS/FDA/CDER; Health and Medical; United States,Identify product risk signals from MedWatch reports by using time series analysis to flag products and topic modeling to summarize the comments.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Assist with consistent monitoring and identification of product risks from MedWatch reporting patterns and report content to support review staff in detecting potential safety problems that could affect patients.,Need to proactively identify emerging issues and clusters within MedWatch reports using advanced analytics.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,UNKNOWN,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_01987,US_OMB_2025_01987,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Health and Human Services,Health and Medical,UNKNOWN,Quality Surveillance Dashboard (QSD),Department of Health and Human Services; HHS/FDA/CDER; Health and Medical; United States,Identifies and extracts keywords/phrases from unstructured documents and presents sentences containing keywords/phrases in context.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Extracts unstructured text from documents and pools that with other available data to form a dashboard that enables consistent assessment of Center for Drug Evaluation and Research (CDER) regulated manufacturing facilities, supporting FDA's oversight of drug quality.","Need for consistent, data-driven assessment of drug manufacturing facilities and proactive detection of potential quality signals that could indicate problems with drug safety or effectiveness.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,UNKNOWN,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
