AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02060,US_OMB_2025_02060,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Health and Human Services,Admin Functions,Manual identification of high-risk health centers is resource-intensive and may miss key indicators across large datasets.,"AI identification of ""High-Risk"" Health Centers",Department of Health and Human Services; HHS/HRSA; Admin Functions; United States,"The system would use predictive analytics and risk modeling to generate a prioritized list of health centers considered ""high-risk"" based on predefined indicators (e.g., patient safety concerns, poor quality metrics, application anomalies). Outputs will support more targeted oversight and TA deployment schedules.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"AI-driven risk identification would allow BPHC to better allocate resources, prioritize site visits, and provide tailored technical assistance. This will help improve compliance, operational performance, and ultimately the quality of care delivered by health centers","Manual identification of high-risk health centers is resource-intensive and may miss key indicators across large datasets. Would support a proactive, data-driven approach to inform site visit schedules and technical assistance planning.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,UNKNOWN,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02061,US_OMB_2025_02061,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Health and Human Services,Health and Medical,UNKNOWN,Targeted Technical Assistance,Department of Health and Human Services; HHS/HRSA; Health and Medical; United States,Outputs will be: 1. List of health centers requiring TA on specific clinical topics (in alignment with MAHA) 2. More focused ROI by implementing the specific TA identified through the process,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,This will lead to better quality of care and improve health outcomes for patients. At the same time this will reduce costs and staff burnout and increase patient satisfaction with their care,AI will help identify the health centers/ geographic areas that will benefit the most from targeted technical assistance on clinical topics for improving quality metrics,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,UNKNOWN,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
