AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02105,US_OMB_2025_02105,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Health and Human Services,Admin Functions,UNKNOWN,Study Section Clustering Tool (SSCT),Department of Health and Human Services; HHS/NIH; Admin Functions; United States,"The AI system’s outputs are lists of study sections grouped together based on the scientific similarity of grant application texts. Specifically, it generates clusters of applications that should be reviewed collectively because they share related scientific topics. These groupings serve as recommendations to subject matter experts, who use them to finalize the organization of study sections for peer review panels.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"The Study Section Clustering Tool (SSCT) enhances the agency’s mission by automating and streamlining the organization of grant applications into scientifically relevant study sections, improving efficiency and reducing manual effort. It ensures applications are reviewed by experts with appropriate expertise, adapting over time to changes in scientific fields through periodic model updates. This data-driven support leads to higher-quality peer review processes, promoting more effective research funding decisions",Efficiently organizing grant applications into appropriate study sections based on scientific similarity.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,UNKNOWN,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
