AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02129,US_OMB_2025_02129,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Health and Human Services,Admin Functions,UNKNOWN,NIGMS Azure Open AI,Department of Health and Human Services; HHS/NIH; Admin Functions; United States,Input: Text from various components of NIH grant applications. Output: Open AI chat completions (text) or text embeddings (vectors of numbers).,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"We are using large language models (LLMs), in particular Open AI's models, for business process improvement. We have used these models for visualization of a grant portfolios as well as numerous classification problems: IC prediction, clinical trial prediction, research area prediction, etc. These models allow us to classify documents through simple prompt engineering rather than the laborious process of creating a custom training set from scratch. These models also allow us to reduce the number of applications that humans need to review from tens of thousands of applications to mere hundreds or fewer for a number of tasks.","There are a number of situations in which administrative activities can be augmented by generative AI, especially when classification of documents is needed but no training data exist.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,UNKNOWN,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
