AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02142,US_OMB_2025_02142,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Health and Human Services,Admin Functions,UNKNOWN,Detection/Identification of Reviewer Expertise and Grant Application Content,Department of Health and Human Services; HHS/NIH; Admin Functions; United States,"The AI system’s outputs are classifications or labels indicating whether a grant application involves specific content areas (e.g., pediatric or other domains) and assessments of reviewer expertise based on biosketches, publications, and related data. These outputs are used to support accurate matching between applications and qualified reviewers.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"The tool is expected to enhance the agency’s mission by improving the accuracy, fairness, and efficiency of processes such as reviewer assignment and grant application analysis. By automating the detection of relevant content and expertise, it reduces manual workload, ensures better alignment between reviewers and applications, and supports more informed decision-making. This leads to more equitable and effective funding outcomes, ultimately benefiting the general public through improved support for research and programs that address critical needs.","The AI is designed to detect and identify grant application content and reviewer expertise such as pediatric or other domains to support accurate matching and more efficient, informed decision-making",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,UNKNOWN,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02143,US_OMB_2025_02143,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Health and Human Services,Science,UNKNOWN,Detection of AI-Generated Reviewer Critiques,Department of Health and Human Services; HHS/NIH; Science; United States,This tool outputs classifications of whether the reviewer critique was likely produced by Generative AI or not.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,NIH policy mandates that reviewers produce independent analyses of grant applications based on their expertise and knowledge. The use of genAI to produce a written critique of a grant application is in violation of NIH policy and fails to provide an independent assessment of the application.,"This tool detects if a given written critique was generated by AI tools, such as large language models (LLMs), as the reviewers are not allowed to write their critiques using these AI assistants. Flagged critiques are examined by NIH staff and discussed with the reviewers.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,UNKNOWN,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02144,US_OMB_2025_02144,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Health and Human Services,Admin Functions,The AI tool addresses the challenge of efficiently and consistently processing incoming study PDFs by automatically extracting key information needed for grant review workflows.,MirBot,Department of Health and Human Services; HHS/NIH; Admin Functions; United States,"The system produces an indexed and preprocessed version of each submitted PDF, enabling context-aware question-answering by the AI. A predefined set of questions is automatically asked to extract relevant information from the document, which is then used to populate the grant prior approval review form details for the associated study.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"The AI tool helps maintain continuity in the grant review process by ensuring consistent extraction and presentation of key study information, even as experienced staff retire or transition. This reduces the training burden on new team members and preserves institutional knowledge through standardized workflows.",The AI tool addresses the challenge of efficiently and consistently processing incoming study PDFs by automatically extracting key information needed for grant review workflows.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,UNKNOWN,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
