AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02207,US_OMB_2025_02207,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Housing and Urban Development,HR,"CAISY is designed to solve the challenge of helping employees practice and improve difficult workplace conversations in a safe, realistic environment.",CAISY - Workforce Training Conversation Simulator,Department of Housing and Urban Development; Office of the Chief Human Capital Officer; HR; United States,"Conversational responses generated by an LLM (Azure OpenAI) tailored to the scenario. Coaching feedback on AI Simulation scenarios Scenario-specific guidance Learner performance rating (non-PII, abstract user ID).",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"CAISY helps employees practice and receive real-time feedback on workplace conversations. It offers several real-world scenarios, allowing users to practice skills like resolving customer concerns, sharing constructive feedback, and leading difficult conversations, within a safe learning environment.","CAISY is designed to solve the challenge of helping employees practice and improve difficult workplace conversations in a safe, realistic environment.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,HUD-2025-004,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02208,US_OMB_2025_02208,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Housing and Urban Development,Admin Functions,UNKNOWN,Microsoft Copilot,Department of Housing and Urban Development; Office of the Chief Information Officer; Admin Functions; United States,"Generated files, including presentations, reports, analysis, and meeting minutes",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Microsoft Copilot will help with employee productivity by helping users draft documents, create summaries, generate data insights, and automate routine tasks. HUD will use Copilot to streamline workflows and automate repetitive activities within Microsoft apps.","To support the HUD Secretary's directive to improve efficiency, HUD has a need to offer office productivity tools and capabilities. This would include the ability to automate repetitive, manual, and time-consuming tasks, streamline processes, and analyze data and produce insights and recommendations.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,HUD-2025-001,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02209,US_OMB_2025_02209,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Archives and Records Administration,Other,UNKNOWN,Generative AI Solutions for Workplace Productivity (aka Gemini),National Archives and Records Administration; National Archives & Records Administration (NARA); Other; United States,"This AI solution will help with draft emails and documents, create images, analyze data, take meeting notes, and manage workflows.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"NARA is exploring how Generative AI tools can help employees work more efficiently and creatively. These AI tools can automate tasks, enhance communication and collaboration, and improve decision-making.","The AI is intended to improve employee productivity by providing smarter tools for employees to summarize, draft, and navigate operational records.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NARA - 0001,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02210,US_OMB_2025_02210,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Archives and Records Administration,Other,UNKNOWN,A1 Museum AI Project,National Archives and Records Administration; National Archives & Records Administration (NARA); Other; United States,This AI use provides enhanced visitor access to NARA records through an easy-to-use interface that identifies NARA records based on visitor responses to a chatbot conversation.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"NARA will use AI generated tags and topics to recommend and make records available to visitors from a pool of approximately 2 million digital records, freeing up staff time and enhancing and personalizing the user experience for A1 museum visitors.",The AI is intended to solve the problem of limited document discoverability and intensive manual labor by using automated tagging to personalize the visitor experience and make millions of digital records instantly accessible.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NARA - 0002,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02211,US_OMB_2025_02211,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Archives and Records Administration,Other,"The AI is intended to solve the problem of inefficient employee information discovery by replacing outdated keyword search with a natural language system that provides instant, context-aware answers from disparate agency resources.",NARA@WORK Kendra Search,National Archives and Records Administration; National Archives & Records Administration (NARA); Other; United States,"This AI-powered tool will drive significant productivity gains across the agency by enabling staff to find critical information faster and more efficiently. By utilizing contextual retrieval and ""Suggested Answers,"" the system ensures higher quality and more accurate results compared to traditional search methods.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"NARA is implementing an AI-driven contextual information retrieval tool (e.g., Amazon Kendra) to modernize search functionality on the NARA@Work internal site. This will enable staff to use Natural Language Processing (NLP) to query a wide range of agency information (Work Life, Benefits, Policies, etc.) and receive ""Suggested Answers.""","The AI is intended to solve the problem of inefficient employee information discovery by replacing outdated keyword search with a natural language system that provides instant, context-aware answers from disparate agency resources.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NARA - 0003,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02212,US_OMB_2025_02212,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Archives and Records Administration,Other,UNKNOWN,Amelia Earhart AI Search,National Archives and Records Administration; National Archives & Records Administration (NARA); Other; United States,"This AI system's outputs will go beyond traditional keyword retrieval to identify, connect, and surface all relevant Amelia Earhart records, including contextual details about her final trip, thus providing researchers with better search results and showing connections between disparate records, making the overall research process easier and more insightful.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"The intended purpose of this AI Proof of Concept (POC) is to efficiently retrieve and prepare for release all government records related to Amelia Earhart and her final trip, following the Presidential directive of September 26, 2025. The expected benefit is to leverage Natural Language Processing (NLP) search capabilities to overcome the limitations of traditional search methods, enabling the National Archives to effectively and accurately locate the necessary results from vast holdings and fulfill its legal mandate to make these specific historical records accessible to the American public.",The AI is intended to solve the manual search limitations when processing massive historical datasets by using Natural Language Processing to accurately locate and declassify specific records required for public release,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NARA - 0004,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02213,US_OMB_2025_02213,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Archives and Records Administration,Other,The AI is intended to solve the problem of manual processing bottlenecks and privacy risks by automating the identification and redaction of sensitive personal information within massive digitized collections to ensure safe and rapid public access.,AI Pilot Project to Screen and Flag for Personally Identifiable Information (PII) in Digitized Archival Records,National Archives and Records Administration; National Archives & Records Administration (NARA); Other; United States,"This AI use case will produce redacted records, a prioritized list for redaction, and a tool for staff to redact unpublished records.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"NARA is using AI to automatically find and remove sensitive personal information from its digitized historical records. This will make the process faster, more accurate, and better protect privacy while allowing for greater public access to these records. The AI will also help NARA manage its vast collection and adapt to future privacy needs.",The AI is intended to solve the problem of manual processing bottlenecks and privacy risks by automating the identification and redaction of sensitive personal information within massive digitized collections to ensure safe and rapid public access.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NARA - 0005,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02214,US_OMB_2025_02214,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Archives and Records Administration,Other,UNKNOWN,AI based Semantic Search for National Archives Catalog (aka ArchiAI),National Archives and Records Administration; National Archives & Records Administration (NARA); Other; United States,"This AI search tool will provide better search results and show connections between records, making research easier and more insightful.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"NARA is using AI to create a smarter search engine for its online catalog. This new search understands the meaning behind your search, not just the keywords, and can even find hidden connections between documents. This will make research faster, easier, and more insightful.","The AI is intended to solve the problem of ""unsophisticated"" keyword-based search limitations by implementing semantic search that understands user intent and historical context, allowing researchers to find relevant records even when they don't match exact search terms.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NARA - 0006,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02215,US_OMB_2025_02215,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Archives and Records Administration,Other,"The AI is intended to solve the problem of the ""descriptive gap"" created by labor-intensive manual cataloging by automatically generating metadata and summaries from document content, allowing NARA to process massive backlogs and make millions of records instantly searchable for the public.",Auto-fill of Descriptive Metadata for Archival Descriptions,National Archives and Records Administration; National Archives & Records Administration (NARA); Other; United States,"This AI use case will create more complete and informative descriptions for records, making them easier to find in the National Archives Catalog.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"NARA is using AI to automatically create descriptions (metadata) for its digital archives. This will save archivists time, make records easier to find, and help the public better understand the information in the National Archives Catalog.","The AI is intended to solve the problem of the ""descriptive gap"" created by labor-intensive manual cataloging by automatically generating metadata and summaries from document content, allowing NARA to process massive backlogs and make millions of records instantly searchable for the public.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NARA - 0007,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02216,US_OMB_2025_02216,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Archives and Records Administration,Other,"The AI is intended to solve the problem of unsearchable digital collections caused by massive descriptive backlogs, automating the creation of metadata for billions of digital objects to ensure they are immediately discoverable and understandable for the public without years of manual archival processing.",Topic Summarizer and Entity Extraction using AI,National Archives and Records Administration; National Archives & Records Administration (NARA); Other; United States,This AI use case will output enriched metadata making NARA's digital assets more accessible and easier to manage.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,NARA plans to use AI to automatically create descriptions for its digital objects. This will free up archivists' time and make it easier for people to find and understand the digital materials in NARA's system.,"The AI is intended to solve the problem of unsearchable digital collections caused by massive descriptive backlogs, automating the creation of metadata for billions of digital objects to ensure they are immediately discoverable and understandable for the public without years of manual archival processing.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NARA - 0008,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02217,US_OMB_2025_02217,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Archives and Records Administration,Other,UNKNOWN,Create an AI based knowledge articles user interface for working with CRG documents,National Archives and Records Administration; National Archives & Records Administration (NARA); Other; United States,This AI tool will give NPRC staff a user-friendly way to quickly find information in the CRG knowledge base.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"NARA is developing an AI-powered tool to help its National Personnel Records Center (NPRC) staff quickly find information in their Case Reference Guide (CRG). This will improve the speed and accuracy of their work, leading to better customer service and less time spent training new employees.","The AI is intended to improve the case processing by providing staff with an automated retrieval tool that navigates the complex Case Reference Guide to deliver instant, accurate answers for veteran and personnel record requests.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NARA - 0009,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02218,US_OMB_2025_02218,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Archives and Records Administration,Other,The AI is intended to solve the problem of inefficient information retrieval within Presidential email archives by testing whether AI-driven semantic search can understand context and intent more effectively than traditional keyword matching to improve record accessibility.,EOP 42 Search PoC using AI Based Semantic Search,National Archives and Records Administration; National Archives & Records Administration (NARA); Other; United States,"The AI system's output will be significantly improved search results that are contextually relevant (semantic), effectively bypassing the limitations of simple keyword matching within EOP 42 digital records, thereby offering a demonstrable improvement in the search experience for users accessing materials, including complex email archives.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"The purpose of this Proof of Concept (POC) is to evaluate whether AI-driven semantic search provides a demonstrable improvement over the current keyword-based search experience for accessing EOP 42 digital records, including email archives.",The AI is intended to solve the problem of inefficient information retrieval within Presidential email archives by testing whether AI-driven semantic search can understand context and intent more effectively than traditional keyword matching to improve record accessibility.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NARA - 0010,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02219,US_OMB_2025_02219,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Archives and Records Administration,Other,"The AI is intended to solve the problem of larger FOIA backlogs and manual review bottlenecks by automating the discovery of relevant records and the redaction of sensitive data, ensuring responses are both rapid and compliant with privacy laws.",Freedom of Information Act (FOIA) Discovery AI Pilot,National Archives and Records Administration; National Archives & Records Administration (NARA); Other; United States,This AI use case will output relevant records matching FOIA requests and redacted versions of those records with sensitive information removed.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"NARA is piloting the use of AI to improve its responses to Freedom of Information Act requests. This includes AI tools for finding relevant records and automatically redacting sensitive information, which will make the process faster, more accurate, and compliant with privacy laws.","The AI is intended to solve the problem of larger FOIA backlogs and manual review bottlenecks by automating the discovery of relevant records and the redaction of sensitive data, ensuring responses are both rapid and compliant with privacy laws.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NARA - 0011,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02220,US_OMB_2025_02220,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Archives and Records Administration,Other,"The AI is intended to solve the problem of ""unstructured data challenges"" in a vast, complex catalog by replacing traditional literal-match search with semantic technology that understands researcher intent, connects disparate records, and surfaces relevant results that would otherwise remain hidden behind inconsistent terminology.",Archives.gov AI search,National Archives and Records Administration; National Archives & Records Administration (NARA); Other; United States,"This AI search tool will provide better search results and show connections between records, making research easier and more insightful.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"NARA is using AI to create a smarter search engine for its online Archives.gov public site. This new search understands the meaning behind your search, not just the keywords, and can even find hidden connections between documents. This will make research faster, easier, and more insightful.","The AI is intended to solve the problem of ""unstructured data challenges"" in a vast, complex catalog by replacing traditional literal-match search with semantic technology that understands researcher intent, connects disparate records, and surfaces relevant results that would otherwise remain hidden behind inconsistent terminology.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,F04_UNSTRUCTURED_INFORMATION_COMPLEXITY,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NARA - 0012,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02221,US_OMB_2025_02221,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Archives and Records Administration,Other,UNKNOWN,Develop a Natural Language Based Chat Interface (like ChatGPT) to Interact With the Archival Documents,National Archives and Records Administration; National Archives & Records Administration (NARA); Other; United States,This AI will create a chat interface that lets users easily get information from NARA's archives by having a conversation with it.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"NARA plans to develop an AI-powered chat interface, similar to ChatGPT, that will allow users to easily explore its digital archives by asking questions in everyday language. This will make historical documents more accessible and engaging, leading to more efficient research and a deeper understanding of history.",The AI is intended to solve the problem of high barriers to entry for historical research by replacing complex database queries with a natural language interface that allows users of all skill levels to discover records and gain insights through simple conversation.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NARA - 0013,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02222,US_OMB_2025_02222,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Archives and Records Administration,Other,"The AI is intended to solve the problem of inefficient manual data governance and risk assessment by testing automated data classification techniques to organize unstructured datasets, accelerate information discovery, and more accurately identify potential security or privacy vulnerabilities.",Automated Data Discovery and Classification Pilot,National Archives and Records Administration; National Archives & Records Administration (NARA); Other; United States,"This AI pilot will categorize data, improve search, and potentially train AI to identify new document types.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"NARA plans to test how well AI can automatically organize and categorize its data. This pilot project will help NARA understand its data better, find information faster, improve efficiency, and manage risks more effectively.","The AI is intended to solve the problem of inefficient manual data governance and risk assessment by testing automated data classification techniques to organize unstructured datasets, accelerate information discovery, and more accurately identify potential security or privacy vulnerabilities.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK|F04_UNSTRUCTURED_INFORMATION_COMPLEXITY,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NARA - 0014,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02223,US_OMB_2025_02223,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Other (use other text field),UNKNOWN,Borescope Artificial Intelligence (BAI),National Aeronautics and Space Administration; AFRC: Armstrong Flight Research Center; Other (use other text field); United States,The system will output areas of potential engine damage to the user to evaluate,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Advanced borescopes would lead to an increased defect capture rate in less maintenance time, keeping engines on wing longer with more confidence in their health.",The BAI will aid jet engine maintainers in identifying compressor and turbine blade defects,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-498,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02224,US_OMB_2025_02224,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,UNKNOWN,Anomaly Detection and Precursor Identification in UAV flight data,National Aeronautics and Space Administration; ARC: Ames Research Center; Science; United States,previously-unknown anomalies and precursors to known issues in UAV (Unmanned Aerial Vehicle) test flights.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,This project is using past algorithms developed by the NASA ARC (Ames Research Center) Data Sciences Group and modifying them with application to identifying previously-unknown anomalies and precursors to known issues in UAV (Unmanned Aerial Vehicle) test flights.,This project is using past algorithms developed by the NASA ARC (Ames Research Center) Data Sciences Group and modifying them with application to identifying previously-unknown anomalies and precursors to known issues in UAV (Unmanned Aerial Vehicle) test flights.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-1,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02225,US_OMB_2025_02225,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Transportation,UNKNOWN,Autoresolver/Tailored Arrival Manager,National Aeronautics and Space Administration; ARC: Ames Research Center; Transportation; United States,autonomous air traffic management,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"The Autoresolver system is a tool for autonomous air traffic management. It is designed to perform many of the tasks that air-traffic controllers have historically performed including maintaining separation between aircraft, sequencing and scheduling aircraft across locations in space, and avoiding airspace volumes like weather systems and restricted airspace.","The Autoresolver system is a tool for autonomous air traffic management. It is designed to perform many of the tasks that air-traffic controllers have historically performed including maintaining separation between aircraft, sequencing and scheduling aircraft across locations in space, and avoiding airspace volumes like weather systems and restricted airspace.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-5,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02226,US_OMB_2025_02226,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,UNKNOWN,Deep Learning for Flood Mapping (DELTA),National Aeronautics and Space Administration; ARC: Ames Research Center; Science; United States,"monitor and map the impact of flood events to support preparedness, response, and critical decision making throughout the flood event lifecycle",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Remotely sensed imagery is increasingly used by emergency managers to monitor and map the impact of flood events to support preparedness, response, and critical decision making throughout the flood event lifecycle. To reduce latency in delivery of imagery-derived information, ensure consistent and reliably derived map products, and facilitate processing of an increasing volume of remote sensed data-streams, automated flood mapping workflows are needed. A joint USGS-NASA-Univ. Alabama initiative developed DELTA and applied it to automatic near-real time flood detection, using multiple sources of satellite imagery for use in disaster response.",DELTA simplifies machine learning for satellite imagery.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,RETIRED,종료,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-8,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02227,US_OMB_2025_02227,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,UNKNOWN,Distributed Spacecraft Autonomy,National Aeronautics and Space Administration; ARC: Ames Research Center; Science; United States,"DSA will demonstrate these capabilities in two contexts. The first context is a flight demonstration consisting of a software payload hosted on the Starling-1 small-spacecraft mission. This software payload will use the on-board GPS receiver to perform in-situ, swarm-level reconfiguration in response to observed features in the Topside Ionosphere. The second context is a scalability study, which shows how the technologies developed in the flight demonstration can scale to a large number of spacecraft (≈ 100). The scalability demonstration applies the tools developed for the flight mission to a hardware-in-the-loop simulation of the flight software payload.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Distributed Spacecraft Autonomy (DSA) is a project developed by the National Aeronautics and Space Administration that enables distributed spacecraft systems through the development of three capabilities: scalable communication, distributed coordination and planning, and human-swarm interaction. DSA will demonstrate these capabilities in two contexts. The first context is a flight demonstration consisting of a software payload hosted on the Starling-1 small-spacecraft mission. This software payload will use the on-board GPS receiver to perform in-situ, swarm-level reconfiguration in response to observed features in the Topside Ionosphere. The second context is a scalability study, which shows how the technologies developed in the flight demonstration can scale to a large number of spacecraft (≈ 100). The scalability demonstration applies the tools developed for the flight mission to a hardware-in-the-loop simulation of the flight software payload. Distributed Spacecraft Systems are a type of multi-spacecraft mission architecture that can not only provide improved resolution, coverage, and availability of existing missions, but also enable missions that would be previously infeasible using traditional approaches. Autonomy is a critical need for these systems, since the cost associated with applying conventional approaches for command and control does not scale with the number of spacecraft.","Distributed Spacecraft Autonomy (DSA) is a project developed by the National Aeronautics and Space Administration that enables distributed spacecraft systems through the development of three capabilities: scalable communication, distributed coordination and planning, and human-swarm interaction. DSA will demonstrate these capabilities in two contexts. The first context is a flight demonstration consisting of a software payload hosted on the Starling-1 small-spacecraft mission. This software payload will use the on-board GPS receiver to perform in-situ, swarm-level reconfiguration in response to observed features in the Topside Ionosphere. The second context is a scalability study, which shows how the technologies developed in the flight demonstration can scale to a large number of spacecraft (≈ 100). The scalability demonstration applies the tools developed for the flight mission to a hardware-in-the-loop simulation of the flight software payload.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-9,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02228,US_OMB_2025_02228,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,UNKNOWN,ExoMiner discovery of ExoPlanets via data from the Kepler and TESS space telescopes,National Aeronautics and Space Administration; ARC: Ames Research Center; Science; United States,ExoMiner produces scores between 0.0 and 1.0 for a number of possible categories relevant to transiting exoplanet searches.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,ExoMiner has been used to validated 370 new exoplanets identified in data from the Kepler space telescope. It is now being used to idenitify promising exoplanet candidates in TESS mission data. It promises to significantly reduce the manual effort required while improving the accuracy of identify promising TESS exoplanet candidates and to reject astrophysical false positives and instrumental false alarms.,ExoMiner is being used to statistically validate exoplanets detected by the Kepler space telescope and to identify promising exoplanet candidates for the TESS space telescope,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-10,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02229,US_OMB_2025_02229,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Transportation,UNKNOWN,Explainable and robust deep semi-supervised model for multi-class anomaly detection in flight data,National Aeronautics and Space Administration; ARC: Ames Research Center; Transportation; United States,anomaly detection,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"This model is a semi-supervised deep learning based anomaly detection for aircraft flight data. It is designed to work when a small subset of data is reviewed and labeled by experts. The most useful realm is where the size of labeled data is small, so that any supervised learning approach won't reach optimum performance.","This model is a semi-supervised deep learning based anomaly detection for aircraft flight data. It is designed to work when a small subset of data is reviewed and labeled by experts. The most useful realm is where the size of labeled data is small, so that any supervised learning approach won't reach optimum performance.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,S4_PREDICTION_DETECTION,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-11,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02230,US_OMB_2025_02230,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,UNKNOWN,Anomaly detection in aeronautics data with quantum-compatible discrete deep generative model,National Aeronautics and Space Administration; ARC: Ames Research Center; Science; United States,anomaly detection,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,This project enabled the additional development of two quantum-capable unsupervised deep-learning models with discrete latent space (Bernoulli and Boltzmann priors). The models exhibit state-of-the-art anomaly-detection performance and robustness. Future versions of our models will be deployed on in-time flight-operations data streams. They will also be used to assess the performance and resource requirements of quantum and other physical computing devices.,"Our team developed high-performance unsupervised deep machine-learning models for the detection of flight-operations anomalies. The models’ engineered-feature (latent) spaces are composed of discrete variables, which allows an integration with quantum computing because (part of) the latent-space variables can be populated by quantum-state measurements, which are discrete in nature.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-13,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02231,US_OMB_2025_02231,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Transportation,UNKNOWN,Machine Learning Airport Surface Model: Airport Configuration Prediction,National Aeronautics and Space Administration; ARC: Ames Research Center; Transportation; United States,The software is designed to point to databases which are not provided as part of the software release and thus this software is only intended to serve as an example of best practices.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"The software provides examples how to build three distinct pipelines for data query and save, data engineering, and data science. These pipelines enable scalable, repeatable, and maintainable development of ML models.",The ML-airport-configuration software is developed to provide a reference implementation to serve as a research example how to train and register Machine Learning (ML) models intended for predicting airport configurations.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-18,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
