AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02237,US_OMB_2025_02237,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Transportation,UNKNOWN,NextGen Advanced Methods: ATCSCC Webinar Speech2Text and Analysis,National Aeronautics and Space Administration; ARC: Ames Research Center; Transportation; United States,Text from speech to text and NLP of air traffic management content.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"The Advanced Methods project explores the use of innovative and emerging technologies to drive post operational analysis of Traffic Management for aircraft. Technologies such as machine learning, (ML), artificial intelligence (AI), and advanced data analytics for use in improving the FAA’s traffic flow management. In this specific use case, our aim is to use deep learning to convert live ATCSCC webinar meeting conversation to text, and then apply natural language processing to the converted text data for later analysis and review.","The Advanced Methods project explores the use of innovative and emerging technologies to drive post operational analysis of Traffic Management for aircraft. Technologies such as machine learning, (ML), artificial intelligence (AI), and advanced data analytics for use in improving the FAA’s traffic flow management. In this specific use case, our aim is to use deep learning to convert live ATCSCC webinar meeting conversation to text, and then apply natural language processing to the converted text data for later analysis and review.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-25,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02238,US_OMB_2025_02238,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Transportation,UNKNOWN,NextGen Data Analytics: Letters of Agreement,National Aeronautics and Space Administration; ARC: Ames Research Center; Transportation; United States,Test-based digitized SOPs and LOAs.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Providing LOAs or SOPs to stakeholders will enable flight planners (pilots and vendors) to study or ingest this information and thereby plan flight trajectories that remain consistent with air traffic constraints. It is also fundamental to Next Gen capabilities to share accurate data for purposes of creating new noise abatement procedures; improve NAS information for common situational awareness and alignment to implement new tools to assist in future time-based flow management.,"Today, operation constraints are documented via Standard Operating Procedures (SOP) and Letters of Agreement (LOA) and are not made available to the public in a consistent manner. SOPs are specific to an air traffic control facility and specify the procedures necessary for safe operation in the sector. LOA outline agreements establishing procedures and responsibilities between two parties (including crossing restrictions, holding patters, emergency procedure coordination, etc.) The LOA/SOPs are published internally as scanned PDFs and are the responsibility of the facility to maintain. To reduce the manual effort of tagging the documents for ease of reference, there is an opportunity to use modern data analytics and machine learning to produce and disseminate constraints in a standardized manner.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-26,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02239,US_OMB_2025_02239,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Transportation,UNKNOWN,Unsupervised anomaly detection in flight data with deep variational autoencoders,National Aeronautics and Space Administration; ARC: Ames Research Center; Transportation; United States,anomaly detection,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,It is currently tested and validated in finding anomaly detection in flight's operational quality assurance data from commerical aircraft.,This model is an unsupervised deep learning based anomaly detection for aircraft flight data based on variational autoencoders with convolutional architecture. The model is designed to find anomalies in multivaraite time-series and can work with heterogeneous data.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,S4_PREDICTION_DETECTION,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-33,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02240,US_OMB_2025_02240,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,UNKNOWN,Federated Learning Using In-Space Data (FLUID ),National Aeronautics and Space Administration; ARC: Ames Research Center; Science; United States,"For example, a neural net model to monitor lunar habitat astronauts for signs of lung toxicity due to regolith inhalation could be largely trained on Earth using similar data (e.g. data collected for volcanic ash inhaltion) and then fine-tuned with data generated in-situ on the lunar surface, without the need to transmit that data back to Earth. The FLUID arhitecture has been fully tested using the Spaceborne Computer-2 on board the ISS; in February of 2024, the world's first neural net model trained with both terrestrial and in-space data was successfully trained.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Enables neural net models to be trained using a combination of terrestrial data and space-borne data without the need to downlink or uplink data for consolidation and training in the normal manner. Instead, small components of the overall neural net model are trained in-situ with the data and transmitted for federation into a single neural net, thereby reducing data transmission demands and reducing overall latencies by several orders of magnitude.","Enables neural net models to be trained using a combination of terrestrial data and space-borne data without the need to downlink or uplink data for consolidation and training in the normal manner. Instead, small components of the overall neural net model are trained in-situ with the data and transmitted for federation into a single neural net, thereby reducing data transmission demands and reducing overall latencies by several orders of magnitude.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-404,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02241,US_OMB_2025_02241,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,UNKNOWN,Mapping Digital Infrastructure (MADI),National Aeronautics and Space Administration; ARC: Ames Research Center; Science; United States,CAS is also working to now validate the use of MADI in generating future scenarios and hypothetical trends that extend beyond the explicit semantic knowledge of the input sources.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"As CAS's Mapping and Synthesis teams work to identify transformational, wicked problems and potential solutions, MADI aims to supplement the information gathering and synthesis steps by clustering, theming, crawling, and summarizing publicly available data about emerging trends, needs, and capabilities.",The Mapping Digital Infrastructure (MADI) is a series of natural-language processing based tools that are designed to supplement the human-in-the-loop data exploration for CAS.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-405,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
