AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02251,US_OMB_2025_02251,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,UNKNOWN,Spaceport Throughput Analysis Resource,National Aeronautics and Space Administration; ARC: Ames Research Center; Science; United States,whether a set proposed launches and associated activities,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"The Spaceport Throughput Analysis Resource (STAR) assesses whether a set proposed launches and associated activities can be performed given the resources KSC currently has available, and external constraints imposed on KSC operations.","The Spaceport Throughput Analysis Resource (STAR) assesses whether a set proposed launches and associated activities can be performed given the resources KSC currently has available, and external constraints imposed on KSC operations.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-527,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02252,US_OMB_2025_02252,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,UNKNOWN,NASA-GPT: Retrieval-Augmented Generation using NTRS and more,National Aeronautics and Space Administration; ARC: Ames Research Center; Science; United States,answers,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"This use case is an example of Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), which roughly speaking is an AI-augmented form of search. It acts much like ChatGPT or one of the other services except that it also provides references.","This use case is an example of Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), which roughly speaking is an AI-augmented form of search. It acts much like ChatGPT or one of the other services except that it also provides references.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,S1_KNOWLEDGE_RETRIEVAL_RAG,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-537,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02253,US_OMB_2025_02253,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,UNKNOWN,Depth from Spectral Defocus for Lunar Regolith,National Aeronautics and Space Administration; ARC: Ames Research Center; Science; United States,3D model of a scene,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Our pipeline has shown success on synthetic lunar data sets taken with the Ames Imaging Module (NIRVSS-AIM) camera system.,Our technique reconstructs a 3D model of a scene based on images taken from a single viewpoint -- via estimating a depth map of a scene based on the defocus of different objects in captured images-- illuminated with light of different wavelengths. This pipeline has potential applications for 3D reconstruction on upcoming lunar missions carrying a multi-spectral imaging system as payload.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-703,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02254,US_OMB_2025_02254,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,UNKNOWN,Neural Scene Representations for Lunar Terrain Modeling,National Aeronautics and Space Administration; ARC: Ames Research Center; Science; United States,"Our LunarNRM generates shadow-controlled Digital Elevation Models (DEMs) of the lunar surface, enabling accurate modeling and relighting of largely shadowed regions such as craters in the lunar south pole.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"By integrating multi-sensor data from the Lunar Reconnaissance Orbiter (LRO)—specifically optical data from the Narrow Angle Camera (NAC) and altimeter data from the Lunar Orbiter Laser Altimeter (LOLA)—we have demonstrated that LunarNRM can effectively reconstruct these critical regions, directly supporting NASA’s Artemis campaign.","We have developed LunarNRM, a novel neural surface reconstruction algorithm based on Neural Radiance Fields (NeRFs) that incorporates shadow-aware and depth-aware methodologies.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-704,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02255,US_OMB_2025_02255,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,"We developed a data augmentation pipeline to enhance the training of vision-based navigation models for robotics, addressing the challenges of limited real-world data.",Data Augmentation Pipeline for Zero-Shot Sim-to-Real Transfer in Vision-Based Robot Navigation,National Aeronautics and Space Administration; ARC: Ames Research Center; Science; United States,"realistic, labeled images from synthetic data",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"By combining foundation model-based segmentation with CycleGAN for sim-to-real style transfer, our approach generates realistic, labeled images from synthetic data, enabling models to better generalize to real-world environments. This innovative capability enhances vision-based navigation tasks, such as vehicle pose estimation and road segmentation, significantly closing the sim-to-real gap in robotic perception applications.","We developed a data augmentation pipeline to enhance the training of vision-based navigation models for robotics, addressing the challenges of limited real-world data.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-705,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02256,US_OMB_2025_02256,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,UNKNOWN,Safe Autonomous Taxiing with Vision-Based Navigation,National Aeronautics and Space Administration; ARC: Ames Research Center; Science; United States,"We developed both a physical rover for real-world testing and a simulator in Unreal Engine with a realistic NASA Ames campus model for extensive, simulation-based validation.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"TaxiNet is a vision-based deep learning model developed to enable autonomous vehicles to follow a designated line safely during aircraft taxiing, a crucial application for assured autonomy research. This project’s goal is to demonstrate safe, closed-loop control using neural network perception from camera images, focusing on meeting rigorous safety standards for learning-enabled components (LECs) in safety-critical contexts.","TaxiNet is a vision-based deep learning model developed to enable autonomous vehicles to follow a designated line safely during aircraft taxiing, a crucial application for assured autonomy research. This project’s goal is to demonstrate safe, closed-loop control using neural network perception from camera images, focusing on meeting rigorous safety standards for learning-enabled components (LECs) in safety-critical contexts.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-706,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02257,US_OMB_2025_02257,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research"", ""social_nonprofit""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Health and Medical,UNKNOWN,Space Precision Health Foundation Model,National Aeronautics and Space Administration; ARC: Ames Research Center; Health and Medical; United States,"This system will be able to generate predictions related to space precision health. For example, it could predict possible drug targets or cellular states.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,These models developed will enable the scientific community to better understand how biological systems respond to spaceflight stressors and inform mission planners.,This project aims to leverage data available within the NASA Open Science Data Repository to train a model or set of models that can predict patterns related space health outcomes.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-764,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02258,US_OMB_2025_02258,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,UNKNOWN,ATLAS,National Aeronautics and Space Administration; GISS: Goddard Institute for Space Studies; Science; United States,"answering questions about NASA standards, directives, and Space Act Agreements",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,The framework developed for this may be applied to other high interest data sets.,"Atlas is a RAG-based solution for answering questions about NASA standards, directives, and Space Act Agreements. It uses publicly available NASA standards, directives and Space Ac Agreements. Users ask questions to Atlas which then fines relevant excerpts from the corpus of NASA public data in order to provide answers.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,S1_KNOWLEDGE_RETRIEVAL_RAG,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-535,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02259,US_OMB_2025_02259,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,UNKNOWN,Aero-Engines AI - a machine-learning app for aircraft engine system-performance prediction,National Aeronautics and Space Administration; GRC: Glenn Research Center; Science; United States,"Predicting engine TSFC, engine weight, core size, and turbomachinery stage counts",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Aero-Engines AI is an easy-to-use and a time-saving tool for aircraft engine design-space exploration during the conceptual design stage.,Aero-Engines AI is a Windows app that deploys machine-learning analytics to predict aircraft engine performance.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-35,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02260,US_OMB_2025_02260,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,UNKNOWN,Graph Neural Networks for Airfoil Performance Prediction,National Aeronautics and Space Administration; GRC: Glenn Research Center; Science; United States,Predictions of blade loss,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,The impact is we have a new type of neural network architecture that we can potentially use for other projects.,"We are investigating the use of Graph Convolutional Neural Networks to learn relationship between airfoil coordinates and predict the performance for aerodynamics analysis. Inputs include the shape of the airfoil and outputs are the coefficient of lift, drag, and moment.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-40,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02261,US_OMB_2025_02261,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,UNKNOWN,Inverse Design of Materials,National Aeronautics and Space Administration; GRC: Glenn Research Center; Science; United States,"Outputs include recipes and approaches for new materials custom-tailored to applications with an 4x speedup for the overall materials discovery / design lifecycle, and potential 10x throughput for the same cycle based on parallizing discovery of multiple materials at once.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"The project is currently being utilized in an NESC investigation to improve SLS core stage weld quality. The technology will be used to select experiments for a fully autonomous robotic lab that is currently being procured to design better insulating materials for electrified aircraft. Bayesian optimization frameworks predicts the next best simulation to run to minimize a target. For the PMC example, for instance, the objective was to minimize weight while maintaining a minimum margin of safety.","Discovering new materials is typically a mix of art and science, with timelines to create and robustly test a new material mix / manufacturing method ranging from ten to twenty years. This project seeks to enable rapid discovery, optimization, qualifaction and deployment of fit-for-purpose materials.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-41,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02262,US_OMB_2025_02262,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,UNKNOWN,MADI - Strategic Foresight and Knowledge Management infrastructure for ARMD/TACP/CAS,National Aeronautics and Space Administration; GRC: Glenn Research Center; Science; United States,Recommendations and associations as natural language output.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"A digital infrastructure would enable a curated problem database. It is essential to minimize rework due to not being able to find previous data, information, and analyses and having to repeat past work. This type of infrastructure would be adaptable to other innovation areas at NASA, especially those that are working in “problem space” rather than technology development space. In addition MADI is able to speculate on futures and generate scenarios. MADI is also able to provide recombinant innovation support to identify ways to use archived technologies and proposals in new ways.","The CAS Discovery team is developing, testing and using digital infrastructure to meet the pace of expected deliverables in an automated, efficient, collaborative manner, including taking advantage of AI/ML capabilities.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-42,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02263,US_OMB_2025_02263,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,UNKNOWN,Pre-trained microscopy image neural network encoders,National Aeronautics and Space Administration; GRC: Glenn Research Center; Science; United States,Automatically segment microscopy features given limited annotated microscopy images.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"When deployed in downstream microscopy tasks through transfer learning, encoders pre-trained on MicroNet outperform ImageNet encoders. These pre-trained MicroNet encoders have been successfully deployed for semantic segmentation, instance segmentation, and regression tasks.","Convolutional Neural Network encoders were trained on over 100,000 microscopy images of materials.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-401,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02264,US_OMB_2025_02264,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,UNKNOWN,Surrogate Models for Efficient Multiscale Modeling of Composite Materials,National Aeronautics and Space Administration; GRC: Glenn Research Center; Science; United States,Predict constitutive behavior as a function of material properties and applied strain.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Surrogate models are attractive because they can be evaluated many orders of magnitude faster than physics-based models and with a high degree of accuracy. Such models can be used for efficient multiscale modeling, design optimization, Monte Carlo methods, and optimal experimental design in ways that would be intractable with many physics-based models.",A custom neural network architecture containing graph convolutional network (GCN) and long short-term memory (LSTM) layers was trained as a computationally efficient surrogate for a physics-based composite modeling simulation.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-402,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
