AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02269,US_OMB_2025_02269,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,UNKNOWN,Creating U-Net + LSTM Hybrid Architecture for Image Series Analysis,National Aeronautics and Space Administration; GSFC: Goddard Space Flight Center; Science; United States,Predictions,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Creating U-Net + LSTM Hybrid Architecture for Image Series Analysis,This work focuses on creating U-Net + long short-term memory Hybrid analysis architectures for image series analysis on solar image data.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-89,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02270,US_OMB_2025_02270,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,"The objective of this project is to investigate the feasibility of applying deep-learning algorithms to communication-limited spacecraft, an operational domain where a slow, restricted, or intermittent downlink bottleneck inhibits the generation of large training datasets on the ground.",Deep Learning for Communication-Limited Spacecraft,National Aeronautics and Space Administration; GSFC: Goddard Space Flight Center; Science; United States,Predictions,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Deep Learning for Communication-Limited Spacecraft,"The objective of this project is to investigate the feasibility of applying deep-learning algorithms to communication-limited spacecraft, an operational domain where a slow, restricted, or intermittent downlink bottleneck inhibits the generation of large training datasets on the ground. With novel complex sensors generating ever-increasing amounts of data, it is imperative to be able to autonomously and robustly classify scientifically useful data to maximize scientific utility per bit transmitted to the ground. This project studies two classification approaches, including supervised transfer learning and unsupervised feature extraction followed by clustering, to optimize selection of data products for download.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-93,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
