AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02272,US_OMB_2025_02272,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,UNKNOWN,Earth Information System Fire Pilot,National Aeronautics and Space Administration; GSFC: Goddard Space Flight Center; Science; United States,Predictions,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Earth Information System Fire Pilot,"EIS-Fire developed a visualization and analysis data portal providing access to a variety of fire data products in a cloud-optimized, analysis-ready format. The team also developed an algorithm for mapping active fire perimeters from satellite fire detections and updated the representation of fire emissions in the Goddard Earth Observing System (GEOS) model to use improved Visible Infrared Imaging Radiometer Suite (VIIRS) fire data. Finally, EIS-Fire engaged stakeholders in identifying use cases to inform data portal development.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-100,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
