AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02294,US_OMB_2025_02294,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,UNKNOWN,Semi-Automatic Landslide Detection (SALaD),National Aeronautics and Space Administration; GSFC: Goddard Space Flight Center; Science; United States,Predictions,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Semi-Automatic Landslide Detection (SALaD),"Semi-Automatic Landslide Detection (SALaD). NASA's Semi-Automatic Landslide Detection (SALaD) system combines three leading-edge technologies: open-source Python packages and modules, object-based image analysis (OBIA), and machine learning (ML).",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-189,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02295,US_OMB_2025_02295,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,UNKNOWN,SpectraClass: Semi-supervised learning in a Jupyter Notebook,National Aeronautics and Space Administration; GSFC: Goddard Space Flight Center; Science; United States,"We have chosen, as a science driver for the initial stage of development, the development of innovative semi-supervised machine learning methods for landscape classification using hyperspectral imagery.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,It provides an extendable interface and toolsuite which can be used to jumpstart the development of novel methods for addressing a wide range of data analysis challenges in both the earth and space sciences.,This is a workbench supporting interactive visual data analysis of sensor data.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-192,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02296,US_OMB_2025_02296,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,UNKNOWN,"SWaP-efficient, fast-wavelength-steering and time-division-multiplexing lidar technology capable of multi-beam ranging and concurrent hyper-spectral imaging",National Aeronautics and Space Administration; GSFC: Goddard Space Flight Center; Science; United States,Predictions,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"A groundbreaking lidar module consisting of a high-pulse-rate, fast-wavelength-tuning fiber laser and time-division-multiplexing receiver will make height measurements using 60 steerable beams with drastically increased efficiency compared to the state-of-the-art. Concurrent hyperspectral imaging will greatly enhance science capabilities and real-time, AI neural network analysis of the images will enable optimized data collection and on-board processing. Incorporating these multiple emerging technologies will substantially reduce instrument size, weight and power thereby enabling lower-cost SmallSat-class missions with enhanced scientific return compared to the present day","We propose to integrate next-generation lidar, compact hyperspectral imaging and Artificial Intelligence (AI) technologies to provide a new remote sensing measurement capability for a broad range of Earth and planetary science objectives.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-198,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02297,US_OMB_2025_02297,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,UNKNOWN,Toward Resilient Spacecraft: Artificially Intelligent Reasoning for Diagnosing Safe Modes,National Aeronautics and Space Administration; GSFC: Goddard Space Flight Center; Science; United States,The framework will leverage classification systems such as Neural Networks (NN) and various uncertainty processing methods such as Dempster–Shafer theory (DST) to make use of low level data as a way to inform higher level reasoning system to generate on-board information at an abstract level which is human readable.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"We will look specifically at implementing our proof-of-concept as a way to diagnose spacecraft safe-mode events, in an attempt to disambiguate non-urgent anomalous safe mode events from more urgent safe-mode events which require a sunward burn maneuver.","This research will develop a proof-of-concept prototype for an intelligent and explainable reasoning system on-board, which is capable of diagnosis and decision making in real-time.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-201,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
