AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02515,US_OMB_2025_02515,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,UNKNOWN,SCOTI (Scientific Captioning of Terrain Images),National Aeronautics and Space Administration; JPL: Jet Propulsion Laboratory; Science; United States,natural language explanations of geological images taken by rovers,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,SCOTI provides onboard data summarization thar would help the ground operation to selectively downlink high priority data under data bandwidth constraint.,"SCOTI (Scientific Captioning of Terrain Images) automatically generates natural language explanations of geological images taken by rovers. It uses ""show-attend-tell"" model consisting of CNN (Convolutional Neural Network) and LSTM (Long Short Term Memory), trained by scientist-genarated labels on MSL images.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-241,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02516,US_OMB_2025_02516,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,UNKNOWN,SPOC (Soil Property and Object Classification),National Aeronautics and Space Administration; JPL: Jet Propulsion Laboratory; Science; United States,"Terrain image classifications such as soil, sand, rock, etc.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,This ability enables rover to drive more safely.,"Using a convolutional neural network (CNN), SPOC (Soil Property and Object Classification) takes rover images and classifies the terrain type (e.g., sand, soil) from visual appearance.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-244,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02517,US_OMB_2025_02517,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,UNKNOWN,Trusted and exPlainable Artificial Intelligence for Saving Lives (TruePAL) Technology for First Responder Safety,National Aeronautics and Space Administration; JPL: Jet Propulsion Laboratory; Science; United States,timely warning to drivers and roadside crews to avoid crashes,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Fatalities caused by emergency vehicle collisions are 4.8 times higher for emergency responders than the national average. The Trusted and exPlainable Artificial Intelligence for Saving Lives (TruePAL) project was funded by DOT to study the AI technology for saving first responders and roadside crews lives in and around active traffic. The TruePAL, an AI assistant, provides real-time warning of risks by analyzing the environment and traffic patterns to generate timely warning to drivers and roadside crews to avoid crashes. A deep neural network (DNN) is developed to detect and track vehicles, pedestrians, traffics signs, etc., and a Non-Axiomatic Reasoning System (NARS) to analyze the risk and provide prioritized warning messages. A mobile app with AI interface is developed to perform verbal communication with the first responders. The TruePAL AI assistant demonstrated real-time crash warning and human factor design capabilities using a CARLA simulator. The TruePAL project has developed cutting-edge AI tools: a Human-machine AI interface has potential to save lives for first responders and roadside crews.","Fatalities caused by emergency vehicle collisions are 4.8 times higher for emergency responders than the national average. The Trusted and exPlainable Artificial Intelligence for Saving Lives (TruePAL) project was funded by DOT to study the AI technology for saving first responders and roadside crews lives in and around active traffic. The TruePAL, an AI assistant, provides real-time warning of risks by analyzing the environment and traffic patterns to generate timely warning to drivers and roadside crews to avoid crashes. A deep neural network (DNN) is developed to detect and track vehicles, pedestrians, traffics signs, etc., and a Non-Axiomatic Reasoning System (NARS) to analyze the risk and provide prioritized warning messages. A mobile app with AI interface is developed to perform verbal communication with the first responders. The TruePAL AI assistant demonstrated real-time crash warning and human factor design capabilities using a CARLA simulator. The TruePAL project has developed cutting-edge AI tools: a Human-machine AI interface has potential to save lives for first responders and roadside crews.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-247,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02518,US_OMB_2025_02518,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN,Volcano SensorWeb,National Aeronautics and Space Administration; JPL: Jet Propulsion Laboratory; United States,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,RETIRED,종료,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-249,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02519,US_OMB_2025_02519,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,UNKNOWN,TAPAS (Track Augmentation and Performance Analysis System),National Aeronautics and Space Administration; JPL: Jet Propulsion Laboratory; Science; United States,anomalies,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"It has three autonomous functions: an automatic comparative analysis of a given track against a set of historical tracks, anomaly detection compared to a reference normal track, and statistical difference comparison between two given tracks. By using TAPAS, DSN operators can quickly identify discrepancies in the telemetry data and respond to them more effectively.","TAPAS is a tool for automating the comparison of DSN telemetry data, designed to help DSN operators find potential anomalies faster and more efficiently.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-449,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02520,US_OMB_2025_02520,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,UNKNOWN,Onboard Planner for Mars2020 Rover (Perseverance),National Aeronautics and Space Administration; JPL: Jet Propulsion Laboratory; Science; United States,"When considering each activity it computes the valid time intervals for placement, taking into account preheating, maintenance heating, and wake/sleep of the rover as required. After an activity is placed (other than a preheat/maintenance or wake/sleep), the activity is never reconsidered by the scheduler for deletion or moving. Therefore the scheduler can be considered non backtracking, and only searches in the sense that it computes valid timeline intervals for legal activity placement.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Research, experiments, and engineering to empower future rovers with onboard autonomy; planning, scheduling & execution; path planning; onboard science; image processing; terrain classification; fault diagnosis; and location estimation. This is a multi-faceted effort and includes experimentation and demonstrations on-site at JPL's simulated mars navigation yard.",The M2020 onboard scheduler incrementally constructs a feasible schedule by iterating through activities in priority-first order.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-450,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02521,US_OMB_2025_02521,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,UNKNOWN,"SensorWeb: Volcano, Flood, Wildfire, and others.",National Aeronautics and Space Administration; JPL: Jet Propulsion Laboratory; Science; United States,"Identification and labelling of terrain, climate and weather features",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"This system of systems is designed with a flexible, modular, architecture to facilitate expansion in sensors, customization of trigger conditions, and customization of responses. This system has been used to implement a global surveillance program to study volcanos. We have also run sensorweb tests to study flooding, cryosphere events, and atmospheric phenomena. Specifically, in our application, we use low resolution, high coverage sensors to trigger observations by high resolution instruments. Note that there are many other rationales to network sensors into a sensorweb. For example automated response might enable observation using complementary instruments such as imaging radar, infra-red, visible, etc. Or automated response might be used to apply more assets to increase the frequency of observation to improve the temporal resolution of available data. Our sensorweb project is being used to monitor the Earth's 50 most active volcanos. We have also run sensorweb experiments to monitor flooding, wildfires, and cryospheric events (snowfall and melt, lake freezing and thawing, sea ice formation and breakup.)",The Sensor Web Project uses a network of sensors linked by software and the internet to an autonomous satellite observation response capability.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-451,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02522,US_OMB_2025_02522,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,UNKNOWN,Mexec Onboard Planning and Execution,National Aeronautics and Space Administration; JPL: Jet Propulsion Laboratory; Science; United States,Activity Plan/Schedule,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Instead of command sequences, MEXEC works with task networks, which include abstract representations of command behavior, constraints on timing, and resources required and/or consumed by the behavior. Using this knowledge on-board, MEXEC can monitor command behavior and react to off-nominal outcomes (e.g. CPU reset), reconstructing command sequences to continue spacecraft operations without jeopardizing spacecraft safety.","MEXEC is a lightweight, multi-mission software for activity scheduling and execution developed to increase the autonomy and efficiency of a robotic explorer. MEXEC was first created as a prototype demonstration for the Europa Clipper project as a potential solution to fail-operational requirements.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-452,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02523,US_OMB_2025_02523,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,UNKNOWN,Requirement Alignment (REQAL),National Aeronautics and Space Administration; JPL: Jet Propulsion Laboratory; Science; United States,solicitations,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Use NLP and large language Model (LLM) such as GPT or BERT to encode experiences of the personnel into a knowledge graph. Then train a graph neural network (GNN) to automatically match solicitations to experts in the organization.,Use NLP and large language Model (LLM) such as GPT or BERT to encode experiences of the personnel into a knowledge graph. Then train a graph neural network (GNN) to automatically match solicitations to experts in the organization.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-454,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02524,US_OMB_2025_02524,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,UNKNOWN,"Robust, Explainable Autonomy for Scientific Icy Moon Operations (REASIMO)",National Aeronautics and Space Administration; JPL: Jet Propulsion Laboratory; Science; United States,"Specifically, we are developing autonomy for onboard mission use that could detect, diagnose, and respond appropriately to anomalies (faults, failures degradations, or unexpected conditions) without the need to always drop into safe mode and call home.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Specifically, we are developing autonomy for onboard mission use that could detect, diagnose, and respond appropriately to anomalies (faults, failures degradations, or unexpected conditions) without the need to always drop into safe mode and call home.",This effort aims to improve the science yield and robustness of a wide range of NASA missions by increasing the level of flight-qualifiable autonomy that can be applied to such operations.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-456,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
