AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02557,US_OMB_2025_02557,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,UNKNOWN,JSC SMA NT Paper WAD Data Extraction,National Aeronautics and Space Administration; JSC: Johnson Space Center; Science; United States,Information on scanned PDF documents.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,This application aims to provide the Quality Flight Equipment Division with a strong paper Work Authorization Document (WAD) data extraction capability using AI models. The data inputs include scanned PDF versions of original paper Work Authorization Documents (WADs) stored in the QFED data center. This application will be leveraging Google's Gemini Pro models to accomplish this effort. Users will be able to query critical quality-based information from large numbers of WADs to better understand Task Performance Sheet and Discrepancy Report execution trends and areas for improvement.,This application aims to provide the Quality Flight Equipment Division with a strong paper Work Authorization Document (WAD) data extraction capability using AI models. The data inputs include scanned PDF versions of original paper Work Authorization Documents (WADs) stored in the QFED data center. This application will be leveraging Google's Gemini Pro models to accomplish this effort. Users will be able to query critical quality-based information from large numbers of WADs to better understand Task Performance Sheet and Discrepancy Report execution trends and areas for improvement.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-791,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02558,US_OMB_2025_02558,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,UNKNOWN,Adaptive Neural Network Molecular Dynamics,National Aeronautics and Space Administration; LaRC: Langley Research Center; Science; United States,"The ANN gives optimized parameters for a predefined empirical function, known as bond-order-potential (BOP). Thus parameterized BOP function is then used to calculate the energy of an atom.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"ML approach, based on artificial neural networks (ANNs) is used in atomistic simulations to efficiently reproduce the very complex energy landscape resulting from the atomic interactions in materials with the accuracy of the more expensive quantum mechanics-based calculations.","ML approach, based on artificial neural networks (ANNs) is used in atomistic simulations to efficiently reproduce the very complex energy landscape resulting from the atomic interactions in materials with the accuracy of the more expensive quantum mechanics-based calculations.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-293,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
