AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02620,US_OMB_2025_02620,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,UNKNOWN,Solar Sail Shape Reconstruction,National Aeronautics and Space Administration; MSFC: Marshall Space Flight Center; Science; United States,"The predicted sail shape as described by several high-level parameters (e.g., boom tip deflection out of the sail plane).",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,The intended use of this model is to predict the shape of a solar sail in flight.,The intended use of this model is to predict the shape of a solar sail in flight.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-530,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02621,US_OMB_2025_02621,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,UNKNOWN,TxP: Artificial Intelligence for Curation (AI-Cure),National Aeronautics and Space Administration; MSFC: Marshall Space Flight Center; Science; United States,curated data,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"This will result in cost savings, faster data availability, improved data quality, and better support for NASA’s open science initiatives. This project enables NASA to advance data curation processes, accelerating scientific discovery while reducing manual effort and operational costs.",The AI-CURE project will integrate advanced AI and machine learning models to automate and standardize data curation across NASA’s SMD databases.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-718,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02622,US_OMB_2025_02622,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,UNKNOWN,Intelligent Chatbot for Science using Microsoft Copilot,National Aeronautics and Space Administration; MSFC: Marshall Space Flight Center; Science; United States,scientifically curated information,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"It uses Microsoft's Large Language model with scientifically curated information from NASA's VEDA (Visualization, Exploration, and Data Analysis) platform to assist users in search, discovery and analysis.","It uses Microsoft's Large Language model with scientifically curated information from NASA's VEDA (Visualization, Exploration, and Data Analysis) platform to assist users in search, discovery and analysis.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-723,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02623,US_OMB_2025_02623,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""social_nonprofit""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,"This includes addressing data challenges such as heterogeneity in spatial and temporal resolution, differences in data formats and calibration standards, and the significant lack of large, accurately labeled datasets (sparse ground truth) for supervised learning.",Foundation Model for Lunar Science,National Aeronautics and Space Administration; MSFC: Marshall Space Flight Center; Science; United States,"Foundation Model: Model that can be adapted for many different applications Representations: Rich, general-purpose, and robust representations of lunar surface features and spatial relationship",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"The LRO Foundation Model (FM) is useful because it offers key advantages over traditional ML: Generalization: It can learn general-purpose representations that generalize better across different tasks and even data from different instruments with minimal fine-tuning. Low-Data Regimes: It excels in transfer learning, allowing knowledge from pretraining on massive unlabeled datasets to be effectively applied to downstream tasks that only have limited labeled data. Efficiency: It significantly reduces the dependence on time-consuming manual data labeling by using self-supervised pretraining on vast amounts of unlabeled LRO data. Scientific Advancement: It enables understanding of lunar features by jointly analyzing multiple data modalities, leading to new scientific insights and supporting mission-critical activities like landing site selection.","The purpose of Lunar FM is to overcome the limitations of traditional, task-specific Machine Learning (ML) models in analyzing the vast, diverse, and long-term datasets collected by the Lunar Reconnaissance Orbiter (LRO) mission. This includes addressing data challenges such as heterogeneity in spatial and temporal resolution, differences in data formats and calibration standards, and the significant lack of large, accurately labeled datasets (sparse ground truth) for supervised learning.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-775,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02624,US_OMB_2025_02624,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,UNKNOWN,Adaptive State-Space Control via Neuromorphic Computing,National Aeronautics and Space Administration; MSFC: Marshall Space Flight Center; Science; United States,governing matrices of the control model,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"This use case addresses the limitations of traditional, fixed-logic control systems by implementing an adaptive state-space model on neuromorphic hardware. By representing a system's states and transitions as a network of spiking neurons and plastic synapses, the governing matrices of the control model are transformed from static constants into dynamic variables that evolve based on real-time sensory input and operational feedback. This enables the system to autonomously learn from its environment, optimize its own control logic, and adapt to unforeseen conditions, creating a foundation for truly intelligent and resilient autonomous systems in fields such as advanced robotics and aerospace.",Neuromorphic hardware for autonomous control logic adaptation in robotics/aerospace,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-920,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02625,US_OMB_2025_02625,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Aeronautics and Space Administration,Science,"NASA's Mission Control currently relies on a manual CHIT (Mission Action Request) system for real-time operational decisions, a process that places a high cognitive load on flight controllers who must complete forms, identify all stakeholders, and search historical data with basic tools, making it difficult to spot subtle trends.",AI-Enhanced Mission Operations Reporting & Decision Support System,National Aeronautics and Space Administration; MSFC: Marshall Space Flight Center; Science; United States,context-aware smart search results,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"The proposed solution would leverage Natural Language Processing (NLP) to enable controllers to initiate CHITs using plain language, while machine learning models would proactively analyze data to identify emerging trends and provide context-aware smart search results from historical mission data. Additionally, the AI would perform an initial automated impact assessment on new requests, flagging potential risks to enhance the speed and safety of decision-making.","NASA's Mission Control currently relies on a manual CHIT (Mission Action Request) system for real-time operational decisions, a process that places a high cognitive load on flight controllers who must complete forms, identify all stakeholders, and search historical data with basic tools, making it difficult to spot subtle trends. This use case proposes transforming this system by integrating an AI engine to streamline operations.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NASA-921,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
