AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02662,US_OMB_2025_02662,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Indian Gaming Commission,Admin Functions,UNKNOWN,Articulate,National Indian Gaming Commission; Admin Functions; United States,E-learning and online training content with intent on interactive courses through digital learning materials.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Efficiency,Assist trainers when creating and building out agency training modules.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NIGC-5,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02663,US_OMB_2025_02663,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Nuclear Regulatory Commission,Energy and Environment,"The process of discovery, retrieval, analysis, and cross-reference is time consuming and often represents the most significant bottleneck in carrying out agency activities and in making agency decisions.",Text Retrieval and Generation for NRC Staff Support,Nuclear Regulatory Commission; NRC; Energy and Environment; United States,"The output is semi-structured content (e.g., text and tables) responsive to the NRC staff's queries.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"This use case enhances the NRC’s efficiency and consistency in licensing, oversight, and other regulatory activities. It enables more efficient capture and use of institutional knowledge to mitigate against the risks associated with staff attrition. The NRC expects this use case to improve the timeliness of its risk- and policy-informed decisions, supporting its mission to enable the safe and secure use and deployment of civilian nuclear energy technologies and radioactive materials.","NRC staff are required to discover, retrieve, and analyze information from internally-managed and externally-provided documents. These documents can be lengthy as well as dense with content and often require cross-reference against multiple policies, standards, guidelines, and procedures. The process of discovery, retrieval, analysis, and cross-reference is time consuming and often represents the most significant bottleneck in carrying out agency activities and in making agency decisions.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NRC-0001,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02664,US_OMB_2025_02664,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Nuclear Regulatory Commission,Energy and Environment,"By reducing manual workload and error rates, they enable staff to focus on higher-value activities and improve overall productivity.",Support routine administrative tasks and enhancing communications,Nuclear Regulatory Commission; NRC; Energy and Environment; United States,"Structured content (e.g., text, tables, and images) responsive to the NRC staff's queries.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"AI improves agency efficiency, accuracy, and responsiveness by automating repetitive tasks, enhancing communication, and streamlining data analysis. These benefits free staff for higher-value work, accelerate decision-making, improve service delivery, and increase transparency, ultimately supporting the agency’s mission and strengthening public trust.","These AI use cases address inefficiencies in administrative workflows, such as scheduling, document drafting, and information retrieval. They help automate repetitive tasks, improve accuracy and accessibility of communications, streamline data analysis and reporting, prioritize service requests, and enhance cybersecurity. By reducing manual workload and error rates, they enable staff to focus on higher-value activities and improve overall productivity.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NRC-0002,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02665,US_OMB_2025_02665,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Nuclear Regulatory Commission,Energy and Environment,"The NRC faces challenges accessing, integrating, and securely managing multiple advanced AI models from different providers.","Unified, secure access to multiple advanced AI language models",Nuclear Regulatory Commission; NRC; Energy and Environment; United States,"The system outputs include natural language responses, document summaries, data analyses, and semantic embeddings generated by leading AI models.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"The service enables NRC staff to securely access top AI models, improving research, analysis, and decision-making efficiency. This accelerates regulatory reviews, enhances data-driven insights, reduces costs, and strengthens NRC’s ability to protect public health and safety through more effective oversight and communication with stakeholders.","The NRC faces challenges accessing, integrating, and securely managing multiple advanced AI models from different providers. This creates inefficiencies, increases costs, and complicates compliance with federal security standards. The service addresses these problems by providing a single, secure platform for accessing, evaluating, and managing leading AI models, streamlining adoption while ensuring compliance and operational efficiency.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NRC-0003,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02666,US_OMB_2025_02666,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Nuclear Regulatory Commission,Energy and Environment,UNKNOWN,Testing industry leading generative AI foundational large language models,Nuclear Regulatory Commission; NRC; Energy and Environment; United States,"The AI system produces draft text, summaries, outlines, and alternative wording for non-sensitive content, as well as explanatory responses to user prompts. Outputs are advisory and informational only and require human review; they are not authoritative, binding, or used for regulatory or safety decisions.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Improved staff understanding of generative AI capabilities and limitations; increased efficiency in drafting, summarizing, and organizing non-sensitive information; identification of appropriate use cases and risks; and informed development of policies, guidance, and governance for potential future AI use.","The AI is intended to address gaps in organizational understanding of how generative AI can support knowledge work. The sprint helps identify potential benefits, limitations, and risks of AI tools, enabling informed decisions on future use, governance, and policy before any deployment.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,NRC-0004,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02667,US_OMB_2025_02667,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""social_nonprofit""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Science Foundation,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN,Comparison of proposal similarities at different levels of National Science Foundation (NSF) organization,National Science Foundation; Directorate for Biological Sciences (BIO); United States,The embeddings are generated using sentence transformer models.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"The goal of the analysis is to compare how any two programs, divisions or , directorates in NSF are similar to each other to assess uniqueness and overlap between units. The comparison is based on a similarity score (cosine similarity) of the embeddings of any two proposal summaries. The embeddings are generated using sentence transformer models.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,56,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02668,US_OMB_2025_02668,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""social_nonprofit""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Science Foundation,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN,Budget Area Topic Classification Tool,National Science Foundation; Directorate for Computer and Information Science and Engineering (CISE); United States,"The Budget Area Topic Classification Tool uses a pre-trained Bidirectional Encoder Representations from Transformers (BERT) model ('bert-base-uncased') to classify proposals into 1 of 8 budget areas: Advanced Manufacturing, Artificial Intelligence, Advanced Wireless, Clean Energy, Microelectronics & Semiconductors, Quantum, or Trustworthy AI. Upon training the model to learn the multi-label structure of the underlying data, the model's accuracy and discriminatory power was tested using a hold-out sample (i.e., 80/20 split).",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"The Budget Area Topic Classification Tool uses a pre-trained Bidirectional Encoder Representations from Transformers (BERT) model ('bert-base-uncased') to classify proposals into 1 of 8 budget areas: Advanced Manufacturing, Artificial Intelligence, Advanced Wireless, Clean Energy, Microelectronics & Semiconductors, Quantum, or Trustworthy AI. This approach is semi-supervised in nature as the training data is comprised of pre-tagged Computer and Information Science and Engineering (CISE) proposals from prior years. Upon training the model to learn the multi-label structure of the underlying data, the model's accuracy and discriminatory power was tested using a hold-out sample (i.e., 80/20 split). The model outputs a numerical vector of probabilities representing the likelihood that a given proposal belongs to 1 or more categories. A cut-off value can then be set for determining the final classification for a given proposal.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,8,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02669,US_OMB_2025_02669,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research"", ""social_nonprofit""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Science Foundation,UNKNOWN,"This is useful for identifying resubmitted proposals for several purposes: evaluating whether to return without review for lack of revision, ensuring continuity of merit review, and the analysis of broader resubmission trends.",Resubmit Checker,National Science Foundation; Directorate for STEM Education (EDU); United States,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"The resubmit checker takes a list of proposal IDs and returns a list of similar proposals submitted to NSF in the past, scored by their similarity. This is useful for identifying resubmitted proposals for several purposes: evaluating whether to return without review for lack of revision, ensuring continuity of merit review, and the analysis of broader resubmission trends.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,19,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02670,US_OMB_2025_02670,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""social_nonprofit""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Science Foundation,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN,Mine Potential Reviewer's areas of expertise,"National Science Foundation; Directorate for Technology, Innovation, and Partnership (TIP); United States","NSF TIP has been approved to use Airtable for several use cases, and Airtable has been certified as secure by the NSF OCIO security team. TIP Team would like to get approval to use Airtable to trial Airtable's AI's ability to match potential reviewer expertise to the reviewer.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Airtable is a low- code platform that incorporates OpenAI services and the data is kept private to Airtable. NSF TIP has been approved to use Airtable for several use cases, and Airtable has been certified as secure by the NSF OCIO security team. TIP Team would like to get approval to use Airtable to trial Airtable's AI's ability to match potential reviewer expertise to the reviewer.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,24,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02671,US_OMB_2025_02671,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""social_nonprofit""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Science Foundation,UNKNOWN,"Typically, an admin person or Program Director will do this work and it is time-consuming and burdensome. Currently, a staff person does this work, and it is burdensome.","Use AI to populate reviewer ""areas of expertise"" and state of potential Regional Engines submitters (members of organizations)","National Science Foundation; Directorate for Technology, Innovation, and Partnership (TIP); United States","TIP is authorized to use Airtable for project management, including reviewer volunteers and recruitment. We have two specific use-cases for which we would like to employ Airtable AI: 1.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"TIP is authorized to use Airtable for project management, including reviewer volunteers and recruitment. Airtable is a no-code platform that includes a built-in database. This system does not store any PII in the database except for ""public PII"" such as name, position, work email address, areas of professional expertise, etc. We have two specific use-cases for which we would like to employ Airtable AI: 1. People who volunteer sometimes do not list all areas of their expertise, or expertise becomes stale. We have been able to do a proof of concept where Airtable AI is prompted to look at the potential reviewer's Linked In profile and identify or update the potential reviewer's expertise in its database based on recent updates to professional experience in LinkedIn. We would like permission to have AI complete this work. Typically, an admin person or Program Director will do this work and it is time-consuming and burdensome. AI can do it much faster and a member of the staff can check it rather than complete it for 400-500 reviewers. 2. We also have a database of potential Engines submitters in Airtable -- people who have attended a webinar, roadshow, or submitted at an earlier time and asked to be contacted when new funding opportunities are available. We track very similar information in the potential submitters data base as we do for reviewers who volunteer to review for the program. The information is used to support outreach to these potential submitters when new funding opportunities are announced, or a new Engines event is announced. We need to know the state associated with the particular submitters institution to determine which regional Engine they should be mapped to geographically (state in the U.S.). We have found that we can prompt the AI to look at the potential submitter's institution, and the AI can locate the state 100% of the time to identify the region that the submitter would be associated with if they were accepted to the program. Currently, a staff person does this work, and it is burdensome. The AI can do this work much faster, so that a member of the staff can redirect their time to more value-added work and then go back and validate the AI's work. This permits the NSF Regional Innovation Engines program to segment outreach by event and regional engine . The Airtable AI is an Airtable private instance of OpenAI.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,25,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02672,US_OMB_2025_02672,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""social_nonprofit""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Science Foundation,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN,"Enhancing Technology, Innovation and Partnerships (TIP) Awards: Efficient Tagging for the 10 Key Technology Areas (KTAs)","National Science Foundation; Directorate for Technology, Innovation, and Partnership (TIP); United States",UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Per the ""CHIPS and Science Act"" mandate, TIP needs to know the investment portfolio based on the 10 KTAs.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,26,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02673,US_OMB_2025_02673,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""social_nonprofit""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Science Foundation,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN,"Technology, Innovation and Partnerships (TIP) Microsoft (MS) Copilot Pilot","National Science Foundation; Directorate for Technology, Innovation, and Partnership (TIP); United States","Copilot for Microsoft 365 uses Microsoft Graph, an API, to evaluate context and available Microsoft 365 user data before modifying and sending user prompts to the language model.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Copilot can be used to rewrite and generate text based on user prompts in Microsoft 365 services, including Microsoft Word, Microsoft Excel, and PowerPoint. Copilot for Microsoft 365 uses Microsoft Graph, an API, to evaluate context and available Microsoft 365 user data before modifying and sending user prompts to the language model. After receiving its output, Microsoft Graph performs additional context-specific processing before sending the response to Microsoft 365 apps to generate content.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,S7_GENERATIVE_CONTENT_CREATION,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,49,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02674,US_OMB_2025_02674,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""social_nonprofit""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Science Foundation,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN,A document summarizer via Natural Language Processing,National Science Foundation; Directorate of Engineering (ENG); United States,"These models are deployed entirely within the agency’'s secure firewalls, ensuring no external data exposure and no external access. This tool automates summarization, reducing the time employees spend reading lengthy documents, enhancing productivity by accurately identifying key points in such documents.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"The AI system utilizes state-of-the-art transformer-based models (e.g., BART, Pegasus, T5, SciBERT) to perform text summarization. These models are deployed entirely within the agency’'s secure firewalls, ensuring no external data exposure and no external access. BART, Pegasus, T5 and SciBERT are state-of-the-art, open-source AI models designed for Natural Language Processing (NLP) tasks. The model will be able to summarize lengthy internal documents, helping employees quickly extract key insights from a large volume of information. This tool automates summarization, reducing the time employees spend reading lengthy documents, enhancing productivity by accurately identifying key points in such documents. The traditional extractive summarization (e.g., via Term Frequency-Inverse Document Frequency TF-IDF) selects key sentences verbatim from the source, often misses several key elements of the document, and results in an inaccurate representation of the content. Unlike traditional extractive summarization, generative summarization (used by BART, Pegasus and T5) creates modified sentences that better capture the meaning and context of the document. This leads to more natural, coherent and concise summaries which enhance readability and contextual accuracy.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,S3_DOCUMENT_INTELLIGENCE,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,51,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02675,US_OMB_2025_02675,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""social_nonprofit""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Science Foundation,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN,Document similarity analysis via Natural Language Processing,National Science Foundation; Directorate of Engineering (ENG); United States,"These models are deployed entirely within the agency’s secure firewalls, ensuring no external data exposure and no external access. Via all-mpnet-base-v2, the model will use utilize deep learning models to capture semantic meaning, ideal for conceptual similarity beyond exact wording.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"The AI system utilizes a sentence-transformer model (all-mpnet-base-v2) and a statistical keyword method (TF-IDF) to perform document similarity tasks. These models are deployed entirely within the agency’s secure firewalls, ensuring no external data exposure and no external access. These AI models are designed for natural language processing (NLP) tasks. Via all-mpnet-base-v2, the model will use utilize deep learning models to capture semantic meaning, ideal for conceptual similarity beyond exact wording. Via Term Frequency-Inverse Document Frequency (TF-IDF), the model will focus on lexical overlap and is effective for direct technical document comparison. Both models calculate Cosine similarity, with scores ranging from -1 to 1. Scores can be interpreted as follows: identical (1), highly similar (0.8-0.99), somewhat similar (~0.5), mostly dissimilar (0.1-0.3), completely dissimilar (0) and opposite (-1 to 0). Document similarity analysis can significantly boost productivity since a large volume of documents can quickly and efficiently be analyzed for extent of contextual or lexical similarity and can aid in routine planning for proposal administration. Cosine similarity is also a well-established method to quantify similarity and is already used within NSF tools.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,52,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02676,US_OMB_2025_02676,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""social_nonprofit""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Science Foundation,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN,AI voice over,National Science Foundation; Office for Legislative and Public Affairs (OLPA); United States,"The AI system generates temporary synthetic voice-over using text-to-speech services (e.g., Eleven Labs, WellSaid Labs) to convert scripts into placeholder audio for video drafts.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"The AI system generates temporary synthetic voice-over using text-to-speech services (e.g., Eleven Labs, WellSaid Labs) to convert scripts into placeholder audio for video drafts. These AI-generated voice-overs are used solely for timing and content review during production and are replaced with professional human voice-over before public release.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,9,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02677,US_OMB_2025_02677,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""social_nonprofit""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Science Foundation,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN,Adobe Photoshop,National Science Foundation; Office for Legislative and Public Affairs (OLPA); United States,"Office for Legislative and Public Affairs (OLPA) Creative Services team will use Photoshop's AI-powered tools to refine edits of photos and graphics, particularly the retouching of portraits.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Office for Legislative and Public Affairs (OLPA) Creative Services team will use Photoshop's AI-powered tools to refine edits of photos and graphics, particularly the retouching of portraits.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,10,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02678,US_OMB_2025_02678,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research"", ""social_nonprofit""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Science Foundation,UNKNOWN,"Data are currently stored in various formats across multiple locations, making it inaccessible for analytic purposes and difficult to reach without impact to current operations.",NSF AI-Ready Research Performance Progress Reports (RPPR) Data,National Science Foundation; Office of Chief Information Officer (OCIO); United States,"The lack of centralized, accessible data limits NSF's ability to assess impacts, make informed decisions, and fully leverage data for insights. Request approval to use AWS Bedrock, AWS SageMaker, AWS Neptune & AWS Comprehend from AIDG (AI Data Governance).",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"OCIO is working to provide AI-ready RPPR data – a key component for determining outcomes of NSF investments. Note: Information in the RPPR may be used to identify outputs and be linked to other data sets (e.g., NSF PAR, Patent, etc.) to assess NSF's ""broader impacts""; however, it is not currently available in an accessible format. Problem Statement: RPPR data, a critical resource for tracking the outcomes of NSF-funded projects. Data are currently stored in various formats across multiple locations, making it inaccessible for analytic purposes and difficult to reach without impact to current operations. The lack of centralized, accessible data limits NSF's ability to assess impacts, make informed decisions, and fully leverage data for insights. Request approval to use AWS Bedrock, AWS SageMaker, AWS Neptune & AWS Comprehend from AIDG (AI Data Governance).",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,48,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02679,US_OMB_2025_02679,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""social_nonprofit""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Science Foundation,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN,"ServiceNow GenAI ""Now Assist""",National Science Foundation; Office of Information and Resource Management (OIRM); United States,ServiceNow GenAI is a FedRAMP High certified system to accelerate digital transformation using Now Assist.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"ServiceNow GenAI is a FedRAMP High certified system to accelerate digital transformation using Now Assist. Automatically generate content such as responses, work notes, and knowledge base articles related to customer service experience. Increase productivity and speed of delivery with intelligent recommendations. Resolve issues swiftly with chatbots that understand human language.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,S2_AGENT_CONVERSATIONAL_AI|S7_GENERATIVE_CONTENT_CREATION,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,7,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02680,US_OMB_2025_02680,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""social_nonprofit""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Science Foundation,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN,Amazon Web Services(AWS) Assisted Software Development (DIS AI Assisted Development),National Science Foundation; Office of Information and Resource Management (OIRM); United States,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Within software development, AI-driven tools, such as Amazon Web Services (AWS) CodeWhisperer, Amazon Q and Bedrock, and integration with development workflow, promise to elevate developer productivity and refine code quality. The objective of this pilot is to explore potential integration of these AWS services with the Division of Information Systems (DIS) Developers Integrated Development Environments (IDEs), Jenkins automation, Bitbucket, laying the groundwork for secure AI Assisted Development at NSF.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,22,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02681,US_OMB_2025_02681,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""social_nonprofit""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Science Foundation,UNKNOWN,"Where feasible, the RTI Science, Technology, Engineering, and Mathematics (STEM) education experts/analysts will manually map the research topics to NSF research programs.",Open-source topic identification for the Public Engagement with Science Initiative data analysis.,National Science Foundation; Office of Integrative Activities (OIA); United States,OIA team proposes using unsupervised Natural Language Processing (NLP) to identify topical themes within responses submitted to the NSF public engagement questionnaire. The system will use an open-source profanity filter such as Python’'s profanity-filter to identify toxic language.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"OIA team proposes using unsupervised Natural Language Processing (NLP) to identify topical themes within responses submitted to the NSF public engagement questionnaire. The AI system will include multiple open-source techniques used together to achieve this goal. Details of the system are as follows: To ensure high-quality topics, the system will first programmatically remove responses that are blank or non-informative. The National Center for Health Statistics (NCHS) Semi-Automated Non-Response Detection for Surveys (SANDS) model will be used to filter out non-response responses (e.g., """"sdfsdfa,"""" """" idkkkkk""""). To reduce duplicate responses potentially caused by bots or submitted to boost relative importance, responses with the exact duplicate question wording will be removed over a threshold of three responses per IP address. If an individual has several different questions they would like to submit, all of their questions will be included. The system will use an open-source profanity filter such as Python’'s profanity-filter to identify toxic language. Any responses that are primarily toxic language will be dropped from analysis. To group questions into themes, we will use a word-embedding model to convert text responses into multidimensional space for topic modeling. Because we anticipate responses in multiple languages, the system will use a multilingual will use a multilingual word-embedding model, such as ""paraphrase-multilingual-MiniLM-L12-v2"" or the most up-to-date version of this model at the time of analysis. Embeddings will be reduced in dimensions using a dimension reduction algorithm such as t-SNE (t-distributed Stochastic Neighbor Embedding) to prepare for clustering. Reduced response embeddings will be clustered into groups using the ClassTfidfTransformer clustering algorithm from the Python package BertTopic. The algorithm will be seeded with words corresponding to a list of NSF programs corresponding to different research areas to map the clusters to these established categorizations. To aid in the review of topics generated by the clustering algorithm, an open-source large language model (LLM), such as Meta Llama, will be used to summarize the responses grouped within a cluster. Using a prompt like the example below, this strategy will produce a plain language summary and title of each of the clusters of responses. The clusters produced will be reviewed by Research Triangle Institute (RTI) staff for accuracy and appropriateness of naming. Staff will make edits to the LLM-generated summaries as necessary and note any clusters that are candidates for merging with other clusters into a single topic. The topics will then be validated by NSF experts and the advisory committee. Once the existing cluster model has been finalized, the cluster model will be applied to all responses. Where feasible, the RTI Science, Technology, Engineering, and Mathematics (STEM) education experts/analysts will manually map the research topics to NSF research programs.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,35,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02682,US_OMB_2025_02682,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""social_nonprofit""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Science Foundation,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN,Hand-written text extraction using Textract for the Public Engagement with Science Initiative,National Science Foundation; Office of Integrative Activities (OIA); United States,"OIA Team proposes using a Commercial Off the Shelf Amazon Web Services (AWS) product, Textract, as a character recognition tool to convert handwritten text into machine-encoded text for a postcard.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"OIA Team proposes using a Commercial Off the Shelf Amazon Web Services (AWS) product, Textract, as a character recognition tool to convert handwritten text into machine-encoded text for a postcard. Handwritten text will be an open format question for science and engineering, and some optional check boxes for demographic and other data questions.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,38,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
