AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02727,US_OMB_2025_02727,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""enterprise_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Small Business Administration,Service Delivery,"Manual code refactoring, test case generation, and project management across modernization initiatives are resource-intensive and error-prone, creating risk during cloud migration.",Multi-Agent Orchestration,Small Business Administration; OCIO: Office of the Chief Information Officer; Service Delivery; United States,"Multi-agent system using Amazon Bedrock with foundation models. Agent Teams coordinate specialized agents for: (1) Code Refactoring — analyzes legacy ColdFusion/COBOL code and recommends modernization patterns, (2) Automated Testing — generates unit, integration, and regression test cases for financial calculation modules, (3) Project Management — synthesizes sprint status, identifies blockers, and coordinates task dependencies across modernization teams. Input: source code repositories, project management data, test specifications. Output: refactored code suggestions, test case files, project status summaries, risk assessments. All outputs require human review and approval before implementation.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Multi-agent AI orchestration will accelerate legacy code modernization by automating code refactoring recommendations, generating comprehensive test suites for financial calculation modules, and streamlining project management workflows. Expected benefits include reduced manual effort for QA testing, improved code quality and test coverage for CAFS applications, faster time-to-migration for AWS EVS initiatives, and better coordination across modernization workstreams.","SBA maintains millions of lines of legacy ColdFusion and COBOL code supporting mission-critical lending systems (CAFS) with minimal test coverage and significant technical debt. Manual code refactoring, test case generation, and project management across modernization initiatives are resource-intensive and error-prone, creating risk during cloud migration.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,SBA-40,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02728,US_OMB_2025_02728,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""enterprise_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Small Business Administration,Cybersecurity,"During cloud migration (AWS EVS) and disaster recovery operations, locating specific data across backup snapshots, identifying clean recovery points, and performing forensic analysis of backup data requires significant manual effort and specialized knowledge of backup infrastructure.",AI-Powered Search and Recovery,Small Business Administration; OCIO: Office of the Chief Information Officer; Cybersecurity; United States,"AI assistant providing natural language search, classification, and summarization across Cohesity Data Cloud backup data. Includes: (1) Conversational search — natural language queries against unstructured data in backup snapshots, (2) AI-powered threat detection — continuous anomaly scanning of backup data for ransomware indicators and insider threats, (3) Recovery intelligence — intelligent recovery point recommendations with blast radius analysis. Input: natural language queries, backup data snapshots, threat intelligence feeds. Output: search results with citations, anomaly alerts, recovery recommendations, data classification reports. All recovery actions require human authorization.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"AI-powered conversational search across enterprise backup data enables faster data discovery during recovery operations, reduces time-to-recovery during cyber incidents, and supports forensic investigation by allowing natural language queries against unstructured backup data. SaaS deployment model reduces operational overhead for backup infrastructure management during AWS EVS migration.","During cloud migration (AWS EVS) and disaster recovery operations, locating specific data across backup snapshots, identifying clean recovery points, and performing forensic analysis of backup data requires significant manual effort and specialized knowledge of backup infrastructure.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,SBA-41,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
