AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02898,US_OMB_2025_02898,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Treasury,Procurement and Finance Mgmt,UNKNOWN,Ink and Paper Consumption Forecast (IPCF),Department of the Treasury; Bureau of Engraving and Printing (BEP); Procurement and Finance Mgmt; United States,"The IPCF Predictive Analytics Model generates predictive outputs that support operational planning. The model produces: 1. Ink mileage estimates based on ink type and associated currency denomination; 2. Ink consumption forecasts tied to the number of sheets scheduled for production; 3. Paper consumption projections over defined time periods; 4. Ink usage predictions across time intervals to support procurement and inventory decisions""",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"The IPCF Predictive Analytics Model contributes to cost efficiency and supply chain resilience by predicting ink mileage based on ink type and denomination, as well as forecasting ink and paper consumption over time and by sheet volume. The model helps ensure accurate procurement, reduce material waste, and support uninterrupted production schedules.",The Ink and Paper Consumption Forecast (IPCF) AI model is intended to predict: 1. Ink mileage predictions based on ink type and associated denom; 2. Ink consumption predictions based on number of sheets; 3. Paper consumption predictions given a time period; 4. Ink consumption predictions given a time period,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,S4_PREDICTION_DETECTION,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,BEP-41,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
