AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02904,US_OMB_2025_02904,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Treasury,Procurement and Finance Mgmt,UNKNOWN,USAspending Natural Language Search Initiative,Department of the Treasury; Bureau of the Fiscal Service (BFS); Procurement and Finance Mgmt; United States,Enhanced search and intuitive experience for users,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Pilot a free text search function for new users to access insights from USAspending.gov in a more intuitive way. This effort will also accelerate technical solutioning and future development, and aid in PO decision-making/prioritization. This pilot will use LLM best practices and technology to accept natural language searches from users. Test Use of Natural Language Cloud Service to enhance User Search Experience in USA Spending","Contextual Research (Exploring policies, regulations, trends, and strategic topics)",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,REQ-2024-01948,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02905,US_OMB_2025_02905,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Treasury,Admin Functions,UNKNOWN,GenAI Productivity Tool Pilot,Department of the Treasury; Bureau of the Fiscal Service (BFS); Admin Functions; United States,Multiple depending on application used or general browser based use.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Pilot AI productivity solution in Fiscal Service tenant to determine business value,"Transcribing, summarizing, or other efforts that improve the accessibility of a virtual meeting or interview using AI. (Meeting Summarization and Recap - Generating notes, action items, and summaries from meetings). Generating first drafts of documents, briefing, or communication materials using AI. Content Generation & Refinement (Drafting, rewriting, and improving documents, emails, presentations, and plans). Summarizing the key points of a lengthy report using AI. (Content Summarization - Summarizing emails, chats, meetings, and documents). Code Assistance - Generating, debugging, and documenting code. Data Analysis and Manipulation (Excel formulas, macros, forecasting, and SQL-based data work). Contextual Research (Exploring policies, regulations, trends, and strategic topics). Knowledge Retrieval (Locating known information and presenting or analyzing the information). Document Comparison and Alignment (Comparing versions of documents for consistency and alignment). Email and Task Automation (Automating rules, reminders, and scheduling). How-To Guidance (Step-by-step instructions for tools and workflows). Editing images, videos, or other public affairs materials using AI. Scheduling and managing social media posts using AI.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,S1_KNOWLEDGE_RETRIEVAL_RAG|S3_DOCUMENT_INTELLIGENCE|S4_PREDICTION_DETECTION|S7_GENERATIVE_CONTENT_CREATION,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,REQ-2024-01953,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_02906,US_OMB_2025_02906,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of the Treasury,IT,UNKNOWN,FRB AI Code Translation POC,Department of the Treasury; Bureau of the Fiscal Service (BFS); IT; United States,Remediation of Legacy code -- migrating to more modern framework,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"This POC will explore the remediation of legacy code by leveraging generative AI to accelerate migration to a more modern framework. The purpose of this POC is simply to evaluate the efficacy of gen AI for this purpose and any code generated would not be moved to production. AI-driven code translation accelerates the conversion of code from one language or framework to another, including updating legacy systems to modern platforms. The use of generative AI in technical debt remediation offers substantial operational efficiencies, cost savings, and strategic benefits, quantifiable through reduced labor hours, lower migration costs, and faster time-to-market for modernized applications. These advantages position teams to better leverage modern technologies and align with the strategic goals of agility and innovation.","Code Assistance - Generating, debugging, and documenting code",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,REQ-2024-01972,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
