AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03295,US_OMB_2025_03295,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Cybersecurity,UNKNOWN,Secure Access Service Edge (SASE),Department of Veterans Affairs; OIT: Office of Information & Technology; Cybersecurity; United States,"The AI produces actionable security alerts, risk scores, and policy compliance reports that identify potential exposure of PHI/PII. Outputs include prioritized incidents, visualized trends in application usage, anomaly detection summaries, and automated compliance audit logs to support remediation and decision-making.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"'- Improved data security by automatically detecting and alerting/blocking risky or non-compliant data transfers in real time. - Operational efficiency by automating policy enforcement and reducing manual review workload. - Enhance compliance with federal mandates by monitoring PHI/PII across all access points, thereby maintaining trust with Veterans and the public through stronger protection of sensitive information.","The AI is intended to identify, prevent, and mitigate risks from unauthorized data access, exfiltration, and misuse of sensitive information, including PHI/PII in cloud applications and network traffic. It addresses gaps in visibility, compliance enforcement, and threat detection across a hybrid work environment.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-25-6479,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03296,US_OMB_2025_03296,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Health and Medical,"By eliminating reliance on costly middleware and reducing process overhead, VRAS enables real-time, SQL compatible data access directly from Vista.",VistA Records Accessed by SQL (VRAS),Department of Veterans Affairs; OIT: Office of Information & Technology; Health and Medical; United States,"All VistA Data, from Supply chain to Medical records.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Full AI access to each VistA instance via ODBC/JDBC.,"The VistA Records Accessed by SQL (VRAS) is a transformative initiative aimed at modernizing data accessibility and analytics within the Department of Veterans Affairs (VA). By eliminating reliance on costly middleware and reducing process overhead, VRAS enables real-time, SQL compatible data access directly from Vista. This initiative establishes a seamless, efficient data pipeline, enhancing reporting capabilities, reducing infrastructure complexity, and supporting data-driven decision-making across all VistA instances. With improved accessibility to high-quality data, VA users can generate timely, accurate insights that drive operational efficiency and better outcomes for departments that directly affect veteran care.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-25-1143,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
