AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03307,US_OMB_2025_03307,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Admin Functions,UNKNOWN,Summit AI Assistant,Department of Veterans Affairs; OIT: Office of Information & Technology; Admin Functions; United States,The outputs of the AI system are: 1. Responses to plain language queries submitted by a business user. 2. A 'chat' like experience with the data.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"The AI increases efficiency within a business process, especially in business processes that involve sifting through large amounts of information/knowledge captured in documents.",The AI is intended to reduce the time required to extract rich and relevant information from a corpus of documents pertaining to a specific business domain. A combination of keyword and vector search methods deliver precise and relevant information from a specific business domain's knowledge base.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,S3_DOCUMENT_INTELLIGENCE,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-25-1676,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03308,US_OMB_2025_03308,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Admin Functions,UNKNOWN,eDiscovery (VASI 2460): Predictive Coding,Department of Veterans Affairs; OIT: Office of Information & Technology; Admin Functions; United States,Predicted ranking for remaining documents,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Prioritizes and surfaces relevant documents early to speed review and improve accuracy.,Document review teams train an AI model to identify positive or negative content within a universe of documents.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-25-3234,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03309,US_OMB_2025_03309,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Other,UNKNOWN,Veteran Experience Office Retention/Trust Models in Customer Experience Insights,Department of Veterans Affairs; OIT: Office of Information & Technology; Other; United States,"Predicted trust, predicted retention, driver importance metrics, driver impact metrics on output variables.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Improved veteran experience, improved veteran trust, improved veteran retention.",The models reside in Customer Experience Insights. The inputs are CDW VISTA data and CX Insights data. The outputs are predictions of veteran trust and retention given veteran experience inputs. The purpose of the models is to predict whether a veteran would say they trust the VA (Trust) and whether they would continue to receive care with VA (Retention) based on their experiences with VA. The intended use is to understand drivers of these important metrics. The problem to be solved is to programmatically identify drivers of veteran experience to inform methods of improving experience metrics such as retention and trust.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-25-5411,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03310,US_OMB_2025_03310,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Admin Functions,"The AI solution is designed to eliminate the manual data entry burden associated with processing CHAMPVA applications. Each application previously required up to 61 administrative steps, contributing to a backlog of over 70,000 unprocessed applications and delays of up to 162 days.",CHAMPVA Automation,Department of Veterans Affairs; OIT: Office of Information & Technology; Admin Functions; United States,The AI system outputs structured data extracted from VA Form 10-10d PDF applications. This data is formatted into text files suitable for ingestion into the CP&E system. The outputs include: Applicant demographic and eligibility information Validated data records for benefit processing Automated alerts via VA Notify to inform applicants of status updates Data logs for tracking and auditing purposes These outputs enable downstream systems to process applications efficiently and support eligibility decision-making.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Increased Efficiency: Automating data extraction and processing reduces time spent on manual tasks. Cost Savings: Reduces labor costs associated with manual data entry and backlog management. Improved Service Delivery: Accelerates application processing, allowing Veterans and their families to receive benefits faster. Enhanced Staff Productivity: Frees up staff to focus on eligibility determinations and higher-value tasks. Supports VA’s Mission: Strengthens the VA’s commitment to serving Veterans and their families with timely and effective healthcare benefits.","The AI solution is designed to eliminate the manual data entry burden associated with processing CHAMPVA applications. Each application previously required up to 61 administrative steps, contributing to a backlog of over 70,000 unprocessed applications and delays of up to 162 days. The AI automates data extraction from VA Form 10-10d PDFs and streamlines ingestion into the Claims Processing and Eligibility (CP&E) system, significantly reducing processing time and administrative workload.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-25-967,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
