AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03327,US_OMB_2025_03327,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,IT,UNKNOWN,E2 HelpBot,Department of Veterans Affairs; Office of the Deputy Secretary of VA; IT; United States,"Chatbot The Help Bot AI use case will be expanded by developing two distinct products. The first product is a Portal Help Bot, intended for deployment on the EEO portal. This external bot will assist users with inquiry intake and provide responses to questions related to the EEO portal. The second product is an Internal Help Bot, designed to support Office of Resolution Management (ORM) personnel in accessing information.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Increased Efficiency,"EEO Users browse through documents like the User Guides or knowledge articles to understand E2 functionality. Additionally, many Help Desk Tickets are entered for support on E2 functions as well. We plan to develop an internal HelpBot using an LLM model (GPT 4.0) that can assist users to ask the Help Bot questions, reducing user frustration and time to figure out how to perform a task. This use case will provide a knowledgebase to assist users to get information on EEO processes.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-25-10,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03328,US_OMB_2025_03328,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Admin Functions,UNKNOWN,Compliance Made Easy,Department of Veterans Affairs; Office of the Executive Secretary; Admin Functions; United States,"Once fully developed, the AI version of CME will provide style guide, grammar, and tone checks returned to the user on the text the user submitted to CME.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Increased efficiency in developing and processing correspondence.,AI is being added to a new version of Compliance Made Easy (CME) in development to assist with grammar and tone checks along with tracking Style Guide updates. This is intended to improve compliance with VA Style Guide and reduce staffing time for correspondence.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-24-4726,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03329,US_OMB_2025_03329,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Benefits Processing,UNKNOWN,Automated Ratings Summarization,Department of Veterans Affairs; VBA: Veterans Benefits Administration; Benefits Processing; United States,"Identifies and generates summarizations or relevant documents from a Veteran's record, associated with the claim under review.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"'- Increased efficiency and lower time to decision on a benefits claim for a Veteran - Improve the quality of decisions, which can ultimately result in a decrease in appeals","We are attempting to reduce the claims backlog and processing time. Additionally, there is a large volume of documentation on a Veteran's record - this tool is intended to reduce the amount of time a claim processor spends sorting through documentation relevant to a Veteran's claimed issue.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-25-1594,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03330,US_OMB_2025_03330,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Benefits Processing,"Due to the constraints, a large number of claims are offboarded each night for manual resolution.",Smart Pension Automation,Department of Veterans Affairs; VBA: Veterans Benefits Administration; Benefits Processing; United States,The AI solution will output reporting data on which claims were awarded or off ramped on a daily basis. The solution will also provide auditable information on why a decision was made for a human to review.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,The AI solution is expected to increase the number of claims awarded on a daily basis by 10% with the minimum viable product (MVP) solution and then continue to improve with iterative deliveries after the MVP solution.,"Reduce the overall average of days to complete a pension related benefit claim. Currently, there is a batch claim processing system in place with Pension Automation that leverages Camunda and is currently only able to process 300 claims/night due to constraints with the original solution. Due to the constraints, a large number of claims are offboarded each night for manual resolution.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-25-3480,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03331,US_OMB_2025_03331,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Benefits Processing,UNKNOWN,Predictive Claims Processing Capability POC,Department of Veterans Affairs; VBA: Veterans Benefits Administration; Benefits Processing; United States,Proposed decision on Education Benefits,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Increased efficiency, faster decisions for veterans, and improved veteran experience.",Faster claims decisions for Veterans by predicting/performing claims adjudication without the need for a rules engine,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-25-393,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03332,US_OMB_2025_03332,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Benefits Processing,Reduce the burden of travel on veterans and expedite the time required for claims processing.,AICES,Department of Veterans Affairs; VBA: Veterans Benefits Administration; Benefits Processing; United States,"The system indexes structured, semi-structured, and unstructured Veteran health and service record data, including diagnosis, severity, and service connection evidence from eFolders, metadata, and lay evidence. It supports Disability Benefits Questionnaire (DBQ) processing to generate SMART Claims with recommendations. Objective 1: Reduce Unnecessary In-Person Examinations through Evidence-Driven Triage and Workflow Automation Goal: Demonstrate the accuracy of the solution to properly execute ACE exams. Metric: Demonstrate the ability to produce 5000 ACE exams during the period of performance within a 72-hour delivery window, through expert review. Objective 2: Enhance the accuracy of documentation for ACE-generated DBQs Goal: Validate the capability of advanced OCR and NLP tools to correctly extract and populate data. Metric: Achieve at least a 96% accuracy rating for all ACE DBQs.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"This initiative aims to: 1. Reduce the backlog and processing times by more efficiently using Acceptable Clinical Evidence (ACE), minimizing unnecessary in-person exams and addressing workflow inefficiencies. 2. Reduce VA costs due to reduced in-person exams. 3. Improve the Veteran experience by reducing the burden of travel on veterans and expediting the time required for claims processing.","1. Reduce the backlog and processing times, minimize unnecessary in-person exams, and address workflow inefficiencies. 2. Reduce the burden of travel on veterans and expedite the time required for claims processing. During the period of performance, this effort will demonstrate the effectiveness of the proposed solution to develop Disability Benefits Questionnaire (DBQs) through Acceptable Clinical Evidence (ACE).",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-25-5578,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03333,US_OMB_2025_03333,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Benefits Processing,"A need exists for a specialized, automated solution to complete several pieces of the Rating process to expedite the delivery of benefits and awards to Veterans, and to reduce errors and delays resulting from remediation.",Smart Ratings Recommendation,Department of Veterans Affairs; VBA: Veterans Benefits Administration; Benefits Processing; United States,The output is a rating recommendation that the Ratings VSR can approve or reject. It is not finalized until the RVSR takes action.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Smart Rating Recommendation empowers VSRs in the Ratings workflow to leverage AI-generated ratings of select claim and contention types in order to lower processing times for a Rating Decision to be made. This is done by allowing RVSRs to leverage AI analysis of selected claims and contentions, and provide a proposed Rating to the user to confirm or review manually themselves.","Due to the rating decision's dependence on the preceding steps of the rating process, there is often a backlog of claims and significant rework required to complete a rating on a claim. A need exists for a specialized, automated solution to complete several pieces of the Rating process to expedite the delivery of benefits and awards to Veterans, and to reduce errors and delays resulting from remediation.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,F08_ERROR_COMPLIANCE_RISK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-25-6965,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03334,US_OMB_2025_03334,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Benefits Processing,Smart Claim Check (SCC) reduces avoidable claims processing errors by addressing the problem of manually reviewing extensive documentation by Veterans Service Representatives (VSRs) to identify and resolve issues.,Smart Claim Check,Department of Veterans Affairs; VBA: Veterans Benefits Administration; Benefits Processing; United States,"The output of the AI system is timely guidance with relevant M21-1 linkage, that will appear in the User Interface (UI) automatically for the claims processors to review and act upon. SCC is referring to these a ""Smart Claim Insights"".",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"By leveraging these technologies described in #12, Smart Claim Check can automatically review claim documentation, identify common patterns, and offer structured recommendations, including context-specific guidance from the M21-1 manual, confidence scores, and links to relevant sections, thereby expediting the claims review process and reducing avoidable re-work and extended processing times.",Smart Claim Check (SCC) reduces avoidable claims processing errors by addressing the problem of manually reviewing extensive documentation by Veterans Service Representatives (VSRs) to identify and resolve issues. Claims processing errors that can be avoided in the claims process leads to extended wait times for Veterans to receive the benefits to which they are entitled. SCC leverages natural language processing (NLP) and machine learning (ML) to analyze past deferral data and identify common patterns and themes.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK|F08_ERROR_COMPLIANCE_RISK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-25-1348,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03335,US_OMB_2025_03335,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Service Delivery,Loan Guaranty Service (LGY) has many policy and procedural documents that are difficult to know and retrieve information for.,Loan Guaranty Lender’s Handbook Chatbot,Department of Veterans Affairs; VBA: Veterans Benefits Administration; Service Delivery; United States,Curated information (answers) to user questions based on LGY policy and procedures.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Increase efficiency and consistency in knowledge retrieval from source documents (manuals, SOPs, other policy & procedural documents).",Loan Guaranty Service (LGY) has many policy and procedural documents that are difficult to know and retrieve information for. This AI tool is designed to make the knowledge retrieval process more efficient and improve consistency.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,S1_KNOWLEDGE_RETRIEVAL_RAG,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-25-1512,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03336,US_OMB_2025_03336,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Service Delivery,UNKNOWN,Education Call Center (ECC) Next Gen POC,Department of Veterans Affairs; VBA: Veterans Benefits Administration; Service Delivery; United States,"• Function of the model: Generative AI Model that can provide real time transcription of calls, capture questions asked by caller, and provide recommended answers with source citation to ECC representatives • Output: Call transcript, answers to questions, querable database for quality control's purpose",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Increased efficiency and improved communication outcomes with Veterans about their benefits. Perhaps improve turnover at the call centers.,"To give easier access to information like approved, current procedures or helpful tips to call center employees that engage directly with Veterans. This is a high turnover position within VA so this would lighten the training barrier and supply our Veterans with better information.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-25-2036,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03337,US_OMB_2025_03337,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Admin Functions,UNKNOWN,AI Personal Assistance POC,Department of Veterans Affairs; VBA: Veterans Benefits Administration; Admin Functions; United States,Answers to questions. The tool would generate a mock SQL query and other useful outputs that would help refine the data inquiry.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Increased efficiency,Help VBA Education Data Analysts create queries and interpret data which can be used for decision making.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-25-2089,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03338,US_OMB_2025_03338,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Benefits Processing,"Currently in order to annotate documents, VSRs have to read large bodies of text and manually summarize them which is time consuming and increases cognitive load.",Generative Annotations,Department of Veterans Affairs; VBA: Veterans Benefits Administration; Benefits Processing; United States,AI Summarized text,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Increased efficiency,"Veteran Service Representatives (VSRs) are required to annotate documents relevant to a Veteran claim so that subsequent reviewers are able to quickly reference information to make claim decisions. Currently in order to annotate documents, VSRs have to read large bodies of text and manually summarize them which is time consuming and increases cognitive load.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-25-2373,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03339,US_OMB_2025_03339,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Other,UNKNOWN,ASKA: Automated Support and Knowledge Assistance,Department of Veterans Affairs; VBA: Veterans Benefits Administration; Other; United States,We are currently looking into building or utilizing what is available to create this. We are looking at a space where all info is extracted and easy to find,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Increase efficiency and productivity for public services,"ASKA is an internal support tool for VBA Public Contact staff. It connects approved policy and procedural content from SharePoint to a searchable question and answer bot. Staff can ask common questions about public contact, FOIA, congressional inquiries, and other customer service duties. ASKA does not use or process PII, claims data, or make any automated decisions, it simply returns standard reference answers an directs staff to relevant SOP or job aids. We are currently using many different websites to obtain information which delays services to the public, Veterans and Service members. Having a tool available to provide this information will help provide this service at a faster rate.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-25-3670,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03340,US_OMB_2025_03340,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Benefits Processing,UNKNOWN,VBA Mail Management Services (MMS) - Modification,Department of Veterans Affairs; VBA: Veterans Benefits Administration; Benefits Processing; United States,Upgrade to QuickSubmit to include a forms validation engine.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,To prevent claims processing inefficiencies in data quality at intake.,"We are shifting data capture from back-office processing to the point of first contact. The system validates VA forms in front of the user interactively as it is being submitted, allowing the submitter to verify and correct errors immediately (reduces churn). This will help with claims modernization.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-25-5852,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03341,US_OMB_2025_03341,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Benefits Processing,UNKNOWN,Call Center Knowledge Navigator,Department of Veterans Affairs; VBA: Veterans Benefits Administration; Benefits Processing; United States,'- Version 1 outputs a string in response to a user query with cited reference materials - Version 2 will hyperlink these materials for user reference - Future versions will include transcription output and automated answer strings based on live transcription,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Increased efficiency and increased accuracy of answers to beneficiary queries,1. Inaccurate transcription of phone calls by the current system. 2. Need for enhanced time-to-effectiveness for new employees of the Education Call Center. 3. Improvements to quality review of transcribed conversations.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-24-2143,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03342,US_OMB_2025_03342,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Benefits Processing,UNKNOWN,Master Claims Assistance Tool (M-CAT),Department of Veterans Affairs; VBA: Veterans Benefits Administration; Benefits Processing; United States,"M-CAT provides quick access to regulatory and/or policy guidance and summarizes information within the prescribed RAG model. These retrieval results are maintained for each user and aggregated to inform focused training support needs. The overall generated response includes contextual integration, interactive elements for source expansion, feedback mechanism, displaying current trending topics as suggested queries, and providing prompted follow-up questions post query.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"M-CAT provides quick access to regulatory and/or policy guidance and summarizes information within the prescribed RAG model, guiding end-users to achieve a clearer understanding and clearer implementation of VA policy. Access to this information improves processing capabilities which immediately transition to more timely and accurate delivery of benefits.","M-CAT is designed to automatically classify, extract, and validate critical information from diverse regulatory and/or policy references. This includes the automation of complex data extraction tasks, which are traditionally time-consuming and prone to human error. M-CAT provides quick access to regulatory and/or policy guidance and summarizes information within the prescribed Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) model. These retrieval results are maintained for each user and aggregated to inform focused training support needs. The overall generated response includes contextual integration, interactive elements for source expansion, feedback mechanism, displays current trending topics as suggested queries, and provides prompted follow-up questions post query.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,S1_KNOWLEDGE_RETRIEVAL_RAG|S3_DOCUMENT_INTELLIGENCE,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-24-4804,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03343,US_OMB_2025_03343,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Benefits Processing,UNKNOWN,National Training Team | Schools — FAQ Gen AI Dashboard,Department of Veterans Affairs; VBA: Veterans Benefits Administration; Benefits Processing; United States,The system outputs data to a Microsoft Power BI report — the report lists the top ten categories of questions asked within a particular office hours session with a suggested question based off submissions and suggested answers to the generated question based off previously provided answers in FAQ documentation.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"increased efficiency. There are currently six permanent members of the NTT|S staff and approximately 40,000 SCOs. It is physically impossible for a staff this size to answer all of the questions they ask in a given session. The model reduces the count of overall questions to a reasonable amount answerable by a subject matter expert (SME). It also uses previous answers provided by SMEs in the case of duplicate or similar questions to speed preparation of FAQ documentation for publication following a session — if they’ve answered a question before, they don’t need to spend time answering it again. Currently, the project has fallen below expectations in terms of usefulness to the end users. NTT|S suffered a major operational setback earlier this year when the contract with Adobe Connect was severed unexpectedly by the new administration. Implementing Office Hours using Microsoft Teams as an alternative has had several obstacles, including a substantial decrease in questions SCOs are able to submit within a session. Because of the lower volume, SMEs can often answer most questions within a session and review remaining questions without the assistance of the model.",Categorization of large volume question submissions with suggested generated answers based on past-provided information.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-24-2184,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03344,US_OMB_2025_03344,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Procurement and Finance Mgmt,UNKNOWN,Payment Redirect Fraud (PRF) Model,Department of Veterans Affairs; VBA: Veterans Benefits Administration; Procurement and Finance Mgmt; United States,The output is a risk indicator on how likely each daily direct deposit change may be fraudulent.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Preventing Veterans from having their benefits stolen by fraudsters builds their trust in the VA. The accurate delivery of benefits without interruption creates operational efficiencies and demonstrates fiscal stewardship and prudent use of tax-payer dollars.,The goal of the Payment Redirect Fraud (PRF) model is to identify which Direct Deposit (DD) changes are likely to be fraudulent and refer them on to investigators.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-24-3291,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03345,US_OMB_2025_03345,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Benefits Processing,UNKNOWN,Automated Decision Support,Department of Veterans Affairs; VBA: Veterans Benefits Administration; Benefits Processing; United States,"Depending on claim criteria, ADS may produce the following five documents: - Automated Review Summary Document (ARSD) - Summarizes relevant medical and service information from Veteran documents with page numbers and hyperlinks to the original source documents. It also explains the ADS outcome. - Health Data Repository (HDR) document - Indexes Veteran medical records data from VistA sources (VAMC and Community Care visits) - Standard Commercial-Off-The-Shelf (COTS) Integration Platform (SCIP) document - Indexes Veteran medical images from VistA sources - Electronic Health Record-Text (EHR-Text) document - Indexes Veteran medical records data from EHR sites - Electronic Health Record-Image (EHR-Image) document - Indexes Veteran medical images from EHR sites ADS also takes action in the Veterans Benefits Management System (VBMS) to update end product (EP) status, order or draft Compensation & Pension (C&P) exams, and add notes. No final benefits decisions are made by ADS and no payments are initiated by ADS.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Automated Decision Support (ADS) automates some of the up-front time-consuming development activities of retrieving information and identifying potentially relevant VA Schedule of Rating Disabilities (VASRD)-related evidence of record. It accelerates the ordering of exams and assists in marking claims as Ready for Decision (RFD). This can lead to faster and more consistent decisions for Veterans and unlock VBA’s ability to uncover data trends.,"Identify medical evidence for claims processing. Automated Decision Support (ADS) is the utilization of technology to maximize operational efficiency by reducing administrative tasks to produce desired outcomes. These tools will improve the efficiency of the existing claims process, reduce future claims backlog, and will result in faster, more accurate and consistent decisions for Veterans and beneficiaries. ADS is not intended to replace trained claims processors – it provides tools to assist with development tasks at a time when VBA is receiving more claims than ever before.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,S5_OPTIMIZATION_DECISION_SUPPORT,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-24-4722,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03346,US_OMB_2025_03346,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Benefits Processing,UNKNOWN,Mail Automation Services,Department of Veterans Affairs; VBA: Veterans Benefits Administration; Benefits Processing; United States,"The most common outcomes are VBA End-Product establishment within the Veterans Benefits Management System (VBMS) and correct business line orientation for ingested submissions. However, MAS also triggers correspondence in certain circumstances and creates or adjusts VBMS notes, tracked items, and flashes. The MAS platform runs under the Veterans Benefits Administration Automation Platform (VBAAP).",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,MAS has completed over 2 million actions in the 2024 calendar year to date. It completes initial intake processing actions to support workload and claims management and has led to cost savings and increased efficiency - cost savings and increased efficiency data is available upon request.,"Mail Automation Services (MAS) is an if-this-then that (ITTT) logic-based service which is utilized to process inbound mail across the VBA enterprise, including the receipt of claims materials from Veterans, Veteran Service Organizations, and other stakeholders. The platform ingests and reviews approximately 40k packets of information per day, primarily derived from the Centralized Mail Portal. It utilizes prescribed machine learning and Natural Language Processing (NLP), Intelligent Form Recognition (IFR), Optical Character Recognition (OCR), and Intelligent Character Recognition (ICR) to extract and process data from an average of 95 fields on over 1,500 form layouts within VA’s purview.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,S3_DOCUMENT_INTELLIGENCE,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-24-4763,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03347,US_OMB_2025_03347,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Benefits Processing,"VBA’s POI is a transformative effort that seeks a Managed Services Provider (MSP) to convert an existing manual business process into automated processing of Pension, Dependency Indemnity Compensation (DIC), and Burial claims.",Pension Optimization Initiative (POI),Department of Veterans Affairs; VBA: Veterans Benefits Administration; Benefits Processing; United States,"1) updated Veteran/Beneficiary files, 2) completed Pension, DIC, and Burial-related claim actions to include stop and start of awards (delivery of benefits), 3) Notification Letters to Claimants.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Reduced average days to complete claims processing. Reduced claims inventory. Reduced amount of manual claims processing hours to accomplish mission.,"VBA’s POI is a transformative effort that seeks a Managed Services Provider (MSP) to convert an existing manual business process into automated processing of Pension, Dependency Indemnity Compensation (DIC), and Burial claims. This effort is focused on dramatically improving the Veteran Experience while significantly reducing costs. POI automation will process Pension, DIC, and Burial claims more quickly, consistently, and efficiently.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-24-790,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03348,US_OMB_2025_03348,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Admin Functions,"Prior to the D.AI solution, this process was highly manual, requiring significant labor resources that led to an ever-increasing backlog.",Privacy Act Automation,Department of Veterans Affairs; VBA: Veterans Benefits Administration; Admin Functions; United States,"The D.AI system retrieves documents based on the request type, as defined by VA, and then completes a preliminary processing review based on defined business rules for redaction. The request is then finalized by VA before release to the Veteran.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Since D.AI deployed, VA has processed over 25,000 cases through the system, using a smaller team of VA FTE to review and release these cases and reducing response time for lower complexity cases from over a month to less than 4 days. Overall, this solution increases the efficiency of CSD personnel, allowing them to release over a hundred cases a day instead of 3.5, reduces the cost to the government by allowing for eDelivery, and improving the Veteran experience by delivery of quicker and more accessible records.","VBA receives over 160,000 Privacy Act requests each year requiring personnel to retrieve, review, and release these records to the Veteran. Prior to the D.AI solution, this process was highly manual, requiring significant labor resources that led to an ever-increasing backlog. AI is used by the contractor to create a preliminary set of recommended redactions that accelerates the review for VBA staff.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-24-2545,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03349,US_OMB_2025_03349,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,HR,"Engaging eLearning helps reduce instructor burden and time in traditional classroom settings, which increases productivity. Efficient training development also helps reduce instructional design burden, especially amidst decreased hiring abilities.",Articulate 360: AI Assistant,Department of Veterans Affairs; VBA: Veterans Benefits Administration; HR; United States,"Text-to-voice audio, images, outlines, polls, quizzes, and sounds for training/eLearning.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"The Articulate AI Assistant helps build more engaging eLearning courses in a timely manner. The AI assistant can help generate text to voice audio, create images, create outlines, create polls/quizzes, etc. This enhances the end-user experience of training and increases efficiency in training development, which in turn provides cost savings related to the amount of time taken to develop training.","The ability to efficiently and quickly create interactive and engaging eLearning for VBA claims processors. Engaging eLearning helps reduce instructor burden and time in traditional classroom settings, which increases productivity. Efficient training development also helps reduce instructional design burden, especially amidst decreased hiring abilities.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-25-1471,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03350,US_OMB_2025_03350,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,HR,UNKNOWN,Customer Sentiment,Department of Veterans Affairs; VBA: Veterans Benefits Administration; HR; United States,The AI system assigns a number to customer comments between 0 and 1 with 1 being very positive comments.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Data assists in the proactive identification of ways to change customer service that can positively impact customer experience with teams.,Proactively identify drops in customer service as perceived by the customer.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-25-5163,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03351,US_OMB_2025_03351,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Admin Functions,UNKNOWN,Auto Doc ID,Department of Veterans Affairs; VBA: Veterans Benefits Administration; Admin Functions; United States,"Suggested doc ID. It provides document type suggestions in the ImageSort application to guide operators. D3P does not perform content-based analysis but makes technical image-quality determinations, such as: - Detecting and correcting image orientation (auto-rotation) - Identifying and removing image noise (de-speckling) - Determining and correcting crooked images (de-skewing) - Detecting whether images are in color, grayscale, or black-and-white - Preparing images for annotations by adjusting size and margins without altering the original text - All inbound images are standardized into TIF IV format for consistent downstream processing. It does not interpret meaning, generate content, or make adjudicative decisions.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"'- Time savings and higher quality - Improved OCR/Data Extraction Accuracy - clearer, properly aligned images increase recognition success for auto classification of Document ID. - Standardization for Automation - converting all documents into TIF IV ensures reliable document classification and processing. - Reduced Manual Corrections - automated alignment, noise removal, and skew correction minimize human intervention. - Preservation of Original Document Integrity - annotations are applied without altering original text, supporting compliance and readability. • Overall, the impacts are limited to operational efficiency and data accuracy. Correct extraction reduces manual data entry for document classification. The AI has no role in determining eligibility, adjudicating claims, or making benefit decisions""",The purpose of the tool is to convert inbound images into a standard format that is required for downstream processing for auto document classification and OCR/Data Extraction. After all document processing is completed and we are preparing the final output the images are converted back into a searchable PDF. Auto Doc ID provides suggestions to operators to decrease turn around time and increase quality.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,S3_DOCUMENT_INTELLIGENCE,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-25-733,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
