AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03365,US_OMB_2025_03365,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Health and Medical,UNKNOWN,Teledermatology Clinical Outcome Classification,Department of Veterans Affairs; VHA: Veterans Health Administration; Health and Medical; United States,Classification of clinical outcomes,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Measure and improve skin disease outcomes for both telehealth and in-person care.,This seeks to develop an NLP LLM tool that reviews dermatology and teledermatology clinical notes in the EHR and classify them into a clinical outcome category. Natural language processing is used to determine qualitative outcomes for skin diseases where quantitative metrics don't exist.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PRE_DEPLOYMENT,도입 전,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-24-3082,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
