AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03521,US_OMB_2025_03521,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Health and Medical,UNKNOWN,Philips 7300 C,Department of Veterans Affairs; VHA: Veterans Health Administration; Health and Medical; United States,Recommended settings for imaging process.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Smart Collimation Thorax reduces exam time by up to 35 seconds, resulting in potential daily time savings of 20 minutes for the medical team.","AI-assisted Smart Collimation Thorax algorithm, developed by Philips, adjusts detector height and proposes collimation for each chest upright patient individually, based upon data from a 3D Camera.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-25-4280,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03522,US_OMB_2025_03522,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Health and Medical,UNKNOWN,ARANZ Medical Silhouette Wound Management System,Department of Veterans Affairs; VHA: Veterans Health Administration; Health and Medical; United States,Charts and graphs representing wound progression and healing: Silhouette employs Machine Learning (ML) algorithms to automatically detect the wound boundary in an image of a wound that has been captured by the user.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Enhance patient outcome by providing non-biased wound metrics and healing data. Automatically detecting wounds in this manner can save the user time and improve the consistency of wound detection and the measurements that result.,"Evaluate parameter, depth, and area of a wound (image): The ARANZ Medical Silhouette system is employed in the VA for monitoring and tracking wounds.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-25-4673,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03523,US_OMB_2025_03523,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Health and Medical,UNKNOWN,VASQIP Mortality Calculator,Department of Veterans Affairs; VHA: Veterans Health Administration; Health and Medical; United States,The Veterans Affairs Surgical Quality Improvement Program (VASQIP) uses the Observed-to-Expected (O/E) ratio as a key metric to evaluate surgical outcomes. The O/E ratio is a statistical measure that compares the actual (observed) outcomes of surgical procedures to the expected outcomes based on national benchmarks and risk-adjusted models.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Increase Veteran safety for surgical procedures. Enhance patient outcomes by rigorously collecting and analyzing surgical data, identifying areas for improvement, and implementing evidence-based practices.","Tracking Surgical Outcomes: Collecting data on surgical procedures and outcomes, such as complications, morbidity, and mortality rates. Benchmarking Performance: Comparing surgical outcomes at VA facilities against national standards and best practices to identify areas where performance can be improved. Quality Improvement Initiatives: Implementing targeted interventions and quality improvement projects based on the analysis of collected data to enhance patient care. Reporting and Accountability: Providing regular reports on surgical outcomes and quality metrics to promote transparency and accountability within the VA healthcare system.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-25-4960,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03524,US_OMB_2025_03524,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Health and Medical,UNKNOWN,Frailty Risk Analysis,Department of Veterans Affairs; VHA: Veterans Health Administration; Health and Medical; United States,Risk analysis index score of frailty.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Alignment of recommended therapies with patient goals. There is a single threshold for a Risk Analysis Index (RAI) score over which severe frailty is considered to exist and that prompts clinicians to have additional discussions of goals of care with Veterans. There is no required action or mandated restriction of care.,Define frailty in surgical patients: screen for potential frailty in pre-surgical patients,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-25-5001,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03525,US_OMB_2025_03525,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Health and Medical,UNKNOWN,Butterfly iQ3 Ultrasound System,Department of Veterans Affairs; VHA: Veterans Health Administration; Health and Medical; United States,The purpose of the Auto B-line Counter is to provide automated detection and automatic calculation of the number of B-lines to a user in a given rib space and also provides the users the capabilities of reviewing the detected B-lines (via visual overlays). The overlay of B-lines does not mark images for detection of specific pathologies. The Auto B-line Counter enables the automated identification and count of B-lines during a lung scan and is integrated into the existing Butterfly iQ/iQ+ mobile application for use with the Butterfly iQ or iQ+ transducers.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Accelerates ultrasound workflows.,"The Butterfly iQ3 Ultrasound System is indicated for use by qualified and trained healthcare professionals to enable diagnostic ultrasound imaging and measurement of anatomical structures and fluids of adult and pediatric patients for the following clinical applications: Peripheral Vessel (including carotid, deep vein thrombosis and arterial studies), Small Organs (including thyroid, scrotum and breast), Cardiac, Abdominal, Lung, Procedural Guidance, Urology, Fetal/Obstetric, Gynecological, Musculoskeletal (conventional), Musculoskeletal (superficial) and Ophthalmic.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-25-5189,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
