AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03538,US_OMB_2025_03538,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Admin Functions,UNKNOWN,"Human-Centered Design (HCD) User Feedback Summary, Analysis, and Design",Department of Veterans Affairs; VHA: Veterans Health Administration; Admin Functions; United States,"Power BI dashboard consolidating app feedback across Mobile App (VA resource), Feedback UI (VA resource), Google, and Apple.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Faster insights, less manual labor for staff, and improved efficiency.","The Human-Centered Design (HCD) team uses Large Language Models (LLMs) and custom agents to enhance user experience (UX) research. The AI system streamlines tasks such as analyzing user feedback, generating user stories, summarizing workshop outcomes, and refining user personas. The primary purpose is to improve the accessibility and clarity of user feedback, providing a better understanding of the needs of veterans and healthcare providers. The main problem to be solved is to maximize insights with massive amounts of app feedback to drive change.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-24-3164,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03539,US_OMB_2025_03539,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Health and Medical,UNKNOWN,Vivid E80/ Vivid E90/ Vivid E95,Department of Veterans Affairs; VHA: Veterans Health Administration; Health and Medical; United States,Measurements of areas of interest.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Improve ultrasound workflows.,"Vivid E80 / Vivid E90 / Vivid E95 is a Track 3, diagnostic ultrasound system for use by qualified and trained healthcare professionals. It is primarily intended for cardiac imaging and analysis but also includes vascular and general radiology applications. It is a full featured diagnostic ultrasound system that provides digital acquisition, processing, analysis and display capabilities.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-24-3254,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03540,US_OMB_2025_03540,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Health and Medical,UNKNOWN,Avicenna CINA,Department of Veterans Affairs; VHA: Veterans Health Administration; Health and Medical; United States,"The user is presented with notifications on cases with suspected ICH or LVO findings. Notifications include compressed preview images - these are meant for informational purposes only and are not intended for diagnostic use beyond notification. The device does not alter the original medical image, and it is not intended to be used as a diagnostic device.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Accelerate detection of ICH and LVO.,The device is intended to assist hospital networks and trained radiologists in workflow triage by flagging and communicating suspected positive findings of (1) head CT images for Intracranial Hemorrhage (ICH) and (2) CT angiographies of the head for large vessel occlusion (LVO).,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-24-3373,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03541,US_OMB_2025_03541,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Health and Medical,UNKNOWN,CLARUS,Department of Veterans Affairs; VHA: Veterans Health Administration; Health and Medical; United States,Automated image merging.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"With a single capture, CLARUS 700 produces a 90º high definition widefield image. Widefield images are automatically merged to achieve a 135º ultra-widefield of view. The CLARUS 700 makes use of a deep learning algorithm for Optic Nerve Head (ONH) detection. The ultra-widefield montage on CLARUS 700 is no longer dependent just on the patient accurately fixating their gaze on the internal fixation. With the ONH detection, the software will find the optic nerve and determine based on the image(s) captured where the patient was gazing at the point of capture. The CLARUS 700 device allows clinicians to easily review and compare high-quality images captured during a single exam while providing annotation and caliper measurement tools that allow in-depth analysis of eye health. CLARUS 700 is designed to optimize each patient’s experience by providing a simple head and chin rest that allows the patient to maintain a stable, neutral position while the operator brings the optics to the patient, facilitating a more comfortable imaging experience. The ability to swivel the device between the right and left eye helps technicians capture an image without realigning the patient. Live Infrared (IR) Preview allows the technician to confirm image quality and screen for lid and lash obstructions, prior to imaging, ensuring fewer image recaptures.",The CLARUS 700 angiography imaging aids in the visualization of the vascular structures of the retina and the choroid.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-24-3418,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03542,US_OMB_2025_03542,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Admin Functions,UNKNOWN,BTSSS 3542 Review,Department of Veterans Affairs; VHA: Veterans Health Administration; Admin Functions; United States,Microsoft Power Platform AI modeling.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Reducing FTE time on process, increase 10 day metric for BTSSS submissions","Power Automate AI model that was trained on ZZpatients filled out on VA form 3542, and scans the PDF's to rename them for travel staff. Decrease the time that FTE was spent on renaming files and creating a dashboard to search and sort the files filled out by patients.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-24-3738,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03543,US_OMB_2025_03543,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Health and Medical,Solution to decrease the provider administrative burdens of typing medical notes.,Dragon Medical One,Department of Veterans Affairs; VHA: Veterans Health Administration; Health and Medical; United States,"DMO is an AI-powered speech recognition solution that utilizes advanced AI algorithms to deliver accurate, real-time medical transcription and drive voice-activated documentation workflows.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Enhancing patient outcomes by increasing provider-patient time, decreasing provider burnout, increasing efficiency in documentation, and therefore improving patient access due to providers having more availability to see patients.",Solution to decrease the provider administrative burdens of typing medical notes.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-24-4148,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03544,US_OMB_2025_03544,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Health and Medical,"While humans can generate word lists for text-matching approaches, the generated word lists are likely to be limited and biased by the vocabulary, language habits, population exposure, and local dialects of the human generating the list. Deep learning methods can help to augment candidate term lists to help overcome some of these challenges.",Deep-Learning approaches to develop candidate lists of terms for use in text searches,Department of Veterans Affairs; VHA: Veterans Health Administration; Health and Medical; United States,"The outputs of this use of AI is a candidate list of terms related to a concept of interest. This candidate list is combined with suggestions generated by human experts and then these are reviewed by a subject matter expert to generate a final list of terms for use in text-matching algorithms to extract medical record free text mentions of interest. For the pre-trained Large Language model approach, the input is a query prompting for synonyms of terms related to the concept of interest. The output is the answer provided by the LLM, including the suggested candidate terms and the original terms that were stated in the query. For the word and phrase embedding models, the input is an initial list of terms that are relevant to the concept of interest and the output are the suggested candidate terms, ranked by their statistical similarity to the original terms, based on the transformation of a clinical corpus into vector space or an “embedding model”. Regardless of the type of model used, all suggested candidate terms are reviewed by subject matter experts to ensure quality term lists are used in all text searches.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Here we (1) query pre-trained large language models (e.g., ChatGPT or Llama) through a user interface that allows prompting (such as the OpenAI API or CodeLlama) and/or (2) query word and phrase “embedding” models (e.g., Word2Vec and Phrase2Vec) to expand candidate term lists for review by subject matter experts. Our team has found both approaches effective for expediting the generation of more comprehensive term to concept mappings for use in text-matching algorithms that increase the accuracy of clinical concept extraction. We expect this use of AI to improve initial brainstorming of terms related to a given concept, resulting in a more sensitive approach to finding information of interest in free-text clinical notes. Experience to date has found that this approach enriches term sets in ways that increase sensitivity for identification of text of interest in clinical TIU notes when used in our CLEVER natural language processing pipeline.","The intended use is to increase the comprehensiveness of term lists to be used in text-matching approaches to identifying concepts of interest in free-text medical record notes. Text-matching approaches are an efficient method for identifying text of interest in medical notes. The success of text-matching approaches depends on the quality of term lists used to search for a concept of interest. While humans can generate word lists for text-matching approaches, the generated word lists are likely to be limited and biased by the vocabulary, language habits, population exposure, and local dialects of the human generating the list. Deep learning methods can help to augment candidate term lists to help overcome some of these challenges. Once generated these augmented candidate terms are reviewed by subject matter experts for appropriateness and accuracy of the suggested terms for the concept and use case of interest.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-24-4193,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03545,US_OMB_2025_03545,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Health and Medical,Try to identify which Veteran with breast cancer has or does not have access to germline genetic testing from unstructured medical notes.,Identify access to genetic testing in Veterans with breast cancer.,Department of Veterans Affairs; VHA: Veterans Health Administration; Health and Medical; United States,If the patient has access to germline genetic testing.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Providers are more aware of if a Veteran has access to germline genetic testing, this helps improve the quality of care VA delivers, since it is recommended to have germline genetic testing for everyone with breast cancer.",Try to identify which Veteran with breast cancer has or does not have access to germline genetic testing from unstructured medical notes.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,F04_UNSTRUCTURED_INFORMATION_COMPLEXITY,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-24-4472,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03546,US_OMB_2025_03546,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Health and Medical,UNKNOWN,Cardiac CT Function Software Application,Department of Veterans Affairs; VHA: Veterans Health Administration; Health and Medical; United States,Volume and mass estimates.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,"Automate volume and mass calculations to support physicians in the visualization, evaluation, and analysis of the heart function.","It is designed to support physicians in the visualization, evaluation, and analysis of the heart function through the calculation of parameters, such as volume and mass. The device is intended to be used as an aid to the existing standard of care and does not replace existing software applications that physicians use.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-24-5550,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_US_OMB_2025_03547,US_OMB_2025_03547,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,U.S. Office of Management and Budget,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Department of Veterans Affairs,Admin Functions,UNKNOWN,Purchase Order Filing,Department of Veterans Affairs; VHA: Veterans Health Administration; Admin Functions; United States,The AI creates a folder on Sharepoint for each purchase order and files the documents related to that purchase order in the folder. There is 1 folder for each purchase order and the purchase order number is the folder name.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,Having the AI file the documents online saves staff time and makes it easier to find the documents we need in the event of an audit.,Filing purchase orders and documents related to them is time consuming for pharmacy staff and the paper files take up floor space.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://github.com/ombegov/2025-Federal-Agency-AI-Use-Case-Inventory,VA-24-5628,U.S. federal public inventory; no separate repository LICENSE found; retain source attribution and review redistribution conditions,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
