AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02233,EU_PSTW_202609_02233,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Institute of statistics and economic studies (STATEC),General services.,UNKNOWN,Machine learning for statistics,National Institute of statistics and economic studies (STATEC); Central-Government; General services.; Luxembourg,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,The National Institute of statistics and economic studies (STATEC) will implement a data science and machine learning program to enable the production of statistics on the mobile telephone database.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,IN_DEVELOPMENT,개발 중,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2882,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02234,EU_PSTW_202609_02234,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Employment Agency ADEM,"General economic, commercial and labour affair",UNKNOWN,ADEM Interact - AI conversational platform for the Employment Agency,"Employment Agency ADEM; Central-Government; General economic, commercial and labour affair; Luxembourg",UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"ADEM Interact is an AI conversational platform that will assist state agents of the Employment Agency ADEM who receive messages from job seekers, by formulating personalised responses. This is expected to apply to emails and enquiries received via a new Chatbot service integrated into the ADEM website.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,S2_AGENT_CONVERSATIONAL_AI,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2883,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02235,EU_PSTW_202609_02235,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Employment Agency ADEM,"General economic, commercial and labour affair",UNKNOWN,ADEM Profiling,"Employment Agency ADEM; Central-Government; General economic, commercial and labour affair; Luxembourg",UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,ADEM Profiling will allow through the analysis of existing data at ADEM to develop a support model for their agents to assess which jobseekers need which measures and level of support to access employment. This diagnostic is possible by taking into consideration the characteristics and professional profile of the jobseeker.,SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2884,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02236,EU_PSTW_202609_02236,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,DEA (Distribution d'Eau des Ardennes),Water supply.,UNKNOWN,Anomaly detection: machine learning to detect water leaks,DEA (Distribution d'Eau des Ardennes); Local Government; Water supply.; Luxembourg,"The 'Anomaly detection' project is designed to enable the local authority association, DEA (Distribution d'Eau des Ardennes), to use machine learning to detect water leaks in the network and identify changes in a set of data with daily and seasonal differences.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"The 'Anomaly detection' project is designed to enable the local authority association, DEA (Distribution d'Eau des Ardennes), to use machine learning to detect water leaks in the network and identify changes in a set of data with daily and seasonal differences. The aim of this project is to increase the monitoring capabilities of the DEA, who is responsible for producing and distributing water to 29 municipalities in Luxembourg.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,S4_PREDICTION_DETECTION,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2885,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02237,EU_PSTW_202609_02237,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Ministry of Digitalisation,Law courts,UNKNOWN,Assitance in drafting judgments JUAIDE,Ministry of Digitalisation; Central-Government; Law courts; Luxembourg,"The initiative is relevant for digital justice because it applies AI to a core professional task in a controlled way, preserving the judge’s responsibility while improving access to the legal materials needed for high-quality decision-writing.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Judicial drafting requires rapid access to legal texts, previous court decisions and accurate references while the judge is developing the reasoning of a decision. JUAIDE supports this work by integrating an artificial intelligence component into the drafting process for legal documents. The system analyses the context of the text being written in real time and identifies legal sources that may be relevant to the point under development. Instead of requiring the judge to interrupt drafting in order to conduct separate legal research, JUAIDE brings potentially applicable legal texts and case law directly into the workflow. This reduces the time spent searching for references, strengthens the accuracy of citations and helps ensure that judicial reasoning is supported by relevant legal material. At operational level, the tool acts as a drafting and research assistant: it does not replace judicial reasoning, but helps the judge identify and verify sources more efficiently while preparing legal documents. Its value lies in combining contextual analysis with immediate access to authoritative legal information, allowing drafting to become more fluid and better supported. The expected impact is faster preparation of judgments, improved quality of legal references, reduced repetitive research work and greater efficiency in the judicial process. The initiative is relevant for digital justice because it applies AI to a core professional task in a controlled way, preserving the judge’s responsibility while improving access to the legal materials needed for high-quality decision-writing.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,IN_DEVELOPMENT,개발 중,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2886,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02238,EU_PSTW_202609_02238,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Land Registry and Topography Administration,General services.,"The operational challenge is that property-rights information from 1824 to 1972 was recorded manually in structured tables, creating a large archive that is valuable but difficult to exploit efficiently in modern digital workflows. Manual interpretation of these registers is time-consuming, specialist-dependent and not easily scalable across municipalities.",UrbIA - AI for cadastral data,Land Registry and Topography Administration; Central-Government; General services.; Luxembourg,"UrbIA is particularly relevant because it applies AI to a long-term institutional archive that remains essential for land administration, legal certainty and territorial information management.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Luxembourg’s cadastral data contain a long historical record of property information, including graphic materials such as cadastral plans and sketch maps and tabular records documenting changes in property rights. UrbIA supports the Land Registry and Topography Administration in making this historical information more usable by applying AI and data-interpretation methods to old handwritten cadastral registers. The operational challenge is that property-rights information from 1824 to 1972 was recorded manually in structured tables, creating a large archive that is valuable but difficult to exploit efficiently in modern digital workflows. Manual interpretation of these registers is time-consuming, specialist-dependent and not easily scalable across municipalities. UrbIA compares different technical approaches for interpreting selected registers in a given municipality, identifies the most effective method and then prepares implementation within the Administration. At operational level, the tool strengthens the digital transformation of cadastral management by converting historical handwritten information into data that can be searched, structured and reused more easily. The initiative helps preserve the continuity between historical land records and modern cadastral systems, improving access to information on property rights and supporting more efficient administrative processing. The expected impact is faster interpretation of historical registers, better integration of legacy cadastral data into contemporary systems, reduced manual workload and improved reliability of property-related public records. UrbIA is particularly relevant because it applies AI to a long-term institutional archive that remains essential for land administration, legal certainty and territorial information management.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,IN_DEVELOPMENT,개발 중,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2887,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02240,EU_PSTW_202609_02240,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research"", ""social_nonprofit""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Zenter fir d'Lëtzebuerger Sprooch (ZLS – Centre for Luxembourgish Language),Cultural services.,"The operational problem is that AI systems cannot provide reliable translation or language support for Luxembourgish unless they are trained on high-quality aligned texts that reflect real usage, terminology and linguistic variation.","""Iwwersetzungskorpus fir d'Lëtzebuergescht"" - multilingual parallel corpus",Zenter fir d'Lëtzebuerger Sprooch (ZLS – Centre for Luxembourgish Language); Non-governmental; Cultural services.; Luxembourg,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"High-quality machine translation and language AI depend on structured parallel datasets that show how the same content is expressed across different languages. Luxembourgish remains under-represented in such resources, creating barriers for translation technologies, language-model training and computational linguistics research. “Iwwersetzungskorpus fir d’Lëtzebuergescht” addresses this need by establishing a multilingual parallel corpus centred on Luxembourgish as the source language, with translations into German, French and English. The operational problem is that AI systems cannot provide reliable translation or language support for Luxembourgish unless they are trained on high-quality aligned texts that reflect real usage, terminology and linguistic variation. The corpus creates a reusable linguistic dataset that connects Luxembourgish with three major languages used in Luxembourg’s administrative, legal, educational and social environment. At operational level, the corpus provides the foundation for advanced machine translation, language-model training and multilingual public-service applications. It can also support researchers working on computational linguistics, language preservation and multilingual communication. The expected impact is improved digital treatment of Luxembourgish, better translation quality, stronger support for multilingual administration and greater inclusion of the national language in future AI systems. The initiative is particularly important because language technologies shape how citizens interact with public services, access information and participate in digital life. By building structured Luxembourgish-centred data, the project strengthens linguistic sovereignty and reduces dependence on datasets designed primarily for larger language markets.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,IN_DEVELOPMENT,개발 중,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2889,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02241,EU_PSTW_202609_02241,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""enterprise_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Commissariat aux affaires maritimes (CAM – Commission for Maritime Affairs),Transport,"The operational challenge is that customers and agents otherwise need to enter and verify data manually, creating delays, avoidable errors and repetitive administrative work. AI Reader reads incoming documents, identifies the relevant fields and extracts the required information without manual intervention.",AI Reader - enhancing the efficiency of data entry processes,Commissariat aux affaires maritimes (CAM – Commission for Maritime Affairs); Central-Government; Transport; Luxembourg,The initiative is relevant because it applies AI to a common but important public-administration bottleneck: transforming unstructured or semi-structured documents into reliable data that can be reused in business processes.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Maritime administrations handle official documents that contain structured data needed for service delivery, verification and case management. AI Reader supports the Commissariat aux affaires maritimes by automating the extraction of predefined information from documents such as visas, whether they are submitted as text-based PDFs, image PDFs or JPEG files. The operational challenge is that customers and agents otherwise need to enter and verify data manually, creating delays, avoidable errors and repetitive administrative work. In the Seafarers’ service, this can affect the efficiency of document handling and the quality of information injected into administrative systems. AI Reader reads incoming documents, identifies the relevant fields and extracts the required information without manual intervention. At operational level, the tool reduces the amount of data that customers must provide directly, limits errors at the point of entry and reduces the need for later verification and correction by CAM agents. The extracted information can then be automatically integrated into the relevant internal systems, improving workflow continuity between document submission and case processing. The expected impact is faster handling of seafarer-related services, fewer data-entry mistakes, reduced administrative burden and a more streamlined user experience for applicants. The initiative is relevant because it applies AI to a common but important public-administration bottleneck: transforming unstructured or semi-structured documents into reliable data that can be reused in business processes. This type of document automation creates practical efficiency gains while preserving administrative control over final validation and service delivery.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,IN_DEVELOPMENT,개발 중,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK|F08_ERROR_COMPLIANCE_RISK,S3_DOCUMENT_INTELLIGENCE,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2890,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02242,EU_PSTW_202609_02242,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Commission for Data Protection’s (CNPD),General public services n.e.c.,"The operational challenge is that, as the number of questions and answers grows, staff need to search through existing databases and previous responses manually, which can be time-consuming and may slow down the delivery of consistent guidance.",AI4DI - AI-Powered Automation of Information Requests,National Commission for Data Protection’s (CNPD); Central-Government; General public services n.e.c.; Luxembourg,"AI4DI uses a large language model-based tool to identify relevant information in the existing knowledge base and produce an initial draft response that staff can review. The initiative is relevant because it applies AI to a regulatory authority’s public-information function, helping manage growing demand while maintaining human oversight in a legally sensitive domain.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Data-protection authorities receive a wide range of information requests from citizens, organisations and professionals, often through multiple channels such as email, post and telephone. AI4DI supports the National Commission for Data Protection by automating the retrieval of relevant information and the preparation of draft responses for its Information Requests service. The operational challenge is that, as the number of questions and answers grows, staff need to search through existing databases and previous responses manually, which can be time-consuming and may slow down the delivery of consistent guidance. AI4DI uses a large language model-based tool to identify relevant information in the existing knowledge base and produce an initial draft response that staff can review. At operational level, the system acts as a knowledge-retrieval and drafting assistant: it accelerates the first stage of response preparation while leaving final validation and responsibility with CNPD staff. This is particularly useful in a field such as data protection, where many questions recur but must still be answered accurately and in line with current rules and institutional positions. The expected impact is shorter response preparation time, greater consistency across replies, better reuse of accumulated institutional knowledge and improved service capacity for citizens and organisations seeking guidance. The initiative is relevant because it applies AI to a regulatory authority’s public-information function, helping manage growing demand while maintaining human oversight in a legally sensitive domain.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,IN_DEVELOPMENT,개발 중,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,S7_GENERATIVE_CONTENT_CREATION,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2891,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02243,EU_PSTW_202609_02243,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Luxembourg Office of Accreditation and Surveillance (OLAS),"General economic, commercial and labour affair","The operational challenge is that OLAS needs to identify, collect and interpret relevant documents from recognised sources such as Legilux, EUR-Lex, ISO, CEN, EA, ILAC and IAF, as well as locally stored files, in order to determine applicable requirements for the accreditation of specific activities. Manual review can be time-consuming and requires specialist knowledge across multiple sources and standards.",Legal and normative text analyser,"Luxembourg Office of Accreditation and Surveillance (OLAS); Central-Government; General economic, commercial and labour affair; Luxembourg","The initiative is relevant because it applies AI to a highly specialised compliance function where reliability, source quality and structured reporting are essential for institutional credibility and for the proper supervision of accredited activities.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Accreditation bodies must work with complex and frequently updated legal, technical and normative materials, including national laws, EU law, international standards and accreditation requirements. The Legal and Normative Text Analyser supports the Luxembourg Office of Accreditation and Surveillance by automating parts of this documentation analysis. The operational challenge is that OLAS needs to identify, collect and interpret relevant documents from recognised sources such as Legilux, EUR-Lex, ISO, CEN, EA, ILAC and IAF, as well as locally stored files, in order to determine applicable requirements for the accreditation of specific activities. Manual review can be time-consuming and requires specialist knowledge across multiple sources and standards. The tool analyses reliable databases and local files, identifies relevant documents or information demonstrating compliance, extracts applicable requirements and generates detailed reports based on the results. At operational level, it functions as a regulatory and normative intelligence assistant for accreditation workflows. It helps staff move more quickly from a broad documentation search to a structured understanding of which requirements apply to a conformity assessment body or activity. The expected impact is faster accreditation preparation, more consistent identification of applicable requirements, reduced manual effort and improved traceability in the analysis of legal and normative sources. The initiative is relevant because it applies AI to a highly specialised compliance function where reliability, source quality and structured reporting are essential for institutional credibility and for the proper supervision of accredited activities.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,IN_DEVELOPMENT,개발 중,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,S7_GENERATIVE_CONTENT_CREATION,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2892,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02244,EU_PSTW_202609_02244,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Government Information and Press Service,Sickness and disability.,UNKNOWN,ScreenreaderLB - AI-Powered Luxembourgish Accessibility for the Visually Impaired,Government Information and Press Service; Central-Government; Sickness and disability.; Luxembourg,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"The ScreenreaderLB solution, developed by the Government Information and Press Service, addresses the increasing need for accessible content in Luxembourgish for visually impaired users. Currently, the absence of speech synthesis technology for this language requires blind or visually impaired individuals to rely on screen readers in German or other languages. ScreenreaderLB aims to create a screen reader specifically for Luxembourgish, providing smooth and accurate speech synthesis to allow visually impaired users to interact more effectively with digital content, enhancing both their browsing experience and access to information.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2893,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02245,EU_PSTW_202609_02245,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Municipality of Chieti,General public services n.e.c.,UNKNOWN,Digitalising key administrative processes using blockchain technology in the Municipality of Chieti,Municipality of Chieti; Local Government; General public services n.e.c.; Italy,"The Municipality of Chieti use case applies blockchain technology to selected administrative processes in order to strengthen traceability, automate parts of the workflow and improve trust in the handling of citizens’ information. The case is significant because it applies blockchain to ordinary municipal administration, not only to financial or experimental digital-asset use cases.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Municipal social-service procedures often involve sensitive information, repeated documentation and several administrative steps, making transparency, data integrity and processing times particularly important for citizens. The Municipality of Chieti use case applies blockchain technology to selected administrative processes in order to strengthen traceability, automate parts of the workflow and improve trust in the handling of citizens’ information. The operational problem is that many social-service files require the municipality to verify eligibility, manage documentation and preserve the chronology of procedural steps, while also respecting privacy rules and avoiding unnecessary repeated requests for the same data. The project, supported by Mangrovia Blockchain Solutions and A Software Factory, integrates a distributed ledger into the management of specific municipal practices. Initial experimental processes included maternity allowances, elderly home-care access, transport services for persons with disabilities, socio-health contribution requests for residential care, educational home-care support for sensory disabilities and home-care services for disabled persons. At a conceptual level, blockchain is used as an administrative integrity layer: it certifies data ownership, chronology and process steps, while smart contracts can support secure automation and the “once only” principle. The expected impact is greater transparency, reduced manipulation risk, faster handling of socially relevant files and a stronger basis for extending similar traceability to procurement and accounts-payable workflows. The case is significant because it applies blockchain to ordinary municipal administration, not only to financial or experimental digital-asset use cases.",NON_AI_OR_UNCONFIRMED_TECHNOLOGY,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2894,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02246,EU_PSTW_202609_02246,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research"", ""social_nonprofit"", ""enterprise_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Municipality of Cosenza,Social protection n.e.c.,UNKNOWN,Blockchain Pilot for Transparent Food Redistribution in Cosenza,Municipality of Cosenza; Local Government; Social protection n.e.c.; Italy,"The Cosenza pilot applies blockchain technology to the reuse of near-expiry food stocks from large-scale retail distribution, with the aim of reducing waste and increasing the resources available to families in need.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Food redistribution programmes need to connect supermarkets, charities, municipal welfare services and vulnerable households in a way that is efficient, transparent and credible for all participants. The Cosenza pilot applies blockchain technology to the reuse of near-expiry food stocks from large-scale retail distribution, with the aim of reducing waste and increasing the resources available to families in need. The operational problem is that surplus food redistribution involves several actors and incentives: retailers need confidence that donations are properly certified, charities need reliable information on available goods, and public authorities need visibility over social needs and the actual destination of donated products. The project was launched by the Municipality of Cosenza with NTT DATA, the University of Calabria and Banco Alimentare. The University of Calabria contributed a mathematical model to support the platform, including the calculation of rewards for donating businesses according to the characteristics of the products and the social benefit generated. Blockchain is used to certify donations, preserve traceability and ensure data immutability across the redistribution chain. At a conceptual level, the system transforms food donation into a verifiable welfare process: goods approaching expiry can be recorded, assigned, rewarded and distributed with greater transparency. The expected impact is lower food waste, greater availability of goods for non-profit organisations, clearer evidence on local social needs and stronger incentives for businesses to participate in solidarity-based redistribution. The case is relevant because it connects blockchain with welfare policy and circular economy objectives.",NON_AI_OR_UNCONFIRMED_TECHNOLOGY,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2895,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02247,EU_PSTW_202609_02247,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Borgo d’Anaunia,Fuel and energy,"Small municipalities with renewable-energy assets often face the challenge of making local infrastructure financially sustainable while complying with rules that limit direct self-consumption of municipally generated energy. Borgo d’Anaunia, a municipality of around 2,500 residents in northern Italy, addressed this challenge by converting part of the output of its municipal hydroelectric plant into computational power for blockchain operations.",Italy’s First Green Blockchain Municipality,Borgo d’Anaunia; Local Government; Fuel and energy; Italy,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Small municipalities with renewable-energy assets often face the challenge of making local infrastructure financially sustainable while complying with rules that limit direct self-consumption of municipally generated energy. Borgo d’Anaunia, a municipality of around 2,500 residents in northern Italy, addressed this challenge by converting part of the output of its municipal hydroelectric plant into computational power for blockchain operations. The operational problem was economic as well as technological: the century-old hydroelectric plant depended on variable water flow, electricity prices were relatively low, and fixed maintenance costs reduced the plant’s value for the municipality. By partnering with Alps Blockchain, the municipality installed mining equipment powered by renewable hydroelectric energy, allowing part of the plant’s output to be monetised as computational power rather than only as electricity sold to the grid. At a conceptual level, the project treats blockchain mining as a local revenue-generating service connected to renewable energy production. The system is designed to remain adaptable to hydrological conditions: when water flow is insufficient, the mining equipment can be switched off, while the remaining energy continues to be sold through conventional channels. The expected impact is higher revenue from an existing public asset, experimentation with more sustainable blockchain operations and a new model for small municipalities seeking to valorise renewable-energy infrastructure. The case is significant because it links blockchain with local public finance and renewable energy, although its primary purpose is municipal revenue generation rather than direct citizen-service delivery.",NON_AI_OR_UNCONFIRMED_TECHNOLOGY,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2896,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02248,EU_PSTW_202609_02248,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,City of Miglianico,Waste management.,UNKNOWN,Blockchain for waste management,City of Miglianico; Local Government; Waste management.; Italy,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Waste-management systems require accurate data on how much waste households produce and how correctly they separate recyclable fractions, especially where municipalities want to apply “polluter pays” principles or reward responsible behaviour. Miglianico, a municipality in the province of Chieti, introduced a blockchain-enhanced waste-management system built around RFID-tagged bins and certified tracking of individual waste contributions. The operational problem was to make waste collection more transparent, measurable and fair, while also reducing costs and encouraging citizens to separate waste properly. The municipality had already adopted an RFID-based system that allowed collection operators to identify bins and measure contributions. Blockchain was then added to certify the resulting data, making records more secure, immutable and auditable. At a conceptual level, the system creates a trusted data layer for timely waste charging and behavioural incentives: each household’s waste contributions can be associated with certified records, supporting more accurate tax calculation, management control and feedback on abnormal waste patterns. The reported results were substantial: separate collection reached nearly 85%, waste-collection expenditure fell from around €900,000 to around €660,000, and virtuous citizens reportedly benefited from savings and rewards. The expected impact is lower municipal expenditure, higher recycling performance, more transparent waste taxation and greater citizen engagement in circular-economy practices. The case is relevant because it demonstrates blockchain as an integrity mechanism for local public-service data, integrated with RFID and incentive-based waste policy rather than used as a stand-alone technology.",NON_AI_OR_UNCONFIRMED_TECHNOLOGY,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2897,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02249,EU_PSTW_202609_02249,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research"", ""enterprise_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,University of Torino,Economic affairs n.e.c,UNKNOWN,Blockchain-based platform for sustainable tourism and local commerce in mountain communities,University of Torino; Academic-Research; Economic affairs n.e.c; Italy,"Using the CommonsHood wallet app, tourists can collect tokens, redeem coupons via QR codes, and earn badges for completing circuits of local businesses.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"BLOCCHI is a blockchain-based platform developed by the University of Turin to promote sustainable tourism and local commerce in mountain communities. Integrating blockchain with an interactive map (FirstLife), it enables tokenisation to create incentives, loyalty programs, and rewards for visiting lesser-known locations and purchasing local products. Using the CommonsHood wallet app, tourists can collect tokens, redeem coupons via QR codes, and earn badges for completing circuits of local businesses. Local businesses and municipalities can create promotional coupons and track engagement. The project is part of NODES, funded by Italy’s PNRR and the EU, aiming to strengthen innovation ecosystems and local leadership in research and development.",NON_AI_OR_UNCONFIRMED_TECHNOLOGY,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2898,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02250,EU_PSTW_202609_02250,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Municipality of Bari,"General economic, commercial and labour affair",UNKNOWN,Blockchain for smart working,"Municipality of Bari; Local Government; General economic, commercial and labour affair; Italy","The project envisaged a prototype using Ethereum distributed-ledger technology combined with advanced encryption techniques. The case is relevant because it applies blockchain to internal public-administration work organisation, rather than to external registries or citizen-facing payments.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Public administrations that introduce smart working need to manage flexible work arrangements while ensuring accountability, data protection, traceability and continuity of service delivery. The Municipality of Bari smart-working pilot, developed with Fincons Group under the EU-funded H2020 CITADEL initiative, applied blockchain technology to support secure and transparent management of agile work by municipal employees. The operational problem was that smart working requires new forms of performance monitoring and organisational control: employees may work partly from offices and partly remotely, with flexible time arrangements, but the administration still needs reliable evidence of work processes, security of information and compliance with GDPR. The project envisaged a prototype using Ethereum distributed-ledger technology combined with advanced encryption techniques. At a conceptual level, blockchain is used as a trust and traceability layer for work-related data, certifying information flows and preserving integrity without compromising privacy. The pilot also reflects a wider shift in public administration towards more citizen-centred, inclusive and efficient digital services, because internal working models influence the quality and continuity of services offered to users. The expected impact is improved organisational flexibility, better employee work-life balance, secure data handling, more efficient administrative processes and a practical demonstration of innovative ICT adoption in local government. The case is relevant because it applies blockchain to internal public-administration work organisation, rather than to external registries or citizen-facing payments.",NON_AI_OR_UNCONFIRMED_TECHNOLOGY,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2899,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02251,EU_PSTW_202609_02251,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,European Commission,Public order and safety n.e.c.,"The operational challenge is that fact-checking individual claims is necessary but insufficient when manipulative campaigns spread through broader stories, frames and emotional patterns that can reappear across languages and platforms.",PROMPT - Narrative Intelligence for Information Integrity,European Commission; European Institution/Agency; Public order and safety n.e.c.; European Union,"The case is significant because it applies AI to democratic resilience while preserving the analytical role of journalists, researchers and civil-society organisations.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Disinformation campaigns increasingly rely on recurring narratives, rhetorical patterns and coordinated circulation across media outlets, social platforms and online knowledge spaces. PROMPT, or Predictive Research On Misinformation & Propagation Trajectories, addresses this problem by developing AI-supported narrative intelligence for information integrity. The operational challenge is that fact-checking individual claims is necessary but insufficient when manipulative campaigns spread through broader stories, frames and emotional patterns that can reappear across languages and platforms. PROMPT analyses large volumes of textual data to identify malicious or manipulative narratives, focusing on case studies such as the war in Ukraine, LGBTQI+ rights and the 2024 European elections. The project combines large language models with dynamic network analysis to detect formal patterns across media outlets, social networks and Wikipedia in eight languages. At a conceptual level, the system moves from isolated content detection to narrative mapping: it seeks to understand how misleading stories are structured, how they travel, which actors amplify them and why they resonate with audiences. Outputs include a refined language model, a narrative-monitoring dashboard and training material for civil-society actors. The expected impact is stronger disinformation analysis, better support for journalists and fact-checkers, earlier recognition of manipulation strategies and improved public understanding of information threats. The case is significant because it applies AI to democratic resilience while preserving the analytical role of journalists, researchers and civil-society organisations.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2900,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02252,EU_PSTW_202609_02252,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Diputación Provincial de Castellón / Provincial Council of Castellón,General public services n.e.c.,"The case addresses a structural public sector challenge: many local governments lack the technical, organisational and legal capacity to deploy AI safely. Its aim is to make AI adoption feasible for local administrations with limited resources, while supporting better services, administrative innovation and evidence-informed policy-making across the province.","Provinc.IA: a provincial AI governance and pilot framework for trustworthy, reusable and interoperable AI adoption in local governments",Diputación Provincial de Castellón / Provincial Council of Castellón; Local Government; General public services n.e.c.; Spain,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Provinc.IA is the Artificial Intelligence Strategy of the Provincial Council of Castellón, Spain. It provides a provincial governance and pilot framework to help small and medium-sized municipalities adopt AI in a trustworthy, legally sound, useful and reusable way. The case addresses a structural public sector challenge: many local governments lack the technical, organisational and legal capacity to deploy AI safely. Provinc.IA combines strategic planning, multi-level governance, stakeholder mapping, ethical and legal safeguards, pilot projects, monitoring mechanisms and capacity-building. Its aim is to make AI adoption feasible for local administrations with limited resources, while supporting better services, administrative innovation and evidence-informed policy-making across the province.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,IN_DEVELOPMENT,개발 중,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2901,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02253,EU_PSTW_202609_02253,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,PagoPA,General public services n.e.c.,The initiative responds to the challenge of moving autonomous-driving technologies from controlled environments into real public-service mobility settings.,AI-powered virtual assistant for payments,PagoPA; Central-Government; General public services n.e.c.; Italy,"The initiative also connects transport innovation with broader regional industrial policy, using Turin’s automotive strengths to support the transition towards software-defined, AI-enabled and service-oriented mobility.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Turin and the Piedmont Region are positioning the city as a European laboratory for autonomous urban mobility, combining the region’s automotive heritage, research capacity and urban infrastructure with AI-enabled transport experimentation. The initiative responds to the challenge of moving autonomous-driving technologies from controlled environments into real public-service mobility settings. Turin’s candidacy aims to secure a formal role within the European network of pilot cities for autonomous driving, with the ambition of testing driverless public mobility services such as taxis or shuttles on public roads. The city’s ecosystem provides strong enabling conditions, including the Politecnico di Torino, an established automotive supply chain, existing innovation infrastructure and previous experimentation around the university campus area. AI models are expected to support real-world testing by monitoring vehicle flows and helping analyse traffic conditions during trials. At operational level, the initiative would allow public authorities, researchers and industry actors to test autonomous vehicles in an urban environment where safety, service quality and interaction with ordinary traffic can be assessed under realistic conditions. The expected impact is stronger European leadership in autonomous mobility, attraction of investment, development of local expertise and creation of a model for AI-supported public transport innovation. The initiative also connects transport innovation with broader regional industrial policy, using Turin’s automotive strengths to support the transition towards software-defined, AI-enabled and service-oriented mobility.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,IN_DEVELOPMENT,개발 중,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2902,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02254,EU_PSTW_202609_02254,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,iDoctors,Outpatient services.,UNKNOWN,Sof-IA: management of online medical appointments,iDoctors; Private sector; Outpatient services.; Italy,"Sof-IA, developed by iDoctors, addresses this problem by using artificial intelligence to make the search for a suitable medical specialist faster and more personalised. The case is relevant because it applies AI to navigation and matching in healthcare, while explicitly limiting the system’s role to search support rather than clinical decision-making.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Patients looking for healthcare appointments often know their symptoms, preferences and constraints, but not the exact specialist, service or search criteria they should select on a booking platform. Sof-IA, developed by iDoctors, addresses this problem by using artificial intelligence to make the search for a suitable medical specialist faster and more personalised. The operational problem is that conventional search filters require users to know how to translate their need into a speciality, procedure, location, cost range or availability window. Sof-IA allows users to describe their request in natural language, including symptoms, location, preferred time, budget and other practical needs, and then returns specialists matching those criteria. For example, a user can ask for a dermatologist in a specific area, a gynaecologist available at a certain time, or a doctor within a maximum price range. At a conceptual level, the system acts as a natural-language interpretation layer above the iDoctors search engine: it analyses the patient’s request, extracts relevant constraints and maps them to structured search results. Importantly, iDoctors states that Sof-IA is not designed to provide diagnoses or recommend treatments, but only to help users identify the specialist they need. The expected impact is easier appointment search, better matching between patient needs and available professionals, reduced friction for users unfamiliar with medical terminology and a more accessible digital healthcare booking experience. The case is relevant because it applies AI to navigation and matching in healthcare, while explicitly limiting the system’s role to search support rather than clinical decision-making.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2903,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02255,EU_PSTW_202609_02255,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Romanian Ministry of Education and Research,Education not definable by level.,"The initiative addresses a major challenge in education systems: learners often need personalised feedback and encouragement, while teachers and institutions face growing demands for monitoring progress, supporting different learning needs and reducing bureaucratic workload.",Saro: AI-powered educational digital assistant,Romanian Ministry of Education and Research; Central-Government; Education not definable by level.; Romania,"Saro is an AI-powered educational assistant designed to support pupils, students and teachers in Romania by improving learning engagement, motivation and administrative efficiency. Saro uses artificial intelligence to provide personalised support, motivational analysis and guidance on learning tasks.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Saro is an AI-powered educational assistant designed to support pupils, students and teachers in Romania by improving learning engagement, motivation and administrative efficiency. The initiative addresses a major challenge in education systems: learners often need personalised feedback and encouragement, while teachers and institutions face growing demands for monitoring progress, supporting different learning needs and reducing bureaucratic workload. Saro uses artificial intelligence to provide personalised support, motivational analysis and guidance on learning tasks. Its role is to help students remain engaged, complete assignments and receive assistance that is adapted to their learning path, while also supporting teachers in understanding where additional intervention may be needed. At operational level, the assistant can help structure learning objectives, provide feedback, identify patterns of reduced engagement and support more continuous interaction between students and educational institutions. It is introduced through a partnership between Digital Nation and the Romanian Ministry of Education and Research, building on Digital Nation’s broader experience in digital skills programmes for students, teachers, SMEs and adult learners. The expected impact is stronger student motivation, improved assignment completion, reduced risk of dropout, more personalised educational support and less administrative pressure on teachers. The initiative is relevant because it embeds AI into the national education system as a practical support layer for both learning and institutional management. It also reflects a wider move towards AI-assisted education in Romania, where digital tools are used not only for content delivery but also for engagement, retention and learner success.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2904,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02256,EU_PSTW_202609_02256,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Italian Senate of the Republic,"Executive and legislative organs, financial and fiscal affairs, external affairs.","This creates a practical burden for legislative offices, committees and parliamentary staff who must organise, compare and process amendments efficiently. The operational problem is that duplicate or near-duplicate amendments can slow legislative analysis, make debates harder to organise and reduce the transparency of the amendment-review process.",Similis: for the identification of similar and identical amendments,"Italian Senate of the Republic; Central-Government; Executive and legislative organs, financial and fiscal affairs, external affairs.; Italy",The GitHub repository indicates that the tool can be invoked either through a REST interface or from the command line using a JSON file containing amendments.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Parliamentary amendment procedures can generate very large numbers of texts, many of which are identical or highly similar. This creates a practical burden for legislative offices, committees and parliamentary staff who must organise, compare and process amendments efficiently. Similis was developed by the IT Department of the Italian Senate in collaboration with the Institute of Legal Informatics and Judicial Systems of the National Research Council to calculate similarity between Senate amendments. The operational problem is that duplicate or near-duplicate amendments can slow legislative analysis, make debates harder to organise and reduce the transparency of the amendment-review process. Similis addresses this by automatically comparing amendment texts and grouping those with similar wording. The system is oriented towards syntactic similarity rather than full semantic interpretation, meaning that it is particularly useful for identifying amendments with similar structure, vocabulary and phrasing. At a conceptual level, each amendment is represented computationally and compared against others so that clusters of similar texts can be identified. The GitHub repository indicates that the tool can be invoked either through a REST interface or from the command line using a JSON file containing amendments. The expected impact is more efficient parliamentary document management, faster identification of duplicated proposals, better organisation of legislative work and support for transparency in amendment handling. The case is relevant because it demonstrates a focused, explainable and open-source digital tool for legislative support, rather than a broad autonomous AI system.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2905,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02257,EU_PSTW_202609_02257,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,City of Espoo,Transport,"DataTalks, presented by NinjaLabo during Espoo’s AI in Mobility Challenge, addresses this problem by creating a natural-language interface to urban data.",AI Mobility Challenge - DataTalks,City of Espoo; Local Government; Transport; Finland,"Cities increasingly collect mobility, parking, weather and infrastructure data, but much of this information remains difficult for residents and visitors to use in everyday decisions. The expected impact is easier access to city data, reduced unnecessary driving, smarter journey planning and better use of existing infrastructure.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Cities increasingly collect mobility, parking, weather and infrastructure data, but much of this information remains difficult for residents and visitors to use in everyday decisions. DataTalks, presented by NinjaLabo during Espoo’s AI in Mobility Challenge, addresses this problem by creating a natural-language interface to urban data. The operational problem is that users may need to combine several sources of information before making a simple mobility choice: whether there is parking available, whether weather conditions make walking or cycling practical, or whether a trip can be planned more efficiently. DataTalks connects to different data interfaces and allows users to ask ordinary-language questions such as whether there is space in a specific parking garage and whether they need an umbrella outside. At a conceptual level, the service acts as a conversational data broker: it translates a user’s practical question into queries against parking, weather and potentially other urban datasets, then returns an integrated answer. The expected impact is easier access to city data, reduced unnecessary driving, smarter journey planning and better use of existing infrastructure. The case is significant because it demonstrates how AI can make open or municipal data more actionable for non-technical users. Rather than presenting a dashboard that requires interpretation, the tool provides answers in a form closer to how people make daily travel decisions. It remains a challenge-stage solution rather than a confirmed deployed municipal service, but it illustrates a promising direction for AI-enabled citizen mobility support.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2906,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02258,EU_PSTW_202609_02258,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,City of Espoo,Public order and safety n.e.c.,"It should be treated as a challenge-stage or potential pilot solution, since the available source describes it as one of several ideas being refined within Espoo’s AI Mobility Challenge.",AI Mobility Challenge - CamTalks,City of Espoo; Local Government; Public order and safety n.e.c.; Finland,"CamTalks, presented by NinjaLabo during Espoo’s AI in Mobility Challenge, addresses this tension by using edge computing to analyse camera feeds locally.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Smart-city cameras can support traffic and public-space management, but they also raise privacy concerns if raw images are transmitted, stored or analysed centrally. CamTalks, presented by NinjaLabo during Espoo’s AI in Mobility Challenge, addresses this tension by using edge computing to analyse camera feeds locally. The operational problem is that city authorities may want information such as how many people are present in a scene, whether a space is crowded, or whether mobility conditions are changing, but they do not necessarily need to retain identifiable images. CamTalks processes video data on site rather than sending raw footage to the cloud, allowing users to ask simple questions such as “how many people are in the picture?” and receive an answer based on local AI analysis. At a conceptual level, the system turns camera feeds into metadata while reducing exposure of personal data. This is important because urban AI systems must balance situational awareness with citizens’ rights to privacy and proportionality. The expected impact is improved real-time understanding of urban movement, better support for transport or event management, and reduced data-protection risks compared with centralised video analytics. The case is relevant because it shows a privacy-preserving design principle for AI-enabled cities: computation can be moved to the edge, and only necessary outputs can be shared. It should be treated as a challenge-stage or potential pilot solution, since the available source describes it as one of several ideas being refined within Espoo’s AI Mobility Challenge.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2907,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02259,EU_PSTW_202609_02259,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,City of Espoo,Transport,UNKNOWN,AI Mobility Challenge - 0Flow,City of Espoo; Local Government; Transport; Finland,"0Flow, presented by Finnish Logistics Group during Espoo’s AI in Mobility Challenge, addresses this problem by using AI and data to improve utilisation of transport capacity. 0Flow proposes to optimise freight loads and route planning so that vehicles make better use of available space and reduce underutilised movements.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Urban freight and service logistics generate emissions when vehicles travel with unused capacity, poorly coordinated routes or unnecessary trips. 0Flow, presented by Finnish Logistics Group during Espoo’s AI in Mobility Challenge, addresses this problem by using AI and data to improve utilisation of transport capacity. The operational problem is that many freight trips are not fully loaded or are planned without a complete view of available capacity, demand and routing possibilities. This creates avoidable traffic, emissions and operating costs. 0Flow proposes to optimise freight loads and route planning so that vehicles make better use of available space and reduce underutilised movements. At a conceptual level, the system treats urban logistics as an optimisation problem: available vehicles, parcels, destinations, time windows and route constraints can be analysed together to identify more efficient combinations. AI can support matching demand with capacity, grouping deliveries, reducing empty or partially empty trips and improving operational planning. The expected impact is lower transport-related emissions, fewer unnecessary kilometres, improved logistics efficiency and better use of existing vehicle fleets. The case is relevant because city climate strategies often focus on passenger mobility, while freight and service traffic also contribute materially to emissions and congestion. 0Flow shows how AI can support the less visible logistics layer of urban mobility. However, it should be framed as a challenge-stage solution under development, not as an already implemented citywide freight-optimisation platform.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,S5_OPTIMIZATION_DECISION_SUPPORT,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2908,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02260,EU_PSTW_202609_02260,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,City of Espoo,Transport,UNKNOWN,AI Mobility Challenge - Traffic Info,City of Espoo; Local Government; Transport; Finland,"Traffic Info, presented by Cadweiser during Espoo’s AI in Mobility Challenge, addresses this issue by using AI to generate traffic updates and announcements in natural language, both written and spoken. Like the other Espoo challenge entries, Traffic Info should be classified as a solution in development or pilot preparation rather than a confirmed deployed municipal service.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Mobility information is only useful if people can access it quickly, understand it and apply it to their journey decisions. In multilingual urban environments, standard traffic bulletins or map-based alerts may not be equally accessible to all residents, commuters or visitors. Traffic Info, presented by Cadweiser during Espoo’s AI in Mobility Challenge, addresses this issue by using AI to generate traffic updates and announcements in natural language, both written and spoken. The operational problem is that traffic data may exist in structured systems, but users need understandable messages in the language and format most convenient to them. Traffic Info proposes a multilingual AI layer that can transform transport information into accessible announcements, improving communication about disruptions, congestion, route changes or travel conditions. At a conceptual level, the system connects mobility data with language generation: raw traffic information is translated into user-facing communication that can be delivered through speech or text. The expected impact is better access to real-time mobility information, improved inclusion for residents and visitors with different language backgrounds, smoother journey planning and potentially more efficient traffic flow as users adjust behaviour based on clearer information. The case is significant because it focuses on communication as a mobility intervention. Better transport systems do not only require sensors and infrastructure; they also require people to receive the right information in a usable form. Like the other Espoo challenge entries, Traffic Info should be classified as a solution in development or pilot preparation rather than a confirmed deployed municipal service.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2909,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02261,EU_PSTW_202609_02261,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,City of Espoo,Transport,"The operational problem is that manual scheduling may not fully account for geography, time windows, task duration, staff availability and route efficiency. At a conceptual level, the tool treats field-service work as a routing and allocation optimisation challenge: AI can analyse tasks, locations and constraints to recommend sequences that reduce unnecessary kilometres.",AI Mobility Challenge - Dynamik Allocator,City of Espoo; Local Government; Transport; Finland,"Mobile workers such as service technicians, inspectors, maintenance staff and field personnel often travel between multiple tasks during the day, and inefficient scheduling can create unnecessary driving, fuel use, emissions and lost working time. Dynamik Allocator, developed by Paavo Kytölä and Anita Kuitunen, addresses this problem by using AI to optimise daily routes and task allocation for mobile workers.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Mobile workers such as service technicians, inspectors, maintenance staff and field personnel often travel between multiple tasks during the day, and inefficient scheduling can create unnecessary driving, fuel use, emissions and lost working time. Dynamik Allocator, developed by Paavo Kytölä and Anita Kuitunen, addresses this problem by using AI to optimise daily routes and task allocation for mobile workers. The operational problem is that manual scheduling may not fully account for geography, time windows, task duration, staff availability and route efficiency. Even small inefficiencies repeated across many workers and days can produce significant emissions and costs. Dynamik Allocator proposes to arrange job sequences and schedules more intelligently, minimising redundant travel while preserving operational requirements. At a conceptual level, the tool treats field-service work as a routing and allocation optimisation challenge: AI can analyse tasks, locations and constraints to recommend sequences that reduce unnecessary kilometres. The expected impact is lower work-related travel emissions, reduced fuel consumption, time savings for organisations and more predictable field operations. The case is relevant because it connects climate objectives with internal organisational logistics, showing that emission reductions can come not only from major infrastructure projects but also from smarter allocation of everyday work. In a municipal context, such tools could support maintenance crews, social-service visits, inspection units or other teams that move across the city. The available source describes the solution within Espoo’s AI Mobility Challenge, so it should be framed as challenge-stage development or potential pilot rather than an implemented municipal routing system.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,S5_OPTIMIZATION_DECISION_SUPPORT,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2910,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02262,EU_PSTW_202609_02262,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,City of Espoo,General public services n.e.c.,"The initiative addresses an important inclusion challenge in local government: residents with different language backgrounds may struggle to access information about public services, integration support and municipal opportunities if content is available only in Finnish and Swedish or if translation is not provided in accessible formats.","Processing of personal data, AI translation service on the Hello Espoo website",City of Espoo; Local Government; General public services n.e.c.; Finland,"The AI-powered service combines text translation and voice functions to make Hello Espoo content easier to use for a wider audience. Usage data, such as use of text and audio functions, pages visited and time of use, support testing, development and user-experience improvement, while data-protection arrangements limit identifiability and keep processing within the EU/EEA.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"The City of Espoo’s AI translation service on the Hello Espoo website improves multilingual access to municipal information by providing content in audio and text formats across 13 languages. The initiative addresses an important inclusion challenge in local government: residents with different language backgrounds may struggle to access information about public services, integration support and municipal opportunities if content is available only in Finnish and Swedish or if translation is not provided in accessible formats. The AI-powered service combines text translation and voice functions to make Hello Espoo content easier to use for a wider audience. It is tested from September 2025 to August 2026, with the City of Espoo responsible for the Finnish and Swedish source content and Voice Intuitive responsible for the translated text and voice functions. At operational level, the service enables multilingual communication directly on the city website, helping users listen to or read translated content according to their needs. Usage data, such as use of text and audio functions, pages visited and time of use, support testing, development and user-experience improvement, while data-protection arrangements limit identifiability and keep processing within the EU/EEA. Feedback from users further supports accessibility improvements. The expected impact is easier access to public information, stronger integration support, better inclusion of multilingual residents and improved evidence for future AI translation services in municipal communication. The initiative is particularly relevant because it combines AI-enabled language accessibility with explicit privacy governance in a live public-service environment.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2911,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02263,EU_PSTW_202609_02263,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,City of Turin,Transport,The initiative responds to the challenge of moving autonomous-driving technologies from controlled environments into real public-service mobility settings.,Pioneering Europe’s Future of Autonomous Urban Mobility,City of Turin; Local Government; Transport; Italy,"The initiative also connects transport innovation with broader regional industrial policy, using Turin’s automotive strengths to support the transition towards software-defined, AI-enabled and service-oriented mobility.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Turin and the Piedmont Region are positioning the city as a European laboratory for autonomous urban mobility, combining the region’s automotive heritage, research capacity and urban infrastructure with AI-enabled transport experimentation. The initiative responds to the challenge of moving autonomous-driving technologies from controlled environments into real public-service mobility settings. Turin’s candidacy aims to secure a formal role within the European network of pilot cities for autonomous driving, with the ambition of testing driverless public mobility services such as taxis or shuttles on public roads. The city’s ecosystem provides strong enabling conditions, including the Politecnico di Torino, an established automotive supply chain, existing innovation infrastructure and previous experimentation around the university campus area. AI models are expected to support real-world testing by monitoring vehicle flows and helping analyse traffic conditions during trials. At operational level, the initiative would allow public authorities, researchers and industry actors to test autonomous vehicles in an urban environment where safety, service quality and interaction with ordinary traffic can be assessed under realistic conditions. The expected impact is stronger European leadership in autonomous mobility, attraction of investment, development of local expertise and creation of a model for AI-supported public transport innovation. The initiative also connects transport innovation with broader regional industrial policy, using Turin’s automotive strengths to support the transition towards software-defined, AI-enabled and service-oriented mobility.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PLANNED,계획,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2912,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02264,EU_PSTW_202609_02264,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Piedmont Region,Outpatient services.,"The operational challenge is territorial inequality in access to care: residents in peripheral or mountain areas may need to travel long distances for diagnostic examinations or specialist medical consultations, creating delays and barriers to timely treatment.",Piedmont harnesses AI to bring healthcare to every corner,Piedmont Region; Local Government; Outpatient services.; Italy,"Piedmont’s AI-healthcare initiative focuses on using artificial intelligence, diagnostics and telemedicine to improve healthcare access across a region where more than 40% of the territory is mountainous. The expected impact is improved healthcare coverage for remote communities, faster access to diagnostic support, reduced travel burden for patients, more efficient use of medical resources and stronger resilience of the regional health system.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Piedmont’s AI-healthcare initiative focuses on using artificial intelligence, diagnostics and telemedicine to improve healthcare access across a region where more than 40% of the territory is mountainous. The operational challenge is territorial inequality in access to care: residents in peripheral or mountain areas may need to travel long distances for diagnostic examinations or specialist medical consultations, creating delays and barriers to timely treatment. The initiative proposes an extended system of telemedicine cabins where patients can undergo examinations with the support of a trained health or social-care operator while a doctor connects remotely from a hospital. Artificial intelligence is positioned as a support layer for diagnostics, organisational efficiency and telemedicine workflows, helping clinicians interpret information, monitor patients and manage remote-service delivery more effectively. At operational level, the system decentralises access to diagnostic services by bringing examination capacity closer to residents while keeping specialist medical expertise connected through video and digital tools. This helps shift healthcare from a hospital-centred model towards more distributed territorial care. The expected impact is improved healthcare coverage for remote communities, faster access to diagnostic support, reduced travel burden for patients, more efficient use of medical resources and stronger resilience of the regional health system. The initiative is particularly relevant because it links AI not only to clinical innovation, but also to equity of access and territorial cohesion, using telemedicine to make the right to health more practical in peripheral areas.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PLANNED,계획,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2913,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02265,EU_PSTW_202609_02265,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""enterprise_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Autonomous Province of Trento,General public services n.e.c.,"The expected impact is improved access to digital public services, reduced burden on information offices, better multilingual support and continuous refinement through anonymised feedback and usage metrics.",ChatPat - Virtual assistant,Autonomous Province of Trento; Local Government; General public services n.e.c.; Italy,"The operational objective is to reduce search time and make provincial services easier to find, understand and use. At a conceptual level, ChatPaT uses retrieval-augmented generation to connect colloquial user questions with the formal taxonomy of administrative services.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Citizens, businesses and professionals often need to identify the correct public service, understand eligibility requirements and access online forms without knowing the internal administrative terminology used by public bodies. ChatPaT addresses this problem by providing a virtual assistant for the public services of the Autonomous Province of Trento. The operational objective is to reduce search time and make provincial services easier to find, understand and use. The assistant allows users to ask questions in natural language and receive immediate answers based on official information from the Province’s Service Catalogue, including direct links to detailed pages and online forms. It supports Italian, English, German, French, Spanish and Portuguese, and is available every day at any time. At a conceptual level, ChatPaT uses retrieval-augmented generation to connect colloquial user questions with the formal taxonomy of administrative services. The technical architecture is based on Microsoft Azure, including Azure AI Search, Azure Document Intelligence, Azure Functions and Azure AI Foundry, with production infrastructure hosted on an ACN-qualified cloud environment. The service includes privacy safeguards: conversations are anonymised, personal data are not intentionally requested or stored, and any personal data provided accidentally are removed before saving the conversation. The expected impact is improved access to digital public services, reduced burden on information offices, better multilingual support and continuous refinement through anonymised feedback and usage metrics. The case is significant because it combines generative AI, official-source retrieval, privacy-by-design and public-service usability in a controlled provincial-government setting.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,S1_KNOWLEDGE_RETRIEVAL_RAG,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2914,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02266,EU_PSTW_202609_02266,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,EDF FR,Fuel and energy,UNKNOWN,EDF Leverages AI to Predict Grid Stress During Heatwaves,EDF FR; Central-Government; Fuel and energy; France,"The EDF use case described in the available secondary source concerns an AI system intended to predict grid stress during heatwaves and help operators prepare corrective actions before outages occur. The reported system combines weather forecasts, consumption patterns, transformer loads and local events to model stress on high-voltage and regional grids, using transformer-based forecasting and graph neural networks.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Electricity systems face increasing stress during extreme heat, when cooling demand rises, grid components operate under thermal constraints and localised overloads may develop quickly. The EDF use case described in the available secondary source concerns an AI system intended to predict grid stress during heatwaves and help operators prepare corrective actions before outages occur. The operational problem is that conventional monitoring can be reactive: operators may detect stress once transformers, substations or local networks are already close to operational limits. The reported system combines weather forecasts, consumption patterns, transformer loads and local events to model stress on high-voltage and regional grids, using transformer-based forecasting and graph neural networks. At a conceptual level, the model treats the electricity grid as a spatial and temporal system: network components influence one another, while weather and demand conditions evolve over time. Forecasts can then be presented through GIS-enhanced dashboards, allowing operators to identify vulnerable areas and consider mitigation measures such as demand shedding, battery dispatch or industrial load adjustment. The expected impact would be faster response, reduced outages, better voltage stability and more targeted protection of ageing grid assets during heatwaves. However, the evidence for this specific deployment is weak. The main source is DigitalDefynd, and I did not find an EDF source confirming the reported Rhône-Alpes results, the exact modelling architecture or the stated impact figures. EDF does publicly describe AI as a major part of its R&D strategy, but not this specific heatwave-stress system in the sources found.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,S4_PREDICTION_DETECTION,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2915,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02267,EU_PSTW_202609_02267,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Assistance Publique – Hôpitaux de Paris (AP-HP),Hospital services.,"Intensive-care coordination becomes especially difficult when hospitals face sudden surges in critically ill patients, as happened during the COVID-19 crisis. If these data are outdated or fragmented, hospitals may lose valuable time when deciding where a patient should be treated.",Paris Hospitals Use AI for ICU Bed Allocation and Mortality Prediction,Assistance Publique – Hôpitaux de Paris (AP-HP); Local Government; Hospital services.; France,"The Paris hospitals use case concerns the reported use of AI to support ICU bed planning, patient transfer decisions and mortality-risk prediction across Assistance Publique – Hôpitaux de Paris. The operational problem is that ICU capacity depends on rapidly changing factors: bed availability, ventilator use, staff capacity, laboratory results, patient comorbidities, ambulance flows and local disease pressure.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Intensive-care coordination becomes especially difficult when hospitals face sudden surges in critically ill patients, as happened during the COVID-19 crisis. The Paris hospitals use case concerns the reported use of AI to support ICU bed planning, patient transfer decisions and mortality-risk prediction across Assistance Publique – Hôpitaux de Paris. The operational problem is that ICU capacity depends on rapidly changing factors: bed availability, ventilator use, staff capacity, laboratory results, patient comorbidities, ambulance flows and local disease pressure. If these data are outdated or fragmented, hospitals may lose valuable time when deciding where a patient should be treated. The reported system uses federated learning so that predictive models can be trained across hospitals without centralising sensitive patient data. LSTM-based forecasting models are described as predicting ICU occupancy from clinical and operational indicators, while a triage module ranks patients according to survival probability and expected resource need. At a conceptual level, the system combines capacity forecasting, mortality-risk modelling and operational coordination, allowing emergency departments, ambulance dispatch and hospital managers to align transfers more effectively. The expected impact is faster ICU transfers, better use of beds, staff and ventilators, more accurate planning during surges and clearer information for families. However, this case should be handled cautiously: the available source is a secondary article, and I did not find an official AP-HP source confirming the exact metrics or system architecture. (digitaldefynd.com",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,S4_PREDICTION_DETECTION,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2916,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02268,EU_PSTW_202609_02268,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Police of Zakarpattia,Police Services,"The operational problem is that human operators cannot continuously review all video streams in real time, especially where checkpoints, infrastructure sites and transport hubs generate large volumes of footage.",AI to notify the police about suspicious persons,Police of Zakarpattia; Local Government; Police Services; Ukraine,The Zakarpattia use case concerns the reported deployment of an AI-supported monitoring system connected to video cameras across the region.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Regional security authorities in wartime or high-risk contexts need to monitor strategic infrastructure, transport entry points and public spaces in order to detect unusual behaviour and respond quickly to potential threats. The Zakarpattia use case concerns the reported deployment of an AI-supported monitoring system connected to video cameras across the region. The operational problem is that human operators cannot continuously review all video streams in real time, especially where checkpoints, infrastructure sites and transport hubs generate large volumes of footage. The system described by the head of the Zakarpattia regional military administration connects regional cameras to an AI system that monitors and analyses the situation across the oblast. When the system detects suspicious presence near strategic infrastructure or identifies a person who is not recognised in the system, it alerts law-enforcement authorities for human follow-up. According to the source, all people entering the region through checkpoints undergo monitoring, cameras capture faces and vehicle numbers, and unrecognised individuals are then approached by police. At a conceptual level, the system acts as an automated surveillance and alerting layer, prioritising potential risks for human assessment rather than replacing police judgement. The expected impact is faster notification of suspicious activity, improved protection of strategic sites and stronger situational awareness for regional security authorities. The case is sensitive because it involves biometric or near-biometric monitoring, public surveillance and possible police questioning or detention; any such system requires strong legal safeguards, proportionality, oversight and protection against false positives. (unian.ua",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,F06_HIGH_VOLUME_SCALABILITY_BOTTLENECK,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2917,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02269,EU_PSTW_202609_02269,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Ballerup Municipality,Protection of biodiversity and landscape.,"Municipal planning, biodiversity policy, climate adaptation and environmental reporting require accurate and up-to-date information on land cover, but producing this information manually can be time-consuming and inconsistent. The operational problem is that municipalities need to understand how areas are distributed between buildings, roads, vegetation, water, bare ground and other land-cover categories, but traditional mapping may depend on periodic surveys or manual GIS updates.",Gismap AI model for land cover analysis,Ballerup Municipality; Local Government; Protection of biodiversity and landscape.; Denmark,"The Gismap use case in Ballerup Municipality applies an AI model to generate land-cover data and combine it with environmental and spatial datasets. Gismap supports this work by using AI-based classification, editing tools and integration with public geospatial sources.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Municipal planning, biodiversity policy, climate adaptation and environmental reporting require accurate and up-to-date information on land cover, but producing this information manually can be time-consuming and inconsistent. The Gismap use case in Ballerup Municipality applies an AI model to generate land-cover data and combine it with environmental and spatial datasets. The operational problem is that municipalities need to understand how areas are distributed between buildings, roads, vegetation, water, bare ground and other land-cover categories, but traditional mapping may depend on periodic surveys or manual GIS updates. Gismap supports this work by using AI-based classification, editing tools and integration with public geospatial sources. The solution draws on publicly available datasets from Danish authorities, including the Danish Climate Data Agency, GeoDanmark, the Danish Environmental Portal and the Ministry of Environment. At a conceptual level, the model converts aerial, map and environmental data into structured land-cover layers that can support analysis across multiple municipal functions. These outputs can be used for biodiversity registration, operational optimisation, ESG reporting, strategic planning and spatial planning. The expected impact is faster production of land-cover information, better evidence for green-space management, improved environmental reporting and more efficient use of GIS capacity. The case is relevant because it shows how AI can strengthen ordinary planning and environmental administration by converting existing public data into decision-ready spatial information. It should be seen as a municipal geospatial-AI support tool rather than an autonomous planning decision system.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2918,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02270,EU_PSTW_202609_02270,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Randers Municipality,General services.,"This creates avoidable workload for support staff and delays for the employee waiting for help. When the system cannot find a suitable response, it helps the user create a support ticket, preserving the escalation route to human support.",Implementation of AI in the knowledge database in Topdesk,Randers Municipality; Local Government; General services.; Denmark,"Randers Municipality’s Ebbot use case integrates an AI chatbot into TOPdesk, the municipality’s IT service-management system, to improve internal support. The expected impact is faster first-line support, more consistent answers, reduced repetitive workload and improved use of existing organisational knowledge.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Municipal employees need fast access to internal guidance on IT, accounting, procurement and support processes, but knowledge is often spread across previous tickets, helpdesk articles and staff experience. Randers Municipality’s Ebbot use case integrates an AI chatbot into TOPdesk, the municipality’s IT service-management system, to improve internal support. The operational problem is that employees often submit recurring questions to support teams, while the relevant answer may already exist in a knowledge article or previous case. This creates avoidable workload for support staff and delays for the employee waiting for help. Ebbot acts as a conversational layer over the TOPdesk knowledge base: employees can ask questions in ordinary language, and the chatbot searches previous support cases and knowledge articles to produce a relevant answer. When the system cannot find a suitable response, it helps the user create a support ticket, preserving the escalation route to human support. At a conceptual level, the solution combines chatbot interaction, retrieval from structured knowledge articles and case-history reuse. The expected impact is faster first-line support, more consistent answers, reduced repetitive workload and improved use of existing organisational knowledge. The case is relevant because it applies AI to internal municipal productivity rather than citizen-facing services. By supporting staff with routine administrative and technical questions, the municipality can improve operational continuity and allow specialist support teams to focus on more complex or exceptional issues.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,S2_AGENT_CONVERSATIONAL_AI,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2919,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02271,EU_PSTW_202609_02271,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Randers Municipality,General services.,"Meeting documentation is a persistent administrative burden in public organisations, particularly where staff must record decisions, action points and discussion summaries while also participating actively in the meeting itself. The operational problem is that manual note-taking can be time-consuming, uneven in quality and potentially distracting for employees who need to listen, contribute and capture key points at the same time.",Roboref - Generative AI in the Randers Municipality,Randers Municipality; Local Government; General services.; Denmark,"Roboref addresses this problem by using speech-to-text and generative AI to record, transcribe and draft meeting summaries. Roboref automates the first draft of meeting documentation by recording the meeting, converting speech into text and generating structured summaries or notes.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Meeting documentation is a persistent administrative burden in public organisations, particularly where staff must record decisions, action points and discussion summaries while also participating actively in the meeting itself. Roboref addresses this problem by using speech-to-text and generative AI to record, transcribe and draft meeting summaries. In Randers Municipality, the tool is being tested by a selected group of employees for internal meetings. The operational problem is that manual note-taking can be time-consuming, uneven in quality and potentially distracting for employees who need to listen, contribute and capture key points at the same time. Roboref automates the first draft of meeting documentation by recording the meeting, converting speech into text and generating structured summaries or notes. At a conceptual level, the tool acts as an AI notetaker: it does not replace human validation, but produces a draft that can be reviewed, corrected and finalised by staff. The expected impact is time savings, more consistent meeting records, better objectivity in documentation and improved ability for employees to focus on the substance of meetings rather than on note-taking. The case is relevant because it represents one of the most common practical uses of generative AI in public administration: reducing documentation work without transferring decision-making authority to the system. It also requires clear governance on consent, recording, data protection and the handling of confidential meeting content. RoboRef is described elsewhere as a collaboration involving more than 20 municipalities, organisations, ATP and Droids Agency. (offentlig-ai.dk",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,S3_DOCUMENT_INTELLIGENCE,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2920,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02272,EU_PSTW_202609_02272,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Randers Municipality,General services.,UNKNOWN,Copilot in the Randers Municipality,Randers Municipality; Local Government; General services.; Denmark,"Municipal employees increasingly use generative AI to draft text, summarise information, prepare communications and support routine productivity tasks. The Randers Municipality Copilot use case concerns staff access to Microsoft Copilot in Edge as a general-purpose assistant for everyday work.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Municipal employees increasingly use generative AI to draft text, summarise information, prepare communications and support routine productivity tasks. The Randers Municipality Copilot use case concerns staff access to Microsoft Copilot in Edge as a general-purpose assistant for everyday work. The operational problem is that employees often need to produce first drafts, simplify complex text, summarise documents or prepare meeting-related material, but these tasks consume time that could otherwise be spent on service delivery, case handling or professional assessment. Copilot in Edge provides a browser-based generative AI interface that can help employees generate text, rephrase content, summarise information and structure ideas. At a conceptual level, the tool functions as a productivity assistant rather than a decision system: the employee remains responsible for checking outputs, correcting inaccuracies and ensuring that final content is appropriate to the administrative context. This is especially important in public administration, where errors, confidentiality issues or unclear provenance can affect citizens and legal obligations. The expected impact is faster drafting, reduced administrative friction and improved individual productivity. However, the source link provided in your table appears to point to the Dutch Municipality of Arnhem’s Microsoft 365 Copilot register entry, not Randers Municipality. It is therefore useful for explaining general public-sector Copilot governance, including human oversight and data risks, but it does not directly verify the Randers deployment. The Randers-specific description should rely on the Danish AI-landkort entry rather than the Dutch algorithm register.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,S7_GENERATIVE_CONTENT_CREATION,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2921,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02273,EU_PSTW_202609_02273,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Randers Municipality,General services.,UNKNOWN,OS2ai - Open-source AI solution in Danish municipalities,Randers Municipality; Local Government; General services.; Denmark,"At a conceptual level, OS2ai is an enabling layer: it makes it easier for municipalities to integrate AI into workflows, develop assistants, automate tasks and reuse components developed by other public authorities.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Danish municipalities are exploring generative AI, but many want solutions that preserve public ownership, reduce dependency on large proprietary providers and allow shared development across authorities. OS2ai addresses this need by providing an open-source AI platform for the public sector, built around common governance, shared costs and stronger ownership control. Randers Municipality participates in this wider public-sector AI community. The operational problem is that individual municipalities may not have the resources to build secure, reusable AI infrastructure alone, while proprietary tools can raise concerns about data control, vendor lock-in and long-term costs. OS2ai offers a shared platform that can be used for both everyday AI support and more specialised municipal applications. At a conceptual level, OS2ai is an enabling layer: it makes it easier for municipalities to integrate AI into workflows, develop assistants, automate tasks and reuse components developed by other public authorities. The platform builds on work initiated by Aarhus Municipality and is further developed through the OS2 community, which has long focused on shared open-source public-sector software. The expected impact is faster AI adoption, lower duplicated development costs, greater transparency, improved public control over data and models, and more scalable experimentation across municipalities and regions. The case is relevant because it treats AI infrastructure as a shared public-good approach rather than a set of isolated local procurements. This is particularly important where municipalities face similar tasks and can benefit from common technical foundations.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2922,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02274,EU_PSTW_202609_02274,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Randers Municipality,General services.,UNKNOWN,RandersGPT,Randers Municipality; Local Government; General services.; Denmark,"Municipalities using generative AI need to balance productivity benefits with data protection, information security and responsible use. At a conceptual level, the tool functions as a secure municipal front door to generative AI: employees can use a general assistant while being directed to domain-specific agents where more tailored support is available.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Municipalities using generative AI need to balance productivity benefits with data protection, information security and responsible use. RandersGPT is an internal GPT environment for Randers Municipality, based on OpenAI through Azure and accessed through the municipality’s AI portal. The operational problem is that employees may otherwise turn to public tools such as ChatGPT or browser-based assistants, which can create uncertainty about where data are processed, what information may be entered and whether outputs are appropriate for municipal tasks. RandersGPT provides a more controlled internal alternative for administrative support. It is designed to assist employees with tasks such as drafting, summarising, structuring text, preparing material and navigating towards more specialised assistants available in the AI portal. At a conceptual level, the tool functions as a secure municipal front door to generative AI: employees can use a general assistant while being directed to domain-specific agents where more tailored support is available. The expected impact is safer and more consistent AI use, reduced reliance on uncontrolled external tools, improved productivity and better organisational oversight of generative-AI adoption. The case is relevant because it reflects a maturing stage in public-sector AI use. Instead of simply allowing or banning external AI tools, the municipality creates its own managed environment with clearer data-processing responsibilities, documentation and governance. Randers Municipality’s own privacy notice states that the AI portal is used to provide general chat and access to specialists, supporting task performance, quality assurance and documentation.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2923,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02275,EU_PSTW_202609_02275,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Kalundborg Kommune,General public services n.e.c.,"This creates a practical tension: manual note-taking can reduce presence in the conversation, while incomplete documentation can weaken case quality and increase the risk of mistakes. This allows the professional to remain responsible for the final documentation while reducing the repetitive burden of manual note-taking.",Fasit Dialogstøtte – AI Assistant for Conversation Notes,Kalundborg Kommune; Local Government; General public services n.e.c.; Denmark,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Caseworkers in employment and social-service settings must listen carefully to citizens while also documenting conversations accurately for case files. This creates a practical tension: manual note-taking can reduce presence in the conversation, while incomplete documentation can weaken case quality and increase the risk of mistakes. Fasit Dialogstøtte addresses this problem by integrating an AI assistant into the Schultz Fasit case-management environment. The operational objective is to support caseworkers by automatically transcribing conversations with citizens and generating draft summaries, minutes or journal notes. At a conceptual level, the assistant acts as a documentation support tool rather than a case-decision system. It captures the spoken conversation, converts it to text and prepares a draft that the caseworker can review, correct and approve before it becomes part of the case record. This allows the professional to remain responsible for the final documentation while reducing the repetitive burden of manual note-taking. The expected impact is more focused citizen dialogue, more consistent records, reduced administrative workload and stronger documentation quality. The system may also support accuracy because key points from the conversation can be captured systematically rather than reconstructed from memory after the meeting. The case is relevant because it shows how AI can support front-line welfare administration in a relatively bounded way: it improves the production of case documentation while leaving professional judgement, case assessment and legal responsibility with the human caseworker.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2924,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02276,EU_PSTW_202609_02276,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Hvidovre Municipality,Transport,"Municipal road maintenance requires up-to-date information on potholes, surface wear, cracking and other defects, but manual inspections can be slow, expensive and unevenly prioritised. The operational problem is that municipalities often lack a continuous, objective and scalable picture of road condition.",Pluto – Road Analysis and Maintenance,Hvidovre Municipality; Local Government; Transport; Denmark,"Pluto Technologies’ solution addresses this problem by using AI, smartphones and GPS to monitor road conditions and support more targeted maintenance planning. The case is relevant because it applies AI to a very concrete municipal asset-management task, making infrastructure maintenance more proactive and evidence-based.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Municipal road maintenance requires up-to-date information on potholes, surface wear, cracking and other defects, but manual inspections can be slow, expensive and unevenly prioritised. Pluto Technologies’ solution addresses this problem by using AI, smartphones and GPS to monitor road conditions and support more targeted maintenance planning. In Hvidovre Municipality, the tool is used through devices installed on municipal vehicles, such as refuse trucks, which already travel regularly across the road network. The operational problem is that municipalities often lack a continuous, objective and scalable picture of road condition. By collecting data from vehicles that are already operating, the system can reduce the need for dedicated inspection rounds and transform routine municipal driving into a source of infrastructure intelligence. The AI model detects damage and wear on road surfaces, while the results are visualised on a digital map for planners and maintenance teams. At a conceptual level, Pluto creates a data-driven road-management loop: sensor and image data are collected, AI identifies defects, maps show where action is needed, and maintenance resources can then be prioritised according to actual condition. The expected impact is faster detection of damage, better prioritisation of repairs, more preventive maintenance, lower costs and potentially longer road lifespan. The case is relevant because it applies AI to a very concrete municipal asset-management task, making infrastructure maintenance more proactive and evidence-based. Pluto describes its product as AI-powered software for detecting damage, planning repairs and managing road maintenance",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2925,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02277,EU_PSTW_202609_02277,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Hvidovre Municipality,General services.,UNKNOWN,InDialog Voicebot – Internal AI Support for ESDH and Topdesk,Hvidovre Municipality; Local Government; General services.; Denmark,"Employees often need quick answers on how to use these systems correctly, but finding the relevant instruction can require searching manuals, intranet pages or previous support material. The expected impact is faster internal support, more efficient use of digital systems, reduced friction in administrative work and improved productivity for municipal employees.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Hvidovre Municipality’s InDialog Voicebot supports municipal employees by making internal guidance easier to access through voice-based interaction. Public administrations rely on many internal systems, including electronic document and case-management systems and service-management platforms such as TOPdesk. Employees often need quick answers on how to use these systems correctly, but finding the relevant instruction can require searching manuals, intranet pages or previous support material. The InDialog Voicebot addresses this problem by allowing staff to ask questions through voice commands and receive guidance rapidly. The solution is used internally to support navigation and guidance in the municipality’s ESDH system and TOPdesk. At operational level, the voicebot works as an internal first-line assistant: employees can obtain immediate answers or locate relevant instructions without interrupting their workflow or submitting routine support requests. This reduces the time spent searching for procedural guidance and allows support staff to focus on more complex issues that require human expertise. The expected impact is faster internal support, more efficient use of digital systems, reduced friction in administrative work and improved productivity for municipal employees. The voice interface is also relevant because it lowers the threshold for using internal knowledge tools, especially in situations where typing a search query or navigating a system manually is inconvenient. The initiative demonstrates how AI can be used inside local government to improve the everyday experience of staff working with digital administrative systems.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2926,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02278,EU_PSTW_202609_02278,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Hvidovre Municipality,"Executive and legislative organs, financial and fiscal affairs, external affairs.",UNKNOWN,KAILA - AI tool for Danish legislation,"Hvidovre Municipality; Local Government; Executive and legislative organs, financial and fiscal affairs, external affairs.; Denmark","At a conceptual level, the system works as a retrieval and drafting assistant for legal work: it uses AI to interpret the user’s question, search trusted legal materials and produce a response with references that the legal professional can verify. The case is relevant because it applies generative AI to a high-accountability domain where human verification remains essential.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Municipal legal staff must interpret current legislation, prepare arguments, draft legal documents and ensure that advice is based on reliable and up-to-date sources. KAILA supports this work by providing an AI assistant grounded in Karnov’s legal content and, in the municipal case-management context, potentially combined with the municipality’s own uploaded documents. The operational problem is that legal professionals spend substantial time locating relevant provisions, guidance, case law and arguments before they can apply them to a concrete case. KAILA is designed to accelerate this research and drafting process while preserving source verification. It can help generate legal text, gather relevant sources and arguments, provide new perspectives and assist preparation for meetings or case discussions. At a conceptual level, the system works as a retrieval and drafting assistant for legal work: it uses AI to interpret the user’s question, search trusted legal materials and produce a response with references that the legal professional can verify. This is important because legal AI must not be treated as an uncheckable answer generator; the value lies in combining speed with transparent source grounding. The expected impact is faster legal research, more efficient preparation of legal documents, improved consistency in municipal legal work and reduced time spent on preliminary information gathering. The case is relevant because it applies generative AI to a high-accountability domain where human verification remains essential. KAILA should therefore be presented as decision support for legal professionals, not as an automated legal decision-maker. (karnovgroup.dk",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,S5_OPTIMIZATION_DECISION_SUPPORT,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2927,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02279,EU_PSTW_202609_02279,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Gentofte Municipality,Sickness and disability.,"Work-related injuries and eye injuries involve specific reporting obligations, rights, responsibilities and procedural steps that can be difficult for employees and managers to understand quickly. The expected impact is easier access to accurate information, fewer procedural mistakes, more consistent handling of work-injury cases and reduced workload for staff who otherwise answer recurring questions manually.",AI-for-Søren: AI for work injuries,Gentofte Municipality; Local Government; Sickness and disability.; Denmark,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Work-related injuries and eye injuries involve specific reporting obligations, rights, responsibilities and procedural steps that can be difficult for employees and managers to understand quickly. AI-for-Søren addresses this problem by providing an AI assistant that answers questions about municipal procedures for handling occupational injury cases. The operational problem is that different users need different kinds of guidance: an injured employee may need to know what to do immediately, a manager may need to understand reporting obligations, and HR or working-environment staff may need consistent procedural information. The assistant communicates the municipality’s procedures and links users to supplementary information from relevant Danish authorities and professional sources, including the Danish Working Environment Authority and the National Board of Industrial Injuries. At a conceptual level, the tool functions as a specialised knowledge assistant for a narrow administrative domain. It does not decide whether an injury is compensable or replace formal case handling; instead, it helps users find correct guidance and understand the steps involved. The expected impact is easier access to accurate information, fewer procedural mistakes, more consistent handling of work-injury cases and reduced workload for staff who otherwise answer recurring questions manually. The intended users include managers, working-environment representatives, injured employees, HR staff, MED organisation representatives and the municipality’s occupational-injury function. The case is relevant because it shows how a municipality can create a focused AI assistant for a specific internal governance and employee-support process, where a well-defined knowledge base can reduce uncertainty and improve procedural compliance.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2928,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02280,EU_PSTW_202609_02280,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""enterprise_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Kyivstar,Communication,UNKNOWN,5G launch in Lviv,Kyivstar; Private sector; Communication; Ukraine,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Kyivstar, Ukraine's largest mobile operator, plans to launch its first commercial fifth-generation (5G) service in Lviv after completing pilot tests. Speaking at the Spring Business Forum, Business Development Director Kostiantyn Vechir confirmed the move, noting that previous 5G tests had been conducted in Kyiv. The launch is part of a coordinated effort with the Ministry of Digital Transformation, as Kyivstar works alongside state authorities and the telecommunications industry to implement a nationwide 5G transition plan.",NON_AI_OR_UNCONFIRMED_TECHNOLOGY,IN_DEVELOPMENT,개발 중,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2929,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02281,EU_PSTW_202609_02281,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Ministry of Digital Transformation,General public services n.e.c.,UNKNOWN,A Sovereign AI Model: National LLM to Enter Beta in 2026,Ministry of Digital Transformation; Central-Government; General public services n.e.c.; Ukraine,"It uses Google’s open Gemma models as a base, which are being adapted and trained on extensive Ukrainian-language datasets drawn from government, academia, media and other sources. An independent expert panel is shaping quality, safety and linguistic benchmarks, while a legal framework for data use and intellectual-property compliance is under development.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Ukraine is developing its own sovereign large language model (LLM)—a national artificial intelligence system tailored to the Ukrainian language, culture and public-sector needs. The project has moved from concept to technical planning and is being built in partnership with Kyivstar, with the first beta version due in spring 2026. It uses Google’s open Gemma models as a base, which are being adapted and trained on extensive Ukrainian-language datasets drawn from government, academia, media and other sources. An independent expert panel is shaping quality, safety and linguistic benchmarks, while a legal framework for data use and intellectual-property compliance is under development. Once tested, the model will be made available to public institutions, researchers and developers, and is intended to bolster Ukraine’s digital sovereignty and reduce reliance on foreign AI technologies.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,IN_DEVELOPMENT,개발 중,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2930,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02282,EU_PSTW_202609_02282,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Cityf of Linz,General public services n.e.c.,UNKNOWN,ELLI - Chatbot of the City of Linz,Cityf of Linz; Local Government; General public services n.e.c.; Austria,"The City of Linz provides an AI-powered chatbot service called “ELLI” (short for Elektronische Linzerin) to help citizens find information about municipal services quickly and easily. ELLI is available 24/7 online and answers questions about topics like administrative services, opening hours, civic procedures, local information and more, using natural language understanding to interpret queries and point users to relevant details or external resources.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"The City of Linz provides an AI-powered chatbot service called “ELLI” (short for Elektronische Linzerin) to help citizens find information about municipal services quickly and easily. ELLI is available 24/7 online and answers questions about topics like administrative services, opening hours, civic procedures, local information and more, using natural language understanding to interpret queries and point users to relevant details or external resources. The chatbot supports multilingual interaction, is continuously updated with new content, and helps reduce routine inquiries to the City’s Teleservice Center by providing instant responses to common questions.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,S2_AGENT_CONVERSATIONAL_AI,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2931,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02283,EU_PSTW_202609_02283,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research"", ""social_nonprofit""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Devbridge Foundation,Secondary education.,UNKNOWN,Innovative Mathematics Learning Platform (Grades 5–12),Devbridge Foundation; Consortium; Secondary education.; Lithuania,"This AI-powered mathematics platform supports students in grades 5–12 by providing curriculum-aligned exercises, intelligent feedback, and adaptive learning paths. It is implemented directly in classroom and independent learning settings to demonstrate how AI can enhance mathematics education at scale.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"This AI-powered mathematics platform supports students in grades 5–12 by providing curriculum-aligned exercises, intelligent feedback, and adaptive learning paths. It helps students strengthen mathematical understanding, practice problem-solving skills, and prepare for assessments, while also supporting teachers with insights into student progress. The platform is integrated into the Learn on.ai initiative as one of the core learning tools used in participating schools. It is implemented directly in classroom and independent learning settings to demonstrate how AI can enhance mathematics education at scale. Learn on.ai is a national initiative by the Devbridge Foundation aimed at introducing AI-powered educational tools into Lithuanian schools. The project supports teachers and students by providing access to innovative digital solutions, fostering personalised learning, and reducing regional disparities in access to modern educational technologies.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2932,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02284,EU_PSTW_202609_02284,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research"", ""social_nonprofit""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Devbridge Foundation,Secondary education.,UNKNOWN,Personalised Mathematics Learning Platform for Every Student (Grades 5–12),Devbridge Foundation; Consortium; Secondary education.; Lithuania,It is implemented in participating schools as a key tool for supporting diverse learning needs and helping students progress at their own pace.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"This platform delivers personalised mathematics learning through adaptive tasks, interactive content, and gamified elements that respond to each student’s individual progress and knowledge gaps. It is designed to improve engagement, reinforce foundational skills, and support steady academic development. The platform is integrated withitn the Learn on.ai initiative, and it is used to demonstrate how artificial intelligence can individualise learning at scale. It is implemented in participating schools as a key tool for supporting diverse learning needs and helping students progress at their own pace. Learn on.ai is a Devbridge Foundation initiative that brings AI-driven educational solutions into real classroom environments. By equipping schools with innovative tools and teacher training, the project aims to modernize education, enhance learning outcomes, and ensure equal access to high-quality digital learning resources.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2933,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02285,EU_PSTW_202609_02285,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research"", ""social_nonprofit""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Devbridge Foundation,Education not definable by level.,UNKNOWN,EditAI – AI Tool for Teachers,Devbridge Foundation; Consortium; Education not definable by level.; Lithuania,"EditAI is an AI-powered tool designed to help teachers create lesson plans, assignments, and learning materials more efficiently.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"EditAI is an AI-powered tool designed to help teachers create lesson plans, assignments, and learning materials more efficiently. It supports modern teaching approaches such as problem-based and personalised learning, while allowing educators to adapt content to different student needs. EditAI is integrated into the Learn on.ai initiative as a teacher-focused solution that supports daily classroom work. It enables educators in participating schools to experiment with AI-assisted content creation and reduce administrative workload while improving lesson quality. The Learn on.ai initiative, led by the Devbridge Foundation, aims to introduce practical AI tools into education by working directly with schools and teachers. Through this program, educators gain access to innovative technologies that enhance teaching effectiveness, promote student engagement, and support long-term digital transformation in education.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2934,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02286,EU_PSTW_202609_02286,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Roskilde Municipality,General services.,"When citizens submit feedback on municipal projects, employees manually had to summarize each response—a time-consuming and variable process.",AI solution in Roskilde Municipality helps create minutes of consultation responses,Roskilde Municipality; Local Government; General services.; Denmark,"Roskilde Municipality uses generative AI to automatically create summaries of consultation responses from residents regarding planning decisions. The AI solution uses Azure GPT to generate initial drafts of these summaries, which employees then review and refine to ensure accuracy.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Roskilde Municipality uses generative AI to automatically create summaries of consultation responses from residents regarding planning decisions. When citizens submit feedback on municipal projects, employees manually had to summarize each response—a time-consuming and variable process. The AI solution uses Azure GPT to generate initial drafts of these summaries, which employees then review and refine to ensure accuracy. Testing shows the AI produces summaries of 75-80% quality initially, potentially saving up to one hour per consultation response. This allows staff to redirect time toward other citizen-facing tasks.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,S7_GENERATIVE_CONTENT_CREATION,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2935,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02287,EU_PSTW_202609_02287,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""enterprise_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Danish Digital Agency,General services.,"The sheer volume—3,673 reports totaling approximately 88,000 pages from 2022-2023—made manual analysis impractical.",AI helps the Danish Digital Agency conduct analyses,Danish Digital Agency; Central-Government; General services.; Denmark,The agency developed a generative AI solution using ChatGPT API with a custom prompt containing 30 classification categories.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Since 2021, large Danish companies must address data ethics in their annual reports. The Digital Agency needed to analyze thousands of reports to strengthen national data ethics guidance. The sheer volume—3,673 reports totaling approximately 88,000 pages from 2022-2023—made manual analysis impractical. The agency developed a generative AI solution using ChatGPT API with a custom prompt containing 30 classification categories. This enables systematic analysis of data ethics policies across entire company populations rather than just samples, allowing faster, more comprehensive insights for policy development.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2936,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02288,EU_PSTW_202609_02288,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,ATP Livslang Pension,General services.,UNKNOWN,AI solution in ATP writes journal notes of conversations with citizens,ATP Livslang Pension; Central-Government; General services.; Denmark,"The automated journaling solution converts call recordings to text, then summarizes conversations using generative AI.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"ATP, Denmark's labor market fund, receives approximately 2.5 million citizen calls annually, each requiring documentation as journal notes. The automated journaling solution converts call recordings to text, then summarizes conversations using generative AI. Results show the system generates draft notes in 5 seconds, with employees spending under 2 minutes correcting them in 70% of cases. This automation frees employees from time-consuming documentation tasks while maintaining consistent, high-quality records of citizen interactions.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2937,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02289,EU_PSTW_202609_02289,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,European Commission,Defence,UNKNOWN,OpenTIDE - Open Threat Informed Detection Engineering,European Commission; Central-Government; Defence; Luxembourg,"DIGIT.S2 has open sourced this amazing platform for security SOC teams around Europe to use. Its cutting edge - a true innovation in the space as it enables data driven implementations of threat detection coverage and automates most detection engineering workflows, which all were mostly manual until this platform was open sourced.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"DIGIT.S2 has open sourced this amazing platform for security SOC teams around Europe to use. Its cutting edge - a true innovation in the space as it enables data driven implementations of threat detection coverage and automates most detection engineering workflows, which all were mostly manual until this platform was open sourced. Additionally, it enables SOC-to-SOC collaboration, so that European SOCs can become force multipliers for each other, which is exactly what the industry has been calling for since 2015 (https://github.com/JohnLaTwC/Shared/blob/master/Defenders%20think%20in%20lists.%20Attackers%20think%20in%20graphs.%20As%20long%20as%20this%20is%20true%2C%20attackers%20win.md)",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2941,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02290,EU_PSTW_202609_02290,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,"Municipality of Agrinio, Greece",Environmental protection n.e.c.,UNKNOWN,Agrinio Environmental Digital Observatory: A Digital Twin Ecosystem for Sustainable and Data-Driven Governance,"Municipality of Agrinio, Greece; Local Government; Environmental protection n.e.c.; Greece","The system combines real-time IoT sensor networks, Copernicus Earth Observation data, GIS analytics and open data services with participatory planning tools, enabling continuous monitoring of environmental conditions, land-use dynamics and urban development in near real time.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"The Agrinio Environmental Digital Observatory establishes a unified digital twin and governance ecosystem operating as a decision-support system for evidence-based, climate-resilient and participatory governance in the Municipality of Agrinio. It integrates environmental monitoring, spatial planning, municipal intelligence and citizen engagement into a single interoperable platform. The system combines real-time IoT sensor networks, Copernicus Earth Observation data, GIS analytics and open data services with participatory planning tools, enabling continuous monitoring of environmental conditions, land-use dynamics and urban development in near real time. It functions as a single source of truth for municipal territory, improving coordination, efficiency and cross-departmental decision-making. A KPI framework aligned with ISO 37120 supports performance monitoring of municipal services. Citizens access environmental and spatial data, strengthening transparency and participation. The solution is aligned with EIF,INSPIRE principles, ensuring interoperability, scalability and reuse across European public administrations.",NON_AI_OR_UNCONFIRMED_TECHNOLOGY,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2942,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02291,EU_PSTW_202609_02291,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research"", ""enterprise_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,MINISTRY OF THE INTERIOR AND PUBLIC ADMINISTRATION,General services.,UNKNOWN,Skrinja: AI-Enhanced Business Intelligence for Evidence-Based Decision-Making and Policymaking in Slovenia,MINISTRY OF THE INTERIOR AND PUBLIC ADMINISTRATION; Central-Government; General services.; Slovenia,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Skrinja is Slovenia’s national Business Intelligence (BI) and AI-enabled analytics platform, supporting evidence-based decision-making and policymaking across public administration. It provides strategic KPI dashboards, advanced analytics, standardised reports, real-time reporting, interactive visualisations and predictive analytics, transforming administrative data into actionable insights. Operating in a secure GDPR-compliant government environment since 2020, Skrinja integrates major national datasets, including the Common Agricultural Policy (covering over 80,000 farms), Administrative Procedures (more than 1 million cases annually), Market and Health Inspections, Public-Sector Salaries (over 180,000 employees and 2,000 budget users), Public Procurement, the Central Personnel Registry and Public Funding Programmes. In 2026, Skrinja Open was launched to provide citizens, businesses, researchers and journalists with direct access to public procurement analytics, strengthening transparency, accountability and data-driven governance.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2943,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02292,EU_PSTW_202609_02292,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""social_nonprofit"", ""enterprise_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Ministry of Smart Administration and Regional Development of the Republic of Latvia,General services.,UNKNOWN,Latvia enables legal recognition of Ukrainian trusted e-signatures,Ministry of Smart Administration and Regional Development of the Republic of Latvia; Central-Government; General services.; Latvia,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Latvia introduced a legal and technical solution enabling Ukrainian electronic signatures to be recognised and verified in Latvia. The initiative builds on Ukraine’s recognition of EU electronic signatures since January 2023, and on the European Commission’s Trusted List of third countries, which together created the legal and technical foundation for the acceptance of Ukrainian electronic signatures within Latvia’s digital environment. It responds to the needs of Ukrainian citizens, residents, entrepreneurs and business representatives who interact with Latvian public institutions and service providers but may not have Latvian digital credentials. It also benefits Latvian citizens and businesses cooperating with Ukrainian partners, by enabling legally valid remote transactions. By amending national legislation and integrating verification functionality into Latvia’s national e-signature infrastructure, documents signed with Ukrainian electronic signatures issued by trusted Ukrainian service providers can now be accepted for legally binding digital interactions. The solution removes administrative barriers, supports remote access to services, and strengthens secure cross-border digital cooperation.",NON_AI_OR_UNCONFIRMED_TECHNOLOGY,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2944,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02293,EU_PSTW_202609_02293,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""enterprise_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,The Communications Regulatory Authority of the Republic of Lithuania,Economic affairs n.e.c,UNKNOWN,Matuok.lt: Open-Source Network Measurement and Data Platform for Public Internet Quality Monitoring,The Communications Regulatory Authority of the Republic of Lithuania; Central-Government; Economic affairs n.e.c; Lithuania,"Matuok.lt is a public network measurement platform implemented and operated by the Communications Regulatory Authority of Lithuania (RRT), based on the open-source RTR-NetTest framework.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Matuok.lt is a public network measurement platform implemented and operated by the Communications Regulatory Authority of Lithuania (RRT), based on the open-source RTR-NetTest framework. It enables citizens and businesses to objectively assess the quality of their internet access services by measuring key parameters such as download/upload speed, latency, and additional quality indicators. The solution builds on an existing European open-source software and adapts it to national needs, providing detailed reports, historical data, and visualized statistics, including maps and open datasets. It empowers users to verify whether their service meets contractual conditions and supports complaint processes with evidence-based measurements. At the same time, aggregated data supports public authorities in monitoring national network performance, identifying coverage gaps, and informing infrastructure investment decisions. The platform is accessible via web and mobile applications, ensuring broad public access and usability.",NON_AI_OR_UNCONFIRMED_TECHNOLOGY,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2945,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02294,EU_PSTW_202609_02294,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Aristotle University of Thessaloniki,General services.,UNKNOWN,"Simple: A Semantic, Voice-Driven Procurement Intelligence and Training System for Auditing and Decision Support in Public Administration",Aristotle University of Thessaloniki; Academic-Research; General services.; Greece,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Simple is a semantic, graph-based procurement intelligence system developed within a university-led public sector innovation context and currently in pilot phase. It integrates European (TED) and national (KIMDIS) procurement data into a unified knowledge graph aligned with the eProcurement Ontology (ePO), enabling large-scale audit and analysis across contracting authorities, time periods and CPV categories. The system supports automated generation of structured audit reports and provides multi-layer diagnosis of procurement markets (macro–meso–micro) through explainable indicators, enhancing audit, policy analysis and decision-making. It also incorporates legal knowledge into a graph-based reasoning framework, enabling structured interpretation within the regulatory context. A voice-driven interface allows non-technical users to interact naturally, while a human-supervised self-correction mechanism ensures continuous refinement and transparency. The solution improves efficiency, compliance and data-driven policymaking in public procurement.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,S7_GENERATIVE_CONTENT_CREATION,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2946,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02295,EU_PSTW_202609_02295,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Regione Toscana,General public services n.e.c.,"Launched as part of the 2021â€“2027 ERDF Operational Programme, the project was created to overcome the fragmentation of information and offer a single, personalised, secure and inclusive point of access to public administration services.",Me Toscana,Regione Toscana; Regional Government; General public services n.e.c.; Italy,"â€¢ Local Support: In addition to the online portal, the project links up with the â€œPunti Digitale Facileâ€ centres located across the region to offer in-person support to those who have difficulty using digital tools.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Me.toscana.it is the Tuscany Regionâ€™s digital platform, designed to simplify access to regional public services and improve citizensâ€™ digital experience. Launched as part of the 2021â€“2027 ERDF Operational Programme, the project was created to overcome the fragmentation of information and offer a single, personalised, secure and inclusive point of access to public administration services. A key feature of the project is the virtual assistant â€˜Chiedilo a Meâ€™ (Ask Me), based on Generative Artificial Intelligence, which enables citizens to obtain immediate and reliable answers in natural language. Main features already live on Me.toscana.it: â€¢ Personalised Digital Space: Users can create a personal profile to manage regional services on a single platform, saving favourites for quicker access. â€¢ Notifications and Updates: The system sends tailored communications and notifications (via email or on the platform) regarding deadlines, the status of applications and news based on the userâ€™s interests. â€¢ Chiedilo a Meâ€™: This is an innovative support service designed to guide citizens through calls for applications, opportunities and services offered by the Region. â€¢ Local Support: In addition to the online portal, the project links up with the â€œPunti Digitale Facileâ€ centres located across the region to offer in-person support to those who have difficulty using digital tools.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2947,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02296,EU_PSTW_202609_02296,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Servizz.gov,General services.,UNKNOWN,Servizz.gov – Reimagining Public Service Delivery Through AI-Powered Citizen Engagement,Servizz.gov; Central-Government; General services.; Malta,"It actively guides citizens through their service journey by using personalisation, life-event information and intelligent recommendations to make public services easier to understand and access. The initiative demonstrates how artificial intelligence can be deployed responsibly within public administration to create measurable public value, while providing a model that can be replicated by other public administrations in Europe.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Servizz.gov is Malta’s next-generation national public service platform, designed to transform how citizens discover, access and interact with government services. The platform consolidates 450-500 public services into a single AI-enabled experience where citizens can identify relevant services, discover benefits and entitlements, manage appointments, track applications and receive support through both AI-assisted and human-assisted channels. Unlike traditional government portals, Servizz.gov does not only present information. It actively guides citizens through their service journey by using personalisation, life-event information and intelligent recommendations to make public services easier to understand and access. The initiative demonstrates how artificial intelligence can be deployed responsibly within public administration to create measurable public value, while providing a model that can be replicated by other public administrations in Europe.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2948,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02297,EU_PSTW_202609_02297,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,"Madrid City Council, Spain Digital Office",General public services n.e.c.,UNKNOWN,Madrid Smart Urban Spaces: Interoperable Edge Intelligence for Real-Time Urban Operations,"Madrid City Council, Spain Digital Office; Local Government; General public services n.e.c.; Spain","Data is harmonized using FIWARE/NGSI-LD and European Smart Data Models, ensuring semantic interoperability across domains and vendors.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Madrid's Smart Urban Spaces (EUI) are interoperable urban ecosystems that connect infrastructure, digital platforms and public services across Madrid's 21 districts. Built on open standards and a common architecture, each EUI integrates IoT devices, AI and real-time analytics through UrbanOS, Madrid's City Operating System, creating a shared data space for urban management. The platform enables automated and coordinated services, including adaptive street lighting, smart parking, environmental monitoring, waste management and EV charging optimization. Two EUIs are already operational: ValdemingÃ³mez and Mercamadrid, integrating energy, mobility and environmental solutions. Data is harmonized using FIWARE/NGSI-LD and European Smart Data Models, ensuring semantic interoperability across domains and vendors. Feeding Madrid's city-scale Digital Twin, the initiative supports evidence-based decisions while offering a scalable, vendor-neutral and replicable framework for cities across Europe.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,IN_DEVELOPMENT,개발 중,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2949,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02298,EU_PSTW_202609_02298,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Diputaciò de Barcelona,General services.,UNKNOWN,"Visor 2030: plataforma de codi obert que permet comprendre, monitoritzar i avaluar la realitat del territori des d'una perspectiva multidimensional vinculada als Objectius de Desenvolupament Sostenible.",Diputaciò de Barcelona; Local Government; General services.; Spain,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"El Visor 2030 és una plataforma de codi obert impulsat per la Diputació de Barcelona que integra dades socials, econòmiques i mediambientals dels 311 municipis de la província de Barcelona per comprendre, monitoritzar i avaluar el territori des d’una perspectiva multidimensional vinculada als Objectius de Desenvolupament Sostenible. La plataforma combina 76 indicadors alineats amb els ODS amb capes addicionals d’informació —pressupost municipal, plans estratègics, percepció ciutadana— per oferir una visió 360º que dona suport a la presa de decisions basada en evidències, la transparència i la rendició de comptes. Amb una arquitectura modular, interoperable i reutilitzable, el Visor 2030 facilita la comparació entre municipis, genera informes automàtics, permet l’exportació de dades i es projecta com una solució transferible per a altres administracions públiques.",NON_AI_OR_UNCONFIRMED_TECHNOLOGY,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2950,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02299,EU_PSTW_202609_02299,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Comisión Nacional de los Mercados y la Competencia (CNMC): Deputy Directorate for Economic Analysis (Advocacy Department). Technical support: Deputy Directorate for Information Systems and ICT (SSTIC).,Economic affairs n.e.c,"It does not replace legal or economic judgement; it structures, documents and prioritises cases, enabling CNMC to identify cases to challenge in court and engage authorities to amend anti-competitive rules, and has already helped remove restrictive regulation.",LExIA - AI-assisted regulatory screening for early detection of competition restrictions.,Comisión Nacional de los Mercados y la Competencia (CNMC): Deputy Directorate for Economic Analysis (Advocacy Department). Technical support: Deputy Directorate for Information Systems and ICT (SSTIC).; Central-Government; Economic affairs n.e.c; Spain,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"LExIA (“Lectura Experta con IA”) is an AI-based internal solution developed by the CNMC to support early detection of public regulatory restrictions to competition in Spanish official gazettes. It addresses a high-volume, time-sensitive process: thousands of legal texts are published across multiple official sources and must be screened quickly when they may require competition advocacy or, ultimately, legal action. LExIA combines preliminary filters, key information extraction, preliminary assessment of restrictions, retrieval of CNMC precedents through Retrieval Augmented Generation –RAG–, legal analysis against related official sources, prioritisation and automatic generation of Word reports and e-mail alerts. The system runs on real regulatory publications and sends daily results and filtering statistics for expert review. It does not replace legal or economic judgement; it structures, documents and prioritises cases, enabling CNMC to identify cases to challenge in court and engage authorities to amend anti-competitive rules, and has already helped remove restrictive regulation.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,S1_KNOWLEDGE_RETRIEVAL_RAG|S7_GENERATIVE_CONTENT_CREATION,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2951,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02300,EU_PSTW_202609_02300,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Digitaal Vlaanderen,General services.,"It was created in response to growing challenges faced by public administrations in adopting AI in a strategic and responsible manner, including fragmented experimentation, rapidly evolving technologies and regulations, and varying levels of organisational readiness. The Playbook turns policy ambitions into concrete tools, checklists and reusable guidance, enabling administrations to move from fragmented experimentation to coordinated and interoperable AI adoption.",AI Playbook,Digitaal Vlaanderen; Regional Government; General services.; Belgium,"The Playbook supports public administrations across the entire AI lifecycle: defining strategy and roadmaps, identifying and prioritising AI use cases, implementing governance aligned with the EU AI Act, strengthening organisational readiness and skills, and embedding AI architecture.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"The AI Playbook developed by Digitaal Vlaanderen establishes a practical operating model for trustworthy, scalable and interoperable AI adoption across the public sector. It was created in response to growing challenges faced by public administrations in adopting AI in a strategic and responsible manner, including fragmented experimentation, rapidly evolving technologies and regulations, and varying levels of organisational readiness. The Playbook supports public administrations across the entire AI lifecycle: defining strategy and roadmaps, identifying and prioritising AI use cases, implementing governance aligned with the EU AI Act, strengthening organisational readiness and skills, and embedding AI architecture. The Playbook turns policy ambitions into concrete tools, checklists and reusable guidance, enabling administrations to move from fragmented experimentation to coordinated and interoperable AI adoption. It provides a common framework and shared language for AI adoption, helping organisations move from fragmented experimentation towards coordinated, interoperable and value-driven AI implementation. The Playbook supports organisations at different stages of AI maturity, from initial exploration to large-scale operational adoption.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2952,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02301,EU_PSTW_202609_02301,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,JSC “Prozorro.Sale”,Economic affairs n.e.c,"It addresses fragmented procedures, limited competition, unequal access to information, and integrity risks in public asset management.",Prozorro.Sale,JSC “Prozorro.Sale”; Central-Government; Economic affairs n.e.c; Ukraine,"It uses APIs, open data, public BI dashboards, cloud infrastructure, and transparency-by-design principles to ensure equal access, accountability, and public oversight.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Prozorro.Sale is Ukraine’s national digital public infrastructure for the transparent sale and lease of public assets and rights. It addresses fragmented procedures, limited competition, unequal access to information, and integrity risks in public asset management. The solution combines a state-administered electronic trading system with more than 40 private e-marketplaces operating under common rules and standards. It uses APIs, open data, public BI dashboards, cloud infrastructure, and transparency-by-design principles to ensure equal access, accountability, and public oversight. Prozorro.Sale enables fair competition and market-based price discovery. Since 2016, the system has conducted over 860k auctions, generated more than UAH 130 billion, and attracted over 149k participants. It improves administrative efficiency and provides a scalable model for digital governance.",NON_AI_OR_UNCONFIRMED_TECHNOLOGY,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2953,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02302,EU_PSTW_202609_02302,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,"The responsible public sector organisations for this case are the “Centre de Telecomunicacions i Tecnologies de la Informació” (CTTI), as the main ICT provider for the Generalitat de Catalunya, and the Departament de Salut,Fundation TIC Salut i Social",Health n.e.c.,"Rural and remote healthcare areas in Catalonia, particularly in the Pyrenees, face logistical challenges in the rapid transport of biological samples, blood products, medicines and medical equipment.",Medical Drone Transport Corridor in Catalonia,"The responsible public sector organisations for this case are the “Centre de Telecomunicacions i Tecnologies de la Informació” (CTTI), as the main ICT provider for the Generalitat de Catalunya, and the Departament de Salut,Fundation TIC Salut i Social; Regional Government; Health n.e.c.; Spain","It uses Unmanned Aircraft Systems (UAS) to complement road transport with regular, on-demand and urgent aerial services between healthcare centres.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Rural and remote healthcare areas in Catalonia, particularly in the Pyrenees, face logistical challenges in the rapid transport of biological samples, blood products, medicines and medical equipment. The Medical Drone Transport Corridor in Catalonia, led by CTTI and the Department of Health, introduces a drone-based logistics service starting with the Lleida–Tremp corridor and Tremp-Sort corridor. It uses Unmanned Aircraft Systems (UAS) to complement road transport with regular, on-demand and urgent aerial services between healthcare centres. The project combines certified drone operations, healthcare air corridors, vertiports, traceability and a digital platform for mission management. Building on two pilots in rural and urban areas, the solution has shown faster deliveries, lower emissions and better sample preservation, including up to 75% shorter delivery times, up to 98% lower emissions and a 50% reduction in sample hemolysis. It also provides a scalable model for future healthcare corridors.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,IN_DEVELOPMENT,개발 중,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2954,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02303,EU_PSTW_202609_02303,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""social_nonprofit""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,The responsible public sector organisations for this is is the “Centre de Telecomunicacions i Tecnologies de la Informació” (CTTI) of the Generalitat de Catalunya.,Environmental protection n.e.c.,"It is now being validated as a cross-domain predictive model for district heating and shore-side electricity demand for vessels through the awarded Horizon Europe COSMIC project, and for public-space management through the awarded DesafIA Madrid challenge.",BRISA: A Cross-Domain AI Foundation Model for Predictive Public Infrastructure Management,The responsible public sector organisations for this is is the “Centre de Telecomunicacions i Tecnologies de la Informació” (CTTI) of the Generalitat de Catalunya.; Regional Government; Environmental protection n.e.c.; Spain,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"BRISA is an interoperable Artificial Intelligence solution that helps public administrations move from reactive management to predictive decision-making in energy and environmental policies. Based on a proprietary time-series foundation model trained on more than 11 billion energy, climate, mobility, occupancy and environmental data points, BRISA forecasts demand, detects anomalies, simulates intervention scenarios and prioritises actions with explainable and auditable outputs. The solution has already been validated in energy-efficiency management through GovTech4All with the Generalitat de Catalunya, and in urban air-quality forecasting and policy simulation with Pamplona City Council. It is now being validated as a cross-domain predictive model for district heating and shore-side electricity demand for vessels through the awarded Horizon Europe COSMIC project, and for public-space management through the awarded DesafIA Madrid challenge.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,S4_PREDICTION_DETECTION,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2955,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02304,EU_PSTW_202609_02304,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""enterprise_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,MKIFK Hungarian Gazette Publishing and Legal Translation Centre Ltd.,General services.,UNKNOWN,Artificial intelligence-based legal search service integrated in the Hungarian Gazette and National Legislation Database,MKIFK Hungarian Gazette Publishing and Legal Translation Centre Ltd.; Central-Government; General services.; Hungary,"The Gazette 2.0 project modernised IT systems supporting official gazette publication and integrated the National Legislation Database with an innovative AI platform accessible via jog.gov.hu, free of charge, implemented by co-financing of EU and hungarian Government.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"The Gazette 2.0 project modernised IT systems supporting official gazette publication and integrated the National Legislation Database with an innovative AI platform accessible via jog.gov.hu, free of charge, implemented by co-financing of EU and hungarian Government. The tool improve digital access to legislation for both the general public and the business sector. By artificial intelligence (LLM, RAG), the search system answers questions formulated in plain, everyday language, improving access for individuals less familiar with legal terminology and less digital skills. Key features include digital access to current gazette issues, AI-based legal search engine and smart summary of gazette content, interoperable and ELI-compatible integration of National Legislation Database, Gazette Portal, and Company Information Portal. The system improves user experience, legal awareness, supports informed decision-making, and serves both common citizens and legal professionals.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,S1_KNOWLEDGE_RETRIEVAL_RAG,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2956,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02305,EU_PSTW_202609_02305,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,The Danish Agency for Planning and Rural Development (Plan- og Landdistriktsstyrelsen)nddistriktsstyrelsen),General public services n.e.c.,UNKNOWN,Transforming environmental assessment with AI for Denmark's state-designated energy parks,The Danish Agency for Planning and Rural Development (Plan- og Landdistriktsstyrelsen)nddistriktsstyrelsen); Central-Government; General public services n.e.c.; Denmark,"The project demonstrates how structured use of AI, combined with digital public infrastructure, can modernise environmental governance, improve administrative efficiency and accelerate the delivery of public services while maintaining transparency, legal certainty and human oversight. It uses structured AI and interoperable public data to turn a complex, resource-intensive environmental assessment process into a faster, more consistent and more transparent workflow.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"The green transition requires public authorities to make faster and better-informed planning decisions while maintaining high environmental standards. To support this ambition, The Danish Agency for Planning and Rural Development has developed an AI-assisted solution that helps prepare Strategic Environmental Assessment (SEA) reports for Denmark's state-designated energy parks. The solution combines interoperable geospatial data, environmental information, planning documents and legislation with Generative AI to produce structured draft environmental reports. Rather than replacing professional judgement, it supports public officials by automating repetitive documentation tasks and enabling experts to focus on analysis, quality assurance and decision-making. The project demonstrates how structured use of AI, combined with digital public infrastructure, can modernise environmental governance, improve administrative efficiency and accelerate the delivery of public services while maintaining transparency, legal certainty and human oversight. At its core, the case is a digital government transformation initiative. It uses structured AI and interoperable public data to turn a complex, resource-intensive environmental assessment process into a faster, more consistent and more transparent workflow.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,IN_DEVELOPMENT,개발 중,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2957,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02306,EU_PSTW_202609_02306,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,The Swedish Agency for Digital Government,General services.,UNKNOWN,The Nordic Trust Model,The Swedish Agency for Digital Government; Central-Government; General services.; Sweden,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"The Nordic Trust Model for AI Systems is a service to support organizations in providing services with AI ethically, responsibly, and transparently. In the beta version of the trust model, verification is primarily supported through self-assessment and analysis. It can advantageously be used before and during development, as well as when a solution is in production. The self assessment and analyze of the result is supported by an AI Assistent and it gives both instant help and good relevant answers and coaching to the organisations when they assess their AI services. The model is based on relevant regulation, guidelines and experiences and refer to the AI Act and its criterias. The AI assistant base its output on a European model.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2958,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02307,EU_PSTW_202609_02307,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research"", ""enterprise_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Ajuntament de Sant Feliu de Llobregat,General services.,"This space works to address urban challenges through innovation, experimentation and public-private collaboration. The vision of the Ecodistrict, as a new urban centrality based on criteria of sustainability, safety, health and innovation, places the Innovation Unit before the challenge of prototyping sustainable technological solutions that can be applied to the future released space and generate a triple impact: social, environmental and economic.",Implementation of the First Autonomous Traffic Light with Artificial Intelligence Functionalities,Ajuntament de Sant Feliu de Llobregat; Local Government; General services.; Spain,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Sant Feliu de Llobregat City Council has an Innovation Unit, which operates through Sant Feliu Innova, the city’s public urban innovation laboratory. This space works to address urban challenges through innovation, experimentation and public-private collaboration. This approach is aligned with the Pla d’Actuació de Mandat 2023-2027, particularly with its 5th Horizon, focused on innovation and city promotion, which establishes the promotion of the economic and productive fabric through innovation as a priority. The initiative is also framed within the Agenda Urbana de Sant Feliu de Llobregat, specifically Objective 7.1, aimed at promoting local productivity, job creation, economic dynamism and the diversification of productive activity. Likewise, it is linked to the Agenda Digital de Sant Feliu de Llobregat, particularly Axis 4: Digital Economy, which promotes the modernisation and digitalisation of the productive fabric, SMEs and local businesses, with the aim of moving towards an agile, inclusive, climate-neutral, competitive and resource-efficient digital economy. In this context, the undergrounding of the railway tracks represents an unprecedented milestone for the city. The release of nearly 150,000 m² in the urban centre opens up a strategic opportunity to rethink the city model from an integrated perspective. The vision of the Ecodistrict, as a new urban centrality based on criteria of sustainability, safety, health and innovation, places the Innovation Unit before the challenge of prototyping sustainable technological solutions that can be applied to the future released space and generate a triple impact: social, environmental and economic. An example of this approach is the deployment of pilots in real urban environments, such as the autonomous traffic light installed in Sant Feliu de Llobregat. Since September 2025, the city has had a pedestrian crossing that operates independently from the electricity grid, thanks to a solar panel system that provides it with energy autonomy. In addition, the system incorporates local, technologically sovereign and sustainable artificial intelligence, designed to protect the most vulnerable pedestrians through voice assistance and to prevent potential failures. This patented technology emerged from CO-Innova Lab Sant Feliu, the city’s own centre for urban innovation and experimentation.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2959,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02308,EU_PSTW_202609_02308,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,District Administration Recklinghausen,Environmental protection n.e.c.,"'- Manual mapping, which is highly time-consuming, costly, and difficult to maintain.",Automatic detection of impervious surfaces using AI,District Administration Recklinghausen; Local Government; Environmental protection n.e.c.; Germany,"To date, imperviousness has mainly been determined using: - Cadastral data, which only partially reflect the actual on-site situation. These developments make the automated detection of impervious surfaces using AI a promising approach.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"In the context of progressing climate change, a precise and up-to-date overview of impervious surfaces in municipalities is essential. Impervious surfaces (approximately 45% of settlement and transport areas in Germany) reduce rainwater infiltration and contribute to the formation of urban heat islands by acting as heat storage. To date, imperviousness has mainly been determined using: - Cadastral data, which only partially reflect the actual on-site situation. - Manual mapping, which is highly time-consuming, costly, and difficult to maintain. At the same time, AI-based methods—particularly deep convolutional neural networks for image analysis—have made significant performance advances. In parallel, the availability of high-resolution georeferenced data has increased, such as annual digital orthophotos (DOPs) with a ground resolution of up to 10 cm (RGB and near-infrared/NIR). These developments make the automated detection of impervious surfaces using AI a promising approach. The district of Recklinghausen, in cooperation with the Westphalian University of Applied Sciences, initiated a project to automatically detect and classify impervious surfaces.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2960,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02309,EU_PSTW_202609_02309,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""social_nonprofit""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Association of Netherlands Municipalities (VNG),General public services n.e.c.,"Public authorities across Europe face a structural implementation challenge: the same authoritative source data is increasingly needed for OOTS, eIDAS 2.0, wallets and future cross-border public services, while source access is often still organised separately for each channel or legal obligation. This creates duplication, higher implementation costs and fragmented interoperability.",BronConnect: Reusable source access for European digital government services,Association of Netherlands Municipalities (VNG); Local Government; General public services n.e.c.; Netherlands,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Public authorities across Europe face a structural implementation challenge: the same authoritative source data is increasingly needed for OOTS, eIDAS 2.0, wallets and future cross-border public services, while source access is often still organised separately for each channel or legal obligation. This creates duplication, higher implementation costs and fragmented interoperability. BronConnect addresses this challenge by taking the authoritative source as the starting point: it defines one reusable way for trusted public-sector data to be made available securely, with the user in control, across multiple European digital government contexts. BronConnect is an initiative led by the Association of Netherlands Municipalities, the national organisation representing Dutch local authorities. It develops a uniform and reusable approach for making municipal source data available to European and national data exchange infrastructures. Rather than building a separate connection for each regulation or channel, BronConnect defines how trusted data from municipal sources can be accessed once and reused for multiple purposes, including OOTS, eIDAS 2.0 and future wallet-based services. The initiative builds on, and works with, the standard OOTS infrastructure. Its added value lies at the source-holder side: standardising source access, developing reusable DATA-API specifications, aligning with the Federated Data System, and creating an implementation model that municipalities and other public authorities can adopt without each designing their own solution. Led by the Association of Netherlands Municipalities, with Indra Henneman as project lead, BronConnect brings together municipalities and key partners in the Dutch SDG/OOTS ecosystem, including RINIS, EnableU, Cleverbase, the Federated Data System, Digilab/BZK and the national SDG/OOTS network. The project translates European legal and technical requirements into a practical model for source-side interoperability. By shifting the focus from individual channels to reusable source access, BronConnect helps make the Once-Only Principle operational in practice. It reduces duplication, supports secure cross-border public services and creates a scalable foundation for future European digital government obligations.",NON_AI_OR_UNCONFIRMED_TECHNOLOGY,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2961,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02310,EU_PSTW_202609_02310,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Community of Madrid | Regional Ministry of Digitalization,General public services n.e.c.,UNKNOWN,SABIA & Sol: AI-Powered Citizen Assistant,Community of Madrid | Regional Ministry of Digitalization; Regional Government; General public services n.e.c.; Spain,"Fully aligned with the EU AI Act, GDPR and the Spanish National Security Framework, SABIA establishes a scalable and citizen-centric model for the responsible use of AI in public administration.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"SABIA Assistant & Avatar Sol is an Artificial Intelligence-based solution developed by the Community of Madrid to transform citizen access to public information and services. The system combines generative AI, semantic search and a conversational avatar to provide accurate, personalised and accessible responses through natural language interactions, available 24/7. Built on a secure Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) architecture, it retrieves and organises information from official government sources, ensuring reliable and up-to-date answers. The solution reduces information search times from several minutes to just a few seconds, improves digital inclusion through multilingual and voice-enabled interactions, and decreases reliance on traditional support channels. Fully aligned with the EU AI Act, GDPR and the Spanish National Security Framework, SABIA establishes a scalable and citizen-centric model for the responsible use of AI in public administration.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,S1_KNOWLEDGE_RETRIEVAL_RAG,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2962,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02311,EU_PSTW_202609_02311,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,"Incubator for AI - Department for Science, Innovation and Technology",Housing and community amenities n.e.c.,"Manual digitisation can take up to two hours per document; on average, Extract produces a draft in about two minutes.",Extract: AI-powered planning data for every council in England,"Incubator for AI - Department for Science, Innovation and Technology; Central-Government; Housing and community amenities n.e.c.; United Kingdom","It combines vision language models, Meta's Segment Anything Model and automated geo-referencing in a modular pipeline, with a human-in-the-loop interface so officers review every output before use.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Extract is an AI tool that turns England's historic planning records — scanned Conservation Area appraisals, Article 4 Directions and Tree Preservation Orders, locked in old PDFs and paper maps — into accurate, standardised digital geospatial data. It combines vision language models, Meta's Segment Anything Model and automated geo-referencing in a modular pipeline, with a human-in-the-loop interface so officers review every output before use. Manual digitisation can take up to two hours per document; on average, Extract produces a draft in about two minutes. Built by DSIT's i.AI in partnership with MHCLG's Digital Planning Programme, it launched free to every local planning authority in England in June 2026. This unlocks decades of trapped planning data, speeds up planning decisions and supports the government's commitment to build 1.5 million new homes.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2963,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02312,EU_PSTW_202609_02312,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,State Technological Reform Agency (ARTE),General public services n.e.c.,UNKNOWN,Digital Twins for Smart Territories,State Technological Reform Agency (ARTE); Central-Government; General public services n.e.c.; Portugal,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Digital Twins for Smart Territories contributes to the goals of the Portuguese National Strategy for Smart Territories, by promoting the development and implementation of digital twins in eight nationally prioritized thematic areas: Health, Mobility, Decarbonization, Tourism, Civil Protection, Climate Resilience, Agriculture, and Water Management. The initiative aims to support the development of reusable digital twins that, can be integrated by public administration entities, for the development ofinto public policies and decision-making processes. It also seeks to promote innovation and technological responsiveness across territories, while engaging the national scientific and technological ecosystem in the creation of digital solutions with a direct impact on public management and citizens’ quality of life.",NON_AI_OR_UNCONFIRMED_TECHNOLOGY,IN_DEVELOPMENT,개발 중,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2964,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02313,EU_PSTW_202609_02313,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Département d'Eure-et-Loir (Eure-et-Loir Departmental Council),Social protection n.e.c.,UNKNOWN,MesAides28: Digital twins of social welfare policies to improve social support through Rules as Code,Département d'Eure-et-Loir (Eure-et-Loir Departmental Council); Regional Government; Social protection n.e.c.; France,MesAides28 is a digital benefits calculator that leverages OpenFisca's Rules-as-Code technology to help citizens of the Eure-et-Loir department in France determine their eligibility and potential benefit amounts across complex social welfare programs. We can also use this resource to design reforms through precise impact simulation.,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"MesAides28 is a digital benefits calculator that leverages OpenFisca's Rules-as-Code technology to help citizens of the Eure-et-Loir department in France determine their eligibility and potential benefit amounts across complex social welfare programs. By transforming legislation into machine-consumable rules, the solution simplifies access to social benefits, reduces administrative complexity, and increases policy uptake. It enables us as a local government to provide accurate information on both national and local benefits, and to better understand and explain the interaction of our policies with national ones. We can also use this resource to design reforms through precise impact simulation.",NON_AI_OR_UNCONFIRMED_TECHNOLOGY,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2965,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02314,EU_PSTW_202609_02314,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Free and Hanseatic City of Hamburg – State Agency for Geoinformation and Surveying,Housing and community amenities n.e.c.,UNKNOWN,From Urban Data to Simulated Decisions: Hamburg's AI-enabled Urban Digital Twin for Real-time Policy Simulation,Free and Hanseatic City of Hamburg – State Agency for Geoinformation and Surveying; Regional Government; Housing and community amenities n.e.c.; Germany,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Hamburg's Digital Twin turns open urban data into evidence for policy decisions. It combines the Urban Data Platform (UDP_HH), Urban Model Platform (UMP), open-source Masterportal and UDP-Agent into an AI-enabled urban digital twin for real-time policy simulation. UDP_HH provides governed geospatial, sensor and urban data through open APIs. UMP exposes models and simulations through standards such as OGC API Processes. Masterportal and its add-ons - 3D Projektplaner, Scenario Explorer and Data Narrator - let users create 3D planning scenarios, run and compare simulations, and explain results through maps and narratives. The UDP-Agent adds a natural-language and agentic layer for data discovery, spatial analysis and evidence generation. Public servants can move from a policy question - for example the impact of a new road layout on traffic noise, wind or heat - to a map-based scenario, simulation result and explainable decision basis. The stack is reusable for other European cities.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2966,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02315,EU_PSTW_202609_02315,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,"Ministry of the Presidency, Justice and Relations with the Courts",Law courts,UNKNOWN,Intelligent Automation of Judicial Proceedings through AI and RPA,"Ministry of the Presidency, Justice and Relations with the Courts; Central-Government; Law courts; Spain",UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"The Ministry of the Presidency, Justice and Relations with the Courts has developed a comprehensive Smart Automation strategy that combines Artificial Intelligence (AI), Robotic Process Automation (RPA) and Hyperautomation to transform the management of judicial proceedings and improve the services provided to citizens. It currently has more than 30 lines of work and more than 60 active robots, which have allowed more than 23 million automated operations to be executed, saving more than 1.18 million working hours and generating economic savings of more than 26 million euros. AI-based initiatives streamline document management and facilitate access to legal information through solutions such as smart summaries, clear reading and easy reading. Currently, more than 600,000 AI processes have been executed. Hyperautomation combines both technologies to process up to 340 monitoring procedures per day from end to end.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,S6_WORKFLOW_PROCESS_AUTOMATION,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2967,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02316,EU_PSTW_202609_02316,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Municipality of Druskininkai,General public services n.e.c.,UNKNOWN,Implementation of an Information System for the Optimization of Strategic Planning and Project Management Processes within the Druskininkai Municipality Administration,Municipality of Druskininkai; Local Government; General public services n.e.c.; Lithuania,"The implemented solution contributes to a smarter, more efficient, and data-driven transformation of the public sector, strengthens the institution’s ability to respond rapidly to change, and helps ensure higher-quality services for residents.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Druskininkai Municipality has developed an innovative Strategic Planning and Project Management Information System that transforms strategic governance, project administration, and planning processes in the public sector. It is one of the first integrated solutions of its kind among Lithuanian municipalities, bringing together strategic planning, project management, budget planning, and public procurement processes within a single digital platform. The project not only modernizes the municipality’s internal operations but also establishes a new model for public service management that can serve as a best-practice example for other municipalities. The implemented solution contributes to a smarter, more efficient, and data-driven transformation of the public sector, strengthens the institution’s ability to respond rapidly to change, and helps ensure higher-quality services for residents.",NON_AI_OR_UNCONFIRMED_TECHNOLOGY,IN_DEVELOPMENT,개발 중,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2968,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02317,EU_PSTW_202609_02317,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Ajuntament de Sant Feliu de Llobregat,General public services n.e.c.,UNKNOWN,SmartCityMAP: Sant Feliu de Llobregat's BIM-Based Digital Twin Platform for Municipal Asset Management,Ajuntament de Sant Feliu de Llobregat; Local Government; General public services n.e.c.; Spain,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"The Ajuntament de Sant Feliu de Llobregat has built an interoperable digital twin ecosystem connecting Building Information Modelling (BIM) with real-time IoT sensing and open data to manage municipal buildings and infrastructure. Centred on the open-source platform BIMROCKET (a common data environment for IFC models) and the open-source AI/rules engine Brain4it, the system links static 3D models with the real behaviour of assets, enabling automated lighting and climate control, remote energy monitoring, faster and cheaper technical audits, and a prototype for automated compliance-checking of building permits. Eighteen municipal facilities (33% of the building stock) are already digitised, with a roadmap to reach 75% by 2030, and the model is now being scaled to other Catalan and Spanish public administrations.",NON_AI_OR_UNCONFIRMED_TECHNOLOGY,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2969,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02318,EU_PSTW_202609_02318,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Berlin Senate Chancellery,General public services n.e.c.,UNKNOWN,BärGPT: An Open-Source AI Assistant for a Sovereign Public Administration,Berlin Senate Chancellery; Regional Government; General public services n.e.c.; Germany,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"BärGPT (https://www.baergpt.berlin) is an open-source AI assistant developed for Berlin’s public administration to support everyday work while ensuring digital sovereignty. Built on European technologies and infrastructure, it helps civil servants analyze documents, draft texts, prepare policy briefs, and evaluate administrative data. Developed through an iterative, user-centered design process involving civil servants, BärGPT combines retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), transparent source citations and persistent document management to deliver trustworthy results. Since its launch in November 2025, there have been over 16,000 account registrations, and BärGPT has enabled users to work more efficiently while complying with public sector requirements. As an open-source solution, BärGPT can be adapted and replicated by other public administrations. It’s the result of a collaboration between Berlin’s Senate Chancellery (Senatskanzlei Berlin) and Berlin’s public innovation lab CityLAB Berlin.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,S1_KNOWLEDGE_RETRIEVAL_RAG,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2970,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02319,EU_PSTW_202609_02319,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""enterprise_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,State Technological Reform Agency (ARTE),General public services n.e.c.,UNKNOWN,Gov.pt’s GenAI-powered Virtual Assistant,State Technological Reform Agency (ARTE); Central-Government; General public services n.e.c.; Portugal,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"The Portuguese single digital gateway, Gov.pt, provides a multilingual GenAI virtual assistant (chatbot) that gives real-time guidanceinformation on +2400 public services, answering both in text and/or audio, in 12 different languages, with an animated avatar. It benefits citizens, foreign residents and businesses by making information easier to find and understand. It was developed to cut bureaucratic friction, such as complex navigation in over 5000 webpages, language barriers or long waits in onsite public attendance or support channels, while reducing workload on public administration.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,S2_AGENT_CONVERSATIONAL_AI,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2971,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02320,EU_PSTW_202609_02320,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,EUROCONTROL,General public services n.e.c.,UNKNOWN,EUROCONTROL – AI-powered Digital Twins for Air Traffic Management,EUROCONTROL; European intergovernmental organisation; General public services n.e.c.; Belgium,"European Air Traffic Management is becoming increasingly complex, requiring new ways to anticipate the impact of operational decisions before they are implemented. To explore the potential of emerging technologies, EUROCONTROL partnered with Cronos Europa to develop an AI-powered Digital Twin Proof of Concept.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"European Air Traffic Management is becoming increasingly complex, requiring new ways to anticipate the impact of operational decisions before they are implemented. To explore the potential of emerging technologies, EUROCONTROL partnered with Cronos Europa to develop an AI-powered Digital Twin Proof of Concept. The solution was designed and implemented by Mr. Watts, a competence center within De Cronos Groep specialising in Artificial Intelligence and advanced digital solutions. By combining Artificial Intelligence with Digital Twin technology, the project demonstrates how realistic operational simulations can support evidence-based decision-making, strengthen collaboration and improve operational resilience. The Proof of Concept also illustrates how interoperable digital technologies can complement existing operational environments while supporting future innovation in Air Traffic Management.",NON_AI_OR_UNCONFIRMED_TECHNOLOGY,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2972,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02321,EU_PSTW_202609_02321,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,National Agency of Information Society,General public services n.e.c.,UNKNOWN,Artificial Intelligence for detecting legal overlaps and improving legislative harmonization in Albania,National Agency of Information Society; Central-Government; General public services n.e.c.; Albania,"The AI-powered Law Overlap Detection System is an innovative solution developed by the National Agency for Information Society (NAIS) and the Ministry of Justice to improve the quality and consistency of Albania’s legal framework. Using artificial intelligence and large language models (LLMs), the system analyzes over 27,000 legal acts in the National Registry of Legislation to identify overlaps, contradictions, and inconsistencies between draft laws and existing legislation.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"The AI-powered Law Overlap Detection System is an innovative solution developed by the National Agency for Information Society (NAIS) and the Ministry of Justice to improve the quality and consistency of Albania’s legal framework. Using artificial intelligence and large language models (LLMs), the system analyzes over 27,000 legal acts in the National Registry of Legislation to identify overlaps, contradictions, and inconsistencies between draft laws and existing legislation. Integrated with the Official Gazette, it enables legal experts to compare legal texts, generate structured comparison tables, and produce evidence-based legal analyses. By automating complex legislative reviews, the platform reduces processing time, improves drafting accuracy, and supports more transparent and reliable decision-making. The initiative modernizes legislative processes and strengthens Albania’s alignment with the EU acquis through AI-assisted legal harmonization.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2973,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02322,EU_PSTW_202609_02322,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Athumi,General public services n.e.c.,"The death of a loved one is one of life's most difficult moments. By replacing fragmented paper-based procedures with one secure digital workflow, eLys enables trusted data exchange between healthcare providers, local authorities and funeral directors.",eLys – Enabling Trusted Data Exchange for Better Public Services,Athumi; Regional Government; General public services n.e.c.; Belgium,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"The death of a loved one is one of life's most difficult moments. Administrative procedures should support citizens during this time, not add unnecessary complexity. Developed by Athumi in collaboration with the Flemish Government, eLys is a trusted digital platform that transforms the civil death registration process across Flanders. The implementation brought together Cronos Public Services, the De Cronos Groep entity specialised in digital transformation for the Belgian public sector, and Kunlabora, a De Cronos Groep competence center specialising in public sector innovation and service design. By replacing fragmented paper-based procedures with one secure digital workflow, eLys enables trusted data exchange between healthcare providers, local authorities and funeral directors. The platform reduces administrative burden, improves data quality and demonstrates how interoperability creates tangible public value.",NON_AI_OR_UNCONFIRMED_TECHNOLOGY,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2974,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02323,EU_PSTW_202609_02323,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""enterprise_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,IdomSoft Zrt. (100% state-owned IT development company),Public order and safety n.e.c.,"IdomSoft’s field-tested pilot was co-designed with police and fire-service professionals and replaces slow spatial documentation based on manual measurements, sketches and photo annexes.",Digital Twin Scene: Rapid 3D Documentation for Public-Safety Investigations,IdomSoft Zrt. (100% state-owned IT development company); Central-Government; Public order and safety n.e.c.; Hungary,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Digital Twin Scene enables the AI-assisted creation of accurate, scale-aware 3D records of traffic accidents, crime and fire scenes, illegal-waste sites and evidence objects within minutes with ordinary cameras and drones. IdomSoft’s field-tested pilot was co-designed with police and fire-service professionals and replaces slow spatial documentation based on manual measurements, sketches and photo annexes. In parallel field testing, an average two-car accident was captured and modelled in under 15 minutes, versus 3–4 hours for the current documentation process. Professionals remain responsible for analysing the models and making decisions. The records support measurement, enlargement and immersive AR/VR review, and are already used in real cases and formal police and fire-investigator training. Over 100 case-related models demonstrate operational maturity. Affordable capture, compact outputs and low computing needs make the method fast, cost-effective, resource-efficient and reusable.",NON_AI_OR_UNCONFIRMED_TECHNOLOGY,PILOT,시험·파일럿,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2975,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02324,EU_PSTW_202609_02324,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Government of New Caledonia – Digital Transformation Directorate,Economic affairs n.e.c,"In early 2025, following a major social crisis, the New Caledonian territory faced a difficult situation: housing aid applications had surged by 30 percent while government revenue collapsed by 14 percent of GDP.",A digital twin of policies to enable reform design and buy-in through Rules as Code,Government of New Caledonia – Digital Transformation Directorate; Regional Government; Economic affairs n.e.c; France,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"In early 2025, following a major social crisis, the New Caledonian territory faced a difficult situation: housing aid applications had surged by 30 percent while government revenue collapsed by 14 percent of GDP. A digital twin of New Caledonia's housing benefit laws, created with the Rules as Code engine OpenFisca and a simple user interface on top, allowed impact assessment of reform scenarios during this major economic crisis. The solution prevented austerity measures that would have backfired significantly by revealing their minimal fiscal impact, leading to a major redesign of the policy through stakeholder collaboration. On top, the resulting increase in taxation received strong buy-in from the taxed subjects once they were presented with the ability to interact with the digital twin themselves.",NON_AI_OR_UNCONFIRMED_TECHNOLOGY,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2976,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02325,EU_PSTW_202609_02325,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,KF norway,General public services n.e.c.,"The model is particularly valuable for smaller administrations that may have limited internal capacity for form design, technical configuration and ongoing maintenance.",Form+: Reuse instead of rebuilding - A shared municipal forms service,KF norway; Regional Government; General public services n.e.c.; Norway,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Form+ is a shared digital form service provided by Kommuneforlaget for Norwegian municipalities and other public-sector organisations. Kommuneforlaget creates digital forms for common administrative and citizen-facing needs and publishes them in a shared form library. Participating organisations can select the forms they need from the library instead of independently designing and implementing equivalent forms. The solution supports reuse across the public sector. A form developed to address a recurring municipal need can be made available to multiple organisations through the same service. This reduces duplicated development work, supports more consistent digital services and gives municipalities access to forms created and maintained by a dedicated service provider. The model is particularly valuable for smaller administrations that may have limited internal capacity for form design, technical configuration and ongoing maintenance.",NON_AI_OR_UNCONFIRMED_TECHNOLOGY,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2977,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02326,EU_PSTW_202609_02326,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""social_nonprofit""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,ISTAT,General public services n.e.c.,UNKNOWN,The Semantic Intelligence Services,ISTAT; Central-Government; General public services n.e.c.; Italy,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"The SIS project, developed by ISTAT with DXC Technology and Lutech, addresses the semantic gap in public sector interoperability. By integrating the transactional Piattaforma Digitale Nazionale Dati (PDND) and the authoritative National Data Catalog (schema.gov.it), SIS supports data providers, consumers, and governors by automating the verification and discovery of data meaning in API specifications and API-based exchanges to enhance ecosystem semantic quality. SIS deploys a collaborative Agent Crew orchestrated by a central Semantic Broker and supported by specialized agents like the Schema Assistant and API Catalog Assistant. These agents dynamically query technical API specifications and map fields onto standardized ontologies and vocabularies. The pilot demonstrates that public sector data can transition from machine-readable to machine-comprehensible, establishing the foundation for trust, automated semantic quality assurance, and seamless cross-border e-Government.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2978,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02327,EU_PSTW_202609_02327,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Italian Ministry of Labour and Social Policies (Ministero del Lavoro e delle Politiche Sociali),Social protection n.e.c.,"These activities generate large volumes of documentation and complex procedures, while being managed by a limited number of officials. The resulting administrative burden has increased processing times and highlighted the need for advanced digital tools to improve efficiency, consistency, knowledge sharing, and decision-making.",Digital Supervisory Intelligence for Private Pension Schemes,Italian Ministry of Labour and Social Policies (Ministero del Lavoro e delle Politiche Sociali); Central-Government; Social protection n.e.c.; Italy,"By combining this legal and regulatory framework with the economic, financial, and actuarial information extracted from the funds' reports, the platform leverages advanced Artificial Intelligence algorithms to support supervisory decision-making. After applicants review and verify the submitted information, the platform performs a preliminary formal review using an artificial intelligence algorithm.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"The Ministry of Labour and Social Policies (MLPS) supervises pension and social security institutions, including private-law entities established under D.Lgs No. 509/1994 and No. 103/1996. Its responsibilities cover both legal-administrative and financial oversight, including the approval of resolutions on contributions, benefits, governance, and appointments; the review of budgets, financial statements, actuarial reports, and investment plans; the assessment of financial sustainability and regulatory compliance in cooperation with other authorities, including MEF and COVIP. These activities generate large volumes of documentation and complex procedures, while being managed by a limited number of officials. The resulting administrative burden has increased processing times and highlighted the need for advanced digital tools to improve efficiency, consistency, knowledge sharing, and decision-making. The platform represents the first integrated digital environment specifically designed to enhance, streamline, and accelerate the supervisory and monitoring activities carried out by the MLPS overseeing private pension schemes. The platform has been conceived to support the supervision of 20 private pension funds currently operating in Italy, providing a comprehensive digital environment for the analysis, management, and assessment of both financial and governance-related information. The system is structured around two integrated modules. 1. Document Management, Analysis, and Knowledge Discovery Module The first module is dedicated to the collection, storage, processing, indexing, and intelligent analysis of all documents periodically submitted by pension funds to their supervisory authority. Through a centralized and highly searchable repository, supervisory staff can rapidly retrieve relevant information, navigate large volumes of documentation, and perform cross-document analyses that would otherwise require significant manual effort. The platform manages a wide range of documents, including annual budgets, financial statements, actuarial balance sheets, investment plans, board resolutions, minutes, reports issued by the Board of Statutory Auditors, and other regulatory filings. Advanced indexing and semantic-search capabilities enable users to identify specific information within seconds, compare data across multiple reporting periods, and conduct in-depth analyses of financial, governance, and operational trends. The system also includes sophisticated analytical tools that allow supervisors to generate reports, perform data aggregations, visualize historical developments through comparative tables and time-series analyses, and monitor key indicators over extended periods. These functionalities significantly improve the efficiency and consistency of supervisory activities while reducing the operational burden on staff. A particularly valuable feature concerns the assessment of board resolutions submitted for approval. In addition to the resolutions themselves, the platform incorporates a comprehensive and constantly updated repository of applicable legislation, regulatory provisions, pension-fund statutes, internal regulations, and governance rules adopted by each scheme. By combining this legal and regulatory framework with the economic, financial, and actuarial information extracted from the funds' reports, the platform leverages advanced Artificial Intelligence algorithms to support supervisory decision-making. Users can interact with the AI engine either through predefined prompts tailored to specific supervisory tasks or through a free-form conversational interface. The system can identify relevant regulatory references, highlighting potential inconsistencies or compliance issues, assessing the coherence of proposed decisions with applicable rules, and providing reasoned analyses to support the approval or rejection of board resolutions. Furthermore, it assists supervisory personnel in drafting technical opinions, advisory reports, and formal assessments, substantially reducing preparation time while improving the quality, consistency, and traceability of regulatory evaluations. 2. Appointment Management and Eligibility Assessment Module The second module issues invitations to complete application forms for appointments to the audit bodies of 20 pension schemes, the 36 administrative committees responsible for managing INPS (National Institute of Pension Schemes) funds, and four private complementary pension funds. Applications are transmitted to and verified by the Supervisory Authority’s staff. The module manages the full initial submission workflow, from the invitation sent to the candidate through the transmission of the completed application and supporting documents to the competent supervisory staff. This also supports efficient handling of each individual appointment procedure. Through a certified authentication system, selected individuals can complete an online form, upload a CV and an ID document and, after confirming the accuracy of the information entered, automatically generate the documents that the Administration must publish on its transparency portal. After applicants review and verify the submitted information, the platform performs a preliminary formal review using an artificial intelligence algorithm. It provides feedback indicating, for example, whether a document is expired, a file has the wrong format, a file submitted as a CV is not a curriculum vitae, the CV contains a name different from the applicant’s, or the CV lacks the declarations required for self-certifications and sworn statements. When formal errors are detected, the platform alerts applicants, enabling them to correct the issues and upload the appropriate documentation. This initial phase reduces completion errors and processing times. Consequently, applications reach the competent authority complete and formally compliant, allowing its staff to focus on substantive rather than formal checks. Immediately after submission, an officer of the Supervisory Authority can review the documentation and initiate automated checks to verify its completeness and formal correctness and, within the information available on the platform, identify potential risks concerning conflicts of interest, incompatibility, or ineligibility for appointment. For example, the platform examines candidates’ CVs and the positions they declare they currently hold or have held during the previous two years, to identify companies affiliated with or controlled by the pension institution concerned. This assessment is conducted by analysing the notes to the institution’s financial statements. If an officer needs to clarify additional issues, an AI-powered free-text chat function is available. It enables the officer to query all documentation stored on the platform, including declarations and supporting documents, conduct further analysis, and investigate matters requiring additional scrutiny. *** A core innovation of the platform is the transformation of previously siloed information into a shared institutional knowledge base. Historically, supervisory processes were managed by different offices, resulting in fragmented information, duplicated activities, and limited knowledge transfer. The platform overcomes these constraints by integrating documents, data, regulatory sources, and procedural information within a single digital environment. This substantially reduces the effort required to store, analyze, and retrieve relevant information, while enhancing collaboration, preserving institutional knowledge, and improving the overall effectiveness and efficiency of supervisory activities",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,F06_HIGH_VOLUME_SCALABILITY_BOTTLENECK,S7_GENERATIVE_CONTENT_CREATION,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2979,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02328,EU_PSTW_202609_02328,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Provincia di Reggio nell' Emilia,General public services n.e.c.,UNKNOWN,OpenPA Local AI: A Modular AI and Document Automation Platform for Public Administration,Provincia di Reggio nell' Emilia; Local Government; General public services n.e.c.; Italy,"OpenPA Local AI is a locally deployed, modular platform designed to increase the operational autonomy of public administration staff. Implemented within the Province of Reggio Emilia, it runs on Ubuntu and combines a locally deployed language model with Python applications built with free and open-source libraries.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"OpenPA Local AI is a locally deployed, modular platform designed to increase the operational autonomy of public administration staff. Implemented within the Province of Reggio Emilia, it runs on Ubuntu and combines a locally deployed language model with Python applications built with free and open-source libraries. The platform supports document search and summarisation, assistance on procedures and services, audio and video transcription, PDF-to-Word conversion, OCR for scanned PDFs and images, PDF compression, and automation of repetitive administrative tasks. Local deployment gives the administration greater control over data, configuration and costs, while the modular architecture allows new applications to be added according to the needs of different offices and reused by other public bodies.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2980,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02329,EU_PSTW_202609_02329,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""enterprise_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,INPS - National Social Security Institute,Social protection n.e.c.,UNKNOWN,INPS ISAC – Generative Artificial Intelligence applied to social security contribution compliance.,INPS - National Social Security Institute; Central-Government; Social protection n.e.c.; Italy,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"INPS, in agreement with the Ministry of Labour and Social Policies, the Ministry of Economy and Finance (MEF) and the National Labour Inspectorate (INL), has developed the Statistical Indicators of Contribution Reliability (Indicatori Statistici di Affidabilità Contributiva, known as ISAC) in order to promote preventive contribution compliance and to identify cases of under-declaration of employment, by means of indicators that compare tax and social security contribution data. The process provides for compliance letters to be sent to companies, setting out any deviations in the indicators, as determined by the Institute. Once the compliance letters have been sent, companies may justify and explain the deviations, including by attaching appropriate documentation, by submitting specific communications through the INPS channels. The generative AI component operates in the analysis of the communications submitted by companies: it analyses and assesses the replies and any attachments in line with the deviations determined by the Institute; it extracts the evidence provided by the company; it assigns the companies’ replies to specific clusters; it proposes an explainable justification of the analysis carried out and also prepares a draft reply to the company itself. INPS staff govern the entire process: they examine, modify, supplement and/or validate the output produced by the AI system, that is, they retain responsibility for the final decision in providing feedback to the company. The outcomes feed into monitoring, enabling continuous improvement of the system. The first application concerns the “Wholesale food trade” sector and the “Hotel and non-hotel accommodation facilities” sector, for a total of 35,491 companies analysed and 20,038 compliance letters sent. The solution improves consistency, timeliness and traceability and will be extended to six further production sectors, namely: - Bar, ice-cream parlour, pastry shop and confectionery production activities, for a total of 91,048 businesses; - Retail sale of medical and orthopaedic goods, for a total of 2,551 businesses; - Installation of electrical, plumbing and other building installations, for a total of 113,063 businesses; - Bespoke and mass production of clothing, accessories and household linen, and related processing, for a total of 17,543 businesses; - Hairdressing services, for a total of 38,794 businesses; - “Maintenance and repair of motor vehicles, motorcycles and mopeds”, for a total of 49,035 businesses. The legal entities affected will total 312,034, while approximately 176,000 letters will be sent. The proposed solution has been designed with features of flexibility and modularity that also allow it to be extended to further processes, promoting the standardisation of activities and the optimisation of the resources employed.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,S5_OPTIMIZATION_DECISION_SUPPORT,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2981,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02330,EU_PSTW_202609_02330,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Ministry of Labour and Social Policies (Ministero del Lavoro e delle Politiche Sociali),Economic affairs n.e.c,"Evidence on artificial intelligence and work evolves rapidly and remains fragmented across public institutions, research bodies, firms, workers and social partners.",SIO: AI-enabled evidence infrastructure for Italy's Observatory on Artificial Intelligence and Labour,Ministry of Labour and Social Policies (Ministero del Lavoro e delle Politiche Sociali); Central-Government; Economic affairs n.e.c; Italy,"Its governed architecture separates orchestration from generation, applies differentiated access and keeps validation and institutional responsibility with the Ministry and the Observatory.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Evidence on artificial intelligence and work evolves rapidly and remains fragmented across public institutions, research bodies, firms, workers and social partners. SIO (Sistema Intelligente dell’Osservatorio, the Intelligent System of the Observatory) is the AI-enabled evidence infrastructure of Italy’s Observatory on Artificial Intelligence and Labour, established within the Ministry of Labour and Social Policies. It combines a curated, source-linked knowledge base, a public conversational interface and an adaptive consultation environment for the Observatory’s bodies. Its governed architecture separates orchestration from generation, applies differentiated access and keeps validation and institutional responsibility with the Ministry and the Observatory. SIO supports a more structured, comparable and traceable evidence-to-policy cycle and provides a transferable model for public institutions addressing fast-moving technological change.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2982,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02336,EU_PSTW_202609_02336,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""enterprise_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Government of Navarra,Economic affairs n.e.c,UNKNOWN,IRIS Navarra: Turning Frontier Technologies into a Shared Public Resource for Regional Innovation,Government of Navarra; Regional Government; Economic affairs n.e.c; Spain,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"IRIS Navarra is a regional public innovation ecosystem promoted by the Government of Navarra and formally supported by a collaboration agreement involving 40 leading public and private organisations. Recognised as a European Digital Innovation Hub since 2023, IRIS has evolved into a permanent regional capability backed by €13 million in public investment. It gives companies and public organisations access to more than 220 services, 104 regional technology providers and advanced experimentation facilities in AI, supercomputing, synthetic biology, genomics, IoT, robotics and advanced manufacturing. More than 3,000 companies have already benefited from the Polo, while over 200 have used IRIS Lab infrastructures. By reducing the cost and risk of experimentation, IRIS enables organisations to test before investing and increasingly positions Navarra as a real-world testbed for frontier technologies.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2985,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02338,EU_PSTW_202609_02338,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Ministry of Education and Merit,Education n.e.c.,UNKNOWN,What's Next - The immersive orientation,Ministry of Education and Merit; Central-Government; Education n.e.c.; Italy,"Through a co-design process involving schools, ITS Academies, and the General Directorates of the Italian Ministry of Education and Merit (MIM), the service use cases were identified and implemented across two releases: the first dedicated to ITS Academies and the second to upper secondary school.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"The adoption of emerging technologies, such as Artificial Intelligence and Spatial Computing, in education has contributed to rethinking the learning experience. Within this context, Whatâ€™s Next was created: the immersive orientation service that guides students and families in exploring upper secondary school pathways and tertiary education. Through a co-design process involving schools, ITS Academies, and the General Directorates of the Italian Ministry of Education and Merit (MIM), the service use cases were identified and implemented across two releases: the first dedicated to ITS Academies and the second to upper secondary school. Integrated into Unica and accessible from PCs, tablets, smartphones, and headsets, the service offers Digital Human-guided tours through immersive environments enriched with 3D objects and interactive laboratories, combining generative AI, Virtual Reality, and Augmented Reality. Whatâ€™s Next ensures privacy and data protection in compliance with applicable regulations.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2987,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02339,EU_PSTW_202609_02339,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Madrid City Council (Ayuntamiento de Madrid),General public services n.e.c.,UNKNOWN,"SyRCI-IA: Human-Supervised AI for Routing Suggestions, Complaints and Compliments",Madrid City Council (Ayuntamiento de Madrid); Local Government; General public services n.e.c.; Spain,"Within the measured scope, rules and AI automate 97.46% of routings; AI accounts for 47.06% of automated routings.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"SyRCI-IA is Madrid City Council’s human-supervised artificial intelligence capability for classifying and routing suggestions, complaints and compliments to the competent municipal unit. Embedded in SYRCI, the corporate case-management system, it combines deterministic rules with three BERT-based classifiers. Municipal staff retain responsibility: receiving units validate or return routings, and corrections inform rules and retraining. In production since 4 November 2024, by 9 May 2026 it had supported 38,221 routings; 30,225 were validated as correct (79.08%). Within the measured scope, rules and AI automate 97.46% of routings; AI accounts for 47.06% of automated routings. A dashboard refreshed daily covers 84 units and 523 users; two full retraining cycles and a formal risk assessment support safe, accountable operation. Published on the Interoperable Europe Portal with a bilingual reuse and implementation guide, it offers public administrations a documented route to replication.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2988,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02340,EU_PSTW_202609_02340,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Municipality of Piacenza,General public services n.e.c.,UNKNOWN,Piacenza Smart: An Innovative and Inclusive City,Municipality of Piacenza; Local Government; General public services n.e.c.; Italy,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"The Piacenza Municipality Smart City project is a strategic tool for local governance, aimed at modernizing public administration and building a more sustainable, inclusive, and resilient city. The core of the project is the Territorial Information System (SIT), already used by the organization and now undergoing further advanced development, integrated with an urban Digital Twin. This system is conceived as a unified digital infrastructure able of collecting, integrating, and enhancing territorial, environmental, infrastructural, and energy data, transforming information into a concrete lever to support public decisions. Within this framework, the project plays an enabling and cross-cutting role, able of systematizing and enhancing further initiatives promoted by the Municipal Administration, such as the introduction of IoT sensor technology, projects financed under the PNRR (National Recovery and Resilience Plan)—particularly those related to the updating and georeferencing of street numbers and place names—as well as activities and collaborations with external entities, such as the PADRION project and other data survey and collection campaigns, ensuring coherence, interoperability, and reuse of information within a single shared digital infrastructure.",NON_AI_OR_UNCONFIRMED_TECHNOLOGY,IN_DEVELOPMENT,개발 중,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2989,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02341,EU_PSTW_202609_02341,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""enterprise_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Statistics Netherlands (CBS),General public services n.e.c.,Dummy or rule-based test data cannot capture the complexity of the real data.,Privacy-safe synthetic test data: AI-generated replicas of statistical microdata for software development and testing at Statistics Netherlands,Statistics Netherlands (CBS); Private sector; General public services n.e.c.; Netherlands,"Together with technology partner BlueGen, CBS generated a synthetic replica of a large, complex relational dataset using generative AI (a diffusion transformer) trained entirely inside CBS's secure, air-gapped environment.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Statistics Netherlands (CBS) builds and maintains the software pipelines that produce official statistics. New software is developed in an environment that is less strictly secured than production, so real microdata about citizens and businesses may not be used there. Dummy or rule-based test data cannot capture the complexity of the real data. Together with technology partner BlueGen, CBS generated a synthetic replica of a large, complex relational dataset using generative AI (a diffusion transformer) trained entirely inside CBS's secure, air-gapped environment. The synthetic data mirrors the structure, statistical patterns and business rules of the real microdata while containing no real records. It enabled a new statistical pipeline to be developed and tested on realistic data, surfaced real defects before production, and removed the risk of a data leak from the development environment. Resemblance and utility scores exceeded 85%; measured privacy risk was zero",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2990,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02343,EU_PSTW_202609_02343,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""enterprise_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Diputación de Sevilla,General public services n.e.c.,UNKNOWN,Analiz@:Cuadro de Mando Integral de la Diputación de Sevilla,Diputación de Sevilla; Local Government; General public services n.e.c.; Spain,"Linked to the company’s mission, vision, values, and strategy, it offers significant advantages as a key tool in decision-making by management, making use of technology as a highly strategic asset. It is a strategic model implemented in the Human Resources management of the Provincial Council of Seville, based on three pillars: strategic planning, knowledge management, and process optimization.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"The Balanced Scorecard (BSC) is a business management tool that translates an organization’s strategy into a coherent set of relevant indicators aimed at achieving its objectives. Linked to the company’s mission, vision, values, and strategy, it offers significant advantages as a key tool in decision-making by management, making use of technology as a highly strategic asset. It is a strategic model implemented in the Human Resources management of the Provincial Council of Seville, based on three pillars: strategic planning, knowledge management, and process optimization. With the necessary adaptations, it can be applied to any public administration. KEYWORDS: Balanced Scorecard, Strategy, Vision, Mission, Management, Knowledge Management, Process Optimization, Human Resources (HR), Analiz@.",NON_AI_OR_UNCONFIRMED_TECHNOLOGY,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2992,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02344,EU_PSTW_202609_02344,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Università degli Studi di Urbino Carlo Bo,Education n.e.c.,"Applied twice by the university's administrative offices, to a technical manual required by national guidelines and to an internal regulation: about 1,370 pages of sources analysed, some 214,000 words produced, 13 effective working days, against the months of expert work a comparable document had previously required.",Memento — auditable AI-assisted drafting of administrative documentation,Università degli Studi di Urbino Carlo Bo; Academic-Research; Education n.e.c.; Italy,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"A method for producing and reviewing complex administrative documentation with AI: vendor-neutral, at near-zero marginal cost, placing human-model collaboration inside a Git-versioned workflow that is traceable, reproducible and adoptable with tools an administration already owns. Four written registers, including a deterministic archive of the interactions, keep the work portable across people, offices and models. Applied twice by the university's administrative offices, to a technical manual required by national guidelines and to an internal regulation: about 1,370 pages of sources analysed, some 214,000 words produced, 13 effective working days, against the months of expert work a comparable document had previously required. Beyond drafting, the model reviews: examining the whole corpus it surfaced coverage gaps that human review had missed. Human validation and editorial responsibility remain with the officers. Published in full in English and Italian under CC BY 4.0.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2993,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02345,EU_PSTW_202609_02345,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Dienst Uitvoering Onderwijs (DUO),Education n.e.c.,UNKNOWN,Synthetic datasets for Privacy-Friendly Education Research,Dienst Uitvoering Onderwijs (DUO); Central-Government; Education n.e.c.; Netherlands,"This allows researchers and public-sector organisations to use detailed education data that could otherwise be difficult to share because of privacy restrictions. After a 2022–2025 pilot, DUO now uses this approach structurally for new and recurring data deliveries.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"DUO provides synthetic data as a privacy-friendly service for research into the Dutch education system. Machine-learning methods generate artificial records that preserve relevant statistical patterns without directly representing real individuals. This allows researchers and public-sector organisations to use detailed education data that could otherwise be difficult to share because of privacy restrictions. After a 2022–2025 pilot, DUO now uses this approach structurally for new and recurring data deliveries.",NON_AI_OR_UNCONFIRMED_TECHNOLOGY,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2994,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02346,EU_PSTW_202609_02346,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Madrid City Council – Digital Office,General public services n.e.c.,"Open standards and a vendor-neutral architecture allow independently developed systems to work together, turning fragmented data into a shared city representation.","Madrid Digital Twin of Twins: a federated, semantic city digital twin for evidence-based policy decisions",Madrid City Council – Digital Office; Local Government; General public services n.e.c.; Spain,"Building on multiple demonstrators across mobility, infrastructure, urban planning, public space and smart urban spaces, Madrid is now moving from individual use cases to city-scale integration.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Madrid, Digital Capital is building a Digital Twin of Digital Twins: a citywide, interoperable ecosystem that connects specialised digital twins, municipal data and real-world infrastructure through a common semantic framework. Building on multiple demonstrators across mobility, infrastructure, urban planning, public space and smart urban spaces, Madrid is now moving from individual use cases to city-scale integration. Open standards and a vendor-neutral architecture allow independently developed systems to work together, turning fragmented data into a shared city representation. This enables Madrid to integrate information across domains, simulate policy interventions, compare scenarios and assess trade-offs before committing public resources. The result is not simply a more detailed digital model, but a new municipal intelligence capability: understanding how policy decisions in one part of the city affect others, supporting more efficient, sustainable and people-centred public investment.",NON_AI_OR_UNCONFIRMED_TECHNOLOGY,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,F07_DATA_VISIBILITY_INTEGRATION_GAP,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2995,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02347,EU_PSTW_202609_02347,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Regione Emilia-Romagna,General public services n.e.c.,UNKNOWN,ASTRA: unlocking Italy's major terrorism-related and criminal case files through AI,Regione Emilia-Romagna; Regional Government; General public services n.e.c.; Italy,"ASTRA is an AI-powered system developed by the Emilia-Romagna Region to enhance access to digitized judicial records relating to some of Italy’s most significant terrorism-related cases of the late 20th century, including the Bologna (1980) and Italicus Express (1974) massacres, and the crimes of the White Uno Gang. Developed with the State Archives of Bologna, its first institutional user and custodian of the original records, ASTRA uses AI as an interface between users and textual and audiovisual heritage.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"ASTRA is an AI-powered system developed by the Emilia-Romagna Region to enhance access to digitized judicial records relating to some of Italy’s most significant terrorism-related cases of the late 20th century, including the Bologna (1980) and Italicus Express (1974) massacres, and the crimes of the White Uno Gang. Developed with the State Archives of Bologna, its first institutional user and custodian of the original records, ASTRA uses AI as an interface between users and textual and audiovisual heritage. Alongside traditional archival navigation and keyword search, AI enables semantic and conversational exploration, allowing users to query collections in natural language and retrieve relevant records, with links to sources that can be immediately viewed or played and contextualized within the archival hierarchy. ASTRA extends access to non-specialist users, facilitating their exploration and understanding of the records and events they document.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2996,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02348,EU_PSTW_202609_02348,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,De Friese Aanpak,Environmental protection n.e.c.,UNKNOWN,OmgevingsChat,De Friese Aanpak; Local Government; Environmental protection n.e.c.; Netherlands,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"OmgevingsChat is a location-aware generative AI platform that helps public-sector professionals interpret and apply the Dutch Environment and Planning Act. Users select a location and ask questions in natural language. The platform combines official DSO data, applicable legislation and organisation-specific sources to generate clear, traceable answers with verifiable references. Developed in partnership with Dutch public authorities and already used by ten clients across municipalities and provinces, it supports legal research, public service delivery, policy development and environmental planning. Human professionals remain responsible for interpretation and decisions. Its modular architecture, evaluation tools and responsible-AI safeguards make OmgevingsChat scalable and reusable across municipalities, provinces, water authorities and regional environmental agencies.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2997,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02349,EU_PSTW_202609_02349,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,"Instituto para o Ensino Superior, I.P.",Education n.e.c.,"It replaced a fragmented and highly manual process (involving dispersed contact lists, individual email preparation and repetitive attachment handling) with a single, standardised and automated workflow. For a communication to 33 projects, the end-to-end process was reduced from approximately 5 hours to 5 minutes (a time reduction of over 98%) while reducing manual errors, ensuring consistent institutional communication standards and freeing technical staff for higher-value tasks.",Auto Send Mails - PRR: An Integrated Low-Code Solution for Automating Public Administration Communications,"Instituto para o Ensino Superior, I.P.; Central-Government; Education n.e.c.; Portugal","Built entirely with existing organisational resources, it integrates SharePoint, Excel, Power Apps, Power Automate, Power BI and Microsoft Teams, without additional procurement, external development or software costs.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Auto Send Mails - PRR is an internally developed low-code solution that transformed how official communications are managed across Portugal's Recovery and Resilience Plan (PRR). It replaced a fragmented and highly manual process (involving dispersed contact lists, individual email preparation and repetitive attachment handling) with a single, standardised and automated workflow. Built entirely with existing organisational resources, it integrates SharePoint, Excel, Power Apps, Power Automate, Power BI and Microsoft Teams, without additional procurement, external development or software costs. The solution currently supports 7 PRR programmes and 99 projects, centralising contact management and enabling controlled recipient selection, content preparation and automated sending. For a communication to 33 projects, the end-to-end process was reduced from approximately 5 hours to 5 minutes (a time reduction of over 98%) while reducing manual errors, ensuring consistent institutional communication standards and freeing technical staff for higher-value tasks.",NON_AI_OR_UNCONFIRMED_TECHNOLOGY,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK|F08_ERROR_COMPLIANCE_RISK,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2998,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02350,EU_PSTW_202609_02350,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Regione Marche,Education n.e.c.,This makes it difficult to certify the skills acquired and to evaluate them for the certification of specific professional profiles.,Regional e-portfolio of certified skills using blockchain technology,Regione Marche; Regional Government; Education n.e.c.; Italy,"The use of Open Badges to track the acquisition of micro-credentials, both formal and informal, is becoming increasingly widespread. However, skills are often described without the use of specific and shared vocabularies, and without the possibility of assessing the duration of courses or the presence of final tests.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"The use of Open Badges to track the acquisition of micro-credentials, both formal and informal, is becoming increasingly widespread. However, skills are often described without the use of specific and shared vocabularies, and without the possibility of assessing the duration of courses or the presence of final tests. This makes it difficult to certify the skills acquired and to evaluate them for the certification of specific professional profiles. The Marche Region has created a single regional e-portfolio, Marche Digital Open Badge, designed to build a digital learning portfolio for citizens of the Marche region, enabling them to certify their skills and share the related attestations in verifiable and standard formats. The system is made available to all organisations carrying out training activities in the regional territory, including schools, universities, companies, voluntary associations and local training providers. This allows each citizen-user to have a comprehensive overview of the training-related skills acquired throughout their lifetime.",NON_AI_OR_UNCONFIRMED_TECHNOLOGY,IN_DEVELOPMENT,개발 중,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2999,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02351,EU_PSTW_202609_02351,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research"", ""enterprise_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Camera di Commercio Irpinia Sannio,"General economic, commercial and labour affair",The Irpinia Sannio Chamber of Commerce carries out its functions in a territory that clearly illustrates a challenge common to much of Europe. The organisation publishes its accessibility statement in accordance with the AgID model and maintains an active feedback mechanism through which users can report accessibility difficulties.,ISIA Intelligenza artificiale generativa come nuovo modello di servizio pubblico alle imprese,"Camera di Commercio Irpinia Sannio; Local Government; General economic, commercial and labour affair; Italy","What distinguishes the case, however, is not the technology adopted, which is widely available, but the decision to use it to adapt the administration to the user rather than requiring the user to adapt to the administration. Finally, it concerns channels: no function can be accessed through only one route, ensuring that users who are unable to use one channel are not excluded from the service.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"The Irpinia Sannio Chamber of Commerce carries out its functions in a territory that clearly illustrates a challenge common to much of Europe. Almost ninety thousand businesses, predominantly micro and small enterprises, are distributed across two provinces characterised by a high proportion of inland areas and served by only two Chamber of Commerce offices. For many of these businesses, access to a public service has never been a question of whether the service is available, but rather of compatibility: between office opening hours and working hours, between the institutional office and the distance separating it from the municipality where the business is located, and between the language of administrative procedures and that of those who must navigate them without qualified intermediaries. The proposed solution addresses this gap. ISIA is the organisation’s virtual assistant, operational since 29 May 2025 and migrated to a generative artificial intelligence-based architecture in May 2026, representing the first such case within the Italian Chamber of Commerce system. It queries the institutional knowledge base to provide contextualised answers, guides users through access to the eight active Online Services, and enables appointments to be booked directly: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pbVtQO1rWyA. What distinguishes the case, however, is not the technology adopted, which is widely available, but the decision to use it to adapt the administration to the user rather than requiring the user to adapt to the administration. First and foremost, this concerns language: following the migration to generative AI, requests asking users to rephrase their questions fell from 4.0% to 0.3% of messages, providing a measure of how significantly the terminology barrier has been reduced. It also concerns time: more than half of interactions take place outside public opening hours, and during evening and night-time hours the assistant is not merely an alternative channel but the only one available. Finally, it concerns channels: no function can be accessed through only one route, ensuring that users who are unable to use one channel are not excluded from the service. Human support has not been removed, but rather repositioned towards higher-value activities. Artificial intelligence is placed at the entry point of a four-level service pathway that always ultimately leads to a person: from independent access to information to assisted conversation, from online transactions to an interview with an operator, either in person or via video call, including document exchange and payments. Content remains under the responsibility of the competent offices; the system provides information and guidance without adopting administrative decisions, while responsibility for the administrative procedure remains with a natural person. By diverting from the service desk those requests that can be resolved upstream, automation has made operators more available for cases that genuinely require human expertise, while also making them accessible without requiring users to travel. The institutionally decisive step took place on 27 July 2026: through an administrative order issued by the Secretary-General, access to the five services involving the highest level of direct interaction was made subject to appointment booking, which can be completed either through the website or directly through a conversation with the virtual assistant, complemented by a remote service desk via videoconference. The virtual assistant does not simply operate alongside the service desk: it orchestrates access to the different service channels while ensuring that human support remains available at all times: https://www.irpiniasannio.camcom.it/notizie/nuova-modalita-accesso-agli-sportelli-prenotazione. The project forms part of “Le Camere del Futuro” (“The Chambers of the Future”), a national programme promoted by Unioncamere for the digital transformation of the Chamber of Commerce system. Irpinia Sannio is the first Chamber to integrate generative artificial intelligence into this framework: what has been implemented is therefore not an isolated experiment, but a prototype embedded within an architecture already shared by all Italian Chambers of Commerce. Alongside this transformation, the organisation has implemented a structured capacity-building programme targeting both its own staff and businesses operating in the territory, based on the principle that public technology that nobody knows how to use cannot generate public value. The solution was designed in accordance with the European and national accessibility framework: Directive (EU) 2016/2102 on the accessibility of the websites and mobile applications of public sector bodies; the harmonised EN 301 549 standard incorporating WCAG 2.1 Level AA criteria; and the relevant Italian implementing legislation (Law No 4/2004, as amended by Legislative Decree No 106/2018), together with the AgID Guidelines on the Accessibility of ICT Tools. The new institutional website, launched as part of the project, is built on the reference model for Italian public administration websites, which incorporates accessibility requirements into its navigation structure, colour contrasts and markup semantics. The organisation publishes its accessibility statement in accordance with the AgID model and maintains an active feedback mechanism through which users can report accessibility difficulties. Accessibility, however, has been interpreted more broadly than technical compliance alone, because the divide affecting businesses in this territory is not solely related to sensory accessibility. **Channel redundancy.** No function is accessible through only one route. An appointment can be booked through the website, in conversation with the virtual assistant, or at the reception desk, which schedules the first available appointment for anyone arriving without a prior booking. Information about an administrative requirement is available as a structured information sheet that can be browsed by category or keyword, as a conversational response, or through a discussion with an operator. Users who are unable to use one channel are therefore not excluded from the service. **Cognitive and linguistic accessibility.** The assistant responds in natural language to questions formulated in natural language, without requiring users to know administrative terminology. The reduction in requests for users to rephrase their questions from 4.0% to 0.3% of messages, measured following the technological upgrade, indicates the extent to which this barrier has been lowered: it is the administration that adapts to the user’s language, rather than the other way around. **Physical and temporal accessibility.** The remote service desk via videoconference, including document exchange and online payments, enables users to access Chamber of Commerce services without travelling. This is particularly relevant for people with reduced mobility and for businesses located in inland municipalities far from the two physical offices. More than half of interactions with the assistant take place outside public opening hours: service availability is therefore no longer dependent on compatibility between office opening hours and entrepreneurs’ working schedules. **Economic accessibility.** All components — the virtual assistant, specialist support, online services and the training programme — are provided to users free of charge. Accessibility is also one of the topics covered by the training programme offered to businesses, through a dedicated corporate case study. Accessibility is therefore not only a requirement applied to the service itself, but also knowledge transferred to the local business community. The solution was not acquired through a procurement procedure to which the EU standard contractual clauses would have been applicable. By means of a managerial decision dated 7 February 2025, the Irpinia Sannio Chamber of Commerce joined “Le Camere del Futuro”, the national programme promoted by Unioncamere for the digital transformation of the Italian Chamber of Commerce system. The solution is developed and operated by InfoCamere, an in-house company owned by the Chambers of Commerce, within the service relationship connecting the infrastructure operator with the entire Chamber system. Consequently, there was no competitive procurement procedure for acquiring an artificial intelligence system from an external supplier; rather, the Chamber joined a system configuration that had already been designed and made available to participating Chambers. Nevertheless, the safeguards that the model contractual clauses are intended to ensure are addressed through other mechanisms. The operator is a publicly owned entity controlled by the contracting administrations and subject to their equivalent control: data, infrastructure and service continuity therefore remain within the public-sector perimeter. Ownership of and responsibility for information content remain with the competent Chamber offices. Traceability of system use is ensured through structured reporting covering the entire period of operation, which is available for audit and internal control purposes. The quality of responses is subject to systematic assessment, with documented results. The system performs an information and guidance function and does not adopt administrative decisions: responsibility for the administrative procedure remains with a natural person, as required by Italian rules governing the use of artificial intelligence within public administration. The organisation nevertheless considers the EU standard contractual clauses to be a useful reference and intends to examine them in connection with future developments of the solution, including as a framework for verifying the safeguards already in place within its relationship with the infrastructure operator. **Technology Partner:** InfoCamere S.C.p.A., the in-house company of the Italian Chamber of Commerce system. **Scientific Partners:** Societing Lab — an action-research programme of the University of Naples Federico II; Giustino Fortunato Telematic University (e-learning platform and issuance of Open Badges).",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-3000,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02352,EU_PSTW_202609_02352,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Ministry of the Interior of the Czech Republic,General public services n.e.c.,UNKNOWN,AI assistant for public decision processes,Ministry of the Interior of the Czech Republic; Central-Government; General public services n.e.c.; Czechia,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"An assistant for administrative proceedings who assists officials in administrative proceedings within the framework of the agenda of offenses, felling of trees and trade licensing agenda. The assistant guides the official through the process, helps with the analysis of input data, checks the completeness of the submission, deadlines and helps with the creation of administrative decisions and speeds up administrative proceedings. It is designed by the central government to be depoyed at local government level.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-3001,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02353,EU_PSTW_202609_02353,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,"Danish Competition and Consumer Authority (Konkurrence- og Forbrugerstyrelsen, KFST)","General economic, commercial and labour affair","Bid rigging in public procurement is difficult to detect through conventional investigation, because collusive tenders are designed to appear competitive.",Bid Viewer – computational screening for bid rigging in public procurement,"Danish Competition and Consumer Authority (Konkurrence- og Forbrugerstyrelsen, KFST); Central-Government; General economic, commercial and labour affair; Denmark",UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Bid rigging in public procurement is difficult to detect through conventional investigation, because collusive tenders are designed to appear competitive. The Danish Competition and Consumer Authority (KFST) developed Bid Viewer in-house to screen large volumes of tender data for signals of horizontal agreements between bidders. The tool computes a set of statistical indicators of non-competitive bidding behaviour — covering the number and pattern of tenders, the variance and distribution of bid prices, bid rotation and incumbency patterns — and feeds these indicators into machine learning screens that combine them into a single model. The models are trained and evaluated on tender data containing known cartel cases, and assign each tender a probability score reflecting its likelihood of collusion, allowing case handlers to prioritise the tenders most worth investigating. Artificial neural networks are used alongside the statistical screens to improve classification performance. Bid Viewer is used operationally by the Authority to support a range of investigations, specifically the identification of bid rigging. The tool has been developed in cooperation with the Spanish and Swedish competition authorities and has been transferred to counterpart authorities in other European countries, including the Estonian Competition Authority and the United Kingdom, making it a reference case for cross-border reuse of an anti-collusion analytics solution. Its public value lies in stronger enforcement capability, better allocation of scarce investigative resources, and protection of public spending against cartel overcharges.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-3002,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_02354,EU_PSTW_202609_02354,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research"", ""enterprise_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,"Ministry for Home Affairs, Local Government, Building and Digitalisation of North Rhine-Westphalia (MHKBD)",General services.,UNKNOWN,GovRadar – AI-assisted preparation of tender documents in North Rhine-Westphalia,"Ministry for Home Affairs, Local Government, Building and Digitalisation of North Rhine-Westphalia (MHKBD); Regional Government; General services.; Germany",UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"North Rhine-Westphalia has established the first statewide digital standard for tender preparation in a large German federal state. The Ministry for Home Affairs, Local Government, Building and Digitalisation (MHKBD) concluded a framework contract with the Munich-based GovTech company GovRadar GmbH, opening access in April 2025 to all 427 municipalities and extending it in July 2025 to all state authorities, agencies, higher education institutions and state-owned undertakings. The cloud-based solution focuses on the content preparation phase of procurement rather than process administration. It supports the drafting of legally compliant technical specifications by generating text proposals from a continuously updated corpus of millions of existing German tender documents, provides semantic search and an AI assistant for targeted research, structures market data for digitalised market exploration across product categories, and guides the creation of contracts and standard documents without media discontinuity. By supporting product-neutral, unambiguous specifications, the tool reduces the scope for specifications tailored to a single supplier and improves the quality and comparability of bids. Authorities report time savings of up to 90% in the preparation of tender drafts. As of mid-2025, 166 municipalities had requested the municipal licence and 2,140 individual user licences had been issued.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-3003,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_RECOVERED_PSTW_47,EU_PSTW_202609_RECOVERED_PSTW_47,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,State Financial IT Agency,"Executive and legislative organs, financial and fiscal affairs, external affairs.","The requests handled manually by level 1 support operators now represent a volume of more than 15,000 per month (18,000 in January!).",ClaudIA - Chatbot for the invoicing portal for purchases by public authorities,"State Financial IT Agency; Central-Government; Executive and legislative organs, financial and fiscal affairs, external affairs.; France",UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Chatbot Claudia has been setup by the AIFE (State Financial IT Agency) for users of the information system Chorus of SME's and microbusinesses. This chatbot, is based on IBM's Watson Artificial Intelligence technology. The AIFE indicates that the number of support contacts ""has not stopped increasing, going from 20,000 per month to more than 40,000 (with a peak at 55,000 in January) all channels combined (phone calls, files, live chat , emails, avatar, chatbot). The requests handled manually by level 1 support operators now represent a volume of more than 15,000 per month (18,000 in January!). The AIFE anticipates a doubling of support requests each year. Before Claudia, only half of the requests were processed automatically. Today, the rate has risen to 65%. “In two months, ClaudIA handled more than 10,000 conversations, with an average of 3.5 interactions per conversation,” says AIFE. Claudia takes the user context into account and knows how to detect inappropriate interactions.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,F01_REPETITIVE_MANUAL_WORK,S2_AGENT_CONVERSATIONAL_AI,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-47,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_RECOVERED_PSTW_748,EU_PSTW_202609_RECOVERED_PSTW_748,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""enterprise_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,European Fund and Asset Management Association,R&D economic affairs,UNKNOWN,Blockchain for Taxes project,European Fund and Asset Management Association; Consortium; R&D economic affairs; European Union,"The Malta Business Registry implemented blockchain technology for company registration and intellectual property records, becoming the first EU member state to join the IP Register on blockchain.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Malta sought to establish itself as the ""Blockchain Island"" through comprehensive adoption of distributed ledger technology across government services, requiring practical applications that would demonstrate national commitment to the strategy. The Malta Business Registry implemented blockchain technology for company registration and intellectual property records, becoming the first EU member state to join the IP Register on blockchain. The system provides immutable records of business incorporation, ownership changes, and intellectual property registrations, enhancing transparency and reducing opportunities for corporate fraud. This technical implementation supports Malta's broader regulatory framework established through dedicated blockchain legislation. The initiative positions Malta as a pioneer in government blockchain adoption within the European Union, attracting blockchain businesses seeking a supportive regulatory environment.",NON_AI_OR_UNCONFIRMED_TECHNOLOGY,PILOT,시험·파일럿,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-748,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_RECOVERED_PSTW_772,EU_PSTW_202609_RECOVERED_PSTW_772,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""enterprise_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Malta Business Registry (MBR),"General economic, commercial and labour affair",UNKNOWN,Registry of Companies system,"Malta Business Registry (MBR); Central-Government; General economic, commercial and labour affair; Malta","The Malta Business Registry implemented blockchain technology for company registration and intellectual property records, becoming the first EU member state to join the IP Register on blockchain.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Malta sought to establish itself as the ""Blockchain Island"" through comprehensive adoption of distributed ledger technology across government services, requiring practical applications that would demonstrate national commitment to the strategy. The Malta Business Registry implemented blockchain technology for company registration and intellectual property records, becoming the first EU member state to join the IP Register on blockchain. The system provides immutable records of business incorporation, ownership changes, and intellectual property registrations, enhancing transparency and reducing opportunities for corporate fraud. This technical implementation supports Malta's broader regulatory framework established through dedicated blockchain legislation. The initiative positions Malta as a pioneer in government blockchain adoption within the European Union, attracting blockchain businesses seeking a supportive regulatory environment.",NON_AI_OR_UNCONFIRMED_TECHNOLOGY,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-772,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_RECOVERED_PSTW_1126,EU_PSTW_202609_RECOVERED_PSTW_1126,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,UK Home Office,Police Services,"The algorithm faced legal challenges from the Joint Council for the Welfare of Immigrants (JCWI) and Foxglove, as it was believed to perpetuate racism and bias in the visa system.",Automated decision making system to determine the risk represented by visa applicants,UK Home Office; Central-Government; Police Services; United Kingdom,"In response to the criticism, the Home Office announced plans to redesign the ADM system, explicitly addressing concerns about unconscious bias and the use of nationality in the new system.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"In August 2020, the UK government's Home Office abandoned an ADM system called the ""Streaming tool"" that assessed the risk of visa applicants. The algorithm faced legal challenges from the Joint Council for the Welfare of Immigrants (JCWI) and Foxglove, as it was believed to perpetuate racism and bias in the visa system. The algorithm suffered from ""feedback loop"" issues, where past bias and discrimination influenced future outcomes. It prioritized applicants from predominantly white countries and subjected people from other nations to a more rigorous review process. In response to the criticism, the Home Office announced plans to redesign the ADM system, explicitly addressing concerns about unconscious bias and the use of nationality in the new system.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,NOT_IN_USE,미사용,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-1126,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_RECOVERED_PSTW_2888,EU_PSTW_202609_RECOVERED_PSTW_2888,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""education_research"", ""social_nonprofit""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Zenter fir d'Lëtzebuerger Sprooch (ZLS – Centre for Luxembourgish Language),Cultural services.,UNKNOWN,"""Sproocherkennung fir d'Lëtzebuergescht"": improving schreifmaschinn.lu, an AI-based speech-to-text tool in various languages",Zenter fir d'Lëtzebuerger Sprooch (ZLS – Centre for Luxembourgish Language); Non-governmental; Cultural services.; Luxembourg,"At operational level, the project strengthens the data foundation behind Luxembourgish speech technology, enabling better automatic transcription for public, educational, cultural and administrative uses.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Luxembourgish is central to the country’s linguistic identity, but speech-recognition technologies often perform better for larger languages with more abundant training data. “Sproocherkennung fir d’Lëtzebuergescht” addresses this gap by improving the speech-to-text capabilities of schreifmaschinn.lu, an AI-based transcription tool developed by the Zenter fir d’Lëtzebuerger Sprooch. The operational problem is that accurate speech recognition requires high-quality synchronised audio and text data, representing different speakers, accents, contexts and recording situations. The existing dataset already provides a foundation for Luxembourgish transcription, but broader and more diverse training material is needed to improve recognition quality and spelling accuracy. The initiative expands the hypersynchronised audio-text dataset from 55 hours to 80 hours, with two main objectives: diversifying the range of speakers and situations represented in the data, and improving orthographic accuracy in the generated transcription. At operational level, the project strengthens the data foundation behind Luxembourgish speech technology, enabling better automatic transcription for public, educational, cultural and administrative uses. It also supports digital inclusion by making spoken Luxembourgish more usable in digital environments, from accessibility tools to language-learning resources and public-service interfaces. The expected impact is more accurate Luxembourgish speech-to-text, stronger support for multilingual digital services and greater visibility of Luxembourgish in AI-enabled communication systems. The initiative is relevant because it treats language resources as strategic digital infrastructure for public-sector innovation and linguistic diversity.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,IN_DEVELOPMENT,개발 중,,S3_DOCUMENT_INTELLIGENCE,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2888,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_RECOVERED_PSTW_2983,EU_PSTW_202609_RECOVERED_PSTW_2983,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Stadt Hamm (City of Hamm),General public services n.e.c.,UNKNOWN,Empowering Local Government: A Sovereign and Human-Centric AI Strategy for Inclusive Citizen Services and Administrative Efficiency,Stadt Hamm (City of Hamm); Local Government; General public services n.e.c.; Germany,"The City of Hamm drives a holistic ""People, Processes, Technology"" transformation via a structured four-pillar AI architecture: (1) ""Tom Hamme"", a 24/7 citizen chatbot supporting 100+ native languages including Easy Language for inclusive public services; (2) ""IDA"", a sovereign, self-hosted internal AI assistant for text-heavy tasks; (3) AI-enhanced RPA for end-to-end process automation; and (4) AI-powered specialized municipal software.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"The City of Hamm drives a holistic ""People, Processes, Technology"" transformation via a structured four-pillar AI architecture: (1) ""Tom Hamme"", a 24/7 citizen chatbot supporting 100+ native languages including Easy Language for inclusive public services; (2) ""IDA"", a sovereign, self-hosted internal AI assistant for text-heavy tasks; (3) AI-enhanced RPA for end-to-end process automation; and (4) AI-powered specialized municipal software. By hosting core internal AI operations locally, the city avoids vendor lock-in and ensures strict data sovereignty aligned with EU values. Our key differentiator is a human-centric approach to change management. Moving beyond mere IT deployment, a city-wide e-learning program proactively fulfills the AI literacy mandate of the EU AI Act (Art. 4). Complemented by an internal ""AI Lab"" for iterative, user-centric testing, this strategy ensures a compliant and resilient digital transformation for civil servants and citizens alike.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,IN_DEVELOPMENT,개발 중,,S2_AGENT_CONVERSATIONAL_AI,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2983,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_RECOVERED_PSTW_2984,EU_PSTW_202609_RECOVERED_PSTW_2984,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work"", ""enterprise_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Secoval srl (In-house public company providing technological services for the Comunità Montana della Valle Sabbia and member Municipalities),Public order and safety n.e.c.,UNKNOWN,Mapperò: AI-Driven Road Infrastructure Governance & Circular Territorial Ecosystem,Secoval srl (In-house public company providing technological services for the Comunità Montana della Valle Sabbia and member Municipalities); Local Government; Public order and safety n.e.c.; Italy,"It makes use of standard public service vehicles already out on the territory (like the waste collection trucks run by Sae Valle Sabbia, another in-house company providing tech services for the Comunità Montana della Valle Sabbia and its member municipalities), and the platform automatically spots road defects using smartphone accelerometers and AI computer vision models.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Mapperò is an integrated technological and methodological platform for smart, preventive, and sustainable management of road networks and municipal infrastructure. It makes use of standard public service vehicles already out on the territory (like the waste collection trucks run by Sae Valle Sabbia, another in-house company providing tech services for the Comunità Montana della Valle Sabbia and its member municipalities), and the platform automatically spots road defects using smartphone accelerometers and AI computer vision models. Mapperò goes beyond the static ""digital twin"" idea to build a circular ecosystem of value for the territory, connecting Public Administration, private contractors, and citizens all together. The municipalities that have adopted this solution are: Agnosine, Anfo, Bagolino, Barghe, Bedizzole, Bione, Capovalle, Casto, Gavardo, Idro, Lavenone, Mazzano, Mura, Muscoline, Nuvolento, Nuvolera, Odolo, Paitone, Pertica Alta, Pertica Bassa, Preseglie, Provaglio V/S, Rezzato, Roè Volciano, Sabbio Chiese, Salò, Serle, Treviso Bresciano, Vallio Terme, Vestone, Villanuova S/C, Vobarno.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2984,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_RECOVERED_PSTW_2986,EU_PSTW_202609_RECOVERED_PSTW_2986,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Regione Emilia-Romagna (Emilia-Romagna Region),Environmental protection n.e.c.,UNKNOWN,VERA (Air Quality Digital Twin of the Emilia-Romagna Region),Regione Emilia-Romagna (Emilia-Romagna Region); Regional Government; Environmental protection n.e.c.; Italy,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"VERA (Air Quality Digital Twin of the Emilia-Romagna Region) is a cutting-edge environmental governance digital twin platform designed to simulate, predict, and visualize territorial and environmental responses to public policies. Funded with â‚¬3M via PR FESR 2021-2027, VERA acts as a decision-support system accelerating the region's path toward air quality improvement and carbon neutrality. By integrating complex multi-source data (IoT, real-time traffic data, environmental data and Copernicus satellite feeds), VERA enables public administrators to model emissions and concentrations of key pollutants (PM10, PM2.5, NOx) through dynamic ""what-if"" scenarios. Structurally aligned with Europe's Digital Valley goals, the platform features specialized environments: VERA for simulations by regional public authorities, VERA City for 3D high-resolution (50x50m grid) micro-territorial zoom monitoring and impact of local actions, and VERA People for open citizen engagement.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,DEPLOYED,원천 보고: 운영,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2986,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
AXALL_EU_PSTW_202609_RECOVERED_PSTW_2991,EU_PSTW_202609_RECOVERED_PSTW_2991,SOURCE_REPORTED_USE_CASE,SOURCE_REPORTED_PROJECT_OR_USE_CASE,European Commission Joint Research Centre,public_work,공공기관·공공서비스,"[""public_work""]",PUBLIC_AGENCY,Regione Marche,General public services n.e.c.,UNKNOWN,"Marche Region’s AI Use Cases related to public procurement, implemented within the projects: “#REG4IA - AI Hubs for PAs”, “ERDF 1.2.2.1 Advanced AI Solutions for public services”, “TrasparenzAI”",Regione Marche; Regional Government; General public services n.e.c.; Italy,"Marche Region uses AI to streamline administrative procedures through three converging public-procurement initiatives. Under the nationally funded interregional project #Reg4IA, Marche runs a PoC using generative and ontology-based AI to assist contracting officers with tender-idcode requests, compliance checklists, drafting of contracts and payment decrees, and timeline planning, under strict human-in-the-loop oversight.",UNKNOWN; 원천의 기대효과와 별도 관측 성과는 구분해야 합니다.,UNKNOWN,"Marche Region uses AI to streamline administrative procedures through three converging public-procurement initiatives. Under the nationally funded interregional project #Reg4IA, Marche runs a PoC using generative and ontology-based AI to assist contracting officers with tender-idcode requests, compliance checklists, drafting of contracts and payment decrees, and timeline planning, under strict human-in-the-loop oversight. This builds on Marche's own AI platform (AIMA, ERDF 2021-27, measure 1.2.2.1), offering customised agent-automation tools and innovative features - including contextual know-how enrichment - reusable in multi-tenant mode by other PAs. Lastly, under an ANAC-CNR protocol and an agreement now being signed with ANAC, the ""TrasparenzAI"" project will test AI web-scraping to verify public-contract data PAs must publish in the ""Transparent Administration"" and ""Public Customer's Profile"" website sections, standardising data collection and strengthening transparency nationwide.",SOURCE_CLASSIFIED_AI,IN_DEVELOPMENT,개발 중,,,https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/public-sector-tech-watch/pstw-cases-viewer-data-download,PSTW-2991,CC BY 4.0,SOURCE_REPORTED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFIED,STRUCTURED_SOURCE_ROW_CHECKED,True,2.5.0-inclusive,False
